{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794669401267,"sessionID":"ses_e255ff46effe7EWyuOLOEwVdy1","part":{"partID":"prt_1daa1d3a5002RSHrbT7FukGoYg","sessionID":"ses_e255ff46effe7EWyuOLOEwVdy1","messageID":"msg_1daa1c54f001f7quTQjI7MsOom","type":"tool","id":"call_cdeefafb4101482e8d5ed5c8","tool":"read","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"limit":400,"offset":2222,"path":".skilled/commands/deep/assets/deep-review-auto.yaml"},"output":"Read file .skilled/commands/deep/assets/deep-review-auto.yaml, lines 2222-2592\n2222:   phase_synthesis:\n2223:     purpose: Compile all iteration findings into review/review-report.md\n2224:     steps:\n2225: \n2226:       step_fanout_merge:\n2227:         description: \"Merge N lineage registries with strongest-restriction; bind p0/p1/p2 counts for step_derive_verdict; skip when single-executor\"\n2228:         skip_when: \"config.fanout is absent\"\n2229:         command: |\n2230:           node .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/fanout-merge.cjs \\\n2231:             --loop-type review \\\n2232:             --artifact-dir {artifact_dir}\n2233:         working_directory: \"{repo_root}\"\n2234:         wait_for_completion: true\n2235:         bind_from_output:\n2236:           p0_count: \"active_p0\"\n2237:           p1_count: \"active_p1\"\n2238:           p2_count: \"active_p2\"\n2239: \n2240:       step_hydrate_summary_metrics:\n2241:         action: \"Hydrate summary metrics before synthesis\"\n2242:         read:\n2243:           - \"{state_paths.config}\"\n2244:           - \"{state_paths.state_log}\"\n2245:           - \"{state_paths.findings_registry}\"\n2246:           - \"{state_paths.strategy}\"\n2247:         read_patterns:\n2248:           - \"{state_paths.packet_dir}/lineages/*/deep-review-state.jsonl\"\n2249:         extract:\n2250:           - iteration_count: \"When direct lineage state logs exist, count distinct run values (the integer iteration, else a numeric run) across those logs in stable lineage order; otherwise count distinct run values (the integer iteration, else a numeric run) across the root state log. Never add root compatibility records to lineage records.\"\n2251:           - highest_run: \"When direct lineage state logs exist, take the highest run value (the integer iteration, else a numeric run) across lines where type === 'iteration' in those logs in stable lineage order, else 0; otherwise take the highest run value (the integer iteration, else a numeric run) across lines where type === 'iteration' in the root state log, else 0. Never add root compatibility records to lineage records.\"\n2252:           - current_iteration: \"max(highest_run, iteration_count) + 1\"\n2253:           - p0_count: \"Total P0 findings across all iterations (deduped)\"\n2254:           - p1_count: \"Total P1 findings across all iterations (deduped)\"\n2255:           - p2_count: \"Total P2 findings across all iterations (deduped)\"\n2256:           - dimensions_covered: \"List of reviewed dimensions\"\n2257:           - dimension_coverage: \"covered / total\"\n2258:           - ac_coverage_signal: \"For spec-folder targets only: if level is 2+ and acceptance-criteria.md exists and implementation-summary.md is in-progress or later, surface the AC_COVERAGE advisory status; otherwise mark exempt.\"\n2259:           - last_3_summaries: \"Summarize the latest 3 iteration records\"\n2260:           - reason: \"Use the latest stop reason if present, else the frozen default 'converged'. (Must be a member of the STOP_REASONS enum: converged, maxIterationsReached, blockedStop, stuckRecovery, error, manualStop, userPaused.)\"\n2261: \n2262:       # H-1 verdict derivation: parse findings JSONL, map highest severity to verdict\n2263:       # - PASS: no P0 or P1 findings (P2-only or clean)\n2264:       # - CONDITIONAL: any P1 findings (no P0)\n2265:       # - FAIL: any P0 findings\n2266:       # Final line of iteration-NNN.md MUST be exactly: \"Review verdict: PASS\" / \"Review verdict: CONDITIONAL\" / \"Review verdict: FAIL\"\n2267:       step_derive_verdict:\n2268:         action: \"Derive review verdict from accumulated findings\"\n2269:         algorithm: |\n2270:           if p0_count > 0:\n2271:             verdict = \"FAIL\"\n2272:           elif p1_count > 0:\n2273:             verdict = \"CONDITIONAL\"\n2274:           else:\n2275:             verdict = \"PASS\"\n2276:           has_advisories = (verdict == \"PASS\" and p2_count > 0)\n2277:           ac_coverage_signal is advisory while the validation rule is INFO/default-off; include it in synthesis traceability, but do not change the exact verdict enum from this signal alone.\n2278:         outputs:\n2279:           - verdict: \"PASS | CONDITIONAL | FAIL\"\n2280:           - has_advisories: \"Boolean true when verdict is PASS and any active P2 findings exist\"\n2281:           - ac_coverage_signal: \"exempt | disabled | pass | advisory-shortfall\"\n2282:         contract: |\n2283:           Every iteration-NNN.md must end with exactly: \"Review verdict: PASS\" (or CONDITIONAL or FAIL).\n2284:           Downstream automation parses this final line via exact string match — do not vary the format.\n2285: \n2286:       step_read_all_iterations:\n2287:         action: \"Read all iteration files and strategy\"\n2288:         read_pattern: \"{state_paths.iteration_dir}/iteration-*.md\"\n2289:         read_also: \"{state_paths.strategy}\"\n2290: \n2291:       step_build_finding_registry:\n2292:         action: \"Build deduplicated finding registry from all iterations\"\n2293:         algorithm: |\n2294:           1. Extract all findings from iteration JSONL delta files\n2295:           2. Compute content_hash for each finding (emission requirement):\n2296:              content_hash = sha256(file_path + \"\\u001f\" + line_range + \"\\u001f\" + finding_type + \"\\u001f\" + normalized_description_80chars)\n2297:              Normalized description = whitespace-collapsed, lowercased, first 80 chars of the finding description.\n2298:           3. Two-tier dedup:\n2299:              PRIMARY: group by content_hash field\n2300:                - Same content_hash, multiple dimensions → single finding, merged `dimensions: [<all>]` array\n2301:                - Keep highest severity on duplicates\n2302:              FALLBACK (legacy records lacking content_hash): file:line + normalized_title\n2303:                - Same file:line, multiple dimensions → single finding, multiple dimension tags\n2304:                - Keep highest severity on duplicates\n2305:           4. Track finding lifecycle:\n2306:              - status: active | duplicate | upgraded | downgraded | contested | resolved_false_positive\n2307:              - Record first_seen, upgraded_in, previous_severity for severity changes\n2308:              - Record dimensions array reflecting all dimensions that emitted this finding\n2309:           5. Resolve contradictions:\n2310:              - Findings marked contested across iterations → referee pass\n2311:              - Determine final severity and status\n2312:           6. Count only 'active' findings for totals\n2313:         outputs:\n2314:           - finding_registry: \"Deduplicated list of all findings with metadata\"\n2315:           - active_p0: \"Count of active P0 findings\"\n2316:           - active_p1: \"Count of active P1 findings\"\n2317:           - active_p2: \"Count of active P2 findings\"\n2318: \n2319:       step_adversarial_selfcheck:\n2320:         action: \"Final adversarial self-check on all P0 and P1 findings\"\n2321:         algorithm: |\n2322:           For each active P0/P1 finding:\n2323:             1. Hunter: Re-verify finding against source code (re-read file:line)\n2324:             2. Skeptic: Challenge severity — is this really P0/P1? Could it be P2?\n2325:             3. Referee: Final call — confirm, downgrade, or mark false_positive\n2326:           Update finding_registry with adjudicated results.\n2327: \n2328:       step_emit_resource_map:\n2329:         skip_when: \"config.fanout is present\"\n2330:         action: \"Emit {state_paths.resource_map_output} from converged review deltas unless config.resource_map.emit is false\"\n2331:         command: \"node .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/reduce-state.cjs {spec_folder} {reducer_artifact_arg} --create-missing-anchors --emit-resource-map\"\n2332:         read:\n2333:           - \"{state_paths.config}\"\n2334:           - \"{state_paths.delta_dir}/iter-*.jsonl\"\n2335:         write:\n2336:           - \"{state_paths.resource_map_output}\"\n2337:         guarantee: \"Reducer skips cleanly when config.resource_map.emit == false and writes a deterministic resource-map when enabled.\"\n2338:         note: \"A fan-out root has no root state log before closeout, so the root reducer would fail on the missing file. Each lineage emits its own map, so the report names the ones that exist at {artifact_dir}/lineages/*/resource-map.md.\"\n2339: \n2340:       step_resource_map_coverage_gate:\n2341:         action: \"If resource_map_present, compute the Resource Map Coverage Gate synthesis inputs; otherwise preserve the skip note\"\n2342:         note: \"Cross-check target_files from {spec_folder}/applied/T-*.md against {spec_folder}/resource-map.md. Report touched entries, untouched entries split into expected-by-scope vs gap, and implementation paths absent from the map. Findings raised here use category resource-map-coverage with severity calibrated to the gate outcome.\"\n2343: \n2344:       step_compile_review_report:\n2345:         action: \"Compile review/review-report.md with 9 core sections, a conditional Resource Map Coverage Gate section, and an embedded Planning Packet\"\n2346:         instructions: |\n2347:           Create review/review-report.md with the following sections:\n2348: \n2349:           1. **Executive Summary**\n2350:              - Overall verdict: PASS | CONDITIONAL | FAIL\n2351:              - hasAdvisories: true when PASS carries active P2 items\n2352:              - P0/P1/P2 counts (active only)\n2353:              - Review scope summary\n2354:              - Operator review focus: config.reviewFocus verbatim, or omit this line when it is null\n2355: \n2356:           2. **Planning Trigger**\n2357:              - State whether `/speckit:plan` is required\n2358:              - Include a fenced `json` block labeled `Planning Packet`\n2359:              - The packet MUST include: `triggered`, `verdict`, `hasAdvisories`, `activeFindings`, `remediationWorkstreams`, `specSeed`, `planSeed`, `findingClasses`, `affectedSurfacesSeed`, `fixCompletenessRequired`\n2360:              - Build `activeFindings`, `findingClasses`, and `affectedSurfacesSeed` from reducer-owned state plus iteration JSONL `findingDetails`; if a field is missing, mark it `UNKNOWN` instead of inferring it from prose\n2361: \n2362:           3. **Active Finding Registry**\n2363:              - Unified registry for active P0/P1/P2 findings\n2364:              - For each: ID, severity, title, dimension, file:line, evidence, impact, fix recommendation, disposition, findingClass, scopeProof, affectedSurfaceHints\n2365: \n2366:           4. **Remediation Workstreams**\n2367:              - Ordered action groups: P0 first, then P1, with P2 advisories separated\n2368: \n2369:           5. **Spec Seed**\n2370:              - Concrete seed bullets for follow-on spec updates\n2371: \n2372:           6. **Plan Seed**\n2373:              - Concrete starter tasks for `/speckit:plan`\n2374: \n2375:            7. **Traceability Status**\n2376:               - Summarize required core protocols first, then applicable overlay protocols\n2377:               - Include status, evidence, and any unresolved drift per protocol\n2378:               - Include `AC_COVERAGE` status for lifecycle-active spec-folder targets: exempt, disabled, pass, or advisory-shortfall, with covered/total and floor when available\n2379: \n2380:           If `resource_map_present` is true, insert **## Resource Map Coverage Gate** after `Traceability Status` with exactly three bullets:\n2381:              - `Entries touched`: count of resource-map paths that appear in applied reports\n2382:              - `Entries not touched`: paths in resource-map not in implementation, labeled `expected-by-scope` or `gap`\n2383:              - `Implementation paths absent from resource-map`: `target_files` in applied reports not on the map\n2384: \n2385:           8. **Deferred Items**\n2386:              - Advisory-only or backlog-worthy follow-ups that do not block the current verdict\n2387: \n2388:           **Dimension Expansion Map**\n2389:              - Insert `## Dimension Expansion Map` after Deferred Items and before Search Ledger.\n2390:              - Render reducer-owned `divergence.saturatedDirections`, completed pivots, failed pivots, audited overrides, Council artifact references, selected review directions, and remaining frontier.\n2391:              - This section records breadth only. It cannot alter the Executive Summary verdict, hasAdvisories, finding registry, or adversarial self-check results.\n2392: \n2393:           9. **Search Ledger**\n2394:              - Always include this section before the appendix.\n2395:              - Render reducer-owned `searchCoverage`, `candidateCoverage`, `searchDebt`, `ruledOutCandidates`, and `cleanSearchProof`.\n2396:              - If all arrays are empty or absent, include: `*No search-depth state captured (legacy v1 record)*`.\n2397:              - When `searchDebt` is non-empty, state `hasSearchDebt: true` and carry the dashboard verdict as CONDITIONAL unless active P0 findings make it FAIL.\n2398: \n2399:           10. **Audit Appendix**\n2400:              - Convergence summary, coverage summary, ruled-out claims, sources reviewed\n2401:              - Cross-reference appendix MUST be split into `Core Protocols` and `Overlay Protocols`\n2402: \n2403:           Preserve machine-owned markers so the reducer-owned registry, dashboard, and strategy anchors can be refreshed on re-run without mutating prior synthesis. (Note: `completed-continue` lineage branch is deferred — see `deep-review/references/protocol/loop-protocol.md §Lifecycle Branches`.)\n2404:         output: \"{state_paths.review_output}\"\n2405: \n2406:       step_derive_release_readiness_state:\n2407:         action: \"Bind release-readiness state from final review results\"\n2408:         algorithm: |\n2409:           if active_p0 > 0:\n2410:             release_readiness_state = \"release-blocking\"\n2411:           elif reason == \"converged\" and verdict in [\"PASS\", \"CONDITIONAL\"]:\n2412:             release_readiness_state = \"converged\"\n2413:           else:\n2414:             release_readiness_state = \"in-progress\"\n2415:         outputs:\n2416:           - release_readiness_state: \"in-progress | converged | release-blocking\"\n2417:         note: \"State meanings follow releaseReadinessStates in deep-review/assets/review-mode-contract.yaml.\"\n2418: \n2419:       step_convergence_report:\n2420:         action: \"Append convergence report to JSONL\"\n2421:         command: |\n2422:           GATEWAY=\".skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/append-mode-event.cjs\"\n2423:           [ -f \"$GATEWAY\" ] || GATEWAY=\"scripts/append-mode-event.cjs\"\n2424:           EVENT_DIR=\"$(mktemp -d \"${TMPDIR:-/tmp}/deep-review-synthesis.XXXXXX\")\"\n2425:           CLOSEOUT=\".skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/synthesis-closeout.cjs\"\n2426:           [ -f \"$CLOSEOUT\" ] || CLOSEOUT=\"scripts/synthesis-closeout.cjs\"\n2427:           node \"$CLOSEOUT\" --mode review --event-dir \"$EVENT_DIR\" \\\n2428:             --artifact-dir \"{state_paths.packet_dir}\" \\\n2429:             --state-log \"{state_paths.state_log}\" \\\n2430:             --registry \"{state_paths.findings_registry}\" \\\n2431:             --output \"{state_paths.review_output}\" \\\n2432:             --dashboard \"{state_paths.dashboard}\" \\\n2433:             --stop-reason \"{reason}\" \\\n2434:             --active-p0 \"{active_p0}\" --active-p1 \"{active_p1}\" --active-p2 \"{active_p2}\" \\\n2435:             --dimension-coverage \"{dimension_coverage}\" \\\n2436:             --verdict \"{verdict}\" \\\n2437:             --release-readiness-state \"{release_readiness_state}\"\n2438:           NODE_STATUS=$?\n2439:           for eventFile in \"$EVENT_DIR\"/*.json; do\n2440:             [ -e \"$eventFile\" ] || continue\n2441:             node \"$GATEWAY\" --mode review --run-directory \"$(dirname \"{state_paths.state_log}\")\" --event-json \"$eventFile\"\n2442:             GATEWAY_STATUS=$?\n2443:             if [ \"$GATEWAY_STATUS\" -ne 0 ]; then\n2444:               rm -rf \"$EVENT_DIR\"\n2445:               exit \"$GATEWAY_STATUS\"\n2446:             fi\n2447:           done\n2448:           rm -rf \"$EVENT_DIR\"\n2449:           exit \"$NODE_STATUS\"\n2450:         note: \"Emit as numeric ratio (e.g., 0.75), not quoted string. Compute: dimensions_covered / total_dimensions.\"\n2451: \n2452:       step_update_config_status:\n2453:         action: \"Mark config as complete\"\n2454:         edit: \"{state_paths.config}\"\n2455:         set_field: { status: \"complete\" }\n2456: \n2457:       step_stage_artifact_dir:\n2458:         skip_when: \"config.fanout_lineage_artifact_dir is present\"\n2459:         action: \"Stage all skill-owned artifacts under artifact_dir for the operator's next git commit\"\n2460:         command: \"git add {state_paths.artifact_dir}\"\n2461:         note: \"Staging the whole artifact_dir keeps the iteration trail (iterations/, deltas/, state.jsonl, strategy, findings-registry, and the report) together; the operator keeps commit authority and can `git restore --staged {path}` before committing. Failure is non-fatal -- log warning and continue.\"\n2462:         on_fail: \"Log warning. Do not block synthesis. The artifact_dir may be outside a git repo (e.g., temp test fixture) which is a valid case.\"\n2463: \n2464:   # ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════\n2465:   # PHASE 4: SAVE\n2466:   # ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════\n2467:   phase_save:\n2468:     purpose: Preserve review context in packet continuity\n2469:     steps:\n2470: \n2471:       step_compose_save_payload:\n2472:         action: \"Compose the structured JSON payload consumed by generate-context.js\"\n2473:         output: \"/tmp/save-context-data-<session-id>.json\"\n2474:         requirements:\n2475:           - \"Write this file before invoking generate-context.js; the loader fails closed if the explicit JSON file is absent.\"\n2476:           - \"Include `specFolder`, a concise `sessionSummary`, curated `observations`, `recent_context`, `toolCalls`, and `exchanges` from the completed review loop.\"\n2477:           - \"Use a session-scoped temp filename; do not use the retired shared `/tmp/save-context-data.json` path.\"\n2478:         example_payload: |\n2479:           {\n2480:             \"specFolder\": \"{spec_folder}\",\n2481:             \"sessionSummary\": \"Deep review completed; see review/review-report.md for verdict, findings, and workstreams.\",\n2482:             \"observations\": [\"Summarize the active findings, verdict, and remediation guidance.\"],\n2483:             \"recent_context\": [\"Point to the generated review artifacts and next action.\"],\n2484:             \"exchanges\": [],\n2485:             \"toolCalls\": []\n2486:           }\n2487: \n2488:       step_generate_context:\n2489:         action: \"Route continuity content into the correct canonical spec document via generate-context.js\"\n2490:         command: \"node .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/dist/continuity/generate-context.js /tmp/save-context-data-<session-id>.json {spec_folder}\"\n2491:         critical_rule: \"NEVER manually author files under retired memory/ paths (the runtime rejects them); use generate-context.js so the save routes into decision-record.md, implementation-summary.md, or handover.md\"\n2492: \n2493:       step_verify_save:\n2494:         action: \"Verify canonical save routed content into the correct spec document\"\n2495:         check: \"Does {spec_folder}/implementation-summary.md, {spec_folder}/decision-record.md, or {spec_folder}/handover.md carry the new continuity update?\"\n2496:         on_fail: \"Log warning but do not block completion\"\n2497: \n2498:       step_release_lock:\n2499:         action: \"Release the single-writer lock after save, skip-save, or cancellation cleanup has resolved\"\n2500:         command: \"node .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/loop-lock.cjs release --lock-path {state_paths.lock_file} --owner-pid {captured_owner_pid} --nonce {captured_acquire_nonce}\"\n2501:         bookkeeping_log: '{\"type\":\"event\",\"event\":\"lock_released\",\"path\":\"{state_paths.lock_file}\",\"releasePhase\":\"save\",\"timestamp\":\"{ISO_8601_NOW}\"}'\n2502: \n2503:   # ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════\n2504:   # COMPLETION\n2505:   # ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════\n2506:   completion:\n2507:     message: |\n2508:       Deep review complete.\n2509:       Iterations: {iteration_count} | Stop reason: {reason}\n2510:       Findings: P0={active_p0} P1={active_p1} P2={active_p2}\n2511:       Verdict: {verdict} | hasAdvisories={has_advisories}\n2512: \n2513:       Artifacts:\n2514:         - review/review-report.md (compiled from {iteration_count} iterations)\n2515:         - {iteration_count} iteration files in review/iterations/\n2516:         - State files in review/: deep-review-config.json, deep-review-state.jsonl, deep-review-findings-registry.json, deep-review-strategy.md, deep-review-dashboard.md\n2517:         - Memory context saved\n2518: \n2519:       STATUS=OK PATH={spec_folder}\n2520:     next_steps:\n2521:       - \"/speckit:plan [remediation] (if FAIL or CONDITIONAL verdict)\"\n2522:       - \"/create:changelog (if PASS, including PASS with hasAdvisories=true)\"\n2523:       - \"/deep:review [target] (for another review)\"\n2524:       - \"/speckit:save {spec_folder} (refresh canonical continuity before the next session)\"\n2525: \n2526: # ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n2527: # ERROR RECOVERY\n2528: # ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n2529: error_recovery:\n2530:   agent_dispatch_timeout: \"Retry once with reduced scope (fewer files per iteration). If second timeout, mark as 'timeout' and continue.\"\n2531:   state_file_missing: \"If JSONL missing during loop, reconstruct from iteration files. If strategy missing, create minimal version.\"\n2532:   consecutive_failures: \"After 3 consecutive errors, halt loop and enter synthesis with partial findings.\"\n2533:   continuity_save_failure: \"Preserve the review packet in review/ as backup. Log warning.\"\n2534: \n2535: # ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n2536: # RULES\n2537: # ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n2538: rules:\n2539:   ALWAYS:\n2540:     - follow_workflow_phases_in_order\n2541:     - dispatch_deep_review_agent_per_iteration\n2542:     - check_convergence_before_each_iteration\n2543:     - write_all_state_to_files\n2544:     - write_continuity_after_synthesis\n2545:     - respect_max_iterations_cap\n2546:     - treat_review_target_as_read_only\n2547:     - deduplicate_findings_before_synthesis\n2548:     - run_adversarial_selfcheck_on_p0_p1\n2549:   NEVER:\n2550:     - skip_convergence_check\n2551:     - dispatch_non_leaf_agents\n2552:     - hold_iteration_findings_in_memory_only\n2553:     - modify_config_after_initialization\n2554:     - overwrite_jsonl_state_log\n2555:     - proceed_without_state_file_verification\n2556:     - modify_files_under_review\n2557:     - report_p0_without_file_line_evidence\n2558: \n2559: # ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n2560: # REFERENCE-ONLY APPENDIX\n2561: # ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n2562: reference_only_appendix:\n2563:   checkpoint_commit:\n2564:     note: \"Checkpoint commits are intentionally excluded from workflow.steps.\"\n2565:     commands:\n2566:       - \"git add {state_paths.iteration_pattern} {state_paths.state_log} {state_paths.findings_registry} {state_paths.strategy} {state_paths.review_output}\"\n2567:       - 'git commit -m \"chore(deep-review): iteration {NNN} complete\" -m \"{one-line summary of what the iteration found}\"'\n2568:   severity_weights:\n2569:     note: \"Severity weights for newFindingsRatio calculation\"\n2570:     weights:\n2571:       P0: 10.0\n2572:       P1: 5.0\n2573:       P2: 1.0\n2574:     p0_override: \"If ANY new P0 discovered → newFindingsRatio = max(calculated, 0.50). A single new P0 blocks convergence.\"\n2575:     clean_pass: \"If total_findings == 0 (clean pass) → newFindingsRatio = 0.0\"\n2576:   review_dimensions:\n2577:     note: \"All 4 default review dimensions with priority ordering\"\n2578:     dimensions:\n2579:       - { priority: 1, name: \"correctness\", checks: \"Logic, state flow, edge cases, error handling\" }\n2580:       - { priority: 2, name: \"security\", checks: \"Auth, input/output safety, data exposure, permissions\" }\n2581:       - { priority: 3, name: \"traceability\", checks: \"Spec/checklist alignment, cross-reference integrity, evidence coverage\" }\n2582:       - { priority: 4, name: \"maintainability\", checks: \"Patterns, documentation quality, safe follow-on change clarity\" }\n2583:   cross_reference_protocols:\n2584:     note: \"Cross-reference verification protocols split into core and overlay classes\"\n2585:     core_protocols:\n2586:       - { check: \"Spec vs Code\", source: \"spec.md claims\", target: \"implementation\" }\n2587:       - { check: \"Checklist vs Evidence\", source: \"[x] items\", target: \"cited evidence\" }\n2588:     overlay_protocols:\n2589:       - { check: \"SKILL.md vs Agent\", source: \"Skill contracts\", target: \"agent files\" }\n2590:       - { check: \"Agent Cross-Runtime\", source: \".claude\", target: \".opencode/.agents\" }\n2591:       - { check: \"Feature Catalog vs Code\", source: \"Catalog claims\", target: \"implementation\" }\n2592:       - { check: \"Playbook vs Support\", source: \"Scenario preconditions\", target: \"actual support\" }","title":"read","metadata":{"metadata":{"truncated":false},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Read file .skilled/commands/deep/assets/deep-review-auto.yaml, lines 2222-2592\n2222:   phase_synthesis:\n2223:     purpose: Compile all iteration findings into review/review-report.md\n2224:     steps:\n2225: \n2226:       step_fanout_merge:\n2227:         description: \"Merge N lineage registries with strongest-restriction; bind p0/p1/p2 counts for step_derive_verdict; skip when single-executor\"\n2228:         skip_when: \"config.fanout is absent\"\n2229:         command: |\n2230:           node .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/fanout-merge.cjs \\\n2231:             --loop-type review \\\n2232:             --artifact-dir {artifact_dir}\n2233:         working_directory: \"{repo_root}\"\n2234:         wait_for_completion: true\n2235:         bind_from_output:\n2236:           p0_count: \"active_p0\"\n2237:           p1_count: \"active_p1\"\n2238:           p2_count: \"active_p2\"\n2239: \n2240:       step_hydrate_summary_metrics:\n2241:         action: \"Hydrate summary metrics before synthesis\"\n2242:         read:\n2243:           - \"{state_paths.config}\"\n2244:           - \"{state_paths.state_log}\"\n2245:           - \"{state_paths.findings_registry}\"\n2246:           - \"{state_paths.strategy}\"\n2247:         read_patterns:\n2248:           - \"{state_paths.packet_dir}/lineages/*/deep-review-state.jsonl\"\n2249:         extract:\n2250:           - iteration_count: \"When direct lineage state logs exist, count distinct run values (the integer iteration, else a numeric run) across those logs in stable lineage order; otherwise count distinct run values (the integer iteration, else a numeric run) across the root state log. Never add root compatibility records to lineage records.\"\n2251:           - highest_run: \"When direct lineage state logs exist, take the highest run value (the integer iteration, else a numeric run) across lines where type === 'iteration' in those logs in stable lineage order, else 0; otherwise take the highest run value (the integer iteration, else a numeric run) across lines where type === 'iteration' in the root state log, else 0. Never add root compatibility records to lineage records.\"\n2252:           - current_iteration: \"max(highest_run, iteration_count) + 1\"\n2253:           - p0_count: \"Total P0 findings across all iterations (deduped)\"\n2254:           - p1_count: \"Total P1 findings across all iterations (deduped)\"\n2255:           - p2_count: \"Total P2 findings across all iterations (deduped)\"\n2256:           - dimensions_covered: \"List of reviewed dimensions\"\n2257:           - dimension_coverage: \"covered / total\"\n2258:           - ac_coverage_signal: \"For spec-folder targets only: if level is 2+ and acceptance-criteria.md exists and implementation-summary.md is in-progress or later, surface the AC_COVERAGE advisory status; otherwise mark exempt.\"\n2259:           - last_3_summaries: \"Summarize the latest 3 iteration records\"\n2260:           - reason: \"Use the latest stop reason if present, else the frozen default 'converged'. (Must be a member of the STOP_REASONS enum: converged, maxIterationsReached, blockedStop, stuckRecovery, error, manualStop, userPaused.)\"\n2261: \n2262:       # H-1 verdict derivation: parse findings JSONL, map highest severity to verdict\n2263:       # - PASS: no P0 or P1 findings (P2-only or clean)\n2264:       # - CONDITIONAL: any P1 findings (no P0)\n2265:       # - FAIL: any P0 findings\n2266:       # Final line of iteration-NNN.md MUST be exactly: \"Review verdict: PASS\" / \"Review verdict: CONDITIONAL\" / \"Review verdict: FAIL\"\n2267:       step_derive_verdict:\n2268:         action: \"Derive review verdict from accumulated findings\"\n2269:         algorithm: |\n2270:           if p0_count > 0:\n2271:             verdict = \"FAIL\"\n2272:           elif p1_count > 0:\n2273:             verdict = \"CONDITIONAL\"\n2274:           else:\n2275:             verdict = \"PASS\"\n2276:           has_advisories = (verdict == \"PASS\" and p2_count > 0)\n2277:           ac_coverage_signal is advisory while the validation rule is INFO/default-off; include it in synthesis traceability, but do not change the exact verdict enum from this signal alone.\n2278:         outputs:\n2279:           - verdict: \"PASS | CONDITIONAL | FAIL\"\n2280:           - has_advisories: \"Boolean true when verdict is PASS and any active P2 findings exist\"\n2281:           - ac_coverage_signal: \"exempt | disabled | pass | advisory-shortfall\"\n2282:         contract: |\n2283:           Every iteration-NNN.md must end with exactly: \"Review verdict: PASS\" (or CONDITIONAL or FAIL).\n2284:           Downstream automation parses this final line via exact string match — do not vary the format.\n2285: \n2286:       step_read_all_iterations:\n2287:         action: \"Read all iteration files and strategy\"\n2288:         read_pattern: \"{state_paths.iteration_dir}/iteration-*.md\"\n2289:         read_also: \"{state_paths.strategy}\"\n2290: \n2291:       step_build_finding_registry:\n2292:         action: \"Build deduplicated finding registry from all iterations\"\n2293:         algorithm: |\n2294:           1. Extract all findings from iteration JSONL delta files\n2295:           2. Compute content_hash for each finding (emission requirement):\n2296:              content_hash = sha256(file_path + \"\\u001f\" + line_range + \"\\u001f\" + finding_type + \"\\u001f\" + normalized_description_80chars)\n2297:              Normalized description = whitespace-collapsed, lowercased, first 80 chars of the finding description.\n2298:           3. Two-tier dedup:\n2299:              PRIMARY: group by content_hash field\n2300:                - Same content_hash, multiple dimensions → single finding, merged `dimensions: [<all>]` array\n2301:                - Keep highest severity on duplicates\n2302:              FALLBACK (legacy records lacking content_hash): file:line + normalized_title\n2303:                - Same file:line, multiple dimensions → single finding, multiple dimension tags\n2304:                - Keep highest severity on duplicates\n2305:           4. Track finding lifecycle:\n2306:              - status: active | duplicate | upgraded | downgraded | contested | resolved_false_positive\n2307:              - Record first_seen, upgraded_in, previous_severity for severity changes\n2308:              - Record dimensions array reflecting all dimensions that emitted this finding\n2309:           5. Resolve contradictions:\n2310:              - Findings marked contested across iterations → referee pass\n2311:              - Determine final severity and status\n2312:           6. Count only 'active' findings for totals\n2313:         outputs:\n2314:           - finding_registry: \"Deduplicated list of all findings with metadata\"\n2315:           - active_p0: \"Count of active P0 findings\"\n2316:           - active_p1: \"Count of active P1 findings\"\n2317:           - active_p2: \"Count of active P2 findings\"\n2318: \n2319:       step_adversarial_selfcheck:\n2320:         action: \"Final adversarial self-check on all P0 and P1 findings\"\n2321:         algorithm: |\n2322:           For each active P0/P1 finding:\n2323:             1. Hunter: Re-verify finding against source code (re-read file:line)\n2324:             2. Skeptic: Challenge severity — is this really P0/P1? Could it be P2?\n2325:             3. Referee: Final call — confirm, downgrade, or mark false_positive\n2326:           Update finding_registry with adjudicated results.\n2327: \n2328:       step_emit_resource_map:\n2329:         skip_when: \"config.fanout is present\"\n2330:         action: \"Emit {state_paths.resource_map_output} from converged review deltas unless config.resource_map.emit is false\"\n2331:         command: \"node .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/reduce-state.cjs {spec_folder} {reducer_artifact_arg} --create-missing-anchors --emit-resource-map\"\n2332:         read:\n2333:           - \"{state_paths.config}\"\n2334:           - \"{state_paths.delta_dir}/iter-*.jsonl\"\n2335:         write:\n2336:           - \"{state_paths.resource_map_output}\"\n2337:         guarantee: \"Reducer skips cleanly when config.resource_map.emit == false and writes a deterministic resource-map when enabled.\"\n2338:         note: \"A fan-out root has no root state log before closeout, so the root reducer would fail on the missing file. Each lineage emits its own map, so the report names the ones that exist at {artifact_dir}/lineages/*/resource-map.md.\"\n2339: \n2340:       step_resource_map_coverage_gate:\n2341:         action: \"If resource_map_present, compute the Resource Map Coverage Gate synthesis inputs; otherwise preserve the skip note\"\n2342:         note: \"Cross-check target_files from {spec_folder}/applied/T-*.md against {spec_folder}/resource-map.md. Report touched entries, untouched entries split into expected-by-scope vs gap, and implementation paths absent from the map. Findings raised here use category resource-map-coverage with severity calibrated to the gate outcome.\"\n2343: \n2344:       step_compile_review_report:\n2345:         action: \"Compile review/review-report.md with 9 core sections, a conditional Resource Map Coverage Gate section, and an embedded Planning Packet\"\n2346:         instructions: |\n2347:           Create review/review-report.md with the following sections:\n2348: \n2349:           1. **Executive Summary**\n2350:              - Overall verdict: PASS | CONDITIONAL | FAIL\n2351:              - hasAdvisories: true when PASS carries active P2 items\n2352:              - P0/P1/P2 counts (active only)\n2353:              - Review scope summary\n2354:              - Operator review focus: config.reviewFocus verbatim, or omit this line when it is null\n2355: \n2356:           2. **Planning Trigger**\n2357:              - State whether `/speckit:plan` is required\n2358:              - Include a fenced `json` block labeled `Planning Packet`\n2359:              - The packet MUST include: `triggered`, `verdict`, `hasAdvisories`, `activeFindings`, `remediationWorkstreams`, `specSeed`, `planSeed`, `findingClasses`, `affectedSurfacesSeed`, `fixCompletenessRequired`\n2360:              - Build `activeFindings`, `findingClasses`, and `affectedSurfacesSeed` from reducer-owned state plus iteration JSONL `findingDetails`; if a field is missing, mark it `UNKNOWN` instead of inferring it from prose\n2361: \n2362:           3. **Active Finding Registry**\n2363:              - Unified registry for active P0/P1/P2 findings\n2364:              - For each: ID, severity, title, dimension, file:line, evidence, impact, fix recommendation, disposition, findingClass, scopeProof, affectedSurfaceHints\n2365: \n2366:           4. **Remediation Workstreams**\n2367:              - Ordered action groups: P0 first, then P1, with P2 advisories separated\n2368: \n2369:           5. **Spec Seed**\n2370:              - Concrete seed bullets for follow-on spec updates\n2371: \n2372:           6. **Plan Seed**\n2373:              - Concrete starter tasks for `/speckit:plan`\n2374: \n2375:            7. **Traceability Status**\n2376:               - Summarize required core protocols first, then applicable overlay protocols\n2377:               - Include status, evidence, and any unresolved drift per protocol\n2378:               - Include `AC_COVERAGE` status for lifecycle-active spec-folder targets: exempt, disabled, pass, or advisory-shortfall, with covered/total and floor when available\n2379: \n2380:           If `resource_map_present` is true, insert **## Resource Map Coverage Gate** after `Traceability Status` with exactly three bullets:\n2381:              - `Entries touched`: count of resource-map paths that appear in applied reports\n2382:              - `Entries not touched`: paths in resource-map not in implementation, labeled `expected-by-scope` or `gap`\n2383:              - `Implementation paths absent from resource-map`: `target_files` in applied reports not on the map\n2384: \n2385:           8. **Deferred Items**\n2386:              - Advisory-only or backlog-worthy follow-ups that do not block the current verdict\n2387: \n2388:           **Dimension Expansion Map**\n2389:              - Insert `## Dimension Expansion Map` after Deferred Items and before Search Ledger.\n2390:              - Render reducer-owned `divergence.saturatedDirections`, completed pivots, failed pivots, audited overrides, Council artifact references, selected review directions, and remaining frontier.\n2391:              - This section records breadth only. It cannot alter the Executive Summary verdict, hasAdvisories, finding registry, or adversarial self-check results.\n2392: \n2393:           9. **Search Ledger**\n2394:              - Always include this section before the appendix.\n2395:              - Render reducer-owned `searchCoverage`, `candidateCoverage`, `searchDebt`, `ruledOutCandidates`, and `cleanSearchProof`.\n2396:              - If all arrays are empty or absent, include: `*No search-depth state captured (legacy v1 record)*`.\n2397:              - When `searchDebt` is non-empty, state `hasSearchDebt: true` and carry the dashboard verdict as CONDITIONAL unless active P0 findings make it FAIL.\n2398: \n2399:           10. **Audit Appendix**\n2400:              - Convergence summary, coverage summary, ruled-out claims, sources reviewed\n2401:              - Cross-reference appendix MUST be split into `Core Protocols` and `Overlay Protocols`\n2402: \n2403:           Preserve machine-owned markers so the reducer-owned registry, dashboard, and strategy anchors can be refreshed on re-run without mutating prior synthesis. (Note: `completed-continue` lineage branch is deferred — see `deep-review/references/protocol/loop-protocol.md §Lifecycle Branches`.)\n2404:         output: \"{state_paths.review_output}\"\n2405: \n2406:       step_derive_release_readiness_state:\n2407:         action: \"Bind release-readiness state from final review results\"\n2408:         algorithm: |\n2409:           if active_p0 > 0:\n2410:             release_readiness_state = \"release-blocking\"\n2411:           elif reason == \"converged\" and verdict in [\"PASS\", \"CONDITIONAL\"]:\n2412:             release_readiness_state = \"converged\"\n2413:           else:\n2414:             release_readiness_state = \"in-progress\"\n2415:         outputs:\n2416:           - release_readiness_state: \"in-progress | converged | release-blocking\"\n2417:         note: \"State meanings follow releaseReadinessStates in deep-review/assets/review-mode-contract.yaml.\"\n2418: \n2419:       step_convergence_report:\n2420:         action: \"Append convergence report to JSONL\"\n2421:         command: |\n2422:           GATEWAY=\".skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/append-mode-event.cjs\"\n2423:           [ -f \"$GATEWAY\" ] || GATEWAY=\"scripts/append-mode-event.cjs\"\n2424:           EVENT_DIR=\"$(mktemp -d \"${TMPDIR:-/tmp}/deep-review-synthesis.XXXXXX\")\"\n2425:           CLOSEOUT=\".skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/synthesis-closeout.cjs\"\n2426:           [ -f \"$CLOSEOUT\" ] || CLOSEOUT=\"scripts/synthesis-closeout.cjs\"\n2427:           node \"$CLOSEOUT\" --mode review --event-dir \"$EVENT_DIR\" \\\n2428:             --artifact-dir \"{state_paths.packet_dir}\" \\\n2429:             --state-log \"{state_paths.state_log}\" \\\n2430:             --registry \"{state_paths.findings_registry}\" \\\n2431:             --output \"{state_paths.review_output}\" \\\n2432:             --dashboard \"{state_paths.dashboard}\" \\\n2433:             --stop-reason \"{reason}\" \\\n2434:             --active-p0 \"{active_p0}\" --active-p1 \"{active_p1}\" --active-p2 \"{active_p2}\" \\\n2435:             --dimension-coverage \"{dimension_coverage}\" \\\n2436:             --verdict \"{verdict}\" \\\n2437:             --release-readiness-state \"{release_readiness_state}\"\n2438:           NODE_STATUS=$?\n2439:           for eventFile in \"$EVENT_DIR\"/*.json; do\n2440:             [ -e \"$eventFile\" ] || continue\n2441:             node \"$GATEWAY\" --mode review --run-directory \"$(dirname \"{state_paths.state_log}\")\" --event-json \"$eventFile\"\n2442:             GATEWAY_STATUS=$?\n2443:             if [ \"$GATEWAY_STATUS\" -ne 0 ]; then\n2444:               rm -rf \"$EVENT_DIR\"\n2445:               exit \"$GATEWAY_STATUS\"\n2446:             fi\n2447:           done\n2448:           rm -rf \"$EVENT_DIR\"\n2449:           exit \"$NODE_STATUS\"\n2450:         note: \"Emit as numeric ratio (e.g., 0.75), not quoted string. Compute: dimensions_covered / total_dimensions.\"\n2451: \n2452:       step_update_config_status:\n2453:         action: \"Mark config as complete\"\n2454:         edit: \"{state_paths.config}\"\n2455:         set_field: { status: \"complete\" }\n2456: \n2457:       step_stage_artifact_dir:\n2458:         skip_when: \"config.fanout_lineage_artifact_dir is present\"\n2459:         action: \"Stage all skill-owned artifacts under artifact_dir for the operator's next git commit\"\n2460:         command: \"git add {state_paths.artifact_dir}\"\n2461:         note: \"Staging the whole artifact_dir keeps the iteration trail (iterations/, deltas/, state.jsonl, strategy, findings-registry, and the report) together; the operator keeps commit authority and can `git restore --staged {path}` before committing. Failure is non-fatal -- log warning and continue.\"\n2462:         on_fail: \"Log warning. Do not block synthesis. The artifact_dir may be outside a git repo (e.g., temp test fixture) which is a valid case.\"\n2463: \n2464:   # ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════\n2465:   # PHASE 4: SAVE\n2466:   # ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════\n2467:   phase_save:\n2468:     purpose: Preserve review context in packet continuity\n2469:     steps:\n2470: \n2471:       step_compose_save_payload:\n2472:         action: \"Compose the structured JSON payload consumed by generate-context.js\"\n2473:         output: \"/tmp/save-context-data-<session-id>.json\"\n2474:         requirements:\n2475:           - \"Write this file before invoking generate-context.js; the loader fails closed if the explicit JSON file is absent.\"\n2476:           - \"Include `specFolder`, a concise `sessionSummary`, curated `observations`, `recent_context`, `toolCalls`, and `exchanges` from the completed review loop.\"\n2477:           - \"Use a session-scoped temp filename; do not use the retired shared `/tmp/save-context-data.json` path.\"\n2478:         example_payload: |\n2479:           {\n2480:             \"specFolder\": \"{spec_folder}\",\n2481:             \"sessionSummary\": \"Deep review completed; see review/review-report.md for verdict, findings, and workstreams.\",\n2482:             \"observations\": [\"Summarize the active findings, verdict, and remediation guidance.\"],\n2483:             \"recent_context\": [\"Point to the generated review artifacts and next action.\"],\n2484:             \"exchanges\": [],\n2485:             \"toolCalls\": []\n2486:           }\n2487: \n2488:       step_generate_context:\n2489:         action: \"Route continuity content into the correct canonical spec document via generate-context.js\"\n2490:         command: \"node .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/dist/continuity/generate-context.js /tmp/save-context-data-<session-id>.json {spec_folder}\"\n2491:         critical_rule: \"NEVER manually author files under retired memory/ paths (the runtime rejects them); use generate-context.js so the save routes into decision-record.md, implementation-summary.md, or handover.md\"\n2492: \n2493:       step_verify_save:\n2494:         action: \"Verify canonical save routed content into the correct spec document\"\n2495:         check: \"Does {spec_folder}/implementation-summary.md, {spec_folder}/decision-record.md, or {spec_folder}/handover.md carry the new continuity update?\"\n2496:         on_fail: \"Log warning but do not block completion\"\n2497: \n2498:       step_release_lock:\n2499:         action: \"Release the single-writer lock after save, skip-save, or cancellation cleanup has resolved\"\n2500:         command: \"node .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/loop-lock.cjs release --lock-path {state_paths.lock_file} --owner-pid {captured_owner_pid} --nonce {captured_acquire_nonce}\"\n2501:         bookkeeping_log: '{\"type\":\"event\",\"event\":\"lock_released\",\"path\":\"{state_paths.lock_file}\",\"releasePhase\":\"save\",\"timestamp\":\"{ISO_8601_NOW}\"}'\n2502: \n2503:   # ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════\n2504:   # COMPLETION\n2505:   # ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════\n2506:   completion:\n2507:     message: |\n2508:       Deep review complete.\n2509:       Iterations: {iteration_count} | Stop reason: {reason}\n2510:       Findings: P0={active_p0} P1={active_p1} P2={active_p2}\n2511:       Verdict: {verdict} | hasAdvisories={has_advisories}\n2512: \n2513:       Artifacts:\n2514:         - review/review-report.md (compiled from {iteration_count} iterations)\n2515:         - {iteration_count} iteration files in review/iterations/\n2516:         - State files in review/: deep-review-config.json, deep-review-state.jsonl, deep-review-findings-registry.json, deep-review-strategy.md, deep-review-dashboard.md\n2517:         - Memory context saved\n2518: \n2519:       STATUS=OK PATH={spec_folder}\n2520:     next_steps:\n2521:       - \"/speckit:plan [remediation] (if FAIL or CONDITIONAL verdict)\"\n2522:       - \"/create:changelog (if PASS, including PASS with hasAdvisories=true)\"\n2523:       - \"/deep:review [target] (for another review)\"\n2524:       - \"/speckit:save {spec_folder} (refresh canonical continuity before the next session)\"\n2525: \n2526: # ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n2527: # ERROR RECOVERY\n2528: # ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n2529: error_recovery:\n2530:   agent_dispatch_timeout: \"Retry once with reduced scope (fewer files per iteration). If second timeout, mark as 'timeout' and continue.\"\n2531:   state_file_missing: \"If JSONL missing during loop, reconstruct from iteration files. If strategy missing, create minimal version.\"\n2532:   consecutive_failures: \"After 3 consecutive errors, halt loop and enter synthesis with partial findings.\"\n2533:   continuity_save_failure: \"Preserve the review packet in review/ as backup. Log warning.\"\n2534: \n2535: # ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n2536: # RULES\n2537: # ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n2538: rules:\n2539:   ALWAYS:\n2540:     - follow_workflow_phases_in_order\n2541:     - dispatch_deep_review_agent_per_iteration\n2542:     - check_convergence_before_each_iteration\n2543:     - write_all_state_to_files\n2544:     - write_continuity_after_synthesis\n2545:     - respect_max_iterations_cap\n2546:     - treat_review_target_as_read_only\n2547:     - deduplicate_findings_before_synthesis\n2548:     - run_adversarial_selfcheck_on_p0_p1\n2549:   NEVER:\n2550:     - skip_convergence_check\n2551:     - dispatch_non_leaf_agents\n2552:     - hold_iteration_findings_in_memory_only\n2553:     - modify_config_after_initialization\n2554:     - overwrite_jsonl_state_log\n2555:     - proceed_without_state_file_verification\n2556:     - modify_files_under_review\n2557:     - report_p0_without_file_line_evidence\n2558: \n2559: # ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n2560: # REFERENCE-ONLY APPENDIX\n2561: # ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n2562: reference_only_appendix:\n2563:   checkpoint_commit:\n2564:     note: \"Checkpoint commits are intentionally excluded from workflow.steps.\"\n2565:     commands:\n2566:       - \"git add {state_paths.iteration_pattern} {state_paths.state_log} {state_paths.findings_registry} {state_paths.strategy} {state_paths.review_output}\"\n2567:       - 'git commit -m \"chore(deep-review): iteration {NNN} complete\" -m \"{one-line summary of what the iteration found}\"'\n2568:   severity_weights:\n2569:     note: \"Severity weights for newFindingsRatio calculation\"\n2570:     weights:\n2571:       P0: 10.0\n2572:       P1: 5.0\n2573:       P2: 1.0\n2574:     p0_override: \"If ANY new P0 discovered → newFindingsRatio = max(calculated, 0.50). A single new P0 blocks convergence.\"\n2575:     clean_pass: \"If total_findings == 0 (clean pass) → newFindingsRatio = 0.0\"\n2576:   review_dimensions:\n2577:     note: \"All 4 default review dimensions with priority ordering\"\n2578:     dimensions:\n2579:       - { priority: 1, name: \"correctness\", checks: \"Logic, state flow, edge cases, error handling\" }\n2580:       - { priority: 2, name: \"security\", checks: \"Auth, input/output safety, data exposure, permissions\" }\n2581:       - { priority: 3, name: \"traceability\", checks: \"Spec/checklist alignment, cross-reference integrity, evidence coverage\" }\n2582:       - { priority: 4, name: \"maintainability\", checks: \"Patterns, documentation quality, safe follow-on change clarity\" }\n2583:   cross_reference_protocols:\n2584:     note: \"Cross-reference verification protocols split into core and overlay classes\"\n2585:     core_protocols:\n2586:       - { check: \"Spec vs Code\", source: \"spec.md claims\", target: \"implementation\" }\n2587:       - { check: \"Checklist vs Evidence\", source: \"[x] items\", target: \"cited evidence\" }\n2588:     overlay_protocols:\n2589:       - { check: \"SKILL.md vs Agent\", source: \"Skill contracts\", target: \"agent files\" }\n2590:       - { check: \"Agent Cross-Runtime\", source: \".claude\", target: \".opencode/.agents\" }\n2591:       - { check: \"Feature Catalog vs Code\", source: \"Catalog claims\", target: \"implementation\" }\n2592:       - { check: \"Playbook vs Support\", source: \"Scenario preconditions\", target: \"actual support\" }"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"limit\":400,\"offset\":2222,\"path\":\".skilled/commands/deep/assets/deep-review-auto.yaml\"}"},"time":{"start":1794669400997,"end":1794669401267}}}}
{"type":"step_finish","timestamp":1794669405163,"sessionID":"ses_e255ff46effe7EWyuOLOEwVdy1","part":{"id":"prt_1daa1e3eb001OPj96ZvN2pRg83","sessionID":"ses_e255ff46effe7EWyuOLOEwVdy1","messageID":"msg_1daa1c54f001f7quTQjI7MsOom","type":"step-finish","reason":"tool-calls","snapshot":"e001cd1fcb46df7d89618068a44c014950ae307e","cost":0,"tokens":{"input":8484,"output":83,"reasoning":27,"cache":{"read":97920,"write":0}}}}
{"type":"step_start","timestamp":1794669409487,"sessionID":"ses_e255ff46effe7EWyuOLOEwVdy1","part":{"id":"prt_1daa1f4cf001MluRnBE2n8qdQX","sessionID":"ses_e255ff46effe7EWyuOLOEwVdy1","messageID":"msg_1daa1e3f6001F5VnjuC6AnTCVf","type":"step-start","snapshot":"918bf53bb415c2d73755224bb77e33912af649c6"}}
{"type":"text","timestamp":1794669414769,"sessionID":"ses_e255ff46effe7EWyuOLOEwVdy1","part":{"id":"prt_1daa2041f002pgT6h7IikT3I7e","sessionID":"ses_e255ff46effe7EWyuOLOEwVdy1","messageID":"msg_1daa1e3f6001F5VnjuC6AnTCVf","type":"text","text":"Now let me look at sibling lineage artifacts for the exact expected shape, and check the reducer/gateway interfaces.","time":{"start":1794669413407,"end":1794669414769}}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794669414789,"sessionID":"ses_e255ff46effe7EWyuOLOEwVdy1","part":{"partID":"prt_1daa20833001lVg0q3WuNzznNW","sessionID":"ses_e255ff46effe7EWyuOLOEwVdy1","messageID":"msg_1daa1e3f6001F5VnjuC6AnTCVf","type":"tool","id":"call_7ca72907c90841aa8af68a58","tool":"read","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"path":".skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/references/state/state-format.md"},"output":"Read file .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/references/state/state-format.md, lines 1-582\n1: ---\n2: title: Deep Review State Format\n3: description: State file schemas for the autonomous deep review loop, config, JSONL log, strategy, iteration files, and review report.\n4: trigger_phrases:\n5:   - \"deep review state format\"\n6:   - \"deep review config schema\"\n7:   - \"review severity weights\"\n8:   - \"file protection levels\"\n9:   - \"review iteration file structure\"\n10: importance_tier: important\n11: contextType: implementation\n12: version: 1.11.1.0\n13: ---\n14: \n15: # Deep Review State Format\n16: \n17: State file schemas for the autonomous deep review loop.\n18: \n19: ---\n20: \n21: ## 1. OVERVIEW\n22: \n23: ### Purpose\n24: \n25: The review packet is reproduced from disk on every resume, so each file's format, mutability, and fields are pinned here for the reducer, the dashboard, the validator, and the resume path.\n26: \n27: ### When to Use\n28: \n29: - Validating deep-review state files emitted by an iteration or by the reducer.\n30: - Implementing a state consumer (e.g. dashboard, advisor probe, downstream packet).\n31: - Debugging JSONL reducer output or auditing schema-version transitions.\n32: - Authoring fixtures that need to round-trip through the reducer.\n33: \n34: The deep review loop uses 9 state files under the resolved `{artifact_dir}/` owned by the target spec:\n35: \n36: | File | Format | Mutability |\n37: |------|--------|------------|\n38: | `deep-review-config.json` | JSON | Immutable after init, except the terminal `status: complete` flip |\n39: | `deep-review-state.jsonl` | JSON Lines | Append-only |\n40: | `deep-review-findings-registry.json` | JSON | Auto-generated reducer state |\n41: | `deep-review-strategy.md` | Markdown | Updated each iteration |\n42: | `deep-review-dashboard.md` | Markdown | Auto-generated (read-only) |\n43: | `.deep-review-pause` | Sentinel | Created/deleted by user |\n44: | `resource-map.md` | Markdown | Emitted once at synthesis unless `resource_map.emit` is false |\n45: | `review-report.md` | Markdown | Updated at synthesis |\n46: | `iterations/iteration-NNN.md` | Markdown | Write-once |\n47: \n48: ```text\n49: {artifact_dir}/\n50:   deep-review-config.json\n51:   deep-review-state.jsonl\n52:   deep-review-findings-registry.json\n53:   deep-review-strategy.md\n54:   deep-review-dashboard.md\n55:   .deep-review-pause\n56:   review-report.md\n57:   iterations/\n58:     iteration-001.md\n59:     iteration-002.md\n60:     ...\n61: ```\n62: \n63: `{artifact_dir}` comes from `resolveArtifactRoot(specFolder, 'review')`. Root-spec runs resolve directly to `{spec_folder}/review/`. Child-phase and sub-phase runs use **flat-first**: a first run with an empty `review/` resolves directly to `{spec_folder}/review/` (no `pt-NN` wrapper). A `pt-NN` packet is allocated only when prior content for a non-matching target already exists. Continuation runs reuse the existing flat artifact (or matching `pt-NN` packet). This avoids the unnecessary `pt-01` wrapper on first runs.\n64: \n65: Example (first run on a child phase): `.../026-graph.../006-continuity-refactor-gates/003-gate-c-writer-ready/` → `003-gate-c-writer-ready/review/` (flat, no subfolder).\n66: \n67: Example (subsequent run with prior content for a different target): `003-gate-c-writer-ready/review/003-gate-c-writer-ready-pt-02/` (`pt-NN` allocated as a sibling to the prior content; subfolder name is `{basename(spec_folder)}-pt-{NN}`).\n68: \n69: ---\n70: \n71: ## 2. CONFIG FILE (deep-review-config.json)\n72: \n73: Created during initialization. Not modified after creation.\n74: \n75: ```json\n76: {\n77:   \"topic\": \"Review of deep-review skill package\",\n78:   \"mode\": \"review\",\n79:   \"reviewTarget\": \"specs/030-deep-review-review-mode\",\n80:   \"reviewTargetType\": \"spec-folder\",\n81:   \"reviewDimensions\": [\"correctness\", \"security\", \"traceability\", \"maintainability\"],\n82:   \"resource_map_present\": false,\n83:   \"sessionId\": \"rvw-2026-04-03T12-00-00Z\",\n84:   \"parentSessionId\": null,\n85:   \"lineageMode\": \"new\",\n86:   \"generation\": 1,\n87:   \"continuedFromRun\": null,\n88:   \"maxIterations\": 7,\n89:   \"convergenceThreshold\": 0.10,\n90:   \"stuckThreshold\": 2,\n91:   \"severityThreshold\": \"P2\",\n92:   \"crossReference\": {\n93:     \"core\": [\"spec_code\", \"checklist_evidence\"],\n94:     \"overlay\": [\"feature_catalog_code\", \"playbook_capability\"]\n95:   },\n96:   \"qualityGateThreshold\": true,\n97:   \"releaseReadinessState\": \"in-progress\",\n98:   \"specFolder\": \"030-deep-review-review-mode\",\n99:   \"createdAt\": \"2026-03-24T14:00:00Z\",\n100:   \"status\": \"initialized\",\n101:   \"executionMode\": \"auto\",\n102:   \"fileProtection\": {\n103:     \"deep-review-config.json\": \"immutable\",\n104:     \"deep-review-state.jsonl\": \"append-only\",\n105:     \"deep-review-findings-registry.json\": \"auto-generated\",\n106:     \"deep-review-strategy.md\": \"mutable\",\n107:     \"deep-review-dashboard.md\": \"auto-generated\",\n108:     \".deep-review-pause\": \"operator-controlled\",\n109:     \"review-report.md\": \"mutable\",\n110:     \"review-report-v*.md\": \"write-once\",\n111:     \"iteration-*.md\": \"write-once\"\n112:   },\n113:   \"reducer\": {\n114:     \"enabled\": true,\n115:     \"inputs\": [\"latestJSONLDelta\", \"newIterationFile\", \"priorReducedState\"],\n116:     \"outputs\": [\"findingsRegistry\", \"dashboardMetrics\", \"strategyUpdates\"],\n117:     \"metrics\": [\n118:       \"dimensionsCovered\",\n119:       \"findingsBySeverity\",\n120:       \"openFindings\",\n121:       \"resolvedFindings\",\n122:       \"convergenceScore\"\n123:     ]\n124:   }\n125: }\n126: ```\n127: \n128: ### Field Reference\n129: \n130: | Field | Type | Default | Description |\n131: |-------|------|---------|-------------|\n132: | mode | `\"review\"` | -- | Session mode discriminator (required) |\n133: | reviewTarget | string | -- | Path or identifier of the review target |\n134: | reviewTargetType | string | `\"spec-folder\"` | `spec-folder`, `skill`, `agent`, `track`, `files` |\n135: | reviewDimensions | string[] | all 4 | Dimensions to evaluate |\n136: | resource_map_present | boolean | false | True only when `{specFolder}/resource-map.md` existed during init, enables the Resource Map Coverage audit pass and conditional report section |\n137: | sessionId | string | -- | Stable identifier for the current review lineage |\n138: | parentSessionId | string \\| null | `null` | Parent lineage reference for restart flows |\n139: | lineageMode | string | `\"new\"` | `new`, `resume`, `restart`. `fork` and `completed-continue` are deferred and not emitted by the current runtime |\n140: | generation | number | 1 | Lineage generation number, incremented on `restart`, unchanged on `resume` |\n141: | continuedFromRun | number \\| null | `null` | Count of completed iteration records at the lifecycle boundary (set on `resume` and `restart`) |\n142: | maxIterations | number | 7 | Hard cap on loop iterations |\n143: | convergenceThreshold | number | 0.10 | Stop when severity-weighted new findings ratio below this |\n144: | stuckThreshold | number | 2 | Consecutive no-progress iterations before recovery |\n145: | severityThreshold | string | `\"P2\"` | Minimum severity to report: `P0`, `P1`, `P2` |\n146: | crossReference | object | -- | Core (hard-gated) and overlay (advisory) protocol sets |\n147: | qualityGateThreshold | boolean | true | Whether binary quality gates are enforced |\n148: | specFolder | string | -- | Spec folder path (relative to specs/) |\n149: | status | string | `\"initialized\"` | `initialized`, `running`, `converged`, `stuck`, `complete`, `error` |\n150: | releaseReadinessState | string | `\"in-progress\"` | `in-progress`, `converged`, `release-blocking` |\n151: | fileProtection | object | -- | Mutability declarations (see protection levels below) |\n152: | reducer | object | -- | Canonical reducer inputs, outputs, and metrics names |\n153: \n154: ### File Protection Levels\n155: \n156: | Level | Meaning |\n157: |-------|---------|\n158: | immutable | Cannot be modified after creation (config: the terminal `status: complete` flip is the one permitted write) |\n159: | append-only | New content added at end only |\n160: | mutable | Can be read, edited, overwritten |\n161: | write-once | Created once, never modified |\n162: | auto-generated | System-managed, overwritten each refresh |\n163: | operator-controlled | Created or deleted only by the human/operator to control loop state |\n164: \n165: ### Review Dimensions\n166: \n167: | Dimension | Priority | Required for Coverage |\n168: |-----------|----------|---------------------|\n169: | correctness | 1 | Yes |\n170: | security | 2 | Yes |\n171: | traceability | 3 | Yes |\n172: | maintainability | 4 | Yes |\n173: \n174: ### Severity Weights\n175: \n176: | Severity | Weight | Label | Requires file:line |\n177: |----------|--------|-------|--------------------|\n178: | P0 | 10.0 | Blocker | Yes |\n179: | P1 | 5.0 | Required | Yes |\n180: | P2 | 1.0 | Suggestion | Yes |\n181: \n182: ---\n183: \n184: ## 3. STATE LOG\n185: \n186: The `deep-review-state.jsonl` record schemas (config, iteration, event, lineage) and the Review Depth Schema (v2) live in `state-jsonl.md` for navigability.\n187: \n188: ---\n189: \n190: ## 4. STRATEGY FILE (deep-review-strategy.md)\n191: \n192: Updated at the end of each iteration. Serves as the persistent brain across fresh-context iterations.\n193: \n194: ### Required Sections\n195: \n196: | Section | Updated By | Purpose |\n197: |---------|-----------|---------|\n198: | topic | Init only | Review topic from config |\n199: | review-dimensions | Each iteration | Unchecked dimensions drive next focus |\n200: | completed-dimensions | Each iteration | Checked dimensions with verdict summary |\n201: | running-findings | Each iteration | P0/P1/P2 active counts + deltas |\n202: | what-worked | Each iteration | Successful approaches for reuse |\n203: | what-failed | Each iteration | Failed approaches to avoid |\n204: | exhausted-approaches | When fully tried | \"Do not retry\" registry |\n205: | ruled-out-directions | Each iteration | Eliminated directions with reasons |\n206: | next-focus | Each iteration | Recommended direction for next iteration |\n207: | known-context | Init only | Prior work from memory context |\n208: | cross-reference-status | Each iteration | Core vs overlay protocol status |\n209: | files-under-review | Each iteration | Per-file coverage state table |\n210: | review-boundaries | Init only | Max iterations, thresholds, config |\n211: \n212: ### Mapping from Research Mode\n213: \n214: | Review Section | Research Equivalent |\n215: |---------------|-------------------|\n216: | review-dimensions | Key Questions (remaining) |\n217: | completed-dimensions | Answered Questions |\n218: | running-findings | _(none, review-specific)_ |\n219: | cross-reference-status | _(none, review-specific)_ |\n220: | files-under-review | _(none, review-specific)_ |\n221: | review-boundaries | Research Boundaries |\n222: \n223: Sections unchanged from research: topic, what-worked, what-failed, exhausted-approaches, ruled-out-directions, next-focus, known-context.\n224: \n225: ### Update Protocol\n226: \n227: 1. Read current strategy file\n228: 2. Move completed dimensions from \"remaining\" to \"completed\" with `[x]` and verdict\n229: 3. Update running-findings with P0/P1/P2 counts and deltas\n230: 4. Add to what-worked / what-failed with iteration number\n231: 5. Move exhausted approaches. Update cross-reference-status and files-under-review\n232: 6. Set next-focus based on remaining dimensions and open findings\n233: \n234: ---\n235: \n236: ## 5. FINDINGS REGISTRY (deep-review-findings-registry.json)\n237: \n238: Reducer-owned JSON document regenerated after every iteration and lifecycle transition.\n239: \n240: ```json\n241: {\n242:   \"sessionId\": \"rvw-2026-04-03T12-00-00Z\",\n243:   \"generation\": 1,\n244:   \"lineageMode\": \"resume\",\n245:   \"openFindings\": [],\n246:   \"resolvedFindings\": [],\n247:   \"blockedStopHistory\": [],\n248:   \"persistentSameSeverity\": [],\n249:   \"severityChanged\": [],\n250:   \"repeatedFindings\": [],\n251:   \"dimensionCoverage\": {\n252:     \"correctness\": true,\n253:     \"security\": true,\n254:     \"traceability\": false,\n255:     \"maintainability\": false\n256:   },\n257:   \"findingsBySeverity\": {\n258:     \"P0\": 0,\n259:     \"P1\": 1,\n260:     \"P2\": 2\n261:   },\n262:   \"openFindingsCount\": 3,\n263:   \"resolvedFindingsCount\": 1,\n264:   \"convergenceScore\": 0.44,\n265:   \"graphConvergenceScore\": 1.01,\n266:   \"graphDecision\": \"STOP_ALLOWED\",\n267:   \"graphBlockers\": [],\n268:   \"corruptionWarnings\": []\n269: }\n270: ```\n271: \n272: This file is machine-owned and must stay synchronized with the latest iteration delta, dashboard metrics, and synthesized review report.\n273: \n274: ### Blocked-Stop and Corruption-Tracking Additions\n275: \n276: | Field | Type | Description |\n277: |-------|------|-------------|\n278: | `blockedStopHistory` | array | One entry per `blocked_stop` JSONL event: `{run, blockedBy, gateResults, recoveryStrategy, timestamp}`. Rendered in the dashboard `BLOCKED STOPS` section and can drive the strategy `next-focus` anchor when blocked-stop is the most recent loop event. |\n279: | `persistentSameSeverity` | array | Findings observed in ≥2 iterations with NO severity transitions beyond initial discovery. REQ-018 split of the deprecated `repeatedFindings` bucket. |\n280: | `severityChanged` | array | Findings that went through at least one severity transition (P0↔P1↔P2) in their `transitions` history. |\n281: | `repeatedFindings` | array | **Deprecated.** Union of `persistentSameSeverity` and `severityChanged`. Retained for backward compatibility, new code should read the split arrays. |\n282: | `corruptionWarnings` | array | Per-line corruption reports from `parseJsonlDetailed()`: `{line, raw, error}`. Non-empty means the reducer detected malformed JSONL. |\n283: \n284: ### Default Values\n285: \n286: When no `graph_convergence` event has been recorded yet, defaults are `graphConvergenceScore: 0`, `graphDecision: null`, and `graphBlockers: []`.\n287: When no `blocked_stop` event has been recorded yet, `blockedStopHistory: []`.\n288: When JSONL parses cleanly, `corruptionWarnings: []`.\n289: \n290: ### Fail-Closed Semantics (REQ-015, REQ-016)\n291: \n292: - **Malformed JSONL**: The reducer CLI exits with code `2` and writes a warning to stderr when `corruptionWarnings.length > 0`. Pass `--lenient` (or `lenient:true` to `reduceReviewState`) to escape-hatch out and preserve the v1.2.0.0 fail-open behavior for legacy packets.\n293: - **Missing machine-owned anchors**: `replaceAnchorSection()` throws `Error('Missing machine-owned anchor \"<id>\" in deep-review strategy file.')` when the strategy file is present but lacks one of the required anchors. Pass `--create-missing-anchors` (or `createMissingAnchors:true`) to bootstrap empty strategy files by appending the missing anchor blocks.\n294: - **Dashboard surfaces**: `CORRUPTION WARNINGS` section lists detected lines. `BLOCKED STOPS` section lists `blockedStopHistory` entries. `GRAPH CONVERGENCE` section reports `graphConvergenceScore` / `graphDecision` / `graphBlockers`.\n295: - **Strategy next-focus override**: When the latest `blocked_stop` event timestamp is newer than the latest iteration timestamp, the reducer rewrites the strategy `next-focus` anchor to surface the blocking gates and recovery hint so operators see the blocker before choosing the next iteration direction.\n296: \n297: ---\n298: \n299: ## 6. ITERATION FILES (review/iterations/iteration-NNN.md)\n300: \n301: Write-once files. One per iteration, zero-padded 3-digit naming.\n302: \n303: ### Structure\n304: \n305: ```markdown\n306: # Iteration [N]: [Focus Area]\n307: \n308: ## Focus\n309: [Dimension(s), files, scope investigated]\n310: \n311: ## Scorecard\n312: - Dimensions covered: [list]\n313: - Files reviewed: [count]\n314: - New findings: P0=[n] P1=[n] P2=[n]\n315: - Refined findings: P0=[n] P1=[n] P2=[n]\n316: - New findings ratio: [0.0-1.0]\n317: \n318: ## Findings\n319: \n320: ### P0, Blocker\n321: - **F[NNN]**: [Title], `file:line`, [Description with evidence]\n322: \n323: ### P1, Required\n324: - **F[NNN]**: [Title], `file:line`, [Description with evidence]\n325: \n326: ### P2, Suggestion\n327: - **F[NNN]**: [Title], `file:line`, [Description with evidence]\n328: \n329: ## Cross-Reference Results\n330: | Protocol | Status | Gate | Evidence | Notes |\n331: |----------|--------|------|----------|-------|\n332: | spec_code | pass/partial/fail | hard | file:line | ... |\n333: \n334: ## Assessment\n335: - New findings ratio: [0.0-1.0]\n336: - Dimensions addressed: [list]\n337: - Novelty justification: [breakdown]\n338: \n339: ## Ruled Out\n340: - [Approach]: [Why], [Evidence]\n341: \n342: ## Dead Ends\n343: - [Direction]: [Why]\n344: \n345: ## Recommended Next Focus\n346: [What to investigate next]\n347: ```\n348: \n349: Every finding must include: unique ID (`F001`...), severity (`P0`/`P1`/`P2`), concrete `file:line` evidence, and dimension tag.\n350: \n351: ---\n352: \n353: ## 7. REVIEW REPORT (review/review-report.md)\n354: \n355: The review synthesis output contains 9 core sections plus a conditional `## Resource Map Coverage Gate` section when `resource_map_present` is true:\n356: \n357: | # | Section | Description |\n358: |---|---------|-------------|\n359: | 1 | Executive Summary | Verdict, active P0/P1/P2 counts, scope, `hasAdvisories` flag |\n360: | 2 | Planning Trigger | Why result routes to planning or changelog |\n361: | 3 | Active Finding Registry | Deduped active findings with evidence, severity, dimension |\n362: | 4 | Remediation Workstreams | Ordered lanes grouped by dependency or area |\n363: | 5 | Spec Seed | Minimal spec updates implied by findings |\n364: | 6 | Plan Seed | Initial remediation tasks from findings |\n365: | 7 | Traceability Status | Core vs overlay protocol outcomes and gaps |\n366: | 8 | Resource Map Coverage Gate | Present only when `{spec_folder}/resource-map.md` existed at init, contains touched entries, untouched entries (`expected-by-scope` vs `gap`), and implementation paths absent from the map |\n367: | 9 | Deferred Items | Advisory findings, blocked items, follow-up checks |\n368: | 10 | Audit Appendix | Coverage, convergence replay, audit detail |\n369: \n370: **Executive Summary** includes verdict (`PASS`/`CONDITIONAL`/`FAIL`), active finding counts, `hasAdvisories` boolean (PASS + P2 > 0), scope description, and convergence reason.\n371: \n372: **Planning Trigger** routes FAIL/CONDITIONAL to remediation planning, PASS to changelog creation.\n373: \n374: **Active Finding Registry** lists each active finding with findingId, severity, dimension, title, file:line evidence, first/last seen iteration, and status.\n375: \n376: **Remediation Workstreams** group related findings into ordered lanes with constituent finding IDs and execution order.\n377: \n378: **Spec Seed / Plan Seed** provide minimal spec updates and initial remediation tasks referencing finding IDs and target files.\n379: \n380: **Traceability Status** reports per-protocol pass/partial/fail with gating class and evidence.\n381: \n382: **Resource Map Coverage Gate** is emitted only when `resource_map_present` is true and MUST contain exactly three bullets: touched entries, untouched entries (`expected-by-scope` vs `gap`), and implementation paths absent from the map.\n383: \n384: **Deferred Items** captures advisory findings, blocked protocols, and future follow-up checks.\n385: \n386: **Audit Appendix** contains iteration table, convergence signal replay, file coverage matrix, and dimension breakdown.\n387: \n388: ---\n389: \n390: ## 8. DASHBOARD (review/deep-review-dashboard.md)\n391: \n392: Auto-generated summary. Never manually edited.\n393: \n394: - **Path**: `{artifact_dir}/deep-review-dashboard.md`\n395: - **Generated from**: JSONL state log + strategy + findings registry\n396: - **Refresh**: Regenerated after every iteration\n397: - **Protection**: `auto-generated` in fileProtection\n398: \n399: ### Sections\n400: \n401: | Section | Source | Description |\n402: |---------|--------|-------------|\n403: | Findings Summary | JSONL | Active P0/P1/P2 counts, new vs refined |\n404: | Progress Table | JSONL | Run, status, focus, dimensions, ratio, duration |\n405: | Coverage | Strategy + JSONL | Dimension completion, file coverage, protocol status |\n406: | Trend | JSONL signals | Rolling average, composite stop score, trajectory |\n407: \n408: **Rules:** Sole inputs are JSONL + strategy. Overwrite entirely on refresh. Read-only for all agents.\n409: \n410: ---\n411: \n412: ## 9. CLAIM ADJUDICATION\n413: \n414: Every new P0/P1 finding must carry a **typed claim-adjudication packet**. The packet is parsed by `step_post_iteration_claim_adjudication` in the review workflow and its pass/fail result is persisted as a `claim_adjudication` event in `deep-review-state.jsonl`. The next iteration's `step_check_convergence` legal-stop decision tree reads the latest event via `claimAdjudicationGate` (gate `f`), a missing or failed packet vetoes STOP even if every other gate passes. Prose-only adjudication blocks are no longer accepted.\n415: \n416: The persisted gate result is the flat `claim_adjudication` event, and it is canonical in its own right. The ledger registers `deep_review.claim_adjudication` for exactly this run-level summary and separately registers `deep_review.claim_adjudication_recorded` for the typed per-finding record (`findingId`, `claimDigest`, `finalSeverity`, `adjudicationOutcome`). They are not aliases: the payloads are closed and disjoint, so a producer holding only gate counts writes the flat stem and never invents the typed fields. Section 11 lists the registered vocabulary and the check that holds it to the emitter surface on disk.\n417: \n418: ### Typed Packet Schema (required)\n419: \n420: Embed the packet inside the iteration file for each new P0/P1 finding. The orchestrator parses it after evaluation and persists the validation result.\n421: \n422: ```json\n423: {\n424:   \"findingId\": \"F003\",\n425:   \"claim\": \"Coverage-graph upsert identity is bare `id`, so cross-session collisions overwrite prior rows.\",\n426:   \"evidenceRefs\": [\n427:     \".skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/lib/coverage-graph/coverage-graph-db.ts:154\",\n428:     \".skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/lib/coverage-graph/coverage-graph-db.ts:292-302\"\n429:   ],\n430:   \"counterevidenceSought\": \"Grepped the module for compound-key upserts, checked migration scripts, and inspected session-isolation.vitest.ts for a collision regression, none found.\",\n431:   \"alternativeExplanation\": \"Could be intentional single-tenant design, but REQ-024 explicitly requires session isolation, so this is rejected.\",\n432:   \"finalSeverity\": \"P1\",\n433:   \"confidence\": 0.86,\n434:   \"downgradeTrigger\": \"If a composite primary key `(spec_folder, loop_type, session_id, id)` lands and a collision regression covers the ID-reuse path, downgrade to P2 tech-debt.\",\n435:   \"transitions\": [\n436:     { \"iteration\": 2, \"from\": null, \"to\": \"P1\", \"reason\": \"Initial discovery\" }\n437:   ]\n438: }\n439: ```\n440: \n441: ### Required Fields\n442: \n443: | Field | Type | Description |\n444: |-------|------|-------------|\n445: | `findingId` | string | Must match the finding ID in the iteration body and registry |\n446: | `claim` | string | The single assertion the finding makes (one sentence, evidence-backed) |\n447: | `evidenceRefs` | string[] | `file:line` or `file:range` citations that substantiate the claim (at least one entry) |\n448: | `counterevidenceSought` | string | Where the reviewer looked for contradicting evidence (commands, paths, docs), blank string is not acceptable |\n449: | `alternativeExplanation` | string | An alternative reading of the evidence, even if the reviewer rejects it |\n450: | `finalSeverity` | `\"P0\"` \\| `\"P1\"` \\| `\"P2\"` | Severity after adjudication (may differ from the severity originally asserted) |\n451: | `confidence` | number `[0, 1]` | Reviewer confidence in `finalSeverity` |\n452: | `downgradeTrigger` | string | The concrete condition under which this finding should be downgraded in a future iteration |\n453: | `transitions` | object[] | Optional severity transition log, required when `finalSeverity` differs from the originally asserted severity |\n454: \n455: ### Validation Rules (enforced by `step_post_iteration_claim_adjudication`)\n456: \n457: 1. A packet MUST exist for every new P0/P1 finding introduced in this iteration. Carried-forward findings reuse the previous packet unless severity transitioned.\n458: 2. All required fields MUST be present and non-empty. `confidence` MUST be a number in `[0, 1]`.\n459: 3. Each `evidenceRefs` entry MUST contain a `:` separating the path from a line or range.\n460: 4. `finalSeverity` MUST match the severity the finding is registered under in the iteration's `Findings` section and in `deep-review-findings-registry.json`.\n461: 5. When any rule fails, the workflow appends `{\"event\":\"claim_adjudication\",\"passed\":false,\"missingPackets\":[...]}` to the state log. The next `step_check_convergence` call reads that event and sets `claimAdjudicationGate` = `false`, producing a `blockedStop` event with `blockedBy: [\"claimAdjudicationGate\"]` until a follow-up iteration rewrites the packet.\n462: \n463: ### Severity Transition Rules\n464: \n465: - **P2 → P1**: confirmed exploitable impact or spec violation with direct evidence\n466: - **P1 → P0**: demonstrated data loss, security breach, or hard-gate failure\n467: - **Downgrade**: requires explicit counterevidence or a confirmed alternative explanation\n468: - Every transition is recorded in the packet's `transitions` array and mirrored into the finding registry's `transitions` field\n469: \n470: ---\n471: \n472: ## 10. FINDING REGISTRY\n473: \n474: Each finding is tracked with a unique identifier enabling deduplication, severity transitions, and status lifecycle.\n475: \n476: ### Schema\n477: \n478: ```json\n479: {\n480:   \"findingId\": \"F003\",\n481:   \"severity\": \"P1\",\n482:   \"category\": \"resource-map-coverage\",\n483:   \"status\": \"active\",\n484:   \"dimension\": \"traceability\",\n485:   \"title\": \"Applied target file missing from resource-map inventory\",\n486:   \"file\": \".skilled/commands/deep/assets/deep-review-auto.yaml\",\n487:   \"line\": 955,\n488:   \"firstSeen\": 2,\n489:   \"lastSeen\": 4,\n490:   \"transitions\": [\n491:     { \"iteration\": 2, \"from\": null, \"to\": \"P2\", \"reason\": \"Initial discovery\" },\n492:     { \"iteration\": 4, \"from\": \"P2\", \"to\": \"P1\", \"reason\": \"Confirmed real coverage gap against applied target inventory\" }\n493:   ]\n494: }\n495: ```\n496: \n497: | Field | Type | Description |\n498: |-------|------|-------------|\n499: | findingId | string | Sequential unique ID: `F001`, `F002`, ... |\n500: | severity | `\"P0\"` / `\"P1\"` / `\"P2\"` | Current severity |\n501: | category | `\"correctness\"` / `\"security\"` / `\"traceability\"` / `\"maintainability\"` / `\"resource-map-coverage\"` | Primary audit category for the finding, `resource-map-coverage` is reserved for implementation-vs-map coverage gaps |\n502: | status | `\"active\"` / `\"resolved\"` / `\"deferred\"` / `\"disproved\"` | Current status |\n503: | dimension | string | Primary dimension: correctness, security, traceability, maintainability |\n504: | title | string | Short description |\n505: | file | string | File path |\n506: | line | number | Line number (approximate) |\n507: | firstSeen / lastSeen | number | Iteration where first discovered / last referenced |\n508: | transitions | array | Severity and status change history |\n509: \n510: ### Status Lifecycle\n511: \n512: ```text\n513: [discovered] --> active --> resolved    (fixed or confirmed non-issue)\n514:                   |\n515:                   +--> deferred    (advisory, below threshold)\n516:                   |\n517:                   +--> disproved   (counterevidence invalidated)\n518: ```\n519: \n520: | Status | Counts Toward Verdict |\n521: |--------|----------------------|\n522: | active | Yes |\n523: | resolved | No |\n524: | deferred | No (listed in Deferred Items) |\n525: | disproved | No |\n526: \n527: ### Deduplication\n528: \n529: Same file + line range + root cause as an existing finding = **refinement**, not new. The existing findingId is updated. Refinements count at half weight (`refinementMultiplier: 0.5`) and are tracked via `findingsRefined` in JSONL.\n530: \n531: ### Cross-Reference Protocols\n532: \n533: | Protocol | Level | Applies To | Gate |\n534: |----------|-------|------------|------|\n535: | spec_code | core | all types | hard |\n536: | checklist_evidence | core | all types | hard |\n537: | skill_agent | overlay | skill | advisory |\n538: | agent_cross_runtime | overlay | agent | advisory |\n539: | feature_catalog_code | overlay | skill, spec-folder, track, files | advisory |\n540: | playbook_capability | overlay | skill, agent, spec-folder | advisory |\n541: \n542: Severity for `resource-map-coverage` findings is calibrated to the coverage-gate outcome:\n543: - `P2` when an untouched map entry is explicitly `expected-by-scope`\n544: - `P1` when an untouched or absent path represents a real coverage gap\n545: - `P0` only when the missing coverage masks a release-blocking correctness or security risk\n546: \n547: ### Quality Gates\n548: \n549: | Gate | Rule |\n550: |------|------|\n551: | Evidence | Every active finding backed by concrete file:line evidence |\n552: | Scope | Reviewed files and conclusions stay inside declared scope |\n553: | Coverage | Required dimensions and required protocols covered |\n554: \n555: All three gates must pass before STOP. Gate failure forces `verdict: \"FAIL\"` regardless of finding counts.\n556: \n557: ---\n558: \n559: ## 11. LEDGER VOCABULARY AND PROJECTION CEILING\n560: \n561: ### Registered vocabulary\n562: \n563: The canonical dotted stems for this mode live in `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/lib/deep-review-ledger-schema/deep-review-ledger-types.ts`:\n564: \n565: - `DeepReviewEventStems` — the registered stems the ledger accepts.\n566: - `DEEP_REVIEW_STEM_PRODUCERS` — one entry per stem recording whether a mechanical producer emits it today (`spoken`, with the producer files) or why nothing does (`reserved`).\n567: \n568: The registry is only honest while it matches the emitter surface. `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/check-ledger-stem-producers.cjs` scans the workflow assets and runtime scripts and fails (exit 2) when a registered stem has no producer, a spoken stem has no emitter, or a reserved stem is emitted anyway:\n569: \n570: ```bash\n571: node .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/check-ledger-stem-producers.cjs\n572: ```\n573: \n574: ### Which file is authoritative\n575: \n576: `deep-review-state.jsonl` is authoritative while the mode's authority record (`authority-deep-review.json`, state `legacy_authoritative`) names the legacy writer. Once the record moves to `new_authoritative_reversible` or `new_authoritative_final` with `selectedWriter: \"dark\"`, the ledger is authoritative and this file becomes a projection that the append gateway refreshes after each append.\n577: \n578: ### What a projection refresh can reproduce\n579: \n580: The projection folds only registered stems, and its `run_initialized` arm rebuilds a thin config row: `type`, `topic`, `maxIterations`, `generation`, `timestamp`. A pre-flip config row written by the workflow carries attribution the fold cannot rebuild — `mode`, `reviewTarget`, `reviewTargetType`, `reviewDimensions`, `resource_map_present`, `resource_map`, `sessionId`, `parentSessionId`, `lineageMode`, `continuedFromRun`, `convergenceThreshold`, `antiConvergence`, `stopPolicy`, `executor`, `createdAt`, `specFolder`.\n581: \n582: Because losing those keys silently would make the projection look complete while the operator's context is gone, a replace that would drop keys from an existing `type: \"config\"` first row is refused with `ATTRIBUTION_COLLAPSE` (invariant `no-attribution-loss-on-replace`) before any bytes are written. An operator who hits it either migrates the attribution into a registered `deep_review.run_initialized` payload or intentionally moves the legacy file aside to accept the loss.","title":"read","metadata":{"metadata":{"truncated":false},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Read file .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/references/state/state-format.md, lines 1-582\n1: ---\n2: title: Deep Review State Format\n3: description: State file schemas for the autonomous deep review loop, config, JSONL log, strategy, iteration files, and review report.\n4: trigger_phrases:\n5:   - \"deep review state format\"\n6:   - \"deep review config schema\"\n7:   - \"review severity weights\"\n8:   - \"file protection levels\"\n9:   - \"review iteration file structure\"\n10: importance_tier: important\n11: contextType: implementation\n12: version: 1.11.1.0\n13: ---\n14: \n15: # Deep Review State Format\n16: \n17: State file schemas for the autonomous deep review loop.\n18: \n19: ---\n20: \n21: ## 1. OVERVIEW\n22: \n23: ### Purpose\n24: \n25: The review packet is reproduced from disk on every resume, so each file's format, mutability, and fields are pinned here for the reducer, the dashboard, the validator, and the resume path.\n26: \n27: ### When to Use\n28: \n29: - Validating deep-review state files emitted by an iteration or by the reducer.\n30: - Implementing a state consumer (e.g. dashboard, advisor probe, downstream packet).\n31: - Debugging JSONL reducer output or auditing schema-version transitions.\n32: - Authoring fixtures that need to round-trip through the reducer.\n33: \n34: The deep review loop uses 9 state files under the resolved `{artifact_dir}/` owned by the target spec:\n35: \n36: | File | Format | Mutability |\n37: |------|--------|------------|\n38: | `deep-review-config.json` | JSON | Immutable after init, except the terminal `status: complete` flip |\n39: | `deep-review-state.jsonl` | JSON Lines | Append-only |\n40: | `deep-review-findings-registry.json` | JSON | Auto-generated reducer state |\n41: | `deep-review-strategy.md` | Markdown | Updated each iteration |\n42: | `deep-review-dashboard.md` | Markdown | Auto-generated (read-only) |\n43: | `.deep-review-pause` | Sentinel | Created/deleted by user |\n44: | `resource-map.md` | Markdown | Emitted once at synthesis unless `resource_map.emit` is false |\n45: | `review-report.md` | Markdown | Updated at synthesis |\n46: | `iterations/iteration-NNN.md` | Markdown | Write-once |\n47: \n48: ```text\n49: {artifact_dir}/\n50:   deep-review-config.json\n51:   deep-review-state.jsonl\n52:   deep-review-findings-registry.json\n53:   deep-review-strategy.md\n54:   deep-review-dashboard.md\n55:   .deep-review-pause\n56:   review-report.md\n57:   iterations/\n58:     iteration-001.md\n59:     iteration-002.md\n60:     ...\n61: ```\n62: \n63: `{artifact_dir}` comes from `resolveArtifactRoot(specFolder, 'review')`. Root-spec runs resolve directly to `{spec_folder}/review/`. Child-phase and sub-phase runs use **flat-first**: a first run with an empty `review/` resolves directly to `{spec_folder}/review/` (no `pt-NN` wrapper). A `pt-NN` packet is allocated only when prior content for a non-matching target already exists. Continuation runs reuse the existing flat artifact (or matching `pt-NN` packet). This avoids the unnecessary `pt-01` wrapper on first runs.\n64: \n65: Example (first run on a child phase): `.../026-graph.../006-continuity-refactor-gates/003-gate-c-writer-ready/` → `003-gate-c-writer-ready/review/` (flat, no subfolder).\n66: \n67: Example (subsequent run with prior content for a different target): `003-gate-c-writer-ready/review/003-gate-c-writer-ready-pt-02/` (`pt-NN` allocated as a sibling to the prior content; subfolder name is `{basename(spec_folder)}-pt-{NN}`).\n68: \n69: ---\n70: \n71: ## 2. CONFIG FILE (deep-review-config.json)\n72: \n73: Created during initialization. Not modified after creation.\n74: \n75: ```json\n76: {\n77:   \"topic\": \"Review of deep-review skill package\",\n78:   \"mode\": \"review\",\n79:   \"reviewTarget\": \"specs/030-deep-review-review-mode\",\n80:   \"reviewTargetType\": \"spec-folder\",\n81:   \"reviewDimensions\": [\"correctness\", \"security\", \"traceability\", \"maintainability\"],\n82:   \"resource_map_present\": false,\n83:   \"sessionId\": \"rvw-2026-04-03T12-00-00Z\",\n84:   \"parentSessionId\": null,\n85:   \"lineageMode\": \"new\",\n86:   \"generation\": 1,\n87:   \"continuedFromRun\": null,\n88:   \"maxIterations\": 7,\n89:   \"convergenceThreshold\": 0.10,\n90:   \"stuckThreshold\": 2,\n91:   \"severityThreshold\": \"P2\",\n92:   \"crossReference\": {\n93:     \"core\": [\"spec_code\", \"checklist_evidence\"],\n94:     \"overlay\": [\"feature_catalog_code\", \"playbook_capability\"]\n95:   },\n96:   \"qualityGateThreshold\": true,\n97:   \"releaseReadinessState\": \"in-progress\",\n98:   \"specFolder\": \"030-deep-review-review-mode\",\n99:   \"createdAt\": \"2026-03-24T14:00:00Z\",\n100:   \"status\": \"initialized\",\n101:   \"executionMode\": \"auto\",\n102:   \"fileProtection\": {\n103:     \"deep-review-config.json\": \"immutable\",\n104:     \"deep-review-state.jsonl\": \"append-only\",\n105:     \"deep-review-findings-registry.json\": \"auto-generated\",\n106:     \"deep-review-strategy.md\": \"mutable\",\n107:     \"deep-review-dashboard.md\": \"auto-generated\",\n108:     \".deep-review-pause\": \"operator-controlled\",\n109:     \"review-report.md\": \"mutable\",\n110:     \"review-report-v*.md\": \"write-once\",\n111:     \"iteration-*.md\": \"write-once\"\n112:   },\n113:   \"reducer\": {\n114:     \"enabled\": true,\n115:     \"inputs\": [\"latestJSONLDelta\", \"newIterationFile\", \"priorReducedState\"],\n116:     \"outputs\": [\"findingsRegistry\", \"dashboardMetrics\", \"strategyUpdates\"],\n117:     \"metrics\": [\n118:       \"dimensionsCovered\",\n119:       \"findingsBySeverity\",\n120:       \"openFindings\",\n121:       \"resolvedFindings\",\n122:       \"convergenceScore\"\n123:     ]\n124:   }\n125: }\n126: ```\n127: \n128: ### Field Reference\n129: \n130: | Field | Type | Default | Description |\n131: |-------|------|---------|-------------|\n132: | mode | `\"review\"` | -- | Session mode discriminator (required) |\n133: | reviewTarget | string | -- | Path or identifier of the review target |\n134: | reviewTargetType | string | `\"spec-folder\"` | `spec-folder`, `skill`, `agent`, `track`, `files` |\n135: | reviewDimensions | string[] | all 4 | Dimensions to evaluate |\n136: | resource_map_present | boolean | false | True only when `{specFolder}/resource-map.md` existed during init, enables the Resource Map Coverage audit pass and conditional report section |\n137: | sessionId | string | -- | Stable identifier for the current review lineage |\n138: | parentSessionId | string \\| null | `null` | Parent lineage reference for restart flows |\n139: | lineageMode | string | `\"new\"` | `new`, `resume`, `restart`. `fork` and `completed-continue` are deferred and not emitted by the current runtime |\n140: | generation | number | 1 | Lineage generation number, incremented on `restart`, unchanged on `resume` |\n141: | continuedFromRun | number \\| null | `null` | Count of completed iteration records at the lifecycle boundary (set on `resume` and `restart`) |\n142: | maxIterations | number | 7 | Hard cap on loop iterations |\n143: | convergenceThreshold | number | 0.10 | Stop when severity-weighted new findings ratio below this |\n144: | stuckThreshold | number | 2 | Consecutive no-progress iterations before recovery |\n145: | severityThreshold | string | `\"P2\"` | Minimum severity to report: `P0`, `P1`, `P2` |\n146: | crossReference | object | -- | Core (hard-gated) and overlay (advisory) protocol sets |\n147: | qualityGateThreshold | boolean | true | Whether binary quality gates are enforced |\n148: | specFolder | string | -- | Spec folder path (relative to specs/) |\n149: | status | string | `\"initialized\"` | `initialized`, `running`, `converged`, `stuck`, `complete`, `error` |\n150: | releaseReadinessState | string | `\"in-progress\"` | `in-progress`, `converged`, `release-blocking` |\n151: | fileProtection | object | -- | Mutability declarations (see protection levels below) |\n152: | reducer | object | -- | Canonical reducer inputs, outputs, and metrics names |\n153: \n154: ### File Protection Levels\n155: \n156: | Level | Meaning |\n157: |-------|---------|\n158: | immutable | Cannot be modified after creation (config: the terminal `status: complete` flip is the one permitted write) |\n159: | append-only | New content added at end only |\n160: | mutable | Can be read, edited, overwritten |\n161: | write-once | Created once, never modified |\n162: | auto-generated | System-managed, overwritten each refresh |\n163: | operator-controlled | Created or deleted only by the human/operator to control loop state |\n164: \n165: ### Review Dimensions\n166: \n167: | Dimension | Priority | Required for Coverage |\n168: |-----------|----------|---------------------|\n169: | correctness | 1 | Yes |\n170: | security | 2 | Yes |\n171: | traceability | 3 | Yes |\n172: | maintainability | 4 | Yes |\n173: \n174: ### Severity Weights\n175: \n176: | Severity | Weight | Label | Requires file:line |\n177: |----------|--------|-------|--------------------|\n178: | P0 | 10.0 | Blocker | Yes |\n179: | P1 | 5.0 | Required | Yes |\n180: | P2 | 1.0 | Suggestion | Yes |\n181: \n182: ---\n183: \n184: ## 3. STATE LOG\n185: \n186: The `deep-review-state.jsonl` record schemas (config, iteration, event, lineage) and the Review Depth Schema (v2) live in `state-jsonl.md` for navigability.\n187: \n188: ---\n189: \n190: ## 4. STRATEGY FILE (deep-review-strategy.md)\n191: \n192: Updated at the end of each iteration. Serves as the persistent brain across fresh-context iterations.\n193: \n194: ### Required Sections\n195: \n196: | Section | Updated By | Purpose |\n197: |---------|-----------|---------|\n198: | topic | Init only | Review topic from config |\n199: | review-dimensions | Each iteration | Unchecked dimensions drive next focus |\n200: | completed-dimensions | Each iteration | Checked dimensions with verdict summary |\n201: | running-findings | Each iteration | P0/P1/P2 active counts + deltas |\n202: | what-worked | Each iteration | Successful approaches for reuse |\n203: | what-failed | Each iteration | Failed approaches to avoid |\n204: | exhausted-approaches | When fully tried | \"Do not retry\" registry |\n205: | ruled-out-directions | Each iteration | Eliminated directions with reasons |\n206: | next-focus | Each iteration | Recommended direction for next iteration |\n207: | known-context | Init only | Prior work from memory context |\n208: | cross-reference-status | Each iteration | Core vs overlay protocol status |\n209: | files-under-review | Each iteration | Per-file coverage state table |\n210: | review-boundaries | Init only | Max iterations, thresholds, config |\n211: \n212: ### Mapping from Research Mode\n213: \n214: | Review Section | Research Equivalent |\n215: |---------------|-------------------|\n216: | review-dimensions | Key Questions (remaining) |\n217: | completed-dimensions | Answered Questions |\n218: | running-findings | _(none, review-specific)_ |\n219: | cross-reference-status | _(none, review-specific)_ |\n220: | files-under-review | _(none, review-specific)_ |\n221: | review-boundaries | Research Boundaries |\n222: \n223: Sections unchanged from research: topic, what-worked, what-failed, exhausted-approaches, ruled-out-directions, next-focus, known-context.\n224: \n225: ### Update Protocol\n226: \n227: 1. Read current strategy file\n228: 2. Move completed dimensions from \"remaining\" to \"completed\" with `[x]` and verdict\n229: 3. Update running-findings with P0/P1/P2 counts and deltas\n230: 4. Add to what-worked / what-failed with iteration number\n231: 5. Move exhausted approaches. Update cross-reference-status and files-under-review\n232: 6. Set next-focus based on remaining dimensions and open findings\n233: \n234: ---\n235: \n236: ## 5. FINDINGS REGISTRY (deep-review-findings-registry.json)\n237: \n238: Reducer-owned JSON document regenerated after every iteration and lifecycle transition.\n239: \n240: ```json\n241: {\n242:   \"sessionId\": \"rvw-2026-04-03T12-00-00Z\",\n243:   \"generation\": 1,\n244:   \"lineageMode\": \"resume\",\n245:   \"openFindings\": [],\n246:   \"resolvedFindings\": [],\n247:   \"blockedStopHistory\": [],\n248:   \"persistentSameSeverity\": [],\n249:   \"severityChanged\": [],\n250:   \"repeatedFindings\": [],\n251:   \"dimensionCoverage\": {\n252:     \"correctness\": true,\n253:     \"security\": true,\n254:     \"traceability\": false,\n255:     \"maintainability\": false\n256:   },\n257:   \"findingsBySeverity\": {\n258:     \"P0\": 0,\n259:     \"P1\": 1,\n260:     \"P2\": 2\n261:   },\n262:   \"openFindingsCount\": 3,\n263:   \"resolvedFindingsCount\": 1,\n264:   \"convergenceScore\": 0.44,\n265:   \"graphConvergenceScore\": 1.01,\n266:   \"graphDecision\": \"STOP_ALLOWED\",\n267:   \"graphBlockers\": [],\n268:   \"corruptionWarnings\": []\n269: }\n270: ```\n271: \n272: This file is machine-owned and must stay synchronized with the latest iteration delta, dashboard metrics, and synthesized review report.\n273: \n274: ### Blocked-Stop and Corruption-Tracking Additions\n275: \n276: | Field | Type | Description |\n277: |-------|------|-------------|\n278: | `blockedStopHistory` | array | One entry per `blocked_stop` JSONL event: `{run, blockedBy, gateResults, recoveryStrategy, timestamp}`. Rendered in the dashboard `BLOCKED STOPS` section and can drive the strategy `next-focus` anchor when blocked-stop is the most recent loop event. |\n279: | `persistentSameSeverity` | array | Findings observed in ≥2 iterations with NO severity transitions beyond initial discovery. REQ-018 split of the deprecated `repeatedFindings` bucket. |\n280: | `severityChanged` | array | Findings that went through at least one severity transition (P0↔P1↔P2) in their `transitions` history. |\n281: | `repeatedFindings` | array | **Deprecated.** Union of `persistentSameSeverity` and `severityChanged`. Retained for backward compatibility, new code should read the split arrays. |\n282: | `corruptionWarnings` | array | Per-line corruption reports from `parseJsonlDetailed()`: `{line, raw, error}`. Non-empty means the reducer detected malformed JSONL. |\n283: \n284: ### Default Values\n285: \n286: When no `graph_convergence` event has been recorded yet, defaults are `graphConvergenceScore: 0`, `graphDecision: null`, and `graphBlockers: []`.\n287: When no `blocked_stop` event has been recorded yet, `blockedStopHistory: []`.\n288: When JSONL parses cleanly, `corruptionWarnings: []`.\n289: \n290: ### Fail-Closed Semantics (REQ-015, REQ-016)\n291: \n292: - **Malformed JSONL**: The reducer CLI exits with code `2` and writes a warning to stderr when `corruptionWarnings.length > 0`. Pass `--lenient` (or `lenient:true` to `reduceReviewState`) to escape-hatch out and preserve the v1.2.0.0 fail-open behavior for legacy packets.\n293: - **Missing machine-owned anchors**: `replaceAnchorSection()` throws `Error('Missing machine-owned anchor \"<id>\" in deep-review strategy file.')` when the strategy file is present but lacks one of the required anchors. Pass `--create-missing-anchors` (or `createMissingAnchors:true`) to bootstrap empty strategy files by appending the missing anchor blocks.\n294: - **Dashboard surfaces**: `CORRUPTION WARNINGS` section lists detected lines. `BLOCKED STOPS` section lists `blockedStopHistory` entries. `GRAPH CONVERGENCE` section reports `graphConvergenceScore` / `graphDecision` / `graphBlockers`.\n295: - **Strategy next-focus override**: When the latest `blocked_stop` event timestamp is newer than the latest iteration timestamp, the reducer rewrites the strategy `next-focus` anchor to surface the blocking gates and recovery hint so operators see the blocker before choosing the next iteration direction.\n296: \n297: ---\n298: \n299: ## 6. ITERATION FILES (review/iterations/iteration-NNN.md)\n300: \n301: Write-once files. One per iteration, zero-padded 3-digit naming.\n302: \n303: ### Structure\n304: \n305: ```markdown\n306: # Iteration [N]: [Focus Area]\n307: \n308: ## Focus\n309: [Dimension(s), files, scope investigated]\n310: \n311: ## Scorecard\n312: - Dimensions covered: [list]\n313: - Files reviewed: [count]\n314: - New findings: P0=[n] P1=[n] P2=[n]\n315: - Refined findings: P0=[n] P1=[n] P2=[n]\n316: - New findings ratio: [0.0-1.0]\n317: \n318: ## Findings\n319: \n320: ### P0, Blocker\n321: - **F[NNN]**: [Title], `file:line`, [Description with evidence]\n322: \n323: ### P1, Required\n324: - **F[NNN]**: [Title], `file:line`, [Description with evidence]\n325: \n326: ### P2, Suggestion\n327: - **F[NNN]**: [Title], `file:line`, [Description with evidence]\n328: \n329: ## Cross-Reference Results\n330: | Protocol | Status | Gate | Evidence | Notes |\n331: |----------|--------|------|----------|-------|\n332: | spec_code | pass/partial/fail | hard | file:line | ... |\n333: \n334: ## Assessment\n335: - New findings ratio: [0.0-1.0]\n336: - Dimensions addressed: [list]\n337: - Novelty justification: [breakdown]\n338: \n339: ## Ruled Out\n340: - [Approach]: [Why], [Evidence]\n341: \n342: ## Dead Ends\n343: - [Direction]: [Why]\n344: \n345: ## Recommended Next Focus\n346: [What to investigate next]\n347: ```\n348: \n349: Every finding must include: unique ID (`F001`...), severity (`P0`/`P1`/`P2`), concrete `file:line` evidence, and dimension tag.\n350: \n351: ---\n352: \n353: ## 7. REVIEW REPORT (review/review-report.md)\n354: \n355: The review synthesis output contains 9 core sections plus a conditional `## Resource Map Coverage Gate` section when `resource_map_present` is true:\n356: \n357: | # | Section | Description |\n358: |---|---------|-------------|\n359: | 1 | Executive Summary | Verdict, active P0/P1/P2 counts, scope, `hasAdvisories` flag |\n360: | 2 | Planning Trigger | Why result routes to planning or changelog |\n361: | 3 | Active Finding Registry | Deduped active findings with evidence, severity, dimension |\n362: | 4 | Remediation Workstreams | Ordered lanes grouped by dependency or area |\n363: | 5 | Spec Seed | Minimal spec updates implied by findings |\n364: | 6 | Plan Seed | Initial remediation tasks from findings |\n365: | 7 | Traceability Status | Core vs overlay protocol outcomes and gaps |\n366: | 8 | Resource Map Coverage Gate | Present only when `{spec_folder}/resource-map.md` existed at init, contains touched entries, untouched entries (`expected-by-scope` vs `gap`), and implementation paths absent from the map |\n367: | 9 | Deferred Items | Advisory findings, blocked items, follow-up checks |\n368: | 10 | Audit Appendix | Coverage, convergence replay, audit detail |\n369: \n370: **Executive Summary** includes verdict (`PASS`/`CONDITIONAL`/`FAIL`), active finding counts, `hasAdvisories` boolean (PASS + P2 > 0), scope description, and convergence reason.\n371: \n372: **Planning Trigger** routes FAIL/CONDITIONAL to remediation planning, PASS to changelog creation.\n373: \n374: **Active Finding Registry** lists each active finding with findingId, severity, dimension, title, file:line evidence, first/last seen iteration, and status.\n375: \n376: **Remediation Workstreams** group related findings into ordered lanes with constituent finding IDs and execution order.\n377: \n378: **Spec Seed / Plan Seed** provide minimal spec updates and initial remediation tasks referencing finding IDs and target files.\n379: \n380: **Traceability Status** reports per-protocol pass/partial/fail with gating class and evidence.\n381: \n382: **Resource Map Coverage Gate** is emitted only when `resource_map_present` is true and MUST contain exactly three bullets: touched entries, untouched entries (`expected-by-scope` vs `gap`), and implementation paths absent from the map.\n383: \n384: **Deferred Items** captures advisory findings, blocked protocols, and future follow-up checks.\n385: \n386: **Audit Appendix** contains iteration table, convergence signal replay, file coverage matrix, and dimension breakdown.\n387: \n388: ---\n389: \n390: ## 8. DASHBOARD (review/deep-review-dashboard.md)\n391: \n392: Auto-generated summary. Never manually edited.\n393: \n394: - **Path**: `{artifact_dir}/deep-review-dashboard.md`\n395: - **Generated from**: JSONL state log + strategy + findings registry\n396: - **Refresh**: Regenerated after every iteration\n397: - **Protection**: `auto-generated` in fileProtection\n398: \n399: ### Sections\n400: \n401: | Section | Source | Description |\n402: |---------|--------|-------------|\n403: | Findings Summary | JSONL | Active P0/P1/P2 counts, new vs refined |\n404: | Progress Table | JSONL | Run, status, focus, dimensions, ratio, duration |\n405: | Coverage | Strategy + JSONL | Dimension completion, file coverage, protocol status |\n406: | Trend | JSONL signals | Rolling average, composite stop score, trajectory |\n407: \n408: **Rules:** Sole inputs are JSONL + strategy. Overwrite entirely on refresh. Read-only for all agents.\n409: \n410: ---\n411: \n412: ## 9. CLAIM ADJUDICATION\n413: \n414: Every new P0/P1 finding must carry a **typed claim-adjudication packet**. The packet is parsed by `step_post_iteration_claim_adjudication` in the review workflow and its pass/fail result is persisted as a `claim_adjudication` event in `deep-review-state.jsonl`. The next iteration's `step_check_convergence` legal-stop decision tree reads the latest event via `claimAdjudicationGate` (gate `f`), a missing or failed packet vetoes STOP even if every other gate passes. Prose-only adjudication blocks are no longer accepted.\n415: \n416: The persisted gate result is the flat `claim_adjudication` event, and it is canonical in its own right. The ledger registers `deep_review.claim_adjudication` for exactly this run-level summary and separately registers `deep_review.claim_adjudication_recorded` for the typed per-finding record (`findingId`, `claimDigest`, `finalSeverity`, `adjudicationOutcome`). They are not aliases: the payloads are closed and disjoint, so a producer holding only gate counts writes the flat stem and never invents the typed fields. Section 11 lists the registered vocabulary and the check that holds it to the emitter surface on disk.\n417: \n418: ### Typed Packet Schema (required)\n419: \n420: Embed the packet inside the iteration file for each new P0/P1 finding. The orchestrator parses it after evaluation and persists the validation result.\n421: \n422: ```json\n423: {\n424:   \"findingId\": \"F003\",\n425:   \"claim\": \"Coverage-graph upsert identity is bare `id`, so cross-session collisions overwrite prior rows.\",\n426:   \"evidenceRefs\": [\n427:     \".skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/lib/coverage-graph/coverage-graph-db.ts:154\",\n428:     \".skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/lib/coverage-graph/coverage-graph-db.ts:292-302\"\n429:   ],\n430:   \"counterevidenceSought\": \"Grepped the module for compound-key upserts, checked migration scripts, and inspected session-isolation.vitest.ts for a collision regression, none found.\",\n431:   \"alternativeExplanation\": \"Could be intentional single-tenant design, but REQ-024 explicitly requires session isolation, so this is rejected.\",\n432:   \"finalSeverity\": \"P1\",\n433:   \"confidence\": 0.86,\n434:   \"downgradeTrigger\": \"If a composite primary key `(spec_folder, loop_type, session_id, id)` lands and a collision regression covers the ID-reuse path, downgrade to P2 tech-debt.\",\n435:   \"transitions\": [\n436:     { \"iteration\": 2, \"from\": null, \"to\": \"P1\", \"reason\": \"Initial discovery\" }\n437:   ]\n438: }\n439: ```\n440: \n441: ### Required Fields\n442: \n443: | Field | Type | Description |\n444: |-------|------|-------------|\n445: | `findingId` | string | Must match the finding ID in the iteration body and registry |\n446: | `claim` | string | The single assertion the finding makes (one sentence, evidence-backed) |\n447: | `evidenceRefs` | string[] | `file:line` or `file:range` citations that substantiate the claim (at least one entry) |\n448: | `counterevidenceSought` | string | Where the reviewer looked for contradicting evidence (commands, paths, docs), blank string is not acceptable |\n449: | `alternativeExplanation` | string | An alternative reading of the evidence, even if the reviewer rejects it |\n450: | `finalSeverity` | `\"P0\"` \\| `\"P1\"` \\| `\"P2\"` | Severity after adjudication (may differ from the severity originally asserted) |\n451: | `confidence` | number `[0, 1]` | Reviewer confidence in `finalSeverity` |\n452: | `downgradeTrigger` | string | The concrete condition under which this finding should be downgraded in a future iteration |\n453: | `transitions` | object[] | Optional severity transition log, required when `finalSeverity` differs from the originally asserted severity |\n454: \n455: ### Validation Rules (enforced by `step_post_iteration_claim_adjudication`)\n456: \n457: 1. A packet MUST exist for every new P0/P1 finding introduced in this iteration. Carried-forward findings reuse the previous packet unless severity transitioned.\n458: 2. All required fields MUST be present and non-empty. `confidence` MUST be a number in `[0, 1]`.\n459: 3. Each `evidenceRefs` entry MUST contain a `:` separating the path from a line or range.\n460: 4. `finalSeverity` MUST match the severity the finding is registered under in the iteration's `Findings` section and in `deep-review-findings-registry.json`.\n461: 5. When any rule fails, the workflow appends `{\"event\":\"claim_adjudication\",\"passed\":false,\"missingPackets\":[...]}` to the state log. The next `step_check_convergence` call reads that event and sets `claimAdjudicationGate` = `false`, producing a `blockedStop` event with `blockedBy: [\"claimAdjudicationGate\"]` until a follow-up iteration rewrites the packet.\n462: \n463: ### Severity Transition Rules\n464: \n465: - **P2 → P1**: confirmed exploitable impact or spec violation with direct evidence\n466: - **P1 → P0**: demonstrated data loss, security breach, or hard-gate failure\n467: - **Downgrade**: requires explicit counterevidence or a confirmed alternative explanation\n468: - Every transition is recorded in the packet's `transitions` array and mirrored into the finding registry's `transitions` field\n469: \n470: ---\n471: \n472: ## 10. FINDING REGISTRY\n473: \n474: Each finding is tracked with a unique identifier enabling deduplication, severity transitions, and status lifecycle.\n475: \n476: ### Schema\n477: \n478: ```json\n479: {\n480:   \"findingId\": \"F003\",\n481:   \"severity\": \"P1\",\n482:   \"category\": \"resource-map-coverage\",\n483:   \"status\": \"active\",\n484:   \"dimension\": \"traceability\",\n485:   \"title\": \"Applied target file missing from resource-map inventory\",\n486:   \"file\": \".skilled/commands/deep/assets/deep-review-auto.yaml\",\n487:   \"line\": 955,\n488:   \"firstSeen\": 2,\n489:   \"lastSeen\": 4,\n490:   \"transitions\": [\n491:     { \"iteration\": 2, \"from\": null, \"to\": \"P2\", \"reason\": \"Initial discovery\" },\n492:     { \"iteration\": 4, \"from\": \"P2\", \"to\": \"P1\", \"reason\": \"Confirmed real coverage gap against applied target inventory\" }\n493:   ]\n494: }\n495: ```\n496: \n497: | Field | Type | Description |\n498: |-------|------|-------------|\n499: | findingId | string | Sequential unique ID: `F001`, `F002`, ... |\n500: | severity | `\"P0\"` / `\"P1\"` / `\"P2\"` | Current severity |\n501: | category | `\"correctness\"` / `\"security\"` / `\"traceability\"` / `\"maintainability\"` / `\"resource-map-coverage\"` | Primary audit category for the finding, `resource-map-coverage` is reserved for implementation-vs-map coverage gaps |\n502: | status | `\"active\"` / `\"resolved\"` / `\"deferred\"` / `\"disproved\"` | Current status |\n503: | dimension | string | Primary dimension: correctness, security, traceability, maintainability |\n504: | title | string | Short description |\n505: | file | string | File path |\n506: | line | number | Line number (approximate) |\n507: | firstSeen / lastSeen | number | Iteration where first discovered / last referenced |\n508: | transitions | array | Severity and status change history |\n509: \n510: ### Status Lifecycle\n511: \n512: ```text\n513: [discovered] --> active --> resolved    (fixed or confirmed non-issue)\n514:                   |\n515:                   +--> deferred    (advisory, below threshold)\n516:                   |\n517:                   +--> disproved   (counterevidence invalidated)\n518: ```\n519: \n520: | Status | Counts Toward Verdict |\n521: |--------|----------------------|\n522: | active | Yes |\n523: | resolved | No |\n524: | deferred | No (listed in Deferred Items) |\n525: | disproved | No |\n526: \n527: ### Deduplication\n528: \n529: Same file + line range + root cause as an existing finding = **refinement**, not new. The existing findingId is updated. Refinements count at half weight (`refinementMultiplier: 0.5`) and are tracked via `findingsRefined` in JSONL.\n530: \n531: ### Cross-Reference Protocols\n532: \n533: | Protocol | Level | Applies To | Gate |\n534: |----------|-------|------------|------|\n535: | spec_code | core | all types | hard |\n536: | checklist_evidence | core | all types | hard |\n537: | skill_agent | overlay | skill | advisory |\n538: | agent_cross_runtime | overlay | agent | advisory |\n539: | feature_catalog_code | overlay | skill, spec-folder, track, files | advisory |\n540: | playbook_capability | overlay | skill, agent, spec-folder | advisory |\n541: \n542: Severity for `resource-map-coverage` findings is calibrated to the coverage-gate outcome:\n543: - `P2` when an untouched map entry is explicitly `expected-by-scope`\n544: - `P1` when an untouched or absent path represents a real coverage gap\n545: - `P0` only when the missing coverage masks a release-blocking correctness or security risk\n546: \n547: ### Quality Gates\n548: \n549: | Gate | Rule |\n550: |------|------|\n551: | Evidence | Every active finding backed by concrete file:line evidence |\n552: | Scope | Reviewed files and conclusions stay inside declared scope |\n553: | Coverage | Required dimensions and required protocols covered |\n554: \n555: All three gates must pass before STOP. Gate failure forces `verdict: \"FAIL\"` regardless of finding counts.\n556: \n557: ---\n558: \n559: ## 11. LEDGER VOCABULARY AND PROJECTION CEILING\n560: \n561: ### Registered vocabulary\n562: \n563: The canonical dotted stems for this mode live in `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/lib/deep-review-ledger-schema/deep-review-ledger-types.ts`:\n564: \n565: - `DeepReviewEventStems` — the registered stems the ledger accepts.\n566: - `DEEP_REVIEW_STEM_PRODUCERS` — one entry per stem recording whether a mechanical producer emits it today (`spoken`, with the producer files) or why nothing does (`reserved`).\n567: \n568: The registry is only honest while it matches the emitter surface. `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/check-ledger-stem-producers.cjs` scans the workflow assets and runtime scripts and fails (exit 2) when a registered stem has no producer, a spoken stem has no emitter, or a reserved stem is emitted anyway:\n569: \n570: ```bash\n571: node .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/check-ledger-stem-producers.cjs\n572: ```\n573: \n574: ### Which file is authoritative\n575: \n576: `deep-review-state.jsonl` is authoritative while the mode's authority record (`authority-deep-review.json`, state `legacy_authoritative`) names the legacy writer. Once the record moves to `new_authoritative_reversible` or `new_authoritative_final` with `selectedWriter: \"dark\"`, the ledger is authoritative and this file becomes a projection that the append gateway refreshes after each append.\n577: \n578: ### What a projection refresh can reproduce\n579: \n580: The projection folds only registered stems, and its `run_initialized` arm rebuilds a thin config row: `type`, `topic`, `maxIterations`, `generation`, `timestamp`. A pre-flip config row written by the workflow carries attribution the fold cannot rebuild — `mode`, `reviewTarget`, `reviewTargetType`, `reviewDimensions`, `resource_map_present`, `resource_map`, `sessionId`, `parentSessionId`, `lineageMode`, `continuedFromRun`, `convergenceThreshold`, `antiConvergence`, `stopPolicy`, `executor`, `createdAt`, `specFolder`.\n581: \n582: Because losing those keys silently would make the projection look complete while the operator's context is gone, a replace that would drop keys from an existing `type: \"config\"` first row is refused with `ATTRIBUTION_COLLAPSE` (invariant `no-attribution-loss-on-replace`) before any bytes are written. An operator who hits it either migrates the attribution into a registered `deep_review.run_initialized` payload or intentionally moves the legacy file aside to accept the loss."}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"path\":\".skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/references/state/state-format.md\"}"},"time":{"start":1794669414451,"end":1794669414789}}}}
