{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794669435919,"sessionID":"ses_e255ff46effe7EWyuOLOEwVdy1","part":{"partID":"prt_1daa259ba001gLTk9jeLqdgiai","sessionID":"ses_e255ff46effe7EWyuOLOEwVdy1","messageID":"msg_1daa226a1001q2FPwUWVXal0I4","type":"tool","id":"call_dc50c2b230094516a37a24ae","tool":"read","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"path":"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/doctor-docs-3/iterations/iteration-004.md"},"output":"Read file specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/doctor-docs-3/iterations/iteration-004.md, lines 1-72\n1: # Review Iteration 004\n2: \n3: ## Dispatcher\n4: \n5: - Lineage: `doctor-docs-3`, session `fanout-doctor-docs-3-1794593402980-zhrui5`, generation 1.\n6: - Mode: review, dimension `security`, budget profile `adjudicate`.\n7: - Operator review focus: pass-three narrow review of the doctor-docs files changed by the pass-two remediation commits, each change judged against its task line and its callers. This iteration addresses the focus by walking the callers of both changed check engines, re-reading the carried P1 against its counterevidence, and auditing the changed surfaces for execution, path or secret exposure.\n8: - Sources read: `doctor-setup.yaml:40,61`, `doctor-symlink-check.yaml:37,60`, `doctor-agents-md-check.yaml:34,54-58`, `doctor-agents-md-embed.yaml:48,74,110`, `doctor-agents-md-restore.yaml:42,62,95`, `doctor-agents-md-presentation.txt:71,268,284`, `hook-wiring-check.cjs:300-347`, `agents-md-check.cjs:1070-1080`, and the carried finding at `hook-wiring-check.cjs:264-269`.\n9: \n10: ## Files Reviewed\n11: \n12: - `.skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/hook-wiring-check.cjs:300-347` (caller surface: `main`, `inspect`, exports)\n13: - `.skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/agents-md-check.cjs:1040-1080` (export surface)\n14: - `.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-setup.yaml:40,61` (caller: delivery leg)\n15: - `.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-symlink-check.yaml:37,60` (caller: symlink route)\n16: - `.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-agents-md-check.yaml:34,54-58`\n17: - `.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-agents-md-embed.yaml:48,74,110`\n18: - `.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-agents-md-restore.yaml:42,62,95`\n19: \n20: ## Findings - New\n21: \n22: ### P0 Findings\n23: \n24: None.\n25: \n26: ### P1 Findings\n27: \n28: None new. The carried finding `DR3-P1-001` stays active: re-reading `hook-wiring-check.cjs:264-269` confirms that `NODE_FLAGS_WITHOUT_RUN.has(flag)` tests the whole token, so `--eval=0`, `-e\"1\"` and `-p\"1\"` never match, and the marker is then accepted as node's script word. The counterevidence searched is unchanged: no later re-test of the marker as an argument, and no test covers the attached spelling. Final severity stays P1 because the check's stated contract is to read the command the way a shell runs it, and the caller at `doctor-setup.yaml:61` turns the false `ok claude` into a PASS delivery leg.\n29: \n30: ### P2 Findings\n31: \n32: None.\n33: \n34: ## Traceability Checks\n35: \n36: | Protocol | Status | Evidence |\n37: |----------|--------|----------|\n38: | `spec_code` | pass | The caller surface matches the changed behavior: both doctor routes read the check's printed lines and its exit codes, and neither parses the internal flag tables. |\n39: | `checklist_evidence` | partial | CHK-FIX-005's matrix covers the space-separated forms only, which is the exact gap the carried P1 names; no checklist row claims the attached form. |\n40: | `feature_catalog_code` | pass | Closed in iteration 3. |\n41: | `playbook_capability` | pass | Closed in iteration 3. |\n42: \n43: ## Integration Evidence\n44: \n45: - `doctor-setup.yaml:61` maps exit 0 to PASS and a `hook-missing` line to DEGRADED, so the false `ok claude` has a named consumer and a user-visible status effect.\n46: - `doctor-symlink-check.yaml:60` maps exit 0 to an unchanged status and exit 1 to WARN, the second consumer of the same wrong result.\n47: - `hook-wiring-check.cjs` holds no `spawnSync`, `execSync` or `exec` call: it parses the settings JSON and never runs the command string, so the reader adds no execution surface.\n48: - `agents-md-check.cjs` exports `main` and its row helpers; the four doctor assets that call it read the printed rows and never parse the A10 detail's first number.\n49: \n50: ## Edge Cases\n51: \n52: - A `--root` that names another checkout is still read-only: `inspect` joins the constant runtime file names onto the root and reads them, with no write path.\n53: - The temporary-directory backup fallback is printed by the embed engine and consumed by the restore route as a path, not evaluated; no shell interpolation reaches it.\n54: - The changed docs name no credentials, tokens or environment values that would expose a secret; `SKILL_ADVISOR_DEBUG` was removed from the setup router rather than added.\n55: \n56: ## Confirmed-Clean Surfaces\n57: \n58: - No changed line in the doctor scripts executes, eval-loads or interpolates the shell command it reads.\n59: - The two check engines keep their exported surface (`main`, `eventPayload`), so every caller keeps working.\n60: - The A10 detail change has no machine parser outside its own test.\n61: \n62: ## Ruled Out\n63: \n64: - A security finding on the reader is ruled out: it treats the settings file as data and never spawns a process.\n65: - A caller regression from the A10 detail change is ruled out: the doctor assets render rows and read states, and no asset reads the detail's leading count.\n66: - A path-traversal finding on `--root` is ruled out: the joined names are constants from the runtime table, and the check only reads them.\n67: \n68: ## Next Focus\n69: \n70: - None: all four dimensions are covered, the convergence ratio is 0 for the last three iterations and the only open finding is the carried P1. Synthesis follows.\n71: \n72: Review verdict: CONDITIONAL","title":"read","metadata":{"metadata":{"truncated":false},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Read file specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/doctor-docs-3/iterations/iteration-004.md, lines 1-72\n1: # Review Iteration 004\n2: \n3: ## Dispatcher\n4: \n5: - Lineage: `doctor-docs-3`, session `fanout-doctor-docs-3-1794593402980-zhrui5`, generation 1.\n6: - Mode: review, dimension `security`, budget profile `adjudicate`.\n7: - Operator review focus: pass-three narrow review of the doctor-docs files changed by the pass-two remediation commits, each change judged against its task line and its callers. This iteration addresses the focus by walking the callers of both changed check engines, re-reading the carried P1 against its counterevidence, and auditing the changed surfaces for execution, path or secret exposure.\n8: - Sources read: `doctor-setup.yaml:40,61`, `doctor-symlink-check.yaml:37,60`, `doctor-agents-md-check.yaml:34,54-58`, `doctor-agents-md-embed.yaml:48,74,110`, `doctor-agents-md-restore.yaml:42,62,95`, `doctor-agents-md-presentation.txt:71,268,284`, `hook-wiring-check.cjs:300-347`, `agents-md-check.cjs:1070-1080`, and the carried finding at `hook-wiring-check.cjs:264-269`.\n9: \n10: ## Files Reviewed\n11: \n12: - `.skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/hook-wiring-check.cjs:300-347` (caller surface: `main`, `inspect`, exports)\n13: - `.skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/agents-md-check.cjs:1040-1080` (export surface)\n14: - `.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-setup.yaml:40,61` (caller: delivery leg)\n15: - `.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-symlink-check.yaml:37,60` (caller: symlink route)\n16: - `.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-agents-md-check.yaml:34,54-58`\n17: - `.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-agents-md-embed.yaml:48,74,110`\n18: - `.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-agents-md-restore.yaml:42,62,95`\n19: \n20: ## Findings - New\n21: \n22: ### P0 Findings\n23: \n24: None.\n25: \n26: ### P1 Findings\n27: \n28: None new. The carried finding `DR3-P1-001` stays active: re-reading `hook-wiring-check.cjs:264-269` confirms that `NODE_FLAGS_WITHOUT_RUN.has(flag)` tests the whole token, so `--eval=0`, `-e\"1\"` and `-p\"1\"` never match, and the marker is then accepted as node's script word. The counterevidence searched is unchanged: no later re-test of the marker as an argument, and no test covers the attached spelling. Final severity stays P1 because the check's stated contract is to read the command the way a shell runs it, and the caller at `doctor-setup.yaml:61` turns the false `ok claude` into a PASS delivery leg.\n29: \n30: ### P2 Findings\n31: \n32: None.\n33: \n34: ## Traceability Checks\n35: \n36: | Protocol | Status | Evidence |\n37: |----------|--------|----------|\n38: | `spec_code` | pass | The caller surface matches the changed behavior: both doctor routes read the check's printed lines and its exit codes, and neither parses the internal flag tables. |\n39: | `checklist_evidence` | partial | CHK-FIX-005's matrix covers the space-separated forms only, which is the exact gap the carried P1 names; no checklist row claims the attached form. |\n40: | `feature_catalog_code` | pass | Closed in iteration 3. |\n41: | `playbook_capability` | pass | Closed in iteration 3. |\n42: \n43: ## Integration Evidence\n44: \n45: - `doctor-setup.yaml:61` maps exit 0 to PASS and a `hook-missing` line to DEGRADED, so the false `ok claude` has a named consumer and a user-visible status effect.\n46: - `doctor-symlink-check.yaml:60` maps exit 0 to an unchanged status and exit 1 to WARN, the second consumer of the same wrong result.\n47: - `hook-wiring-check.cjs` holds no `spawnSync`, `execSync` or `exec` call: it parses the settings JSON and never runs the command string, so the reader adds no execution surface.\n48: - `agents-md-check.cjs` exports `main` and its row helpers; the four doctor assets that call it read the printed rows and never parse the A10 detail's first number.\n49: \n50: ## Edge Cases\n51: \n52: - A `--root` that names another checkout is still read-only: `inspect` joins the constant runtime file names onto the root and reads them, with no write path.\n53: - The temporary-directory backup fallback is printed by the embed engine and consumed by the restore route as a path, not evaluated; no shell interpolation reaches it.\n54: - The changed docs name no credentials, tokens or environment values that would expose a secret; `SKILL_ADVISOR_DEBUG` was removed from the setup router rather than added.\n55: \n56: ## Confirmed-Clean Surfaces\n57: \n58: - No changed line in the doctor scripts executes, eval-loads or interpolates the shell command it reads.\n59: - The two check engines keep their exported surface (`main`, `eventPayload`), so every caller keeps working.\n60: - The A10 detail change has no machine parser outside its own test.\n61: \n62: ## Ruled Out\n63: \n64: - A security finding on the reader is ruled out: it treats the settings file as data and never spawns a process.\n65: - A caller regression from the A10 detail change is ruled out: the doctor assets render rows and read states, and no asset reads the detail's leading count.\n66: - A path-traversal finding on `--root` is ruled out: the joined names are constants from the runtime table, and the check only reads them.\n67: \n68: ## Next Focus\n69: \n70: - None: all four dimensions are covered, the convergence ratio is 0 for the last three iterations and the only open finding is the carried P1. Synthesis follows.\n71: \n72: Review verdict: CONDITIONAL"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"path\":\"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/doctor-docs-3/iterations/iteration-004.md\"}"},"time":{"start":1794669435322,"end":1794669435919}}}}
