{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794669561365,"sessionID":"ses_e255ff46effe7EWyuOLOEwVdy1","part":{"partID":"prt_1daa444d10012DsYNGmQkvQODa","sessionID":"ses_e255ff46effe7EWyuOLOEwVdy1","messageID":"msg_1daa4215e001ZnMCmYyyLOgO06","type":"tool","id":"call_2b197054719147d89dbb0810","tool":"read","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"path":".skilled/commands/create/sk-skill.md"},"output":"Read file .skilled/commands/create/sk-skill.md, lines 1-72\n1: ---\n2: description: Create or update OpenCode skills via one unified command with operation routing. :auto/:confirm.\n3: argument-hint: \"<skill-name> [operation] [type] [--path <dir>] [--chained] [:auto|:confirm]\"\n4: allowed-tools: Read, Write, Edit, Bash, Glob, Grep, TodoWrite\n5: ---\n6: \n7: # /create:sk-skill Router\n8: \n9: This command is a thin router. It separates execution routing from user-facing presentation.\n10: \n11: ## 1. ROUTER CONTRACT\n12: \n13: Route /create:sk-skill to its presentation contract and workflow YAML for creating or updating OpenCode skills through the unified skill command.\n14: \n15: - Do not split behavior across legacy command definitions.\n16: - Do not edit workflow YAML while executing this command.\n17: \n18: ---\n19: \n20: ## 2. OWNED ASSETS\n21: \n22: | Purpose | Asset |\n23: |---------|-------|\n24: | Presentation contract | `.skilled/commands/create/assets/create-skill-presentation.txt` |\n25: | Auto workflow | `.skilled/commands/create/assets/create-skill-auto.yaml` |\n26: | Confirm workflow | `.skilled/commands/create/assets/create-skill-confirm.yaml` |\n27: \n28: ---\n29: \n30: ## 3. MODE ROUTING\n31: \n32: - If any referenced asset is missing, stop and report the missing path.\n33: - The YAML owns workflow behavior; the presentation Markdown owns user-visible wording and layout.\n34: \n35: 1. Read `.skilled/commands/create/assets/create-skill-presentation.txt`.\n36: 2. Run the presentation contract's Phase 0 verification and setup resolution.\n37: 3. Resolve operation from setup: `full-create`, `full-update`, `reference-only`, or `asset-only`.\n38: 4. Resolve execution mode from `$ARGUMENTS` or the setup answer: `:auto` or `:confirm`.\n39: 5. Load the workflow YAML bound to the resolved mode from the EXECUTION TARGETS table below.\n40: 6. Execute the selected YAML step by step and route to the resolved operation branch.\n41: 7. Use the presentation contract, not this router, for user prompts, setup/status dashboards, and final result display.\n42: \n43: ---\n44: \n45: ## 4. EXECUTION TARGETS\n46: \n47: | Mode | Target |\n48: |------|--------|\n49: | `:auto` | `.skilled/commands/create/assets/create-skill-auto.yaml` |\n50: | `:confirm` or omitted mode | `.skilled/commands/create/assets/create-skill-confirm.yaml` |\n51: \n52: ---\n53: \n54: ## 5. PRESENTATION BOUNDARY\n55: \n56: The following content lives only in `.skilled/commands/create/assets/create-skill-presentation.txt`:\n57: \n58: - Startup questions, Phase 0 verification, setup dashboard, operation display, status display, completion template, and next-step text.\n59: \n60: The router must not invent visible wording for those surfaces; it only resolves operation, execution mode, and workflow selection.\n61: \n62: ---\n63: \n64: ## 6. WORKFLOW SUMMARY\n65: \n66: The bound workflow YAML (`create-skill-auto.yaml` for `:auto`, `create-skill-confirm.yaml` for `:confirm` or an omitted mode) runs the unified skill workflow step by step after Phase 0 verification and setup resolution, then routes to the resolved `full-create`, `full-update`, `reference-only`, or `asset-only` operation branch to create or update OpenCode skills.\n67: `:auto` executes autonomously.\n68: `:confirm` runs the same steps as an interactive checkpointed workflow.\n69: All user-facing prompts, setup/status dashboards, and result display come from the presentation contract, not this router.\n70: \n71: Generated routing follows the routing canon: `SMART ROUTING` is 8 to 12 lines of plain prose, every generated skill and mode packet owns a sibling `ROUTER.md` inside its own folder, and that file holds the machine router under a final `## MACHINE ROUTER` heading. The `SKILL.md` links to its sibling router in relative markdown and carries no `## MACHINE ROUTER` section itself. For a hub, that sibling file is the root `ROUTER.md`.\n72: ","title":"read","metadata":{"metadata":{"truncated":false},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Read file .skilled/commands/create/sk-skill.md, lines 1-72\n1: ---\n2: description: Create or update OpenCode skills via one unified command with operation routing. :auto/:confirm.\n3: argument-hint: \"<skill-name> [operation] [type] [--path <dir>] [--chained] [:auto|:confirm]\"\n4: allowed-tools: Read, Write, Edit, Bash, Glob, Grep, TodoWrite\n5: ---\n6: \n7: # /create:sk-skill Router\n8: \n9: This command is a thin router. It separates execution routing from user-facing presentation.\n10: \n11: ## 1. ROUTER CONTRACT\n12: \n13: Route /create:sk-skill to its presentation contract and workflow YAML for creating or updating OpenCode skills through the unified skill command.\n14: \n15: - Do not split behavior across legacy command definitions.\n16: - Do not edit workflow YAML while executing this command.\n17: \n18: ---\n19: \n20: ## 2. OWNED ASSETS\n21: \n22: | Purpose | Asset |\n23: |---------|-------|\n24: | Presentation contract | `.skilled/commands/create/assets/create-skill-presentation.txt` |\n25: | Auto workflow | `.skilled/commands/create/assets/create-skill-auto.yaml` |\n26: | Confirm workflow | `.skilled/commands/create/assets/create-skill-confirm.yaml` |\n27: \n28: ---\n29: \n30: ## 3. MODE ROUTING\n31: \n32: - If any referenced asset is missing, stop and report the missing path.\n33: - The YAML owns workflow behavior; the presentation Markdown owns user-visible wording and layout.\n34: \n35: 1. Read `.skilled/commands/create/assets/create-skill-presentation.txt`.\n36: 2. Run the presentation contract's Phase 0 verification and setup resolution.\n37: 3. Resolve operation from setup: `full-create`, `full-update`, `reference-only`, or `asset-only`.\n38: 4. Resolve execution mode from `$ARGUMENTS` or the setup answer: `:auto` or `:confirm`.\n39: 5. Load the workflow YAML bound to the resolved mode from the EXECUTION TARGETS table below.\n40: 6. Execute the selected YAML step by step and route to the resolved operation branch.\n41: 7. Use the presentation contract, not this router, for user prompts, setup/status dashboards, and final result display.\n42: \n43: ---\n44: \n45: ## 4. EXECUTION TARGETS\n46: \n47: | Mode | Target |\n48: |------|--------|\n49: | `:auto` | `.skilled/commands/create/assets/create-skill-auto.yaml` |\n50: | `:confirm` or omitted mode | `.skilled/commands/create/assets/create-skill-confirm.yaml` |\n51: \n52: ---\n53: \n54: ## 5. PRESENTATION BOUNDARY\n55: \n56: The following content lives only in `.skilled/commands/create/assets/create-skill-presentation.txt`:\n57: \n58: - Startup questions, Phase 0 verification, setup dashboard, operation display, status display, completion template, and next-step text.\n59: \n60: The router must not invent visible wording for those surfaces; it only resolves operation, execution mode, and workflow selection.\n61: \n62: ---\n63: \n64: ## 6. WORKFLOW SUMMARY\n65: \n66: The bound workflow YAML (`create-skill-auto.yaml` for `:auto`, `create-skill-confirm.yaml` for `:confirm` or an omitted mode) runs the unified skill workflow step by step after Phase 0 verification and setup resolution, then routes to the resolved `full-create`, `full-update`, `reference-only`, or `asset-only` operation branch to create or update OpenCode skills.\n67: `:auto` executes autonomously.\n68: `:confirm` runs the same steps as an interactive checkpointed workflow.\n69: All user-facing prompts, setup/status dashboards, and result display come from the presentation contract, not this router.\n70: \n71: Generated routing follows the routing canon: `SMART ROUTING` is 8 to 12 lines of plain prose, every generated skill and mode packet owns a sibling `ROUTER.md` inside its own folder, and that file holds the machine router under a final `## MACHINE ROUTER` heading. The `SKILL.md` links to its sibling router in relative markdown and carries no `## MACHINE ROUTER` section itself. For a hub, that sibling file is the root `ROUTER.md`.\n72: "}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"path\":\".skilled/commands/create/sk-skill.md\"}"},"time":{"start":1794669561041,"end":1794669561365}}}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794669561416,"sessionID":"ses_e255ff46effe7EWyuOLOEwVdy1","part":{"partID":"prt_1daa440e30011loNSlh7jiGNmE","sessionID":"ses_e255ff46effe7EWyuOLOEwVdy1","messageID":"msg_1daa4215e001ZnMCmYyyLOgO06","type":"tool","id":"call_6a66898fe84d42f9bb7b7cbf","tool":"read","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"path":".skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/tests/hooks/gate-3-menu-parity.test.mjs"},"output":"Read file .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/tests/hooks/gate-3-menu-parity.test.mjs, lines 1-57\n1: // ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n2: // MODULE: Gate 3 Menu Parity Tests\n3: // ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n4: // Drift guard: every presentation and compiled contract that shows the Gate 3\n5: // spec-folder menu must carry the canonical option C wording from the shared\n6: // core, so a rewording of GATE_3_CHOICE_RELATED cannot leave a stale menu\n7: // behind. A failure names the file, the drifting line and the expected text.\n8: // Run with: node --test gate-3-menu-parity.test.mjs\n9: import { test } from 'node:test';\n10: import assert from 'node:assert/strict';\n11: import { readFileSync } from 'node:fs';\n12: import { join } from 'node:path';\n13: import { fileURLToPath } from 'node:url';\n14: \n15: import { GATE_3_CHOICE_RELATED } from '../../hooks/lib/spec-gate/spec-gate-core.mjs';\n16: \n17: // This suite sits six directories below the repository root.\n18: const REPO_ROOT = fileURLToPath(new URL('../../../../../../', import.meta.url));\n19: \n20: const GATE_3_MENU_FILES = [\n21:   '.skilled/commands/create/assets/create-agent-presentation.txt',\n22:   '.skilled/commands/create/assets/create-command-presentation.txt',\n23:   '.skilled/commands/create/assets/create-feature-catalog-presentation.txt',\n24:   '.skilled/commands/create/assets/create-manual-testing-playbook-presentation.txt',\n25:   '.skilled/commands/create/assets/create-skill-parent-presentation.txt',\n26:   '.skilled/commands/create/assets/create-skill-presentation.txt',\n27:   '.skilled/commands/deep/assets/deep-ai-council-presentation.txt',\n28:   '.skilled/commands/deep/assets/deep-research-presentation.txt',\n29:   '.skilled/commands/deep/assets/deep-review-presentation.txt',\n30:   '.skilled/commands/deep/assets/compiled/deep-ai-council.contract.markdown',\n31:   '.skilled/commands/deep/assets/compiled/deep-research.contract.markdown',\n32:   '.skilled/commands/deep/assets/compiled/deep-review.contract.markdown',\n33:   '.skilled/commands/speckit/assets/speckit-complete-presentation.txt',\n34:   '.skilled/commands/speckit/assets/speckit-implement.yaml',\n35:   '.skilled/commands/speckit/assets/speckit-plan-presentation.txt',\n36:   '.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/references/memory/trigger-config.md',\n37:   '.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/references/workflows/worked-examples.md',\n38: ];\n39: \n40: function findOptionCLine(content) {\n41:   const lines = content.split('\\n');\n42:   const index = lines.findIndex((line) => /\\bC\\)\\s*Related\\b/.test(line));\n43:   return index === -1 ? null : { number: index + 1, text: lines[index].trim() };\n44: }\n45: \n46: for (const file of GATE_3_MENU_FILES) {\n47:   test(`option C menu in ${file} matches GATE_3_CHOICE_RELATED`, () => {\n48:     const content = readFileSync(join(REPO_ROOT, file), 'utf8');\n49:     const found = findOptionCLine(content);\n50:     assert.ok(\n51:       found !== null && found.text.includes(GATE_3_CHOICE_RELATED),\n52:       `${file} has drifted from the canonical Gate 3 option C wording`\n53:         + (found ? ` (line ${found.number}): ${found.text}` : ' and has no \"C) Related\" menu line')\n54:         + `\\nExpected to contain: ${GATE_3_CHOICE_RELATED}`,\n55:     );\n56:   });\n57: }","title":"read","metadata":{"metadata":{"truncated":false},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Read file .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/tests/hooks/gate-3-menu-parity.test.mjs, lines 1-57\n1: // ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n2: // MODULE: Gate 3 Menu Parity Tests\n3: // ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n4: // Drift guard: every presentation and compiled contract that shows the Gate 3\n5: // spec-folder menu must carry the canonical option C wording from the shared\n6: // core, so a rewording of GATE_3_CHOICE_RELATED cannot leave a stale menu\n7: // behind. A failure names the file, the drifting line and the expected text.\n8: // Run with: node --test gate-3-menu-parity.test.mjs\n9: import { test } from 'node:test';\n10: import assert from 'node:assert/strict';\n11: import { readFileSync } from 'node:fs';\n12: import { join } from 'node:path';\n13: import { fileURLToPath } from 'node:url';\n14: \n15: import { GATE_3_CHOICE_RELATED } from '../../hooks/lib/spec-gate/spec-gate-core.mjs';\n16: \n17: // This suite sits six directories below the repository root.\n18: const REPO_ROOT = fileURLToPath(new URL('../../../../../../', import.meta.url));\n19: \n20: const GATE_3_MENU_FILES = [\n21:   '.skilled/commands/create/assets/create-agent-presentation.txt',\n22:   '.skilled/commands/create/assets/create-command-presentation.txt',\n23:   '.skilled/commands/create/assets/create-feature-catalog-presentation.txt',\n24:   '.skilled/commands/create/assets/create-manual-testing-playbook-presentation.txt',\n25:   '.skilled/commands/create/assets/create-skill-parent-presentation.txt',\n26:   '.skilled/commands/create/assets/create-skill-presentation.txt',\n27:   '.skilled/commands/deep/assets/deep-ai-council-presentation.txt',\n28:   '.skilled/commands/deep/assets/deep-research-presentation.txt',\n29:   '.skilled/commands/deep/assets/deep-review-presentation.txt',\n30:   '.skilled/commands/deep/assets/compiled/deep-ai-council.contract.markdown',\n31:   '.skilled/commands/deep/assets/compiled/deep-research.contract.markdown',\n32:   '.skilled/commands/deep/assets/compiled/deep-review.contract.markdown',\n33:   '.skilled/commands/speckit/assets/speckit-complete-presentation.txt',\n34:   '.skilled/commands/speckit/assets/speckit-implement.yaml',\n35:   '.skilled/commands/speckit/assets/speckit-plan-presentation.txt',\n36:   '.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/references/memory/trigger-config.md',\n37:   '.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/references/workflows/worked-examples.md',\n38: ];\n39: \n40: function findOptionCLine(content) {\n41:   const lines = content.split('\\n');\n42:   const index = lines.findIndex((line) => /\\bC\\)\\s*Related\\b/.test(line));\n43:   return index === -1 ? null : { number: index + 1, text: lines[index].trim() };\n44: }\n45: \n46: for (const file of GATE_3_MENU_FILES) {\n47:   test(`option C menu in ${file} matches GATE_3_CHOICE_RELATED`, () => {\n48:     const content = readFileSync(join(REPO_ROOT, file), 'utf8');\n49:     const found = findOptionCLine(content);\n50:     assert.ok(\n51:       found !== null && found.text.includes(GATE_3_CHOICE_RELATED),\n52:       `${file} has drifted from the canonical Gate 3 option C wording`\n53:         + (found ? ` (line ${found.number}): ${found.text}` : ' and has no \"C) Related\" menu line')\n54:         + `\\nExpected to contain: ${GATE_3_CHOICE_RELATED}`,\n55:     );\n56:   });\n57: }"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"path\":\".skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/tests/hooks/gate-3-menu-parity.test.mjs\"}"},"time":{"start":1794669560035,"end":1794669561416}}}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794669561459,"sessionID":"ses_e255ff46effe7EWyuOLOEwVdy1","part":{"partID":"prt_1daa4425a001NK6XliF1CA9Tje","sessionID":"ses_e255ff46effe7EWyuOLOEwVdy1","messageID":"msg_1daa4215e001ZnMCmYyyLOgO06","type":"tool","id":"call_34cb7a97312f43c0b95bc46f","tool":"read","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"limit":180,"offset":1,"path":".skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/doctor-helper-handoff.vitest.ts"},"output":"Read file .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/doctor-helper-handoff.vitest.ts, lines 1-133\n1: // ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n2: // MODULE: Doctor Helper Hand-off Tests\n3: // ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n4: // A doctor problem worded unlike any bridge phrase reaches /doctor:helper through the helper's\n5: // own ranker. These cases pin the cue tiers and the ranker bridge; the routing slice pins the\n6: // end-to-end ranking.\n7: \n8: import { mkdtempSync } from 'node:fs';\n9: import { tmpdir } from 'node:os';\n10: import { dirname, join } from 'node:path';\n11: import { fileURLToPath } from 'node:url';\n12: \n13: import { describe, expect, it } from 'vitest';\n14: \n15: import {\n16:   DOCTOR_HELPER_UNCUED_MIN_SCORE,\n17:   doctorProblemCue,\n18:   genericRepairCue,\n19:   matchDoctorProblem,\n20: } from '../lib/scorer/doctor-helper-handoff.js';\n21: import { findAdvisorWorkspaceRoot } from '../lib/utils/workspace-root.js';\n22: \n23: const HERE = dirname(fileURLToPath(import.meta.url));\n24: const WORKSPACE = findAdvisorWorkspaceRoot(HERE, { maxDepth: 14, sentinel: '.skilled' });\n25: \n26: describe('doctor problem cue', () => {\n27:   it('reads a wrong state or a health check as a strong cue', () => {\n28:     expect(doctorProblemCue('code mode mcp is not registered in my runtime')).toBe('strong');\n29:     expect(doctorProblemCue('my deep research run never converges')).toBe('strong');\n30:     expect(doctorProblemCue('the trigger index lookup returns nothing')).toBe('strong');\n31:     expect(doctorProblemCue('turn off one of the github actions workflows')).toBe('strong');\n32:   });\n33: \n34:   // A hook that does not fire is a broken state, not a bare problem word: the\n35:   // operator reports it in exactly this shape, and the cue is what lets the\n36:   // hand-off stand beside a passing skill.\n37:   it('reads a hook that does not fire as a strong cue', () => {\n38:     expect(doctorProblemCue('my hooks are not firing, what do I run')).toBe('strong');\n39:     expect(doctorProblemCue('the git hooks are not triggering on commit')).toBe('strong');\n40:   });\n41: \n42:   // A tool that never appears is the same wrong state as one that does not\n43:   // register, and the operator reports it in the negative rather than with a\n44:   // problem adjective.\n45:   it('reads a tool that does not show up as a strong cue', () => {\n46:     expect(doctorProblemCue('the deploy button is not showing up after the update')).toBe('strong');\n47:     expect(doctorProblemCue(\"my new agent isn't appearing in the picker\")).toBe('strong');\n48:     expect(doctorProblemCue(\"it doesn't appear to cover the routing case\")).toBeNull();\n49:     expect(doctorProblemCue(\"don't show up-to-date entries only\")).toBeNull();\n50:     expect(doctorProblemCue('the linter does not appear in the tool list')).toBe('strong');\n51:     expect(doctorProblemCue(\"don't show line numbers in the diff\")).toBeNull();\n52:     expect(doctorProblemCue('show me how the advisor ranks skills')).toBeNull();\n53:   });\n54: \n55:   it('reads a contraction typed with a curly apostrophe', () => {\n56:     expect(doctorProblemCue('Code Mode tools aren’t showing up in my session')).toBe('strong');\n57:     expect(doctorProblemCue('my new agent isn’t appearing in the picker')).toBe('strong');\n58:   });\n59: \n60:   // A loop that stopped converging reports the same wrong state in the past\n61:   // tense, which the \"never <verb>\" form does not cover.\n62:   it('reads a loop that stopped converging as a strong cue', () => {\n63:     expect(doctorProblemCue('my research loop stopped converging and I cannot see why')).toBe('strong');\n64:   });\n65: \n66:   it('reads a bare problem word as a weak cue', () => {\n67:     expect(doctorProblemCue('Fix the broken JSON example and revalidate the packet.')).toBe('weak');\n68:     expect(doctorProblemCue('my AGENTS.md is out of date with the template')).toBe('weak');\n69:   });\n70: \n71:   it('finds no cue in a plain request', () => {\n72:     expect(doctorProblemCue('Start a deep review loop over the packet docs.')).toBeNull();\n73:     expect(doctorProblemCue('my doctor update came in')).toBeNull();\n74:   });\n75: });\n76: \n77: describe('generic repair request cue', () => {\n78:   // A repair route asked for in these words names no problem the ranker knows,\n79:   // and the helper lists every route with its reason.\n80:   it('reads a request for a repair route as a doctor request', () => {\n81:     expect(genericRepairCue('I have a problem and want the right repair path suggested with reasons')).toBe(true);\n82:   });\n83: \n84:   // The same words in a remark about resolved work describe no open problem.\n85:   it('ignores the same words once the problem is fixed', () => {\n86:     expect(genericRepairCue('much appreciated, that fixed the problem completely')).toBe(false);\n87:   });\n88: });\n89: \n90: describe('doctor helper ranker bridge', () => {\n91:   it('returns the command the helper ranks first for a doctor problem', () => {\n92:     const match = matchDoctorProblem('my deep research run never converges', WORKSPACE);\n93:     expect(match?.command).toBe('/doctor:deep-loop');\n94:     expect(match?.score).toBeGreaterThanOrEqual(6);\n95:   });\n96: \n97:   // The manifest phrases are the whole reason this reaches a command: the ranker\n98:   // carries no synonym list of its own.\n99:   it('reaches the git route for hooks that stopped firing', () => {\n100:     const match = matchDoctorProblem('my hooks are not firing, what do I run', WORKSPACE);\n101:     expect(match?.command).toBe('/doctor:git');\n102:     expect(match?.score).toBeGreaterThanOrEqual(6);\n103:   });\n104: \n105:   // The ranker names the runnable with its subcommand, so a hand-off can offer\n106:   // the exact command that runs instead of the helper that lists it.\n107:   it('returns the ranked runnable with its subcommand', () => {\n108:     expect(matchDoctorProblem('confirm the AGENTS.md sections in this repo have not drifted', WORKSPACE)?.runnable).toBe('/doctor:agents-md check');\n109:     expect(matchDoctorProblem('show me every GitHub Actions workflow and whether each is enabled', WORKSPACE)?.runnable).toBe('/doctor:ci report');\n110:   });\n111: \n112:   it('returns null for a prompt the helper does not match', () => {\n113:     expect(matchDoctorProblem('write me a poem about cats', WORKSPACE)).toBeNull();\n114:   });\n115: \n116:   // The helper ranks on shared words, so a doctor route phrase built from\n117:   // everyday repair words pulls a code or release request onto a doctor command.\n118:   it('keeps a code repair request off the doctor commands', () => {\n119:     expect(matchDoctorProblem('tell me what to fix where the tests fail', WORKSPACE)).toBeNull();\n120:     expect(matchDoctorProblem('fix the failing tests', WORKSPACE)).toBeNull();\n121:   });\n122: \n123:   it('keeps a release notes request under the bar for a prompt with no problem cue', () => {\n124:     const prompt = 'summarize what changed in the newer release';\n125:     expect(doctorProblemCue(prompt)).toBeNull();\n126:     expect(matchDoctorProblem(prompt, WORKSPACE)?.score ?? 0).toBeLessThan(DOCTOR_HELPER_UNCUED_MIN_SCORE);\n127:     expect(matchDoctorProblem('what changed in the last release of our api', WORKSPACE)).toBeNull();\n128:   });\n129: \n130:   it('returns null when the workspace has no doctor helper', () => {\n131:     expect(matchDoctorProblem('my deep research run never converges', mkdtempSync(join(tmpdir(), 'no-doctor-')))).toBeNull();\n132:   });\n133: });","title":"read","metadata":{"metadata":{"truncated":false},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Read file .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/doctor-helper-handoff.vitest.ts, lines 1-133\n1: // ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n2: // MODULE: Doctor Helper Hand-off Tests\n3: // ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n4: // A doctor problem worded unlike any bridge phrase reaches /doctor:helper through the helper's\n5: // own ranker. These cases pin the cue tiers and the ranker bridge; the routing slice pins the\n6: // end-to-end ranking.\n7: \n8: import { mkdtempSync } from 'node:fs';\n9: import { tmpdir } from 'node:os';\n10: import { dirname, join } from 'node:path';\n11: import { fileURLToPath } from 'node:url';\n12: \n13: import { describe, expect, it } from 'vitest';\n14: \n15: import {\n16:   DOCTOR_HELPER_UNCUED_MIN_SCORE,\n17:   doctorProblemCue,\n18:   genericRepairCue,\n19:   matchDoctorProblem,\n20: } from '../lib/scorer/doctor-helper-handoff.js';\n21: import { findAdvisorWorkspaceRoot } from '../lib/utils/workspace-root.js';\n22: \n23: const HERE = dirname(fileURLToPath(import.meta.url));\n24: const WORKSPACE = findAdvisorWorkspaceRoot(HERE, { maxDepth: 14, sentinel: '.skilled' });\n25: \n26: describe('doctor problem cue', () => {\n27:   it('reads a wrong state or a health check as a strong cue', () => {\n28:     expect(doctorProblemCue('code mode mcp is not registered in my runtime')).toBe('strong');\n29:     expect(doctorProblemCue('my deep research run never converges')).toBe('strong');\n30:     expect(doctorProblemCue('the trigger index lookup returns nothing')).toBe('strong');\n31:     expect(doctorProblemCue('turn off one of the github actions workflows')).toBe('strong');\n32:   });\n33: \n34:   // A hook that does not fire is a broken state, not a bare problem word: the\n35:   // operator reports it in exactly this shape, and the cue is what lets the\n36:   // hand-off stand beside a passing skill.\n37:   it('reads a hook that does not fire as a strong cue', () => {\n38:     expect(doctorProblemCue('my hooks are not firing, what do I run')).toBe('strong');\n39:     expect(doctorProblemCue('the git hooks are not triggering on commit')).toBe('strong');\n40:   });\n41: \n42:   // A tool that never appears is the same wrong state as one that does not\n43:   // register, and the operator reports it in the negative rather than with a\n44:   // problem adjective.\n45:   it('reads a tool that does not show up as a strong cue', () => {\n46:     expect(doctorProblemCue('the deploy button is not showing up after the update')).toBe('strong');\n47:     expect(doctorProblemCue(\"my new agent isn't appearing in the picker\")).toBe('strong');\n48:     expect(doctorProblemCue(\"it doesn't appear to cover the routing case\")).toBeNull();\n49:     expect(doctorProblemCue(\"don't show up-to-date entries only\")).toBeNull();\n50:     expect(doctorProblemCue('the linter does not appear in the tool list')).toBe('strong');\n51:     expect(doctorProblemCue(\"don't show line numbers in the diff\")).toBeNull();\n52:     expect(doctorProblemCue('show me how the advisor ranks skills')).toBeNull();\n53:   });\n54: \n55:   it('reads a contraction typed with a curly apostrophe', () => {\n56:     expect(doctorProblemCue('Code Mode tools aren’t showing up in my session')).toBe('strong');\n57:     expect(doctorProblemCue('my new agent isn’t appearing in the picker')).toBe('strong');\n58:   });\n59: \n60:   // A loop that stopped converging reports the same wrong state in the past\n61:   // tense, which the \"never <verb>\" form does not cover.\n62:   it('reads a loop that stopped converging as a strong cue', () => {\n63:     expect(doctorProblemCue('my research loop stopped converging and I cannot see why')).toBe('strong');\n64:   });\n65: \n66:   it('reads a bare problem word as a weak cue', () => {\n67:     expect(doctorProblemCue('Fix the broken JSON example and revalidate the packet.')).toBe('weak');\n68:     expect(doctorProblemCue('my AGENTS.md is out of date with the template')).toBe('weak');\n69:   });\n70: \n71:   it('finds no cue in a plain request', () => {\n72:     expect(doctorProblemCue('Start a deep review loop over the packet docs.')).toBeNull();\n73:     expect(doctorProblemCue('my doctor update came in')).toBeNull();\n74:   });\n75: });\n76: \n77: describe('generic repair request cue', () => {\n78:   // A repair route asked for in these words names no problem the ranker knows,\n79:   // and the helper lists every route with its reason.\n80:   it('reads a request for a repair route as a doctor request', () => {\n81:     expect(genericRepairCue('I have a problem and want the right repair path suggested with reasons')).toBe(true);\n82:   });\n83: \n84:   // The same words in a remark about resolved work describe no open problem.\n85:   it('ignores the same words once the problem is fixed', () => {\n86:     expect(genericRepairCue('much appreciated, that fixed the problem completely')).toBe(false);\n87:   });\n88: });\n89: \n90: describe('doctor helper ranker bridge', () => {\n91:   it('returns the command the helper ranks first for a doctor problem', () => {\n92:     const match = matchDoctorProblem('my deep research run never converges', WORKSPACE);\n93:     expect(match?.command).toBe('/doctor:deep-loop');\n94:     expect(match?.score).toBeGreaterThanOrEqual(6);\n95:   });\n96: \n97:   // The manifest phrases are the whole reason this reaches a command: the ranker\n98:   // carries no synonym list of its own.\n99:   it('reaches the git route for hooks that stopped firing', () => {\n100:     const match = matchDoctorProblem('my hooks are not firing, what do I run', WORKSPACE);\n101:     expect(match?.command).toBe('/doctor:git');\n102:     expect(match?.score).toBeGreaterThanOrEqual(6);\n103:   });\n104: \n105:   // The ranker names the runnable with its subcommand, so a hand-off can offer\n106:   // the exact command that runs instead of the helper that lists it.\n107:   it('returns the ranked runnable with its subcommand', () => {\n108:     expect(matchDoctorProblem('confirm the AGENTS.md sections in this repo have not drifted', WORKSPACE)?.runnable).toBe('/doctor:agents-md check');\n109:     expect(matchDoctorProblem('show me every GitHub Actions workflow and whether each is enabled', WORKSPACE)?.runnable).toBe('/doctor:ci report');\n110:   });\n111: \n112:   it('returns null for a prompt the helper does not match', () => {\n113:     expect(matchDoctorProblem('write me a poem about cats', WORKSPACE)).toBeNull();\n114:   });\n115: \n116:   // The helper ranks on shared words, so a doctor route phrase built from\n117:   // everyday repair words pulls a code or release request onto a doctor command.\n118:   it('keeps a code repair request off the doctor commands', () => {\n119:     expect(matchDoctorProblem('tell me what to fix where the tests fail', WORKSPACE)).toBeNull();\n120:     expect(matchDoctorProblem('fix the failing tests', WORKSPACE)).toBeNull();\n121:   });\n122: \n123:   it('keeps a release notes request under the bar for a prompt with no problem cue', () => {\n124:     const prompt = 'summarize what changed in the newer release';\n125:     expect(doctorProblemCue(prompt)).toBeNull();\n126:     expect(matchDoctorProblem(prompt, WORKSPACE)?.score ?? 0).toBeLessThan(DOCTOR_HELPER_UNCUED_MIN_SCORE);\n127:     expect(matchDoctorProblem('what changed in the last release of our api', WORKSPACE)).toBeNull();\n128:   });\n129: \n130:   it('returns null when the workspace has no doctor helper', () => {\n131:     expect(matchDoctorProblem('my deep research run never converges', mkdtempSync(join(tmpdir(), 'no-doctor-')))).toBeNull();\n132:   });\n133: });"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"limit\":180,\"offset\":1,\"path\":\".skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/doctor-helper-handoff.vitest.ts\"}"},"time":{"start":1794669560410,"end":1794669561459}}}}
