{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794669574716,"sessionID":"ses_e255ff46effe7EWyuOLOEwVdy1","part":{"partID":"prt_1daa475c9001WVgAYxhtOq4BgA","sessionID":"ses_e255ff46effe7EWyuOLOEwVdy1","messageID":"msg_1daa454a0001bbKcFWt3ii130l","type":"tool","id":"call_338d1de0bc7f48b780f333dc","tool":"grep","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"path":".skilled/commands/doctor","pattern":"A11|shipped row","limit":80},"output":"Found 34 matches\n/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.skilled/commands/doctor/agents-md.md:\n  Line 61: | `--create-router` | `embed` | Create `REPO RULES.md` from the shipped rows when it is missing |\n\n\n/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-agents-md-check.yaml:\n  Line 38:   repo_rules_checker: \".skilled/skills/sk-doc/sk-create-repo-rule/scripts/check-repo-rules.cjs, started once by the engine for the A11 row\"\n\n  Line 58:     - \"A10 reports each runtime copy the manifest expects, A11 the REPO RULES.md rows through the repo-rules checker, and A12 the template purity of the shipped body. The three rows the engine must not invent belong to the tools this workflow never re-implements: the canary, the pointer sync and the repo-rules checker.\"\n\n\n/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.skilled/commands/doctor/_routes.yaml:\n  Line 543:     gate3_location: \"AGENTS.md (created when absent, replaced with the shipped sections plus the composed block), CLAUDE.md and .codex/AGENTS.md (folded into the block and removed, unless --keep-claude-md), .cursor/rules/repo-local.md (the generated mirror of a non-empty block) and REPO RULES.md (missing shipped rows appended, or the file created behind --create-router), with a copy of every touched path taken to the plan's backup folder, .skilled/output/doctor-agents-md/<first 16 characters of the plan digest>/ or the folder of that name under the operating system's tempor