ne 813: // shipped rows to the file is the only way to say which of them a consumer dropped, and a\n\n\n/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-agents-md-presentation.txt:\n  Line 71: The twelve rows are A1 install state, A2 sections present, A3 order and numbering, A4 section currency, A5 pins, A6 delivery budget, A7 repo-local block, A8 unmarked repo-unique content, A9 unmarked local edits, A10 runtime copies, A11 REPO RULES.md and A12 template purity. Read A1 first: it says which state the repository is in, and every other row is a detail of that state. A8 and A9 are the two rows that name a line somebody wrote, so quote them in full.\n\n  Line 267: | `A11` reports missing router rows | `/doctor:agents-md embed` adds the shipped rows that are missing and touches no other row |\n\n  Line 283: | The repository has no `REPO RULES.md` | `/doctor:agents-md embed --create-router` | The router is created from the shipped rows and the checker runs after it |\n\n\n/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/agents-md-embed.cjs:\n  Line 115:   '  --create-router            create REPO RULES.md from the shipped rows when it is missing',\n\n  Line 373:  * The router with the shipped rows it is missing, added at the end of each table.\n\n  Line 782:   // The router gains the shipped rows it is missing, or is created from them when asked.\n\n  Line 802:     notes.push(`router: no ${manifest.router_file}, so no repository rule can load; pass --create-router to create one from the shipped rows`);\n\n\n/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/tests/agents-md-check.test.cjs:\n  Line 58: const ROWS = ['A1', 'A2', 'A3', 'A4', 'A5', 'A6', 'A7', 'A8', 'A9', 'A10', 'A11', 'A12'];\n\n  Line 145: // or index row is absent would make A11 report a missing row rather than the shape a\n\n  Line 1