ds/doctor/_routes.yaml](../../commands/doctor/_routes.yaml)\n\n\n/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.skilled/manual-testing-playbook/doctor-commands/doctor-sk-code-pre-v4-checkout.md:\n  Line 101: - Route manifest: [.skilled/commands/doctor/_routes.yaml](../../commands/doctor/_routes.yaml)\n\n\n/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.skilled/manual-testing-playbook/doctor-commands/doctor-install.md:\n  Line 26: - Preconditions: The Skilled checkout on the current branch with `.skilled/commands/doctor/install.md`, `.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-install.yaml`, `.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-install-presentation.txt`, `.skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/symlink-engine.cjs` and `.skilled/commands/doctor/_routes.yaml` in place, plus a runtime that can execute `/doctor:install` with Bash access. Node and git available. A scratch target folder the operator can create under a temporary directory. No network access needed.\n\n  Line 28: - Expected signals: `list` prints the five steps of the presentation contract in order, each with its exact command, its class and its `Why:` line: `/doctor:symlink link --root <dir> --runtimes <list> --mode <shape>`, `/doctor:agents-md embed --root <dir>`, `/doctor:mcp install`, `/doctor:git setup` and `/doctor:setup`, with `<dir>`, `<list>` and `<shape>` left as they stand. It prints no build block and inspects nothing. The guided run prints `DOCTOR INSTALL — BUILDS`, `Source: <the checkout>`, `Spec Kit build: found at .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/dist` and `Advisor CLI: answers list-tools` on a checkout where both builds are present, and prints the four `npm` commands as step 0 when one is missing. It asks once, for the link shape and the instruction file only, because `--root` and `--runtimes` already answered the first two questions, and it takes `auto` and `embed`. It then prints `DOCTOR INSTALL — WHAT IS ALREADY THERE`, `Root: <the scratch path>` and the engine's entry lines verbatim, without re-sorting or re-wording them, which on an empty scratch folder with `--runtimes claude` reads `missing` for `.skilled`, `.claude` and `.mcp.json`. It prints the checklist under `DOCTOR INSTALL — <the scratch path>`, `Source:`, and one `Runtimes: claude   Link shape: auto   Instruction file: embed` line. Each of the five steps carries the class of the route that owns it, read from `_routes.yaml`: `mutates` for steps 1, 2 and 3 and `read-only` for steps 4 and 5. The fixed caveat line follows the steps word for word, then `DOCTOR INSTALL RESULT` with `Builds: both found`, `Steps: 5 printed, 3 of them write`, `Next: run step 1 from the Skilled checkout, then the rest in order` and `STATUS=OK STEPS=5`, and the presentation closes on `What would you like to do next?`.\n\n  Line 45: 1. Confirm the checkout assets exist: `.skilled/commands/doctor/install.md`, `.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-install.yaml`, `.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-install-presentation.txt`, `.skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/symlink-engine.cjs` and `.skilled/commands/doctor/_routes.yaml`. Record the checkout root and its `git status --porcelain` as the checkout baseline.\n\n  Line 67: 8. Read the class of each printed step from `.skilled/commands/doctor/_routes.yaml` and compare it with the class on the printed line: `link` under `/doctor:symlink` is `mutates`, `embed` under `/doctor:agents-md` is `mutates`, `install` under `/doctor:mcp` is `mutates`, `setup` under `/doctor:git` is `read-only`, and `setup` under `/doctor:setup` is `read-only`.\n\n  Line 79: The checklist prints under its header, with the runtime list, the link shape and the instruction file on one line. The five steps stay in order and each class matches the owning route in `_routes.yaml`, so steps 1 to 3 read `mutates` and steps 4 and 5 read `read-only`. The class is the route's own `mutating` value, never guessed, and a printed command with no route of its own would read `n/a`.\n\n  Line 93: - The class comparison from step 8 between each printed step and `_routes.yaml`.\n\n  Line 103: If the engine exits 2 with `ERROR:` while the guide checks the target, the root is absent, is the checkout, sits inside it or holds it, and the guide asks for question 1 again rather than guessing. If a step prints `n/a` as its class, that printed command has no route in `_routes.yaml`, and the command still works. If the build block reports a missing build, run the four `npm` commands the guide printed as step 0 from the checkout and rerun the guide, and read the missing build as a checkout condition rather than a guide failure. If the caveat line is missing or shortened, the run departed from the presentation contract, which fixes that line word for word. If the checklist prints a class other than the one in `_routes.yaml`, the run guessed a class instead of reading the route table. If the scratch folder or the checkout changed, the guide crossed its read-only boundary, which is a failure of the mutation class in `_routes.yaml`.\n\n  Line 114: - Route manifest: [.skilled/commands/doctor/_routes.yaml](../../commands/doctor/_routes.yaml)\n\n\n/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.skilled/manual-testing-playbook/doctor-commands/doctor-ci-toggle.md:\n  Line 94: - Route manifest: [.skilled/commands/doctor/_routes.yaml](../../commands/doctor/_routes.yaml)\n\n\n/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.skilled/manual-testing-playbook/doctor-commands/doctor-mcp-target-menu.md:\n  Line 84: - Route manifest: [.skilled/commands/doctor/_routes.yaml](../../commands/doctor/_routes.yaml)\n\n\n/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.skilled/manual-testing-playbook/doctor-commands/doctor-update-apply.md:\n  Line 96: - Route manifest: [.skilled/commands/doctor/_routes.yaml](../../commands/doctor/_routes.yaml)\n\n\n(Results are truncated: showing first 60 results. Consider using a more specific path or pattern.)","title":"grep","metadata":{"metadata":{"matches":60,"truncated":true},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Found 60 matches\n/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.skilled/changelog/skilled/v3+/v3.4.1.0.md:\n  Line 368: Ten `/doctor:*` markdown commands collapsed to three: `/doctor <target>`, `/doctor:mcp` and `/doctor:update`. `/doctor:mcp` takes the `install` and `debug` sub-actions. The argv-positional router covers memory, causal-graph, code-graph, deep-loop, cocoindex, skill-advisor and skill-budget through `.opencode/commands/doctor/_routes.yaml`. `/doctor:update` is unchanged.\n\n  Line 401: - **Repoint.** Invoke `/doctor:memory`, `/doctor:causal-graph`, `/doctor:code-graph`, `/doctor:deep-loop`, `/doctor:cocoindex`, `/doctor:skill-advisor` and `/doctor:skill-budget` as `/doctor <target>`. For example, `/doctor:memory --dry-run` becomes `/doctor memory --dry-run`, and `/doctor:causal-graph --confidence-threshold=0.8` becomes `/doctor causal-graph --confidence-threshold=0.8`. Skill Advisor lexical routing handles old-form prompts through target trigger phrases in `_routes.yaml`.\n\n\n/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.skilled/skills/sk-git/feature-catalog/workflow-playbooks/doctor-git-settings.md:\n  Line 48: | `.skilled/commands/doctor/_routes.yaml` | Manifest | The three routes and their mutation classes |\n\n\n/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.skilled/manual-testing-playbook/manual-testing-playbook.md:\n  Line 29: This playbook covers every `/doctor` command. Seventeen routers under `.skilled/commands/doctor/` each own a command: the router binds a target from `.skilled/commands/doctor/_routes.yaml`, loads that target's workflow YAML and renders through the command's presentation contract. A scenario tests what an operator sees when a target runs against a real repository: the plan a plan-fir