{"type":"step_start","timestamp":1794669587289,"sessionID":"ses_e255ff46effe7EWyuOLOEwVdy1","part":{"id":"prt_1daa4ab59001dudDp9Af73GF06","sessionID":"ses_e255ff46effe7EWyuOLOEwVdy1","messageID":"msg_1daa489db001Aseho3DlFTOeBL","type":"step-start","snapshot":"1c44de07400b99eda92a884088bc465aa0fb9a95"}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794669614544,"sessionID":"ses_e255ff46effe7EWyuOLOEwVdy1","part":{"partID":"prt_1daa510be001h35n8JMJ6uQgi2","sessionID":"ses_e255ff46effe7EWyuOLOEwVdy1","messageID":"msg_1daa489db001Aseho3DlFTOeBL","type":"tool","id":"call_767929ebaa1a47bfad5eecef","tool":"read","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"limit":360,"path":".skilled/commands/doctor/_routes.yaml"},"output":"Read file .skilled/commands/doctor/_routes.yaml, lines 1-360\n1: # ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n2: # DOCTOR ROUTER — CANONICAL ROUTE MANIFEST\n3: # ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n4: # Source of truth for the routed doctor commands. Each route names the command\n5: # that owns it, so one manifest serves every router. The list below is every one of\n6: # the 17 router files in this folder, in no particular order:\n7: #   /doctor:speckit         .skilled/commands/doctor/speckit.md\n8: #   /doctor:skill-advisor   .skilled/commands/doctor/skill-advisor.md\n9: #   /doctor:deep-loop       .skilled/commands/doctor/deep-loop.md\n10: #   /doctor:runtime-mirrors .skilled/commands/doctor/runtime-mirrors.md\n11: #   /doctor:sk-code         .skilled/commands/doctor/sk-code.md\n12: #   /doctor:git             .skilled/commands/doctor/git.md\n13: #   /doctor:ci              .skilled/commands/doctor/ci.md\n14: #   /doctor:sk-skill        .skilled/commands/doctor/sk-skill.md\n15: #   /doctor:agents-md       .skilled/commands/doctor/agents-md.md\n16: #   /doctor:setup           .skilled/commands/doctor/setup.md\n17: #   /doctor:helper          .skilled/commands/doctor/helper.md\n18: #   /doctor:env             .skilled/commands/doctor/env.md\n19: #   /doctor:update          .skilled/commands/doctor/update.md\n20: #   /doctor:mcp             .skilled/commands/doctor/mcp.md\n21: #   /doctor:symlink         .skilled/commands/doctor/symlink.md\n22: #   /doctor:install         .skilled/commands/doctor/install.md\n23: #   /doctor:overlay         .skilled/commands/doctor/overlay.md\n24: # A command that owns one route needs no positional target.\n25: # Validated by: .skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/route-validate.sh\n26: # Consumed by: .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/command-bridges/derive-command-bridges.cjs\n27: #   turns every route, every standalone command and every mcp_subroutes\n28: #   entry into one advisor command bridge, copies its trigger_phrases into\n29: #   the TypeScript scorer and its runnable command into the Python slash\n30: #   markers and the brief's lookup. A bridge routes only once\n31: #   scoring-compatibility.json beside the deriver activates it. Doctor\n32: #   dispatch itself stays argv-driven (see each router).\n33: #\n34: # Schema (per route):\n35: #   command:          string — the doctor command that owns the route\n36: #   target:           string — positional name the user types\n37: #   yaml:             string — YAML asset filename in assets/\n38: #   setup_vars:       list   — variables the router resolves and passes to YAML\n39: #   allowed_flags:    list   — per-target flag schema (target-first parsing)\n40: #   mutating:         enum   — read-only | add-only | mutates\n41: #   gate3_location:   string — concrete mutation target (or \"n/a\" for read-only)\n42: #   write_scope:      enum   — optional; spec-folder marks an add-only route whose every write lands in the bound spec folder\n43: #   mcp_tools:        list   — subset of router's frontmatter allowed-tools union\n44: #   trigger_phrases:  list   — diagnostic routing phrases for this target, three or\n45: #                              more words each; the bridge deriver copies them\n46: #                              into the advisor (see \"Consumed by\" above)\n47: #   default_target:   bool   — optional; true marks the read-only target a bare typed command\n48: #                              should suggest (the router's no-token target, or its read-only\n49: #                              entry point), so /doctor:ci alone also reaches this route's\n50: #                              advisor bridge. At most one per command, only on a command with\n51: #                              several targets, and never on a mutating route.\n52: #   lead_phrases:     list   — optional subset of trigger_phrases that puts this bridge ahead of a passing skill when the prompt contains the phrase. Use it only where the doctor command must lead the skill.\n53: #\n54: # Skill-advisor recommendation tools are registered through system-skill-advisor.\n55: # To add a new target:\n56: #   1. Append the route here with its owning command and trigger_phrases of three or more words. Add lead_phrases only for a phrase where the doctor command must rank above a passing skill.\n57: #   2. List the target in that command's router and presentation, and add its row to the /doctor:setup target list in .skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-setup-presentation.txt.\n58: #   3. To let the advisor suggest it, add its activation entry to both the \"typescript\" and \"python\" lists in .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/command-bridges/scoring-compatibility.json. A bridge without one stays inactive.\n59: #   4. Rerun node .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/command-bridges/derive-command-bridges.cjs, then bash .skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/route-validate.sh and node .skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/doctor-phrase-reach.cjs.\n60: #   5. /doctor:helper needs no edit: it ranks this manifest at run time, and its contract test fails until the new route is reachable and listed in the /doctor:setup target list.\n61: # To remove a target: delete the route AND its corresponding assets/doctor-<target>.yaml.\n62: # ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n63: schema_version: 1\n64: routes:\n65:   - command: /doctor:speckit\n66:     target: speckit-retrieval\n67:     yaml: doctor-speckit-retrieval.yaml\n68:     setup_vars: [execution_mode, intent]\n69:     allowed_flags: []\n70:     mutating: add-only\n71:     write_scope: spec-folder\n72:     gate3_location: \"<packet_scratch>/doctor-speckit-retrieval-report.<timestamp>.md + <packet_scratch>/doctor-speckit-retrieval-state.<timestamp>.json + <packet_scratch>/doctor-speckit-retrieval-moved.<timestamp>.txt\"\n73:     mcp_tools: []   # file-and-script diagnostic; no MCP calls and no background service\n74:     script_invocations:\n75:       - 'node .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/retrieval/generate-trigger-index.mjs --check --json  # the staleness verdict: exit 0 = fresh, 1 = stale documents named, 2+ = unreadable index; writes nothing'\n76:       - 'node .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/retrieval/lookup-trigger-index.mjs --json -- \"resume work session context\"  # index present AND lookup runs: exit 0 = hits, 1 = clean no-hit, 2+ = missing or unreadable index, reported with stderr and never as a no-hit'\n77:       - \"rg --no-config --hidden --files-with-matches --max-count 1 --fixed-strings --ignore-case --glob '*.md' --glob '!**/z_archive/**' --glob '!**/node_modules/**' --glob '!**/.git/**' --glob '!**/scratch/**' -- 'trigger index generator' specs .skilled  # the section 2.2 recipe, flags verbatim\"\n78:       - 'node .skilled/skills/sk-doc/shared/scripts/cite-drift-scan.mjs --corpus <all|skills> --moved  # the citation-drift census, run only when the operator picks a scope at the citation_drift_scope gate; zero model calls, writes nothing, exit 2 = bad invocation or unreadable redirect table'\n79:     trigger_phrases:\n80:       - \"trigger index drift\"\n81:       - \"trigger index lookup fails\"\n82:       - \"retrieval conventions doctor\"\n83:       - \"ripgrep recipe check\"\n84:       - \"citation drift summary\"\n85:       - \"is the trigger index fresh\"\n86:       - \"spec search never finds anything\"\n87:       - \"search does not find terms we know are indexed\"\n88:       - \"spec search is broken even for indexed terms\"\n89:       - \"our spec lookup finds nothing\"\n90:       - \"indexed terms are not found by spec search\"\n91: \n92:   - command: /doctor:deep-loop\n93:     target: deep-loop\n94:     yaml: doctor-deep-loop.yaml\n95:     setup_vars: [execution_mode, intent, scope]\n96:     allowed_flags: [\"--scope=research|review|council|both|all\"]\n97:     mutating: add-only\n98:     write_scope: spec-folder\n99:     gate3_location: \"<active-spec-folder>/scratch/doctor-deep-loop-state.<timestamp>.json\"\n100:     mcp_tools: []\n101:     script_invocations:\n102:       - 'node .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/status.cjs --spec-folder \"{spec_folder}\" --loop-type \"{loop_type}\" --session-id \"{session_id}\" --read-only'\n103:       - 'node .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/query.cjs --spec-folder \"{spec_folder}\" --loop-type \"{loop_type}\" --session-id \"{session_id}\" --query-type \"{query_type}\" --limit 50 --read-only'\n104:       - 'node .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/convergence.cjs --spec-folder \"{spec_folder}\" --loop-type \"{loop_type}\" --session-id \"{session_id}\" --iteration \"{latest_iteration}\" --read-only'\n105:       - 'node .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/rules/check-source-tags-helper.mjs \"{spec_folder}\"  # [SOURCE:] tag resolution per lineage; writes nothing, zero model calls'\n106:     trigger_phrases:\n107:       - \"deep-loop coverage graph check\"\n108:       - \"deep-loop graph empty or stale\"\n109:       - \"deep-research convergence drift\"\n110:       - \"deep-review iteration graph\"\n111:       - \"deep loop convergence check\"\n112: \n113:   - command: /doctor:skill-advisor\n114:     target: tune\n115:     yaml: doctor-skill-advisor-tune.yaml\n116:     setup_vars: [execution_mode, scope, skip_tests, dry_run]\n117:     allowed_flags: [\"--skip-tests\", \"--dry-run\", \"--scope=all|explicit|derived|lexical\"]\n118:     mutating: mutates\n119:     gate3_location: \".skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/scorer/lanes/explicit.ts + .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/scorer/lanes/lexical.ts + .skilled/skills/*/graph-metadata.json\"\n120:     cli_commands:\n121:       - 'node .skilled/bin/skill-advisor.cjs advisor_recommend --prompt \"<prompt>\" --format json --warm-only'\n122:       - 'node .skilled/bin/skill-advisor.cjs advisor_status --workspace-root \"$PWD\" --format json --warm-only'\n123:       - 'node .skilled/bin/skill-advisor.cjs advisor_validate --confirm-heavy-run true --format json'\n124:       - 'node .skilled/bin/skill-advisor.cjs advisor_rebuild --trusted --force true --format json'\n125:       - 'node .skilled/bin/skill-advisor.cjs skill_graph_scan --trusted --format json'\n126:       - 'node .skilled/bin/skill-advisor.cjs skill_graph_validate --format json --warm-only'\n127:       - 'node .skilled/bin/skill-advisor.cjs skill_graph_query --queryType <depends_on|dependents|enhances|enhanced_by|family_members|conflicts|transitive_path|hub_skills|orphans|subgraph> --format json'\n128:       - 'node .skilled/bin/skill-advisor.cjs skill_graph_status --format json --warm-only'\n129:     mcp_tools: []   # CLI front door only, no MCP calls\n130:     script_invocations:\n131:       - 'Warm-only: probe the existing system-skill-advisor IPC socket first. Only when it answers, run node .skilled/bin/skill-advisor.cjs skill_graph_status --format json --warm-only. The flag guarantees no daemon start. Exit 75 means backend unavailable and retryable.'\n132:     trigger_phrases:\n133:       - \"skill advisor scoring\"\n134:       - \"advisor recommendation tuning\"\n135:       - \"skill advisor recommends the wrong skill\"\n136: \n137:   - command: /doctor:skill-advisor\n138:     target: rebuild\n139:     yaml: doctor-skill-advisor-rebuild.yaml\n140:     setup_vars: [execution_mode, dry_run]\n141:     allowed_flags: [\"--dry-run\"]\n142:     mutating: mutates\n143:     gate3_location: \".skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/database/skill-graph.sqlite (backed up beside itself before the rebuild)\"\n144:     cli_commands:\n145:       - 'node .skilled/bin/skill-advisor.cjs advisor_status --workspace-root \"$PWD\" --format json --warm-only'\n146:       - 'node .skilled/bin/skill-advisor.cjs advisor_rebuild --trusted --force true --format json'\n147:       - 'node .skilled/bin/skill-advisor.cjs skill_graph_scan --trusted --format json'\n148:       - 'node .skilled/bin/skill-advisor.cjs skill_graph_validate --format json --warm-only'\n149:     mcp_tools: []   # CLI front door only, no MCP calls\n150:     trigger_phrases:\n151:       - \"skill advisor rebuild\"\n152:       - \"rebuild the skill graph database\"\n153:       - \"rerun the skill_graph scan\"\n154:       - \"new skill not appearing in advisor results\"\n155:       - \"advisor daemon is stale\"\n156: \n157:   - command: /doctor:skill-advisor\n158:     target: skill-budget\n159:     yaml: doctor-skill-budget.yaml\n160:     setup_vars: [execution_mode, json_output, top_n, fail_over, project_ceiling]\n161:     allowed_flags: [\"--json\", \"--top-n=N\", \"--fail-over=N\", \"--project-ceiling=N\"]\n162:     mutating: read-only\n163:     gate3_location: \"n/a (read-only audit; no spec folder required)\"\n164:     mcp_tools: []   # script-only audit; no MCP calls\n165:     script_invocations:\n166:       - 'python3 .skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/audit_descriptions.py --repo-root \"$PWD\"  # description-budget audit. The workflow adds --json, --top-n, --fail-over, and --project-ceiling from the resolved flags'\n167:       - 'Warm-only: probe the existing system-skill-advisor IPC socket first; only when it answers, run node .skilled/bin/skill-advisor.cjs advisor_status --workspace-root \"$PWD\" --format json --timeout-ms 500 --warm-only (the flag guarantees no daemon start; exit 75 = backend unavailable, retryable)'\n168:     trigger_phrases:\n169:       - \"skill budget audit\"\n170:       - \"description budget check\"\n171:       - \"skill char count drift\"\n172:       - \"frontmatter description trim\"\n173:       - \"skill description too long\"\n174:       - \"description longer than the limit\"\n175: \n176:   - command: /doctor:skill-advisor\n177:     target: parent-skill\n178:     yaml: doctor-parent-skill.yaml\n179:     setup_vars: [execution_mode, parent_skill_dir]\n180:     allowed_flags: [\"--dir=<path>\"]\n181:     mutating: read-only\n182:     gate3_location: \"n/a (read-only structural audit; inspects a parent skill's graph-metadata/registry and reports, no writes)\"\n183:     mcp_tools: []   # script-only structural audit; no MCP calls\n184:     script_invocations:\n185:       # The fleet class gate runs first: it starts from SKILL.md, so it is the only\n186:       # check that can report a metadata file a root never wrote. The per-hub audit\n187:       # then goes deep on the one directory the operator named.\n188:       - 'node .skilled/skills/sk-doc/sk-create-skill/scripts/ci-skill-root-metadata.cjs'\n189:       - 'node .skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/parent-skill-check.cjs \"{parent_skill_dir}\"'\n190:     trigger_phrases:\n191:       - \"parent skill structure audit\"\n192:       - \"nested mode packet check\"\n193:       - \"mode-registry drift guard\"\n194:       - \"single graph-metadata identity\"\n195:       - \"skill root metadata contract\"\n196:       - \"missing skill json files\"\n197: \n198:   - command: /doctor:skill-advisor\n199:     target: skill-graph-freshness\n200:     yaml: doctor-skill-graph-freshness.yaml\n201:     setup_vars: [execution_mode]\n202:     allowed_flags: []\n203:     mutating: read-only\n204:     gate3_location: \"n/a (read-only diagnostic; 3-way diffs the skill-graph representations and reports drift, writes nothing)\"\n205:     mcp_tools: []   # script-only read; no MCP calls\n206:     script_invocations:\n207:       - 'node .skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/skill-graph-freshness.cjs'\n208:     trigger_phrases:\n209:       - \"skill graph freshness\"\n210:       - \"skill-graph zombie ghost nodes\"\n211:       - \"compiled vs sqlite vs disk graph drift\"\n212:       - \"reindex staleness check\"\n213: \n214:   - command: /doctor:skill-advisor\n215:     target: router-reach\n216:     yaml: doctor-router-reach.yaml\n217:     setup_vars: [execution_mode, hub, concurrency]\n218:     allowed_flags: [\"--hub=<skill-id>\", \"--concurrency=<n>\"]\n219:     mutating: read-only\n220:     gate3_location: \"n/a (read-only routing diagnostic; probes the live advisor for every declared phrase and reports, writes nothing)\"\n221:     mcp_tools: []   # spawns the advisor CLI per phrase; no MCP calls\n222:     script_invocations:\n223:       - 'node .skilled/skills/sk-doc/sk-create-skill/scripts/ci-router-vocabulary-reach.cjs'\n224:       - 'node .skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/doctor-phrase-reach.cjs  # doctor bridges: every admitted manifest phrase reaches its /doctor:x bridge as the top pick or the second line; scores in process, writes nothing tracked (the freshness check may refresh a cached build record in the ignored dist folder)'\n225:     trigger_phrases:\n226:       - \"router reach check\"\n227:       - \"does a declared phrase reach its hub\"\n228:       - \"router vocabulary reach\"\n229:       - \"phrase reaches nobody\"\n230:       - \"routing residue allowlist\"\n231: \n232:   - command: /doctor:skill-advisor\n233:     target: embedder\n234:     yaml: doctor-skill-advisor-embedder.yaml\n235:     setup_vars: [execution_mode, dry_run]\n236:     allowed_flags: [\"--dry-run\"]\n237:     mutating: mutates\n238:     gate3_location: \"the advisor database .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/database/skill-graph.sqlite, through skill_graph_scan only, and the user's Ollama model store, one pulled copy of nomic-embed-text:v1.5\"\n239:     cli_commands:\n240:       - 'node .skilled/bin/skill-advisor.cjs advisor_status --workspace-root \"$PWD\" --include-semantic-health true --format json --warm-only'\n241:       - 'node .skilled/bin/skill-advisor.cjs skill_graph_scan --trusted --format json'\n242:     mcp_tools: []   # CLI front door only, no MCP calls\n243:     trigger_phrases:\n244:       - \"set up meaning matching\"\n245:       - \"install the local embedder\"\n246:       - \"ollama is not running for the advisor\"\n247:       - \"meaning matching for commands\"\n248:       - \"semantic lane is off\"\n249:       - \"embedder setup and cost\"\n250: \n251:   - command: /doctor:runtime-mirrors\n252:     target: runtime-mirrors\n253:     yaml: doctor-runtime-mirrors.yaml\n254:     setup_vars: [execution_mode]\n255:     allowed_flags: []\n256:     mutating: read-only\n257:     gate3_location: \"n/a (read-only mirror-parity diagnostic; every checker runs in its check-only form and writes nothing)\"\n258:     mcp_tools: []   # script-only mirror parity read; no MCP calls\n259:     script_invocations:\n260:       - 'node .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/runtime-mirrors/sync-runtime-mirrors.cjs --check'\n261:       - 'node .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/codex/sync-agents.cjs --check'\n262:       - 'node .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/codex/sync-prompts.cjs --check'\n263:       - 'node .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/pi/sync-agents-pi.cjs --check'\n264:       - 'node .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/pi/sync-prompts-pi.cjs --check'\n265:       - 'node .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/dsh/sync-skills-dsh.cjs --check  # n/a, not run, while .dsh/ is absent'\n266:       - 'node .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/dsh/sync-prompts-dsh.cjs --check  # n/a, not run, while .dsh/ is absent'\n267:       - 'node .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/dsh/sync-agents-dsh.cjs --check  # n/a, not run, while .dsh/ is absent'\n268:       - 'node .skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/agent-roster-mirror-check.cjs'\n269:       - 'node .skilled/bin/check-agent-mirror-sync.cjs --all'\n270:       - 'node .skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/command-catalog-mirror-check.cjs'\n271:       - 'node .skilled/bin/install-codex-hooks.mjs --check --allow-worktree'\n272:     trigger_phrases:\n273:       - \"runtime mirror drift\"\n274:       - \"agent command mirror parity\"\n275:       - \"command catalog drift\"\n276:       - \"cursor devin codex sync check\"\n277:       - \"discovery mirror out of sync\"\n278:       - \"runtime copies drift from source\"\n279:       - \"runtime prompts out of date after a pull\"\n280:       - \"check the runtime mirrors match skilled\"\n281:       - \"runtime mirrors match .skilled\"\n282: \n283:   - command: /doctor:sk-code\n284:     target: setup\n285:     default_target: true\n286:     yaml: doctor-sk-code-setup.yaml\n287:     setup_vars: [execution_mode, prompt]\n288:     allowed_flags: [\"--prompt=<text>\"]\n289:     mutating: read-only\n290:     gate3_location: \"n/a (read-only setup battery; runs each check in its check-only form and prints repair commands, writes nothing)\"\n291:     mcp_tools: []   # script-only battery; no MCP calls\n292:     script_invocations:\n293:       - 'node .skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/sk-code-setup-check.cjs  # the workflow adds --prompt=<text> when the operator passed one'\n294:     trigger_phrases:\n295:       - \"sk-code setup check\"\n296:       - \"verify my sk-code surface\"\n297:       - \"sk-code battery fails\"\n298:       - \"does my sk-code surface route\"\n299: \n300:   - command: /doctor:sk-code\n301:     target: quality\n302:     yaml: doctor-sk-code-quality.yaml\n303:     setup_vars: [execution_mode, dry_run]\n304:     allowed_flags: [\"--dry-run\"]\n305:     mutating: mutates\n306:     gate3_location: \".skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-quality/repository/quality.json, where init --apply creates it once and never overwrites it\"\n307:     mcp_tools: []   # script-only, no MCP calls\n308:     script_invocations:\n309:       - 'node .skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/sk-code-quality-config.cjs status --json'\n310:       - 'node .skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/sk-code-quality-config.cjs init --json  # a dry run, with --apply only after approval'\n311:       - 'node .skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/sk-code-quality-config.cjs check --json'\n312:     trigger_phrases:\n313:       - \"sk-code quality config\"\n314:       - \"create the quality config file\"\n315:       - \"quality json is missing\"\n316:       - \"which checks does the quality gate run\"\n317:       - \"add my lint command to the quality gate\"\n318: \n319:   - command: /doctor:git\n320:     target: hooks\n321:     yaml: doctor-git-hooks.yaml\n322:     setup_vars: [execution_mode, dry_run]\n323:     allowed_flags: [\"--dry-run\"]\n324:     mutating: mutates\n325:     gate3_location: \"git config speckit.hooks.<key> in the repository's local config or the operator's global config\"\n326:     mcp_tools: []   # script-only; no MCP calls\n327:     script_invocations:\n328:       - 'node .skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/git-hook-gates.cjs list --json'\n329:       - 'node .skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/git-hook-gates.cjs set <key> on|off --scope local|global --json  # a dry run; the workflow adds --apply only after the plan is approved'\n330:       - 'bash .skilled/scripts/install-git-hooks.sh --status'\n331:     trigger_phrases:\n332:       - \"turn off a git hook check\"\n333:       - \"disable comment hygiene gate\"\n334:       - \"pre-commit gate keeps blocking\"\n335:       - \"git hook settings\"\n336:     lead_phrases:\n337:       - \"disable comment hygiene gate\"\n338: \n339:   - command: /doctor:git\n340:     target: standards\n341:     yaml: doctor-git-standards.yaml\n342:     setup_vars: [execution_mode, dry_run]\n343:     allowed_flags: [\"--dry-run\"]\n344:     mutating: mutates\n345:     gate3_location: \".sk-git/ at the repository root (or the directory git config skgit.contractDir names); the shipped sk-git templates are never written\"\n346:     mcp_tools: []   # script-only; no MCP calls\n347:     script_invocations:\n348:       - 'node .skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/git-standards.cjs status --json'\n349:       - 'node .skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/git-standards.cjs init --json  # a dry run; --apply after approval'\n350:       - 'node .skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/git-standards.cjs set <kind> <dotted.path> <json-value> --json  # a dry run; --apply after approval'\n351:       - 'node .skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/git-standards.cjs disable <kind> --json  # a dry run; --apply after approval'\n352:       - 'node .skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/git-standards.cjs check --json'\n353:       - 'node .skilled/skills/sk-git/scripts/validate-message.mjs --explain'\n354:     trigger_phrases:\n355:       - \"change commit message rules\"\n356:       - \"allow longer commit subjects\"\n357:       - \"stop checking pr descriptions\"\n358:       - \"branch name pattern rules\"\n359:       - \"customize sk-git standards\"\n360: \n[Output truncated. Continue reading with offset: 361]","title":"read","metadata":{"metadata":{"truncated":true},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Read file .skilled/commands/doctor/_routes.yaml, lines 1-360\n1: # ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n2: # DOCTOR ROUTER — CANONICAL ROUTE MANIFEST\n3: # ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n4: # Source of truth for the routed doctor commands. Each route names the command\n5: # that owns it, so one manifest serves every router. The list below is every one of\n6: # the 17 router files in this folder, in no particular order:\n7: #   /doctor:speckit         .skilled/commands/doctor/speckit.md\n8: #   /doctor:skill-advisor   .skilled/commands/doctor/skill-advisor.md\n9: #   /doctor:deep-loop       .skilled/commands/doctor/deep-loop.md\n10: #   /doctor:runtime-mirrors .skilled/commands/doctor/runtime-mirrors.md\n11: #   /doctor:sk-code         .skilled/commands/doctor/sk-code.md\n12: #   /doctor:git             .skilled/commands/doctor/git.md\n13: #   /doctor:ci              .skilled/commands/doctor/ci.md\n14: #   /doctor:sk-skill        .skilled/commands/doctor/sk-skill.md\n15: #   /doctor:agents-md       .skilled/commands/doctor/agents-md.md\n16: #   /doctor:setup           .skilled/commands/doctor/setup.md\n17: #   /doctor:helper          .skilled/commands/doctor/helper.md\n18: #   /doctor:env             .skilled/commands/doctor/env.md\n19: #   /doctor:update          .skilled/commands/doctor/update.md\n20: #   /doctor:mcp             .skilled/commands/doctor/mcp.md\n21: #   /doctor:symlink         .skilled/commands/doctor/symlink.md\n22: #   /doctor:install         .skilled/commands/doctor/install.md\n23: #   /doctor:overlay         .skilled/commands/doctor/overlay.md\n24: # A command that owns one route needs no positional target.\n25: # Validated by: .skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/route-validate.sh\n26: # Consumed by: .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/command-bridges/derive-command-bridges.cjs\n27: #   turns every route, every standalone command and every mcp_subroutes\n28: #   entry into one advisor command bridge, copies its trigger_phrases into\n29: #   the TypeScript scorer and its runnable command into the Python slash\n30: #   markers and the brief's lookup. A bridge routes only once\n31: #   scoring-compatibility.json beside the deriver activates it. Doctor\n32: #   dispatch itself stays argv-driven (see each router).\n33: #\n34: # Schema (per route):\n35: #   command:          string — the doctor command that owns the route\n36: #   target:           string — positional name the user types\n37: #   yaml:             string — YAML asset filename in assets/\n38: #   setup_vars:       list   — variables the router resolves and passes to YAML\n39: #   allowed_flags:    list   — per-target flag schema (target-first parsing)\n40: #   mutating:         enum   — read-only | add-only | mutates\n41: #   gate3_location:   string — concrete mutation target (or \"n/a\" for read-only)\n42: #   write_scope:      enum   — optional; spec-folder marks an add-only route whose every write lands in the bound spec folder\n43: #   mcp_tools:        list   — subset of router's frontmatter allowed-tools union\n44: #   trigger_phrases:  list   — diagnostic routing phrases for this target, three or\n45: #                              more words each; the bridge deriver copies them\n46: #                              into the advisor (see \"Consumed by\" above)\n47: #   default_target:   bool   — optional; true marks the read-only target a bare typed command\n48: #                              should suggest (the router's no-token target, or its read-only\n49: #                              entry point), so /doctor:ci alone also reaches this route's\n50: #                              advisor bridge. At most one per command, only on a command with\n51: #                              several targets, and never on a mutating route.\n52: #   lead_phrases:     list   — optional subset of trigger_phrases that puts this bridge ahead of a passing skill when the prompt contains the phrase. Use it only where the doctor command must lead the skill.\n53: #\n54: # Skill-advisor recommendation tools are registered through system-skill-advisor.\n55: # To add a new target:\n56: #   1. Append the route here with its owning command and trigger_phrases of three or more words. Add lead_phrases only for a phrase where the doctor command must rank above a passing skill.\n57: #   2. List the target in that command's router and presentation, and add its row to the /doctor:setup target list in .skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-setup-presentation.txt.\n58: #   3. To let the advisor suggest it, add its activation entry to both the \"typescript\" and \"python\" lists in .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/command-bridges/scoring-compatibility.json. A bridge without one stays inactive.\n59: #   4. Rerun node .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/command-bridges/derive-command-bridges.cjs, then bash .skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/route-validate.sh and node .skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/doctor-phrase-reach.cjs.\n60: #   5. /doctor:helper needs no edit: it ranks this manifest at run time, and its contract test fails until the new route is reachable and listed in the /doctor:setup target list.\n61: # To remove a target: delete the route AND its corresponding assets/doctor-<target>.yaml.\n62: # ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n63: schema_version: 1\n64: routes:\n65:   - command: /doctor:speckit\n66:     target: speckit-retrieval\n67:     yaml: doctor-speckit-retrieval.yaml\n68:     setup_vars: [execution_mode, intent]\n69:     allowed_flags: []\n70:     mutating: add-only\n71:     write_scope: spec-folder\n72:     gate3_location: \"<packet_scratch>/doctor-speckit-retrieval-report.<timestamp>.md + <packet_scratch>/doctor-speckit-retrieval-state.<timestamp>.json + <packet_scratch>/doctor-speckit-retrieval-moved.<timestamp>.txt\"\n73:     mcp_tools: []   # file-and-script diagnostic; no MCP calls and no background service\n74:     script_invocations:\n75:       - 'node .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/retrieval/generate-trigger-index.mjs --check --json  # the staleness verdict: exit 0 = fresh, 1 = stale documents named, 2+ = unreadable index; writes nothing'\n76:       - 'node .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/retrieval/lookup-trigger-index.mjs --json -- \"resume work session context\"  # index present AND lookup runs: exit 0 = hits, 1 = clean no-hit, 2+ = missing or unreadable index, reported with stderr and never as a no-hit'\n77:       - \"rg --no-config --hidden --files-with-matches --max-count 1 --fixed-strings --ignore-case --glob '*.md' --glob '!**/z_archive/**' --glob '!**/node_modules/**' --glob '!**/.git/**' --glob '!**/scratch/**' -- 'trigger index generator' specs .skilled  # the section 2.2 recipe, flags verbatim\"\n78:       - 'node .skilled/skills/sk-doc/shared/scripts/cite-drift-scan.mjs --corpus <all|skills> --moved  # the citation-drift census, run only when the operator picks a scope at the citation_drift_scope gate; zero model calls, writes nothing, exit 2 = bad invocation or unreadable redirect table'\n79:     trigger_phrases:\n80:       - \"trigger index drift\"\n81:       - \"trigger index lookup fails\"\n82:       - \"retrieval conventions doctor\"\n83:       - \"ripgrep recipe check\"\n84:       - \"citation drift summary\"\n85:       - \"is the trigger index fresh\"\n86:       - \"spec search never finds anything\"\n87:       - \"search does not find terms we know are indexed\"\n88:       - \"spec search is broken even for indexed terms\"\n89:       - \"our spec lookup finds nothing\"\n90:       - \"indexed terms are not found by spec search\"\n91: \n92:   - command: /doctor:deep-loop\n93:     target: deep-loop\n94:     yaml: doctor-deep-loop.yaml\n95:     setup_vars: [execution_mode, intent, scope]\n96:     allowed_flags: [\"--scope=research|review|council|both|all\"]\n97:     mutating: add-only\n98:     write_scope: spec-folder\n99:     gate3_location: \"<active-spec-folder>/scratch/doctor-deep-loop-state.<timestamp>.json\"\n100:     mcp_tools: []\n101:     script_invocations:\n102:       - 'node .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/status.cjs --spec-folder \"{spec_folder}\" --loop-type \"{loop_type}\" --session-id \"{session_id}\" --read-only'\n103:       - 'node .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/query.cjs --spec-folder \"{spec_folder}\" --loop-type \"{loop_type}\" --session-id \"{session_id}\" --query-type \"{query_type}\" --limit 50 --read-only'\n104:       - 'node .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/convergence.cjs --spec-folder \"{spec_folder}\" --loop-type \"{loop_type}\" --session-id \"{session_id}\" --iteration \"{latest_iteration}\" --read-only'\n105:       - 'node .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/rules/check-source-tags-helper.mjs \"{spec_folder}\"  # [SOURCE:] tag resolution per lineage; writes nothing, zero model calls'\n106:     trigger_phrases:\n107:       - \"deep-loop coverage graph check\"\n108:       - \"deep-loop graph empty or stale\"\n109:       - \"deep-research convergence drift\"\n110:       - \"deep-review iteration graph\"\n111:       - \"deep loop convergence check\"\n112: \n113:   - command: /doctor:skill-advisor\n114:     target: tune\n115:     yaml: doctor-skill-advisor-tune.yaml\n116:     setup_vars: [execution_mode, scope, skip_tests, dry_run]\n117:     allowed_flags: [\"--skip-tests\", \"--dry-run\", \"--scope=all|explicit|derived|lexical\"]\n118:     mutating: mutates\n119:     gate3_location: \".skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/scorer/lanes/explicit.ts + .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/scorer/lanes/lexical.ts + .skilled/skills/*/graph-metadata.json\"\n120:     cli_commands:\n121:       - 'node .skilled/bin/skill-advisor.cjs advisor_recommend --prompt \"<prompt>\" --format json --warm-only'\n122:       - 'node .skilled/bin/skill-advisor.cjs advisor_status --workspace-root \"$PWD\" --format json --warm-only'\n123:       - 'node .skilled/bin/skill-advisor.cjs advisor_validate --confirm-heavy-run true --format json'\n124:       - 'node .skilled/bin/skill-advisor.cjs advisor_rebuild --trusted --force true --format json'\n125:       - 'node .skilled/bin/skill-advisor.cjs skill_graph_scan --trusted --format json'\n126:       - 'node .skilled/bin/skill-advisor.cjs skill_graph_validate --format json --warm-only'\n127:       - 'node .skilled/bin/skill-advisor.cjs skill_graph_query --queryType <depends_on|dependents|enhances|enhanced_by|family_members|conflicts|transitive_path|hub_skills|orphans|subgraph> --format json'\n128:       - 'node .skilled/bin/skill-advisor.cjs skill_graph_status --format json --warm-only'\n129:     mcp_tools: []   # CLI front door only, no MCP calls\n130:     script_invocations:\n131:       - 'Warm-only: probe the existing system-skill-advisor IPC socket first. Only when it answers, run node .skilled/bin/skill-advisor.cjs skill_graph_status --format json --warm-only. The flag guarantees no daemon start. Exit 75 means backend unavailable and retryable.'\n132:     trigger_phrases:\n133:       - \"skill advisor scoring\"\n134:       - \"advisor recommendation tuning\"\n135:       - \"skill advisor recommends the wrong skill\"\n136: \n137:   - command: /doctor:skill-advisor\n138:     target: rebuild\n139:     yaml: doctor-skill-advisor-rebuild.yaml\n140:     setup_vars: [execution_mode, dry_run]\n141:     allowed_flags: [\"--dry-run\"]\n142:     mutating: mutates\n143:     gate3_location: \".skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/database/skill-graph.sqlite (backed up beside itself before the rebuild)\"\n144:     cli_commands:\n145:       - 'node .skilled/bin/skill-advisor.cjs advisor_status --workspace-root \"$PWD\" --format json --warm-only'\n146:       - 'node .skilled/bin/skill-advisor.cjs advisor_rebuild --trusted --force true --format json'\n147:       - 'node .skilled/bin/skill-advisor.cjs skill_graph_scan --trusted --format json'\n148:       - 'node .skilled/bin/skill-advisor.cjs skill_graph_validate --format json --warm-only'\n149:     mcp_tools: []   # CLI front door only, no MCP calls\n150:     trigger_phrases:\n151:       - \"skill advisor rebuild\"\n152:       - \"rebuild the skill graph database\"\n153:       - \"rerun the skill_graph scan\"\n154:       - \"new skill not appearing in advisor results\"\n155:       - \"advisor daemon is stale\"\n156: \n157:   - command: /doctor:skill-advisor\n158:     target: skill-budget\n159:     yaml: doctor-skill-budget.yaml\n160:     setup_vars: [execution_mode, json_output, top_n, fail_over, project_ceiling]\n161:     allowed_flags: [\"--json\", \"--top-n=N\", \"--fail-over=N\", \"--project-ceiling=N\"]\n162:     mutating: read-only\n163:     gate3_location: \"n/a (read-only audit; no spec folder required)\"\n164:     mcp_tools: []   # script-only audit; no MCP calls\n165:     script_invocations:\n166:       - 'python3 .skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/audit_descriptions.py --repo-root \"$PWD\"  # description-budget audit. The workflow adds --json, --top-n, --fail-over, and --project-ceiling from the resolved flags'\n167:       - 'Warm-only: probe the existing system-skill-advisor IPC socket first; only when it answers, run node .skilled/bin/skill-advisor.cjs advisor_status --workspace-root \"$PWD\" --format json --timeout-ms 500 --warm-only (the flag guarantees no daemon start; exit 75 = backend unavailable, retryable)'\n168:     trigger_phrases:\n169:       - \"skill budget audit\"\n170:       - \"description budget check\"\n171:       - \"skill char count drift\"\n172:       - \"frontmatter description trim\"\n173:       - \"skill description too long\"\n174:       - \"description longer than the limit\"\n175: \n176:   - command: /doctor:skill-advisor\n177:     target: parent-skill\n178:     yaml: doctor-parent-skill.yaml\n179:     setup_vars: [execution_mode, parent_skill_dir]\n180:     allowed_flags: [\"--dir=<path>\"]\n181:     mutating: read-only\n182:     gate3_location: \"n/a (read-only structural audit; inspects a parent skill's graph-metadata/registry and reports, no writes)\"\n183:     mcp_tools: []   # script-only structural audit; no MCP calls\n184:     script_invocations:\n185:       # The fleet class gate runs first: it starts from SKILL.md, so it is the only\n186:       # check that can report a metadata file a root never wrote. The per-hub audit\n187:       # then goes deep on the one directory the operator named.\n188:       - 'node .skilled/skills/sk-doc/sk-create-skill/scripts/ci-skill-root-metadata.cjs'\n189:       - 'node .skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/parent-skill-check.cjs \"{parent_skill_dir}\"'\n190:     trigger_phrases:\n191:       - \"parent skill structure audit\"\n192:       - \"nested mode packet check\"\n193:       - \"mode-registry drift guard\"\n194:       - \"single graph-metadata identity\"\n195:       - \"skill root metadata contract\"\n196:       - \"missing skill json files\"\n197: \n198:   - command: /doctor:skill-advisor\n199:     target: skill-graph-freshness\n200:     yaml: doctor-skill-graph-freshness.yaml\n201:     setup_vars: [execution_mode]\n202:     allowed_flags: []\n203:     mutating: read-only\n204:     gate3_location: \"n/a (read-only diagnostic; 3-way diffs the skill-graph representations and reports drift, writes nothing)\"\n205:     mcp_tools: []   # script-only read; no MCP calls\n206:     script_invocations:\n207:       - 'node .skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/skill-graph-freshness.cjs'\n208:     trigger_phrases:\n209:       - \"skill graph freshness\"\n210:       - \"skill-graph zombie ghost nodes\"\n211:       - \"compiled vs sqlite vs disk graph drift\"\n212:       - \"reindex staleness check\"\n213: \n214:   - command: /doctor:skill-advisor\n215:     target: router-reach\n216:     yaml: doctor-router-reach.yaml\n217:     setup_vars: [execution_mode, hub, concurrency]\n218:     allowed_flags: [\"--hub=<skill-id>\", \"--concurrency=<n>\"]\n219:     mutating: read-only\n220:     gate3_location: \"n/a (read-only routing diagnostic; probes the live advisor for every declared phrase and reports, writes nothing)\"\n221:     mcp_tools: []   # spawns the advisor CLI per phrase; no MCP calls\n222:     script_invocations:\n223:       - 'node .skilled/skills/sk-doc/sk-create-skill/scripts/ci-router-vocabulary-reach.cjs'\n224:       - 'node .skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/doctor-phrase-reach.cjs  # doctor bridges: every admitted manifest phrase reaches its /doctor:x bridge as the top pick or the second line; scores in process, writes nothing tracked (the freshness check may refresh a cached build record in the ignored dist folder)'\n225:     trigger_phrases:\n226:       - \"router reach check\"\n227:       - \"does a declared phrase reach its hub\