{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794669733414,"sessionID":"ses_e255ff46effe7EWyuOLOEwVdy1","part":{"partID":"prt_1daa6e1370014QNMK6u3HWtGh4","sessionID":"ses_e255ff46effe7EWyuOLOEwVdy1","messageID":"msg_1daa67cb9001OqtPX6m9Q6YC7A","type":"tool","id":"call_762615c1bb4e4ec3898426f0","tool":"grep","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"limit":60,"path":".skilled/commands/create/assets/create-skill-confirm.yaml","pattern":"spec_choice|spec_path|Related|sub-track"},"output":"Found 13 matches\n/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.skilled/commands/create/assets/create-skill-confirm.yaml:\n  Line 110:   applies_when: \"spec_path resolves to an existing spec folder (Q3 choice A - Existing, or C - Related) that contains handover.md or _memory.continuity in implementation-summary.md; not applicable to a freshly created spec folder (Q3 choice B - New) or when spec_choice is D (Skip)\"\n\n  Line 114:       - \"Read {spec_path}/handover.md when present and recent\"\n\n  Line 115:       - \"Read the _memory.continuity frontmatter block in {spec_path}/implementation-summary.md\"\n\n  Line 117:       - \"Only for a still-missing named gap, run the packet-scoped context recipe from .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/references/retrieval/retrieval-conventions.md section 2.4 with {spec_path} as the search root\"\n\n  Line 120:     memory_choice_A: \"Load handover.md (if <24h old) plus _memory.continuity from implementation-summary.md in {spec_path}; sets memory_loaded: handover+continuity\"\n\n  Line 121:     memory_choice_B: \"Load canonical spec docs (tasks.md, plan.md, decision-record.md) in {spec_path} up to a recent cap (3 most recently modified); sets memory_loaded: spec-docs\"\n\n  Line 123:   when_to_skip: [\"New spec folder (spec_choice == B, Create new) with no prior context\", \"spec_choice == D (Skip documentation)\", \"User says 'skip context' or 'fresh start'\"]\n\n  Line 146:     spec_choice_required_for:\n\n  Line 151:     - spec_choice\n\n  Line 152:     - spec_path\n\n  Line 513:     condition: \"spec_path exists\"\n\n  Line 519:       command: \"node .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/dist/continuity/generate-context.js [spec_path]\"\n\n  Line 565:       - Spec path: [spec_path or none]\n","title":"grep","metadata":{"metadata":{"matches":13,"truncated":false},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Found 13 matches\n/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.skilled/commands/create/assets/create-skill-confirm.yaml:\n  Line 110:   applies_when: \"spec_path resolves to an existing spec folder (Q3 choice A - Existing, or C - Related) that contains handover.md or _memory.continuity in implementation-summary.md; not applicable to a freshly created spec folder (Q3 choice B - New) or when spec_choice is D (Skip)\"\n\n  Line 114:       - \"Read {spec_path}/handover.md when present and recent\"\n\n  Line 115:       - \"Read the _memory.continuity frontmatter block in {spec_path}/implementation-summary.md\"\n\n  Line 117:       - \"Only for a still-missing named gap, run the packet-scoped context recipe from .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/references/retrieval/retrieval-conventions.md section 2.4 with {spec_path} as the search root\"\n\n  Line 120:     memory_choice_A: \"Load handover.md (if <24h old) plus _memory.continuity from implementation-summary.md in {spec_path}; sets memory_loaded: handover+continuity\"\n\n  Line 121:     memory_choice_B: \"Load canonical spec docs (tasks.md, plan.md, decision-record.md) in {spec_path} up to a recent cap (3 most recently modified); sets memory_loaded: spec-docs\"\n\n  Line 123:   when_to_skip: [\"New spec folder (spec_choice == B, Create new) with no prior context\", \"spec_choice == D (Skip documentation)\", \"User says 'skip context' or 'fresh start'\"]\n\n  Line 146:     spec_choice_required_for:\n\n  Line 151:     - spec_choice\n\n  Line 152:     - spec_path\n\n  Line 513:     condition: \"spec_path exists\"\n\n  Line 519:       command: \"node .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/dist/continuity/generate-context.js [spec_path]\"\n\n  Line 565:       - Spec path: [spec_path or none]\n"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"limit\":60,\"path\":\".skilled/commands/create/assets/create-skill-confirm.yaml\",\"pattern\":\"spec_choice|spec_path|Related|sub-track\"}"},"time":{"start":1794669732151,"end":1794669733414}}}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794669733440,"sessionID":"ses_e255ff46effe7EWyuOLOEwVdy1","part":{"partID":"prt_1daa6e459001M6OOyjofLNkJYA","sessionID":"ses_e255ff46effe7EWyuOLOEwVdy1","messageID":"msg_1daa67cb9001OqtPX6m9Q6YC7A","type":"tool","id":"call_2f43da6b9473485aa89002bf","tool":"grep","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"limit":50,"path":".skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/references/structure","pattern":"sub-track|subtrack"},"output":"Found 22 matches\n/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/references/structure/folder-structure.md:\n  Line 99: A track may hold one optional level of named sub-tracks between itself and its packets:\n\n  Line 104: ├── <sub-track>/\n\n  Line 105: │   ├── 001-<slug>/                # numbering restarts inside the sub-track\n\n  Line 110: A sub-track is declared, not inferred. All of these hold:\n\n  Line 115: | `description.json` | `\"level\": \"sub-track\"` and `specFolder` set to `<track>/<sub-track>`. `specId` is not required: the description producers write only `specFolder`, and no reader derives a sub-track identity from `specId`. |\n\n  Line 116: | `graph-metadata.json` | Track-root shape: `packet_id` `<track>/<sub-track>`, `parent_id` the track, `children_ids` its immediate numbered packets |\n\n  Line 117: | Track registration | The sub-track id appears in the track's `graph-metadata.json` `children_ids` |\n\n  Line 119: Numbering continues per folder, so each sub-track numbers its own packets from `001`. One level is supported: a sub-track holds numbered packets, not another sub-track. A declared folder that contains `spec.md` gets the diagnostic `declared folder has spec.md and cannot be a sub-track`, and `create.sh` refuses it.\n\n  Line 121: A track's `children_ids` lists its direct numbered packets and its declared sub-tracks. A sub-track's `children_ids` lists only its own immediate numbered packets. A numbered phase parent counts as one entry, and its phases stay its own children.\n\n  Line 123: A sub-track has its own `z_archive/`. Any `z_` folder inside a track or sub-track is never a sub-track and is never discovered as content. A non-numbered folder without the declaration gets one diagnostic and is never promoted. A symlinked sub-track is skipped with one diagnostic in both the working-tree and the commit view. The sweep treats these diagnostics as advisory and does not change its exit code. `create.sh` uses sub-track diagnostics to explain invalid `--track` values and exits with status 1.\n\n  Line 127: A sub-track is a proposal the operator approves, never a move made silently. Propose one at two moments.\n\n  Line 129: **When a packet is created.** `create.sh` prints one advisory line to stderr when the track has grown into clusters, when the new packet fits no existing sub-track, or when it fits a different sub-track better than the one named. The line never blocks the scaffold. Ask the same question directly with:\n\n  Line 132: node .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/suggest-subtracks.mjs --track <track> --describe \"<what the packet is for>\"\n\n  Line 138: node .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/suggest-subtracks.mjs --track <track> > map.json\n\n  Line 141: For a flat track, the map names every live packet of the track exactly once, because a track holds either packets or sub-tracks and never both. The tool prints no map in three cases, each with one line and exit `0`: a track below the threshold, a track where no grouping is found, and a track that already has a declared sub-track.\n\n  Line 143: A track that already has a declared sub-track gets `track <track> is already grouped into sub-tracks; no map`, also when numbered packets still sit beside the sub-tracks. For such a track, ask where each packet fits with `--describe`, which prints `best fit: <track>/<sub-track>` or `none fits: propose a new sub-track in <track>`. Then write the map by hand, one `{ \"from\": \"<track>/NNN-slug\", \"to\": \"<track>/<sub-track>/NNN-slug\" }` entry for every packet still at the track level, and run it through `relocate.mjs --map`. The map must cover all of them, because `relocate.mjs` refuses a plan that leaves flat packets beside sub-tracks. A single remaining packet can move with `relocate.mjs --from <path> --to <path>`.\n\n  Line 145: Rename the candidate sub-track names when a clearer name exists, show the map to the operator, and apply the approved map with the relocation tool:\n\n  Line 152: `relocate.mjs` declares each new sub-track, moves and renumbers the packets and rewrites every store that records a packet path. Do not move a packet by hand.\n\n  Line 317: A declared sub-track archives into its own `z_archive/`, not the track's:\n\n  Line 418: ├── invoicing/                       # declared sub-track\n\n  Line 419: │   ├── description.json             # level: \"sub-track\"\n\n\n/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/references/structure/phase-definitions.md:\n  Line 72: A series parent groups changes to one artifact. Grouping a whole track's packets by theme is a sub-track instead, and [folder-structure.md](folder-structure.md) says when to propose one under \"When to Propose a Sub-Track\".\n","title":"grep","metadata":{"metadata":{"matches":22,"truncated":false},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Found 22 matches\n/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/references/structure/folder-structure.md:\n  Line 99: A track may hold one optional level of named sub-tracks between itself and its packets:\n\n  Line 104: ├── <sub-track>/\n\n  Line 105: │   ├── 001-<slug>/                # numbering restarts inside the sub-track\n\n  Line 110: A sub-track is declared, not inferred. All of these hold:\n\n  Line 115: | `description.json` | `\"level\": \"sub-track\"` and `specFolder` set to `<track>/<sub-track>`. `specId` is not required: the description producers write only `specFolder`, and no reader derives a sub-track identity from `specId`. |\n\n  Line 116: | `graph-metadata.json` | Track-root shape: `packet_id` `<track>/<sub-track>`, `parent_id` the track, `children_ids` its immediate numbered packets |\n\n  Line 117: | Track registration | The sub-track id appears in the track's `graph-metadata.json` `children_ids` |\n\n  Line 119: Numbering continues per folder, so each sub-track numbers its own packets from `001`. One level is supported: a sub-track holds numbered packets, not another sub-track. A declared folder that contains `spec.md` gets the diagnostic `declared folder has spec.md and cannot be a sub-track`, and `create.sh` refuses it.\n\n  Line 121: A track's `children_ids` lists its direct numbered packets and its declared sub-tracks. A sub-track's `children_ids` lists only its own immediate numbered packets. A numbered phase parent counts as one entry, and its phases stay its own children.\n\n  Line 123: A sub-track has its own `z_archive/`. Any `z_` folder inside a track or sub-track is never a sub-track and is never discovered as content. A non-numbered folder without the declaration gets one diagnostic and is never promoted. A symlinked sub-track is skipped with one diagnostic in both the working-tree and the commit view. The sweep treats these diagnostics as advisory and does not change its exit code. `create.sh` uses sub-track diagnostics to explain invalid `--track` values and exits with status 1.\n\n  Line 127: A sub-track is a proposal the operator approves, never a move made silently. Propose one at two moments.\n\n  Line 129: **When a packet is created.** `create.sh` prints one advisory line to stderr when the track has grown into clusters, when the new packet fits no existing sub-track, or when it fits a different sub-track better than the one named. The line never blocks the scaffold. Ask the same question directly with:\n\n  Line 132: node .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/suggest-subtracks.mjs --track <track> --describe \"<what the packet is for>\"\n\n  Line 138: node .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/suggest-subtracks.mjs --track <track> > map.json\n\n  Line 141: For a flat track, the map names every live packet of the track exactly once, because a track holds either packets or sub-tracks and never both. The tool prints no map in three cases, each with one line and exit `0`: a track below the threshold, a track where no grouping is found, and a track that already has a declared sub-track.\n\n  Line 143: A track that already has a declared sub-track gets `track <track> is already grouped into sub-tracks; no map`, also when numbered packets still sit beside the sub-tracks. For such a track, ask where each packet fits with `--describe`, which prints `best fit: <track>/<sub-track>` or `none fits: propose a new sub-track in <track>`. Then write the map by hand, one `{ \"from\": \"<track>/NNN-slug\", \"to\": \"<track>/<sub-track>/NNN-slug\" }` entry for every packet still at the track level, and run it through `relocate.mjs --map`. The map must cover all of them, because `relocate.mjs` refuses a plan that leaves flat packets beside sub-tracks. A single remaining packet can move with `relocate.mjs --from <path> --to <path>`.\n\n  Line 145: Rename the candidate sub-track names when a clearer name exists, show the map to the operator, and apply the approved map with the relocation tool:\n\n  Line 152: `relocate.mjs` declares each new sub-track, moves and renumbers the packets and rewrites every store that records a packet path. Do not move a packet by hand.\n\n  Line 317: A declared sub-track archives into its own `z_archive/`, not the track's:\n\n  Line 418: ├── invoicing/                       # declared sub-track\n\n  Line 419: │   ├── description.json             # level: \"sub-track\"\n\n\n/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/references/structure/phase-definitions.md:\n  Line 72: A series parent groups changes to one artifact. Grouping a whole track's packets by theme is a sub-track instead, and [folder-structure.md](folder-structure.md) says when to propose one under \"When to Propose a Sub-Track\".\n"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"limit\":50,\"path\":\".skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/references/structure\",\"pattern\":\"sub-track|subtrack\"}"},"time":{"start":1794669732953,"end":1794669733440}}}}
