{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794670137206,"sessionID":"ses_e255ff46effe7EWyuOLOEwVdy1","part":{"partID":"prt_1daad0a1b002er6n7EkgvgoqwY","sessionID":"ses_e255ff46effe7EWyuOLOEwVdy1","messageID":"msg_1daacf9bc0016Orhqe1luVLEmp","type":"tool","id":"chatcmpl-tool-884b5292492f7b6b","tool":"read","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"path":"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/doctor-docs-4/deep-review-strategy.md"},"output":"Read file specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/doctor-docs-4/deep-review-strategy.md, lines 1-146\n1: # Deep Review Strategy - doctor-docs pass four\n2: \n3: ## 1. OVERVIEW\n4: \n5: - Session `fanout-doctor-docs-4-1794669272137-9v23rz`, generation 1, lineage mode `new`.\n6: - Detached fan-out lineage for the `doctor-docs` area of command-surfacing review pass four.\n7: - Write surface is this lineage directory only. Review targets are read-only. The repository test suites are not run here: they write temp fixtures outside the lineage, and a single out-of-scope write fails the lineage.\n8: - Holdout hygiene: no `command-prompts.jsonl` or `holdout-prompts.jsonl` is opened; the only prompt material read is a `split: tune` row already materialized in a scratch artifact and the non-holdout tests that name prompts.\n9: \n10: ## 2. TOPIC\n11: \n12: Review the `doctor-docs` files changed since review pass three (`0cdc9fa3ef`, HEAD `400c90e158`) plus the shared docs that describe them:\n13: \n14: - `.skilled/commands/create/assets/create-skill-presentation.txt`\n15: - `.skilled/commands/doctor/_routes.yaml`\n16: - `.skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/agents-md-check.cjs`\n17: - `.skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/tests/agents-md-check.test.cjs`\n18: \n19: The diff is 4 files, +11/-9. The brief asks five questions: behaviour on claude, codex, opencode, pi, devin and dsh; whether a refusal, question or command mention can still attach or start a mutating command; whether the transcript scorer counts a load, followed step or offer that did not happen; holdout hygiene; and docs that disagree with code.\n20: \n21: <!-- ANCHOR:review-dimensions -->\n22: ## 3. REVIEW DIMENSIONS (remaining)\n23: - [ ] correctness\n24: - [ ] security\n25: - [ ] traceability\n26: - [ ] maintainability\n27: \n28: <!-- /ANCHOR:review-dimensions -->\n29: ## 4. NON-GOALS\n30: \n31: - No code fixes; findings only.\n32: - No review of files outside the `doctor-docs` area and the shared docs/context named in the scope.\n33: - No prompt-corpus reading, no holdout inspection, no transcript scoring beyond the test contracts already in the tree.\n34: - No re-litigation of the pass-three lineage's carried P1 on `hook-wiring-check.cjs`; that file is outside this pass's area.\n35: \n36: ## 5. STOP CONDITIONS\n37: \n38: - Hard cap: 3 iterations (`config.maxIterations`).\n39: - Convergence threshold 0.10 on the severity-weighted new-findings ratio.\n40: - Stop policy `convergence`; at the cap the stop reason is `maxIterationsReached`.\n41: - Stop early only on the legal-stop gates (dimension coverage + required traceability protocols + evidence/scope/coverage gates).\n42: \n43: <!-- ANCHOR:completed-dimensions -->\n44: ## 4. COMPLETED DIMENSIONS\n45: [None yet]\n46: \n47: <!-- /ANCHOR:completed-dimensions -->\n48: <!-- ANCHOR:running-findings -->\n49: ## 5. RUNNING FINDINGS\n50: - P0 (Blockers): 0\n51: - P1 (Required): 0\n52: - P2 (Suggestions): 0\n53: - Resolved: 0\n54: \n55: <!-- /ANCHOR:running-findings -->\n56: ## 8. WHAT WORKED\n57: \n58: [First iteration -- populated after iteration 1 completes]\n59: \n60: ## 9. WHAT FAILED\n61: \n62: [First iteration -- populated after iteration 1 completes]\n63: \n64: <!-- ANCHOR:exhausted-approaches -->\n65: ## 9. EXHAUSTED APPROACHES (do not retry)\n66: [No exhausted approach categories yet]\n67: \n68: <!-- /ANCHOR:exhausted-approaches -->\n69: ## 10A. SATURATED / SWEPT DIMENSIONS AND EXPANSION FRONTIER\n70: - Completed pivots: 0\n71: - Failed pivots: 0\n72: - Audited overrides: 0\n73: - Swept: none yet\n74: - Pivot lineage: none yet\n75: - Remaining frontier: none recorded\n76: \n77: ## 11. RULED OUT DIRECTIONS\n78: \n79: - A holdout-leak finding is ruled out so far: the changed files do not read either prompt corpus; `_routes.yaml` only declares trigger phrases, and the route derivation output was checked without opening a prompt row.\n80: - A cross-runtime branching defect in the changed presentation is ruled out so far: `create-skill-presentation.txt` is plain text read by every runtime, and the canonical Gate 3 constant it must match lives in one shared module.\n81: \n82: <!-- ANCHOR:next-focus -->\n83: ## 11. NEXT FOCUS\n84: correctness\n85: \n86: <!-- /ANCHOR:next-focus -->\n87: ## 13. KNOWN CONTEXT\n88: \n89: ### Bounded Context Snapshot\n90: \n91: - **Target pointers**: the four changed files above; the diff `0cdc9fa3ef..400c90e158` is +11/-9; the changed lines are `agents-md-check.cjs:798-809`, `agents-md-check.test.cjs:763-764`, `_routes.yaml:403-406,797-806`, and `create-skill-presentation.txt:89`.\n92: - **Behavior claims to verify**: A11 now names a malformed row in its detail when nothing is missing; the create Q3 option C matches the canonical `GATE_3_CHOICE_RELATED` constant; the removed `/doctor:setup` and `/doctor:update` phrases keep generic code-repair and release-note questions off those routes; the remaining phrases stay three or more words and still reach their derived bridges; the test suite's A11 malformed case pins the new detail.\n93: - **Reuse and conventions**: A11 states are PASS/FINDING/UNKNOWN/INFO; the doctor presentation owns the repair mapping; `_routes.yaml` is the source of truth for route phrases and mutation class, and `derive-command-bridges.cjs` copies them into `command-bridges.generated.json`; `GATE_3_CHOICE_RELATED` is the canonical Gate 3 option C; `review-core.md` owns P0/P1/P2 reach calibration.\n94: - **Prior context (read-only, outside this area)**: pass-three lineage `doctor-docs-3` carried P1 `DR3-P1-001` on `hook-wiring-check.cjs:264-269` (attached node flag spellings). That file is not in this pass's area; the carried finding is noted for continuity only.\n95: - **Review risks and gaps**: no `resource-map.md` in the packet; the reducer-owned DB and runtime mirror are not exercised; the repo suites are not run because their temp fixtures are outside the lineage write surface; no holdout row is inspected; the derived bridge file is checked as data, not regenerated.\n96: \n97: ## 14. CROSS-REFERENCE STATUS\n98: <!-- MACHINE-OWNED: START -->\n99: [Alignment checks completed across core and overlay protocols]\n100: \n101: | Protocol | Level | Status | Iteration | Notes |\n102: |----------|-------|--------|-----------|-------|\n103: | `spec_code` | core | [pending/pass/partial/fail/blocked] | [N] | [details] |\n104: | `checklist_evidence` | core | [pending/pass/partial/fail/blocked] | [N] | [details] |\n105: | `skill_agent` | overlay | [pending/pass/partial/fail/blocked/notApplicable] | [N] | [details] |\n106: | `agent_cross_runtime` | overlay | [pending/pass/partial/fail/blocked/notApplicable] | [N] | [details] |\n107: | `feature_catalog_code` | overlay | [pending/pass/partial/fail/blocked/notApplicable] | [N] | [details] |\n108: | `playbook_capability` | overlay | [pending/pass/partial/fail/blocked/notApplicable] | [N] | [details] |\n109: <!-- MACHINE-OWNED: END -->\n110: \n111: ## 15. FILES UNDER REVIEW\n112: <!-- MACHINE-OWNED: START -->\n113: | File | Dimensions Reviewed | Last Iteration | Findings | Status |\n114: |------|-------------------|----------------|----------|--------|\n115: | `.skilled/commands/create/assets/create-skill-presentation.txt` | pending | - | 0 | pending |\n116: | `.skilled/commands/doctor/_routes.yaml` | pending | - | 0 | pending |\n117: | `.skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/agents-md-check.cjs` | pending | - | 0 | pending |\n118: | `.skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/tests/agents-md-check.test.cjs` | pending | - | 0 | pending |\n119: | `.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-agents-md-presentation.txt` | pending | - | 0 | pending |\n120: | `.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-agents-md-check.yaml` | pending | - | 0 | pending |\n121: | `.skilled/commands/create/sk-skill.md` | pending | - | 0 | pending |\n122: | `.skilled/commands/create/assets/create-skill-auto.yaml` | pending | - | 0 | pending |\n123: | `.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/hooks/lib/spec-gate/spec-gate-core.mjs` | pending | - | 0 | pending |\n124: | `.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/tests/hooks/gate-3-menu-parity.test.mjs` | pending | - | 0 | pending |\n125: | `.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/references/structure/folder-structure.md` | pending | - | 0 | pending |\n126: | `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/scorer/doctor-helper-handoff.ts` | pending | - | 0 | pending |\n127: | `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/doctor-helper-handoff.vitest.ts` | pending | - | 0 | pending |\n128: | `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/command-bridges/command-bridges.generated.json` | pending | - | 0 | pending |\n129: <!-- MACHINE-OWNED: END -->\n130: \n131: ## 16. REVIEW BOUNDARIES\n132: <!-- MACHINE-OWNED: START -->\n133: - Max iterations: 3\n134: - Convergence threshold: 0.10\n135: - Rolling STOP threshold: 0.08\n136: - No-progress threshold: 0.05\n137: - Coverage stabilization passes required: 1\n138: - Session lineage: sessionId=fanout-doctor-docs-4-1794669272137-9v23rz, parentSessionId=null, generation=1, lineageMode=new\n139: - Findings registry: `deep-review-findings-registry.json`\n140: - Release-readiness states: in-progress | converged | release-blocking\n141: - Per-iteration budget: 12 tool calls, 10 minutes\n142: - Severity threshold: P2\n143: - Review target type: spec-folder (narrowed by `review-scope-4.txt` to the doctor-docs area)\n144: - Cross-reference checks: core=[spec_code, checklist_evidenc