{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794670422035,"sessionID":"ses_e255ff46effe7EWyuOLOEwVdy1","part":{"partID":"prt_1dab1569a002zH2AyznukCHluP","sessionID":"ses_e255ff46effe7EWyuOLOEwVdy1","messageID":"msg_1dab132ed001rAa90ALqoILGA6","type":"tool","id":"chatcmpl-tool-88404f240a431ba5","tool":"edit","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"path":"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/doctor-docs-4/deep-review-strategy.md","oldString":"## 8. WHAT WORKED\n\n[First iteration -- populated after iteration 1 completes]\n\n## 9. WHAT FAILED\n\n[First iteration -- populated after iteration 1 completes]","newString":"## 8. WHAT WORKED\n\n- Tracing the changed A11 detail to its two consumers (the presentation's repair table and the embed engine's router write) found the one actionable gap in an otherwise clean diff. (iteration 1)\n- Querying the derived `command-bridges.generated.json` as data, rather than reading a prompt corpus, proved all six removed phrases reached the advisor surface's removal. (iteration 1)\n- Comparing the create presentation line against `GATE_3_CHOICE_RELATED` and its parity test proved the canonical wording match without a runtime branch. (iteration 1)\n\n## 9. WHAT FAILED\n\n- The A11-specific troubleshooting row was assumed to cover every A11 finding; it covers missing rows only, so the malformed-row case has no named repair. Recorded as `DR4-P2-001`, not a failed approach. (iteration 1)"},"output":"Edited specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/doctor-docs-4/deep-review-strategy.md (1 replacement)","title":"edit","metadata":{"metadata":{"files":[{"file":"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/doctor-docs-4/deep-review-strategy.md","patch":"Index: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/doctor-docs-4/deep-review-strategy.md\n===================================================================\n--- specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/doctor-docs-4/deep-review-strategy.md\n+++ specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/doctor-docs-4/deep-review-strategy.md\n@@ -54,13 +54,15 @@\n \n <!-- /ANCHOR:running-findings -->\n ## 8. WHAT WORKED\n \n-[First iteration -- populated after iteration 1 completes]\n+- Tracing the changed A11 detail to its two consumers (the presentation's repair table and the embed engine's router write) found the one actionable gap in an otherwise clean diff. (iteration 1)\n+- Querying the derived `command-bridges.generated.json` as data, rather than reading a prompt corpus, proved all six removed phrases reached the advisor surface's removal. (iteration 1)\n+- Comparing the create presentation line against `GATE_3_CHOICE_RELATED` and its parity test proved the canonical wording match without a runtime branch. (iteration 1)\n \n ## 9. WHAT FAILED\n \n-[First iteration -- populated after iteration 1 completes]\n+- The A11-specific troubleshooting row was assumed to cover every A11 finding; it covers missing rows only, so the malformed-row case has no named repair. Recorded as `DR4-P2-001`, not a failed approach. (iteration 1)\n \n <!-- ANCHOR:exhausted-approaches -->\n ## 9. EXHAUSTED APPROACHES (do not retry)\n [No exhausted approach categories yet]\n","status":"modified","additions":4,"deletions":2}],"truncated":false},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Edited specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/doctor-docs-4/deep-review-strategy.md (1 replacement)"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"path\": \"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/doctor-docs-4/deep-review-strategy.md\", \"oldString\": \"## 8. WHAT WORKED\\n\\n[First iteration -- populated after iteration 1 completes]\\n\\n## 9. WHAT FAILED\\n\\n[First iteration -- populated after iteration 1 completes]\", \"newString\": \"## 8. WHAT WORKED\\n\\n- Tracing the changed A11 detail to its two consumers (the presentation's repair table and the embed engine's router write) found the one actionable gap in an otherwise clean diff. (iteration 1)\\n- Querying the derived `command-bridges.generated.json` as data, rather than reading a prompt corpus, proved all six removed phrases reached the advisor surface's removal. (iteration 1)\\n- Comparing the create presentation line against `GATE_3_CHOICE_RELATED` and its parity test proved the canonical wording match without a runtime branch. (iteration 1)\\n\\n## 9. WHAT FAILED\\n\\n- The A11-specific troubleshooting row was assumed to cover every A11 finding; it covers missing rows only, so the malformed-row case has no named repair. Recorded as `DR4-P2-001`, not a failed approach. (iteration 1)\"}"},"time":{"start":1794670417562,"end":1794670422035}}}}
