{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794670435338,"sessionID":"ses_e255ff46effe7EWyuOLOEwVdy1","part":{"partID":"prt_1dab189fa002r6ads2LSmfZ56N","sessionID":"ses_e255ff46effe7EWyuOLOEwVdy1","messageID":"msg_1dab17519001wUVDQhWjezWXCF","type":"tool","id":"chatcmpl-tool-adcf3667b6319a3a","tool":"edit","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"newString":"## 11. RULED OUT DIRECTIONS\n\n- A holdout-leak finding is ruled out so far: the changed files do not read either prompt corpus; `_routes.yaml` only declares trigger phrases, and the route derivation output was checked without opening a prompt row. (iteration 1)\n- A cross-runtime branching defect in the changed presentation is ruled out so far: `create-skill-presentation.txt` is plain text read by every runtime, and the canonical Gate 3 constant it must match lives in one shared module. (iteration 1)\n- A P0/P1 in the A11 count logic is ruled out: the count is derived from the same arrays that build the printed lines, and the test's malformed row keeps its rule path so it is not reported missing. (iteration 1)\n- A P1 on the removed doctor phrases is ruled out: the remaining phrases cover each route's core requests, the derived bridge data is in sync, and the hand-off test pins the generic repair and release-note prompts as no-match. (iteration 1)\n- A P1 on the create sub-track wording is ruled out: the canonical Gate 3 menu and `suggest-subtracks.mjs` own sub-track creation, and the create workflow consumes an existing `spec_path`. (iteration 1)\n- A transcript-scorer phantom-count finding is out of area: the changed files contain no transcript-scoring code. (iteration 1)","oldString":"## 11. RULED OUT DIRECTIONS\n\n- A holdout-leak finding is ruled out so far: the changed files do not read either prompt corpus; `_routes.yaml` only declares trigger phrases, and the route derivation output was checked without opening a prompt row.\n- A cross-runtime branching defect in the changed presentation is ruled out so far: `create-skill-presentation.txt` is plain text read by every runtime, and the canonical Gate 3 constant it must match lives in one shared module.","path":"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/doctor-docs-4/deep-review-strategy.md"},"output":"Edited specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/doctor-docs-4/deep-review-strategy.md (1 replacement)","title":"edit","metadata":{"metadata":{"files":[{"file":"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/doctor-docs-4/deep-review-strategy.md","patch":"Index: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/doctor-docs-4/deep-review-strategy.md\n===================================================================\n--- specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/doctor-docs-4/deep-review-strategy.md\n+++ specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/doctor-docs-4/deep-review-strategy.md\n@@ -77,10 +77,14 @@\n - Remaining frontier: none recorded\n \n ## 11. RULED OUT DIRECTIONS\n \n-- A holdout-leak finding is ruled out so far: the changed files do not read either prompt corpus; `_routes.yaml` only declares trigger phrases, and the route derivation output was checked without opening a prompt row.\n-- A cross-runtime branching defect in the changed presentation is ruled out so far: `create-skill-presentation.txt` is plain text read by every runtime, and the canonical Gate 3 constant it must match lives in one shared module.\n+- A holdout-leak finding is ruled out so far: the changed files do not read either prompt corpus; `_routes.yaml` only declares trigger phrases, and the route derivation output was checked without opening a prompt row. (iteration 1)\n+- A cross-runtime branching defect in the changed presentation is ruled out so far: `create-skill-presentation.txt` is plain text read by every runtime, and the canonical Gate 3 constant it must match lives in one shared module. (iteration 1)\n+- A P0/P1 in the A11 count logic is ruled out: the count is derived from the same arrays that build the printed lines, and the test's malformed row keeps its rule path so it is not reported missing. (iteration 1)\n+- A P1 on the removed doctor phrases is ruled out: the remaining phrases cover each route's core requests, the derived bridge data is in sync, and the hand-off test pins the generic repair and release-note prompts as no-match. (iteration 1)\n+- A P1 on the create sub-track wording is ruled out: the canonical Gate 3 menu and `suggest-subtracks.mjs` own sub-track creation, and the create workflow consumes an existing `spec_path`. (iteration 1)\n+- A transcript-scorer phantom-count finding is out of area: the changed files contain no transcript-scoring code. (iteration 1)\n \n <!-- ANCHOR:next-focus -->\n ## 11. NEXT FOCUS\n correctness\n","status":"modified","additions":6,"deletions":2}],"truncated":false},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Edited specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/doctor-docs-4/deep-review-strategy.md (1 replacement)"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"newString\": \"## 11. RULED OUT DIRECTIONS\\n\\n- A holdout-leak finding is ruled out so far: the changed files do not read either prompt corpus; `_routes.yaml` only declares trigger phrases, and the route derivation output was checked without opening a prompt row. (iteration 1)\\n- A cross-runtime branching defect in the changed presentation is ruled out so far: `create-skill-presentation.txt` is plain text read by every runtime, and the canonical Gate 3 constant it must match lives in one shared module. (iteration 1)\\n- A P0/P1 in the A11 count logic is ruled out: the count is derived from the same arrays that build the printed lines, and the test's malformed row keeps its rule path so it is not reported missing. (iteration 1)\\n- A P1 on the removed doctor phrases is ruled out: the remaining phrases cover each route's core requests, the derived bridge data is in sync, and the hand-off test pins the generic repair and release-note prompts as no-match. (iteration 1)\\n- A P1 on the create sub-track wording is ruled out: the canonical Gate 3 menu and `suggest-subtracks.mjs` own sub-track creation, and the create workflow consumes an existing `spec_path`. (iteration 1)\\n- A transcript-scorer phantom-count finding is out of area: the changed files contain no transcript-scoring code. (iteration 1)\", \"oldString\": \"## 11. RULED OUT DIRECTIONS\\n\\n- A holdout-leak finding is ruled out so far: the changed files do not read either prompt corpus; `_routes.yaml` only declares trigger phrases, and the route derivation output was checked without opening a prompt row.\\n- A cross-runtime branching defect in the changed presentation is ruled out so far: `create-skill-presentation.txt` is plain text read by every runtime, and the canonical Gate 3 constant it must match lives in one shared module.\", \"path\": \"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/doctor-docs-4/deep-review-strategy.md\"}"},"time":{"start":1794670430714,"end":1794670435338}}}}
