{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794670618725,"sessionID":"ses_e255ff46effe7EWyuOLOEwVdy1","part":{"partID":"prt_1dab467da001TZzDfSCR0sR10S","sessionID":"ses_e255ff46effe7EWyuOLOEwVdy1","messageID":"msg_1dab45147001od5cC7GW8f42QD","type":"tool","id":"chatcmpl-tool-8d6c5ac7c715ccce","tool":"read","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"limit":90,"path":"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/doctor-docs-4/deep-review-strategy.md"},"output":"Read file specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/doctor-docs-4/deep-review-strategy.md, lines 1-90\n1: # Deep Review Strategy - doctor-docs pass four\n2: \n3: ## 1. OVERVIEW\n4: \n5: - Session `fanout-doctor-docs-4-1794669272137-9v23rz`, generation 1, lineage mode `new`.\n6: - Detached fan-out lineage for the `doctor-docs` area of command-surfacing review pass four.\n7: - Write surface is this lineage directory only. Review targets are read-only. The repository test suites are not run here: they write temp fixtures outside the lineage, and a single out-of-scope write fails the lineage.\n8: - Holdout hygiene: no `command-prompts.jsonl` or `holdout-prompts.jsonl` is opened; the only prompt material read is a `split: tune` row already materialized in a scratch artifact and the non-holdout tests that name prompts.\n9: \n10: ## 2. TOPIC\n11: \n12: Review the `doctor-docs` files changed since review pass three (`0cdc9fa3ef`, HEAD `400c90e158`) plus the shared docs that describe them:\n13: \n14: - `.skilled/commands/create/assets/create-skill-presentation.txt`\n15: - `.skilled/commands/doctor/_routes.yaml`\n16: - `.skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/agents-md-check.cjs`\n17: - `.skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/tests/agents-md-check.test.cjs`\n18: \n19: The diff is 4 files, +11/-9. The brief asks five questions: behaviour on claude, codex, opencode, pi, devin and dsh; whether a refusal, question or command mention can still attach or start a mutating command; whether the transcript scorer counts a load, followed step or offer that did not happen; holdout hygiene; and docs that disagree with code.\n20: \n21: <!-- ANCHOR:review-dimensions -->\n22: ## 3. REVIEW DIMENSIONS (remaining)\n23: - [ ] security\n24: - [ ] traceability\n25: - [ ] maintainability\n26: \n27: <!-- /ANCHOR:review-dimensions -->\n28: ## 4. NON-GOALS\n29: \n30: - No code fixes; findings only.\n31: - No review of files outside the `doctor-docs` area and the shared docs/context named in the scope.\n32: - No prompt-corpus reading, no holdout inspection, no transcript scoring beyond the test contracts already in the tree.\n33: - No re-litigation of the pass-three lineage's carried P1 on `hook-wiring-check.cjs`; that file is outside this pass's area.\n34: \n35: ## 5. STOP CONDITIONS\n36: \n37: - Hard cap: 3 iterations (`config.maxIterations`).\n38: - Convergence threshold 0.10 on the severity-weighted new-findings ratio.\n39: - Stop policy `convergence`; at the cap the stop reason is `maxIterationsReached`.\n40: - Stop early only on the legal-stop gates (dimension coverage + required traceability protocols + evidence/scope/coverage gates).\n41: \n42: <!-- ANCHOR:completed-dimensions -->\n43: ## 4. COMPLETED DIMENSIONS\n44: - [x] correctness\n45: \n46: <!-- /ANCHOR:completed-dimensions -->\n47: <!-- ANCHOR:running-findings -->\n48: ## 5. RUNNING FINDINGS\n49: - P0 (Blockers): 0\n50: - P1 (Required): 0\n51: - P2 (Suggestions): 1\n52: - Resolved: 0\n53: \n54: <!-- /ANCHOR:running-findings -->\n55: ## 8. WHAT WORKED\n56: \n57: - Tracing the changed A11 detail to its two consumers (the presentation's repair table and the embed engine's router write) found the one actionable gap in an otherwise clean diff. (iteration 1)\n58: - Querying the derived `command-bridges.generated.json` as data, rather than reading a prompt corpus, proved all six removed phrases reached the advisor surface's removal. (iteration 1)\n59: - Comparing the create presentation line against `GATE_3_CHOICE_RELATED` and its parity test proved the canonical wording match without a runtime branch. (iteration 1)\n60: \n61: ## 9. WHAT FAILED\n62: \n63: - The A11-specific troubleshooting row was assumed to cover every A11 finding; it covers missing rows only, so the malformed-row case has no named repair. Recorded as `DR4-P2-001`, not a failed approach. (iteration 1)\n64: \n65: <!-- ANCHOR:exhausted-approaches -->\n66: ## 9. EXHAUSTED APPROACHES (do not retry)\n67: ### A cross-runtime defect in the changed create presentation is ruled out: the line is plain text, the canonical constant is shared, and the parity test covers it. -- BLOCKED (iteration 1, 1 attempts)\n68: - What was tried: A cross-runtime defect in the changed create presentation is ruled out: the line is plain text, the canonical constant is shared, and the parity test covers it.\n69: - Why blocked: Repeated iteration evidence ruled this direction out.\n70: - Do NOT retry: A cross-runtime defect in the changed create presentation is ruled out: the line is plain text, the canonical constant is shared, and the parity test covers it.\n71: \n72: ### A P0/P1 in the A11 count logic is ruled out: the count is derived from the same arrays that produce the printed lines, and the test's malformed row keeps its rule path so it is not double-counted as missing (`agents-md-check.test.cjs:761-762`). -- BLOCKED (iteration 1, 1 attempts)\n73: - What was tried: A P0/P1 in the A11 count logic is ruled out: the count is derived from the same arrays that produce the printed lines, and the test's malformed row keeps its rule path so it is not double-counted as missing (`agents-md-check.test.cjs:761-762`).\n74: - Why blocked: Repeated iteration evidence ruled this direction out.\n75: - Do NOT retry: A P0/P1 in the A11 count logic is ruled out: the count is derived from the same arrays that produce the printed lines, and the test's malformed row keeps its rule path so it is not double-counted as missing (`agents-md-check.test.cjs:761-762`).\n76: \n77: ### A P1 on the new sub-track wording is ruled out: the canonical Gate 3 menu and `suggest-subtracks.mjs` own sub-track creation, and the create workflow consumes an existing `spec_path` rather than promising to create one. -- BLOCKED (iteration 1, 1 attempts)\n78: - What was tried: A P1 on the new sub-track wording is ruled out: the canonical Gate 3 menu and `suggest-subtracks.mjs` own sub-track creation, and the create workflow consumes an existing `spec_path` rather than promising to create one.\n79: - Why blocked: Repeated iteration evidence ruled this direction out.\n80: - Do NOT retry: A P1 on the new sub-track wording is ruled out: the canonical Gate 3 menu and `suggest-subtracks.mjs` own sub-track creation, and the create workflow consumes an existing `spec_path` rather than promising to create one.\n81: \n82: ### A P1 on the removed doctor phrases is ruled out: the remaining phrases cover each route's core requests, the derived bridge data is in sync, and the hand-off tests pin the generic repair/release prompts as no-match. -- BLOCKED (iteration 1, 1 attempts)\n83: - What was tried: A P1 on the removed doctor phrases is ruled out: the remaining phrases cover each route's core requests, the derived bridge data is in sync, and the hand-off tests pin the generic repair/release prompts as no-match.\n84: - Why blocked: Repeated iteration evidence ruled this direction out.\n85: - Do NOT retry: A P1 on the removed doctor phrases is ruled out: the remaining phrases cover each route's core requests, the derived bridge data is in sync, and the hand-off tests pin the generic repair/release prompts as no-match.\n86: \n87: ### A transcript-scorer phantom-count finding is ruled out as out of area: the changed files contain no transcript-scoring code; the only scorer-facing change is the manifest-to-bridge data checked above. -- BLOCKED (iteration 1, 1 attempts)\n88: - What was tried: A transcript-scorer phantom-count fin