{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794670745186,"sessionID":"ses_e255ff46effe7EWyuOLOEwVdy1","part":{"partID":"prt_1dab6513200137l6S4054ohlhV","sessionID":"ses_e255ff46effe7EWyuOLOEwVdy1","messageID":"msg_1dab5eeee0014SUZIVRAMxhRI0","type":"tool","id":"chatcmpl-tool-aece733c205146e6","tool":"shell","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"rg -n 'what changed|tell me what to fix|which checks fail|show me every check' .skilled/manual-testing-playbook/doctor-commands .skilled/commands/doctor/assets 2>/dev/null | head -40","workdir":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research"},"output":".skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-symlink-link.yaml:100:    purpose: \"Report what changed and where the engine recorded it\"\n.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-mcp-presentation.txt:138:Do not repair credentials during debug. Report expected key names with present or missing status only. For each approved repair, rerun the JSON health check and report what changed.\n.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/agents-md-manifest.json:970:        \"body\": \"#### Quality Principles\\n\\n- **Test what changed, not what exists** — the coverage floor comes first and this rule never waives it: happy path plus one edge case per public surface, per `sk-code`'s universal quality tiers. ABOVE that floor, a new test earns its place by failing for one real reason no current test catches. Do not add a test per branch, re-assert the framework or the language, or mirror the implementation. Changed behavior gets coverage; unchanged behavior does not get new tests\\n\\n\"\n","title":"shell","metadata":{"metadata":{"status":"completed","truncated":false,"exit":0},"content":[{"type":"text","text":".skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-symlink-link.yaml:100:    purpose: \"Report what changed and where the engine recorded it\"\n.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-mcp-presentation.txt:138:Do not repair credentials during debug. Report expected key names with present or missing status only. For each approved repair, rerun the JSON health check and report what changed.\n.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/agents-md-manifest.json:970:        \"body\": \"#### Quality Principles\\n\\n- **Test what changed, not what exists** — the coverage floor comes first and this rule never waives it: happy path plus one edge case per public surface, per `sk-code`'s universal quality tiers. ABOVE that floor, a new test earns its place by failing for one real reason no current test catches. Do not add a test per branch, re-assert the framework or the language, or mirror the implementation. Changed behavior gets coverage; unchanged behavior does not get new tests\\n\\n\"\n"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"command\": \"rg -n 'what changed|tell me what to fix|which checks fail|show me every check' .skilled/manual-testing-playbook/doctor-commands .skilled/commands/doctor/assets 2>/dev/null | head -40\", \"workdir\": \"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research\"}"},"time":{"start":1794670743858,"end":1794670745186}}}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794670745197,"sessionID":"ses_e255ff46effe7EWyuOLOEwVdy1","part":{"partID":"prt_1dab647be002NUZ5lU2ro8i3ur","sessionID":"ses_e255ff46effe7EWyuOLOEwVdy1","messageID":"msg_1dab5eeee0014SUZIVRAMxhRI0","type":"tool","id":"chatcmpl-tool-b6cc45b23590050e","tool":"shell","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"rg -n --glob '*.md' --glob '!**/review/**' 'X-05|A-2|malformed row|detail names|create:sk-skill|1,189' specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/016-claude-create-reach-and-doctor-default specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/024-fable-review-remediation specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/025-release-notes-and-doc-sync | head -60","workdir":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research"},"output":"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/016-claude-create-reach-and-doctor-default/spec.md:3:description: \"Claude Code lists 32 of the 44 tracked commands, because a command file named skill.md makes it read the create folder as one skill. This phase renames /create:skill to /create:sk-skill on every runtime with no alias, offers /doctor:helper on a doctor prompt that says a tool is not showing up, shows the AGENTS.md Gate 2 call with the request on stdin, adds intent phrases to five no-recommendation commands and keeps the brief-cost run out of the shared health log.\"\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/016-claude-create-reach-and-doctor-default/spec.md:44:**Scope Boundary**: The rename of `/create:skill` to `/create:sk-skill` in every live file outside `specs/`, the mirror check that counts Claude's commands, the doctor problem cue, `AGENTS.md` line 65 with its two derived copies, the intent phrases of five commands and the child environment of the brief-cost script. Generated files change only through their generators. No scorer weight, hub routing logic or renderer changes. `/create:skill-parent`, the `sk-create-skill` mode and its folder, the `.claude/skills` link, every file under `specs/`, every published changelog entry, the dated benchmark reports and the served copy of the sk-doc canary fixture keep the old text.\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/016-claude-create-reach-and-doctor-default/spec.md:52:- `/create:sk-skill` on every runtime, matching `/doctor:sk-skill`, with no alias for the old name, so no command file is named `skill.md` and Claude lists all 44 tracked commands.\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/016-claude-create-reach-and-doctor-default/spec.md:189:- Rename. `derive-command-bridges.cjs` names each bridge `command-` plus the command with its colon replaced (`derive-command-bridges.cjs:117`), so `/create:sk-skill` becomes `command-create-sk-skill`. It requires every `scoring-compatibility.json` entry to name a known inventory id, so that file changes before the deriver runs. It writes the marked blocks of `projection.ts`, `skill_advisor.py` and `command-attach.ts` and the bridge file. The mode-to-command map comes from `mode-registry.json`.\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/016-claude-create-reach-and-doctor-default/spec.md:208:- A. Rename `/create:skill` to `/create:sk-skill` in every live file, with generated files rewritten by their generators, and drop the collapse allowlist from the mirror check.\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/016-claude-create-reach-and-doctor-default/spec.md:250:| REQ-001 | `/create:skill` is renamed to `/create:sk-skill` with no alias: `.skilled/commands/create/sk-skill.md` exists, no file named `skill.md` in any capitalisation sits under `.skilled/commands` outside `tests/fixtures`, where 22 `SKILL.md` fixtures of the sk-skill doctor checks are not command files, and the `OLDP` scan lists only the nine kept history files and the new changelog entry, which must name the old command. |\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/016-claude-create-reach-and-doctor-default/spec.md:253:| REQ-004 | The routing corpus rows whose expected command was `/create:skill` read `/create:sk-skill`: the three non-holdout rows edited by id, and the one holdout row changed only in `expected_command` by a script that never prints or reads its prompt and reports a count of 1. `holdout-prompts.jsonl` holds no old spelling and is never opened. |\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/016-claude-create-reach-and-doctor-default/spec.md:266:| REQ-012 | Claude's command folder holds `sk-skill.md` and twelve siblings with no `skill.md` in any capitalisation, and a live Claude Code listing, run by the coordinator in place of the operator, names `create:sk-skill` and the twelve other `create:*` names. |\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/016-claude-create-reach-and-doctor-default/spec.md:354:- Q1. How does Claude Code reach all 44 commands? Answered by the operator on 2026-11-13: rename `/create:skill` to `/create:sk-skill` on every runtime, matching `/doctor:sk-skill`, with no alias. The rank 7 design changed from a managed `.claude/skills` tree with a Claude-only `create` skill to a rename, because the cause is an open upstream bug in Claude Code (`anthropics/claude-code#85786`): a command file named `skill.md`, in any capitalisation and on any filesystem, hides its folder's other commands, and another file name is the only documented way out. The flat root mirror this plan proposed earlier is dropped.\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/016-claude-create-reach-and-doctor-default/plan.md:3:description: \"Rename /create:skill to /create:sk-skill on every runtime with no alias and drop the mirror check's allowlist, read a negated show-up or appear phrase as a strong doctor problem cue, show the AGENTS.md Gate 2 call on stdin, add intent phrases to five commands with a real-embedding holdout count, and keep the brief-cost run's health records in its sandbox.\"\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/016-claude-create-reach-and-doctor-default/plan.md:29:Five lanes. Lane A renames `/create:skill` to `/create:sk-skill`: the coordinator moves the file with `git mv`, workers change the name area by area, the deriver and the mirror and agent generators rewrite what they own, and the mirror check loses its allowlist and matches `skill.md` in any capitalisation. Lane B adds the negated show-up cue. Lane C rewrites `AGENTS.md` line 65, test first. Lane D adds intent phrases to five commands after lanes A and B are built, and the coordinator measures holdout as a count on the real embedder before and after. Lane E points the cost run's hook children at the sandbox for `TMPDIR`, test first.\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/016-claude-create-reach-and-doctor-default/implementation-summary.md:3:description: \"Built and verified on 2026-11-13. /create:skill is now /create:sk-skill on every runtime with no alias, and Claude Code lists all 44 tracked commands. The mcp doctor tune row now gets /doctor:helper, the AGENTS.md Gate 2 call reads stdin, five commands carry intent phrases and real holdout rose from 3 to 5 of 44. All 13 acceptance criteria are Met. The work sits in the working tree on top of 087888ec4a and is not committed yet.\"\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/016-claude-create-reach-and-doctor-default/implementation-summary.md:60:`/create:skill` is `/create:sk-skill` on every runtime, with no alias. No command file is named `skill.md` now, so Claude Code lists all 44 tracked commands. A doctor prompt that says a tool is not showing up gets `/doctor:helper` beside the skills. The `AGENTS.md` Gate 2 example sends the request on stdin. Four doctor commands and `/speckit:search` carry intent phrases. A brief-cost run keeps its health records inside its own sandbox.\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/016-claude-create-reach-and-doctor-default/implementation-summary.md:92:| `ADV/scripts/routing-accuracy/command-prompts.jsonl` | Modified | Four rows expect `/create:sk-skill`. The holdout row changed by a count-only `sed` |\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/016-claude-create-reach-and-doctor-default/implementation-summary.md:128:| Rename the command to `/create:sk-skill` on every runtime with no alias | The operator's choice. An open Claude Code bug (`anthropics/claude-code#85786`) hides a folder's other commands behind any file named `skill.md` in any capitalisation, so the mirror check drops its allowlist and refuses the name everywhere |\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/016-claude-create-reach-and-doctor-default/acceptance-criteria.md:58:| AC-003 | REQ-003 | Given every generated output, When each generator has written it and its check runs, Then `DRV` prints `\"changed\": []`, `SRM`, `PSY`, `ASY`, `AMSC`, `MAN` and `GPC` pass and the recaptured `BASE` keys `/create:sk-skill` | The T014, T015, T016 and T021 verify lines and the same checks in `$SP/after.txt` Met 2026-11-13: `scratch/after.txt` reads `DRV` `{\"status\":\"fresh\",\"changed\":[]}`, `SRM` in sync, `PSY` 45 three times, `ASY` 11 three times, `AMSC` in sync, `MAN` `PASS` and `GPC` `PASS`. `jq -r '.commands \\| keys[]' $BASE \\| rg -cx '/create:sk-skill'` prints 1. The sk-doc compiled-route manifest, which the plan did not list, was refreshed by its own generator and all seven hubs read `fresh`. Receipts: `scratch/after.txt:23` `scratch/after.txt:27` `scratch/after.txt:53` `scratch/after.txt:57` `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/scorer/projection.ts:1074` | Met | - |\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/016-claude-create-reach-and-doctor-default/acceptance-criteria.md:59:| AC-004 | REQ-004 | Given the routing corpus, When its expected commands are counted, Then four rows read `/create:sk-skill` and none reads `/create:skill`, the holdout row changed only in `expected_command` by the count-only `sed` with a reported count of 1, and `holdout-prompts.jsonl` was never opened | The T010 count, the `numstat` line `4`, `4` and CHK-030 Met 2026-11-13: `jq` over the corpus counts four `/create:sk-skill` rows, one each of `[\"holdout\",\"plain\"]`, `[\"none\",\"slash-variant\"]`, `[\"none\",\"typed\"]` and `[\"tune\",\"plain\"]`. `rg -c` for the old expected command prints nothing and `git diff --numstat HEAD` reads `4`, `4`. The holdout row changed by the count-only `sed`, which reported 1. No task opened `holdout-prompts.jsonl`. Receipts: `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/command-prompts.jsonl:35` `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/command-prompts.jsonl:36` `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/command-prompts.jsonl:171` | Met | - |\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/016-claude-create-reach-and-doctor-default/acceptance-criteria.md:67:| AC-012 | REQ-012 | Given the regenerated Claude tree, When the folder is listed and the operator lists the Skill tool in a copy of it, Then `.claude/commands/create` holds `sk-skill.md` and twelve siblings with no `skill.md` in any capitalisation, and the listing names `create:sk-skill` and the twelve other `create:*` names | `$SP/claude-observed.txt` from T022 and the empty `comm` output over `$SP/claude-listing.txt` from T023 Met 2026-11-13: `scratch/claude-observed.txt` reads `visibility claude 44/44`, 13 entries in `.claude/commands/create` with `sk-skill.md` among them and a `skill.md` count of 0. The coordinator ran T023 in place of the operator, in a throwaway folder outside any repository. `scratch/claude-expected.txt` holds 44 names, `comm -23` against the listing prints nothing and the listing holds 13 `create:` names. Receipts: `scratch/claude-observed.txt:1` `scratch/claude-observed.txt:13` `scratch/claude-observed.txt:16` `scratch/claude-listing.txt:11` | Met | - |\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/016-claude-create-reach-and-doctor-default/tasks.md:3:description: \"Ordered worker-sized tasks in five lanes: rename /create:skill to /create:sk-skill on every runtime with generated files rewritten by their generators, read a negated show-up or appear phrase as a doctor problem cue, show the AGENTS.md Gate 2 call on stdin, add intent phrases to five commands with a real-embedding holdout count, and keep the brief-cost run's health records in its sandbox.\"\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/016-claude-create-reach-and-doctor-default/tasks.md:92:- [x] T005 [P] Lane A. Rename the command inside its own folder, its assets and the command catalogs (`.skilled/commands/create/sk-skill.md`, `.skilled/commands/create/assets/create-skill-auto.yaml`, `.skilled/commands/create/assets/create-skill-confirm.yaml`, `.skilled/commands/create/assets/create-skill-presentation.txt`, `.skilled/commands/create/README.txt`, `.skilled/commands/README.txt`, `.skilled/commands/prompt/assets/prompt_improve_presentation.txt`, `$DS/command-catalog-mirror-check.cjs`). Replace every `/create:skill` that no `-` or word character follows with `/create:sk-skill`, and in `create/README.txt` the tree line `skill.md` with `sk-skill.md`. In the catalog checker, rewrite the comment example `(/create:skill inside /create:skill-parent)` as a generic `(/group:name inside /group:name-parent)`, because no real pair is left. The asset file names stay. Verify: `OLD` over the eight files prints nothing, `CCM` prints `STATUS=OK` and `rg -c '/create:sk-skill' .skilled/commands/create/sk-skill.md` prints at least 2.\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/016-claude-create-reach-and-doctor-default/tasks.md:93:- [x] T006 [P] Lane A. Rename the command in the sk-doc hub (`.skilled/skills/sk-doc/command-metadata.json`, `.skilled/skills/sk-doc/hub-router.json`, `.skilled/skills/sk-doc/mode-registry.json`, `.skilled/skills/sk-doc/README.md`, `.skilled/skills/sk-doc/ROUTER.md`, `.skilled/skills/sk-doc/SKILL.md`, `.skilled/skills/sk-doc/sk-create-command/assets/command-contract.json`, `.skilled/skills/sk-doc/sk-create-frontmatter/SKILL.md`). Replace the old name with `/create:sk-skill` in the command entry, the two `sibling` fields, the trigger phrase, the mode's `command`, the keyword lists and the prose. Change no version field. Verify: `OLD` over the eight files prints nothing, `jq empty` passes on the four JSON files, `PSC` holds `all hard invariants passed` and `CRS` prints both lines.\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/016-claude-create-reach-and-doctor-default/tasks.md:94:- [x] T007 [P] Lane A. Rename the command in the `sk-create-skill` packet (`.skilled/skills/sk-doc/sk-create-skill/README.md`, `ROUTER.md`, `SKILL.md`, `references/shared/advisor-index-handoff.md`, `references/skill/upgrading-a-skill-to-v4.md`, `scripts/lib/command-metadata-schema.cjs`, `scripts/tests/skill-root-metadata-contract.test.cjs`). Replace the old name and the path `create/skill.md` with `/create:sk-skill` and `create/sk-skill.md`, including the schema helper's comment example and the contract test's sample of `commandDefinitionRelPath`. The packet and its folder keep their names. Verify: `OLD` over the seven files prints nothing, `node --check` passes on the schema helper and `node --test .skilled/skills/sk-doc/sk-create-skill/scripts/tests/skill-root-metadata-contract.test.cjs` reports `fail 0`.\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/016-claude-create-reach-and-doctor-default/tasks.md:95:- [x] T008 [P] Lane A. Rename the bridge's hand-kept entry and the hook guide's Claude row (`$ADV/scripts/command-bridges/scoring-compatibility.json`, `HD`). In the compatibility entry, change `inventoryId` and `id` to `command-create-sk-skill` and the description and the two keywords to `/create:sk-skill` and `create:sk-skill`. In `HD`, rewrite the Claude Code row of the `Starting a surfaced command` table: the second cell reads `Yes, through the Skill tool, as a shortcut for the names it lists` and the Basis cell reads ``The Skill tool lists names, not files. A command file named `skill.md` in any capitalisation makes Claude Code read its folder as one skill, an open upstream bug, so no command file carries that name``. Verify: `jq empty` passes on the compatibility file, `OLD` over the two files prints nothing and `rg -c '33 of the 45' $HD` prints nothing.\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/016-claude-create-reach-and-doctor-default/tasks.md:97:- [x] T010 [P] Lane A. Point the corpus rows at the new name (`CORPUS`). For `cmd-create-skill-typed-01` and `sv-07`, check that each `split` is not `holdout`, then replace `/create:skill` with `/create:sk-skill` in `prompt` and set `expected_command` to `/create:sk-skill`. For `cmd-create-skill-plain-tune-01`, check that its `split` is `tune`, then set `expected_command` only. For the one holdout row, change only `expected_command`, with one scripted substitution that never reads or prints a prompt: `sed -i '' -E '/\"split\":\"holdout\"/ s#\"expected_command\":\"/create:skill\"#\"expected_command\":\"/create:sk-skill\"#' $CORPUS`, and report only the count, from `awk '/\"split\":\"holdout\"/ && /\"expected_command\":\"\\/create:sk-skill\"/ {n++} END {print n+0}' $CORPUS`. Row ids stay. Verify: the `awk` count prints 1, `rg -c '\"expected_command\":\"/create:skill\"' $CORPUS` prints nothing, `jq -c 'select(.expected_command == \"/create:sk-skill\") | [.split, .row_type]' $CORPUS | sort | uniq -c` prints the four pairs of `spec.md` section 2, every line parses with `jq -c . $CORPUS > /dev/null` and `G diff --numstat HEAD -- $CORPUS` prints `4`, `4` and the path.\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/016-claude-create-reach-and-doctor-default/tasks.md:103:- [x] T014 Lane A. Regenerate the bridges under the new name and move the typed-attach cases (`$ADV/lib/command-attach.ts`, `$ADV/tests/command-attach-guards.vitest.ts` and the `DER` outputs). After T006 and T008, rewrite the comment above the longest-key rule in `command-attach.ts`, outside the marked blocks, so its example of one command name inside another is generic, `/group:name` inside `/group:name-parent`, because no real pair is left. Run `DER`. In the guards test, change the four `/create:skill` inputs and expectations to `/create:sk-skill`. Verify: `DRV` prints `\"changed\": []` and exits 0, `OLD $ADV/lib $ADV/scripts/command-bridges $ADV/scripts/skill_advisor.py $ADV/tests` prints nothing, `rg -c 'command-create-sk-skill' $ADV/lib/scorer/projection.ts` prints at least 1, `TC` exits 0 and `V tests/command-attach-guards.vitest.ts tests/command-attach.vitest.ts` reports 0 failed.\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/016-claude-create-reach-and-doctor-default/tasks.md:112:- [x] T017 [C] Rebuild the advisor, restart the worktree's daemon and re-embed (`$ADV/dist`, the advisor database). Run `npm run build` in `ADV`, restart the advisor daemon this worktree serves, then `CLI skill_graph_scan --trusted --format text`. Verify: the build exits 0, `TC` exits 0, `rg -c 'appear' $ADV/dist/runtime/lib/scorer/doctor-helper-handoff.js` prints at least 1, `rg -c 'create:sk-skill' $ADV/dist/runtime/lib/command-attach.js` prints at least 1 and the scan prints its status with no error. When Ollama does not answer, mark this task `[B]` and start nothing.\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/016-claude-create-reach-and-doctor-default/tasks.md:124:- [x] T021 [P] Recapture the fixture baseline and check the scorer eval (`BASE`, and `$RA/scorer-eval-baseline.json` only when its values move). Run `node $CAP --write`, `FLOOR` and `EVAL`. When `EVAL` differs from the committed baseline and still holds the floor, recapture it with `node $RA/capture-scorer-eval-baseline.mjs --write` as its header documents and run `V tests/parity/scorer-eval-baseline-ratchet.vitest.ts tests/parity/scorer-eval-baseline-capture-date.vitest.ts`. Verify: `FLOOR` prints typed recall of 24 of 44 or more, `{\"count\":0,\"total\":35}`, a typed delivery `combined` of 44 of 44, a plain tune `combined` of 23 or more and `{\"count\":0,\"total\":35}`, `jq -c '.rows[\"cmd-doctor-mcp-plain-tune-01\"].offered, .rows[\"cmd-doctor-skill-advisor-plain-tune-01\"].offered' $BASE` prints `true` and `false`, `jq -r '.commands | keys[]' $BASE | rg -cx '/create:sk-skill'` prints 1, `OLD $BASE` prints nothing, `SLICE` reports 0 failed and `EVAL` prints at least `[160,50,21,5]` with the fourth value no higher than 5.\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/016-claude-create-reach-and-doctor-default/tasks.md:128:- [x] T023 [C] Ask the operator for one live Claude Code listing of the regenerated tree (`$SP/claude-listing.txt`). It needs a model session, so it is the operator's to run and confirm. Write the expected names with `(cd .claude/commands && find . -name '*.md' -not -name 'local-*' | sed -e 's|^\\./||' -e 's|\\.md$||' -e 's|/|:|') | sort > $SP/claude-expected.txt`. In a directory from `mktemp -d` outside any repository, copy the tree with `cp -RL .claude/commands <tmp>/x/.claude/commands`, start Claude Code once in `<tmp>/x` with the prompt \"List the names of every entry your Skill tool offers, one per line, and nothing else.\", save the answer to `$SP/claude-listing.txt` and delete the temp directory. Verify: `wc -l < $SP/claude-expected.txt` prints 44 and `comm -23 $SP/claude-expected.txt <(sed -E 's/^[-*/ ]+//' $SP/claude-listing.txt | sort -u)` prints nothing, so `create:sk-skill` and the twelve other `create:*` names are listed. Until the operator runs it, this task stays open and REQ-012 rests on T022.\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/016-claude-create-reach-and-doctor-default/tasks.md:133:- [x] T026 Write the changelog entry for the breaking rename at `v2.10.0.0`, the version the operator chose in Q3 (the `sk-doc` changelog entry and the `version` fields of `.skilled/skills/sk-doc/SKILL.md`, `hub-router.json`, `mode-registry.json` and `description.json`). Write the entry through the `sk-create-changelog` workflow as `v2.10.0.0`, a minor bump whose text calls out the break, and set the four version fields to `2.10.0.0`. Its first line of substance says `/create:skill` is now `/create:sk-skill` on every runtime with no alias, and why. Edit no existing entry. Verify: `G status --short -- '*/changelog/*'` lists only the new entry, `G diff --quiet HEAD -- .skilled/skills/sk-doc/changelog .skilled/changelog` exits 0 and `PSC` holds `all hard invariants passed, 0 warnings`.\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/016-claude-create-reach-and-doctor-default/tasks.md:142:- [x] T028 [C] Check the rename's end state and the boundaries. Verify: `OLD` prints exactly the nine `KEPT` files, `rg -l -F 'create:sk-skill' .skilled/commands/create/sk-skill.md .skilled/skills/sk-doc/mode-registry.json $ADV/lib/command-attach.ts` lists all three, `G diff --quiet HEAD -- .claude/skills .skilled/commands/create/skill-parent.md $ADV/lib/render.ts` exits 0, every `KEPT` file is unchanged by `G diff --quiet HEAD --`, `G diff --stat HEAD -- '*package.json' '*package-lock.json'` prints nothing, `G diff HEAD -U0 -- .skilled .claude .cursor .codex .pi .dsh AGENTS.md | rg \"^\\+.*(//|#|\\*).*(specs/|REQ-0|ADR-0|T0[0-9]{2}|[Pp]hase [0-9]|[Rr]ank [0-9]|R4-P2)\"` prints nothing, `G diff --numstat HEAD -- AGENTS.md` prints `1`, `1` and `AGENTS.md`, and `G status --short -- .skilled .claude .cursor .codex .pi .dsh AGENTS.md README.md CONTRIBUTING.md` lists only files named in this phase's tasks.\n","title":"shell","metadata":{"metadata":{"status":"completed","truncated":false,"exit":0},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/016-claude-create-reach-and-doctor-default/spec.md:3:description: \"Claude Code lists 32 of the 44 tracked commands, because a command file named skill.md makes it read the create folder as one skill. This phase renames /create:skill to /create:sk-skill on every runtime with no alias, offers /doctor:helper on a doctor prompt that says a tool is not showing up, shows the AGENTS.md Gate 2 call with the request on stdin, adds intent phrases to five no-recommendation commands and keeps the brief-cost run out of the shared health log.\"\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/016-claude-create-reach-and-doctor-default/spec.md:44:**Scope Boundary**: The rename of `/create:skill` to `/create:sk-skill` in every live file outside `specs/`, the mirror check that counts Claude's commands, the doctor problem cue, `AGENTS.md` line 65 with its two derived copies, the intent phrases of five commands and the child environment of the brief-cost script. Generated files change only through their generators. No scorer weight, hub routing logic or renderer changes. `/create:skill-parent`, the `sk-create-skill` mode and its folder, the `.claude/skills` link, every file under `specs/`, every published changelog entry, the dated benchmark reports and the served copy of the sk-doc canary fixture keep the old text.\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/016-claude-create-reach-and-doctor-default/spec.md:52:- `/create:sk-skill` on every runtime, matching `/doctor:sk-skill`, with no alias for the old name, so no command file is named `skill.md` and Claude lists all 44 tracked commands.\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/016-claude-create-reach-and-doctor-default/spec.md:189:- Rename. `derive-command-bridges.cjs` names each bridge `command-` plus the command with its colon replaced (`derive-command-bridges.cjs:117`), so `/create:sk-skill` becomes `command-create-sk-skill`. It requires every `scoring-compatibility.json` entry to name a known inventory id, so that file changes before the deriver runs. It writes the marked blocks of `projection.ts`, `skill_advisor.py` and `command-attach.ts` and the bridge file. The mode-to-command map comes from `mode-registry.json`.\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/016-claude-create-reach-and-doctor-default/spec.md:208:- A. Rename `/create:skill` to `/create:sk-skill` in every live file, with generated files rewritten by their generators, and drop the collapse allowlist from the mirror check.\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/016-claude-create-reach-and-doctor-default/spec.md:250:| REQ-001 | `/create:skill` is renamed to `/create:sk-skill` with no alias: `.skilled/commands/create/sk-skill.md` exists, no file named `skill.md` in any capitalisation sits under `.skilled/commands` outside `tests/fixtures`, where 22 `SKILL.md` fixtures of the sk-skill doctor checks are not command files, and the `OLDP` scan lists only the nine kept history files and the new changelog entry, which must name the old command. |\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/016-claude-create-reach-and-doctor-default/spec.md:253:| REQ-004 | The routing corpus rows whose expected command was `/create:skill` read `/create:sk-skill`: the three non-holdout rows edited by id, and the one holdout row changed only in `expected_command` by a script that never prints or reads its prompt and reports a count of 1. `holdout-prompts.jsonl` holds no old spelling and is never opened. |\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/016-claude-create-reach-and-doctor-default/spec.md:266:| REQ-012 | Claude's command folder holds `sk-skill.md` and twelve siblings with no `skill.md` in any capitalisation, and a live Claude Code listing, run by the coordinator in place of the operator, names `create:sk-skill` and the twelve other `create:*` names. |\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/016-claude-create-reach-and-doctor-default/spec.md:354:- Q1. How does Claude Code reach all 44 commands? Answered by the operator on 2026-11-13: rename `/create:skill` to `/create:sk-skill` on every runtime, matching `/doctor:sk-skill`, with no alias. The rank 7 design changed from a managed `.claude/skills` tree with a Claude-only `create` skill to a rename, because the cause is an open upstream bug in Claude Code (`anthropics/claude-code#85786`): a command file named `skill.md`, in any capitalisation and on any filesystem, hides its folder's other commands, and another file name is the only documented way out. The flat root mirror this plan proposed earlier is dropped.\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/016-claude-create-reach-and-doctor-default/plan.md:3:description: \"Rename /create:skill to /create:sk-skill on every runtime with no alias and drop the mirror check's allowlist, read a negated show-up or appear phrase as a strong doctor problem cue, show the AGENTS.md Gate 2 call on stdin, add intent phrases to five commands with a real-embedding holdout count, and keep the brief-cost run's health records in its sandbox.\"\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/016-claude-create-reach-and-doctor-default/plan.md:29:Five lanes. Lane A renames `/create:skill` to `/create:sk-skill`: the coordinator moves the file with `git mv`, workers change the name area by area, the deriver and the mirror and agent generators rewrite what they own, and the mirror check loses its allowlist and matches `skill.md` in any capitalisation. Lane B adds the negated show-up cue. Lane C rewrites `AGENTS.md` line 65, test first. Lane D adds intent phrases to five commands after lanes A and B are built, and the coordinator measures holdout as a count on the real embedder before and after. Lane E points the cost run's hook children at the sandbox for `TMPDIR`, test first.\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/016-claude-create-reach-and-doctor-default/implementation-summary.md:3:description: \"Built and verified on 2026-11-13. /create:skill is now /create:sk-skill on every runtime with no alias, and Claude Code lists all 44 tracked commands. The mcp doctor tune row now gets /doctor:helper, the AGENTS.md Gate 2 call reads stdin, five commands carry intent phrases and real holdout rose from 3 to 5 of 44. All 13 acceptance criteria are Met. The work sits in the working tree on top of 087888ec4a and is not committed yet.\"\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/016-claude-create-reach-and-doctor-default/implementation-summary.md:60:`/create:skill` is `/create:sk-skill` on every runtime, with no alias. No command file is named `skill.md` now, so Claude Code lists all 44 tracked commands. A doctor prompt that says a tool is not showing up gets `/doctor:helper` beside the skills. The `AGENTS.md` Gate 2 example sends the request on stdin. Four doctor commands and `/speckit:search` carry intent phrases. A brief-cost run keeps its health records inside its own sandbox.\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/016-claude-create-reach-and-doctor-default/implementation-summary.md:92:| `ADV/scripts/routing-accuracy/command-prompts.jsonl` | Modified | Four rows expect `/create:sk-skill`. The holdout row changed by a count-only `sed` |\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/016-claude-create-reach-and-doctor-default/implementation-summary.md:128:| Rename the command to `/create:sk-skill` on every runtime with no alias | The operator's choice. An open Claude Code bug (`anthropics/claude-code#85786`) hides a folder's other commands behind any file named `skill.md` in any capitalisation, so the mirror check drops its allowlist and refuses the name everywhere |\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/016-claude-create-reach-and-doctor-default/acceptance-criteria.md:58:| AC-003 | REQ-003 | Given every generated output, When each generator has written it and its check runs, Then `DRV` prints `\"changed\": []`, `SRM`, `PSY`, `ASY`, `AMSC`, `MAN` and `GPC` pass and the recaptured `BASE` keys `/create:sk-skill` | The T014, T015, T016 and T021 verify lines and the same checks in `$SP/after.txt` Met 2026-11-13: `scratch/after.txt` reads `DRV` `{\"status\":\"fresh\",\"changed\":[]}`, `SRM` in sync, `PSY` 45 three times, `ASY` 11 three times, `AMSC` in sync, `MAN` `PASS` and `GPC` `PASS`. `jq -r '.commands \\| keys[]' $BASE \\| rg -cx '/create:sk-skill'` prints 1. The sk-doc compiled-route manifest, which the plan did not list, was refreshed by its own generator and all seven hubs read `fresh`. Receipts: `scratch/after.txt:23` `scratch/after.txt:27` `scratch/after.txt:53` `scratch/after.txt:57` `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/scorer/projection.ts:1074` | Met | - |\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/016-claude-create-reach-and-doctor-default/acceptance-criteria.md:59:| AC-004 | REQ-004 | Given the routing corpus, When its expected commands are counted, Then four rows read `/create:sk-skill` and none reads `/create:skill`, the holdout row changed only in `expected_command` by the count-only `sed` with a reported count of 1, and `holdout-prompts.jsonl` was never opened | The T010 count, the `numstat` line `4`, `4` and CHK-030 Met 2026-11-13: `jq` over the corpus counts four `/create:sk-skill` rows, one each of `[\"holdout\",\"plain\"]`, `[\"none\",\"slash-variant\"]`, `[\"none\",\"typed\"]` and `[\"tune\",\"plain\"]`. `rg -c` for the old expected command prints nothing and `git diff --numstat HEAD` reads `4`, `4`. The holdout row changed by the count-only `sed`, which reported 1. No task opened `holdout-prompts.jsonl`. Receipts: `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/command-prompts.jsonl:35` `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/command-prompts.jsonl:36` `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/command-prompts.jsonl:171` | Met | - |\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/016-claude-create-reach-and-doctor-default/acceptance-criteria.md:67:| AC-012 | REQ-012 | Given the regenerated Claude tree, When the folder is listed and the operator lists the Skill tool in a copy of it, Then `.claude/commands/create` holds `sk-skill.md` and twelve siblings with no `skill.md` in any capitalisation, and the listing names `create:sk-skill` and the twelve other `create:*` names | `$SP/claude-observed.txt` from T022 and the empty `comm` output over `$SP/claude-listing.txt` from T023 Met 2026-11-13: `scratch/claude-observed.txt` reads `visibility claude 44/44`, 13 entries in `.claude/commands/create` with `sk-skill.md` among them and a `skill.md` count of 0. The coordinator ran T023 in place of the operator, in a throwaway folder outside any repository. `scratch/claude-expected.txt` holds 44 names, `comm -23` against the listing prints nothing and the listing holds 13 `create:` names. Receipts: `scratch/claude-observed.txt:1` `scratch/claude-observed.txt:13` `scratch/claude-observed.txt:16` `scratch/claude-listing.txt:11` | Met | - |\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/016-claude-create-reach-and-doctor-default/tasks.md:3:description: \"Ordered worker-sized tasks in five lanes: rename /create:skill to /create:sk-skill on every runtime with generated files rewritten by their generators, read a negated show-up or appear phrase as a doctor problem cue, show the AGENTS.md Gate 2 call on stdin, add intent phrases to five commands with a real-embedding holdout count, and keep the brief-cost run's health records in its sandbox.\"\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/016-claude-create-reach-and-doctor-default/tasks.md:92:- [x] T005 [P] Lane A. Rename the command inside its own folder, its assets and the command catalogs (`.skilled/commands/create/sk-skill.md`, `.skilled/commands/create/assets/create-skill-auto.yaml`, `.skilled/commands/create/assets/create-skill-confirm.yaml`, `.skilled/commands/create/assets/create-skill-presentation.txt`, `.skilled/commands/create/README.txt`, `.skilled/commands/README.txt`, `.skilled/commands/prompt/assets/prompt_improve_presentation.txt`, `$DS/command-catalog-mirror-check.cjs`). Replace every `/create:skill` that no `-` or word character follows with `/create:sk-skill`, and in `create/README.txt` the tree line `skill.md` with `sk-skill.md`. In the catalog checker, rewrite the comment example `(/create:skill inside /create:skill-parent)` as a generic `(/group:name inside /group:name-parent)`, because no real pair is left. The asset file names stay. Verify: `OLD` over the eight files prints nothing, `CCM` prints `STATUS=OK` and `rg -c '/create:sk-skill' .skilled/commands/create/sk-skill.md` prints at least 2.\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/016-claude-create-reach-and-doctor-default/tasks.md:93:- [x] T006 [P] Lane A. Rename the command in the sk-doc hub (`.skilled/skills/sk-doc/command-metadata.json`, `.skilled/skills/sk-doc/hub-router.json`, 