{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794670765982,"sessionID":"ses_e255ff46effe7EWyuOLOEwVdy1","part":{"partID":"prt_1dab6a00600136iaYdxOqq0qNt","sessionID":"ses_e255ff46effe7EWyuOLOEwVdy1","messageID":"msg_1dab65c94001re0hvhsUzXh4mK","type":"tool","id":"chatcmpl-tool-a4ea843b52fcec06","tool":"read","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"limit":110,"path":".skilled/manual-testing-playbook/doctor-commands/doctor-update-check.md"},"output":"Read file .skilled/manual-testing-playbook/doctor-commands/doctor-update-check.md, lines 1-109\n1: ---\n2: title: \"DOC-357 -- Doctor update check\"\n3: description: \"Manual scenario validating that /doctor:update check on the shared update fixture reports the release position, upstream latest and per-unit status, keeps unavailable upstream data visible as UNKNOWN, and writes no checkout file or state log.\"\n4: version: 1.2.0.0\n5: id: doctor-commands-doctor-update-check\n6: expected_workflow_mode: UNKNOWN\n7: expected_leaf_resources: []\n8: ---\n9: # DOC-357 -- Doctor update check\n10: \n11: ## 1. OVERVIEW\n12: \n13: This scenario validates the default action of `/doctor:update` against the shared doctor update fixture at `.worktrees/.doctor-update-test-environment`. A `/doctor:update` invocation with no action token runs `check`, which reports where the fixture stands against a named release: the release position, the ahead and behind counts, the upstream latest release or UNKNOWN, and every unit status. Check is read-only for the checkout. The only network write it may perform is a release-commit fetch into the git object store, which creates no ref, and `--offline` prevents every fetch.\n14: \n15: The scenario also confirms that unavailable upstream data stays visible as UNKNOWN, that a `--json` run returns one JSON report with no prose around it, that check writes no state-log file, and that the fixture keeps its baseline files, refs and empty run root after the runs. It also confirms that the spec folder compatibility block reports the layout map and the era report, or `Compatibility: UNKNOWN` when the fixture cannot run them, and that both compatibility commands write nothing.\n16: \n17: ---\n18: \n19: ## 2. SCENARIO CONTRACT\n20: \n21: - Objective: Prove the check reports the fixture release position and per-unit status, keeps unknown upstream data visible as UNKNOWN, and leaves the checkout, its refs and the state-log paths untouched.\n22: - Playbook ID: DOC-357.\n23: - Real user request: `Check where this checkout stands against the latest spec-kit release.`\n24: - Prompt: `Check where this checkout stands against the latest spec-kit release.`\n25: - Preconditions: The `/doctor:update` fixture at `.worktrees/.doctor-update-test-environment` with its committed fixture units, an empty `git status --porcelain` and no run directory under `.skilled/skills/.state/doctor-update/runs/`, plus a runtime that can execute `/doctor:update` with Bash access. Node and git available. The offline runs need no network reachability.\n26: - Expected execution process: Move into the fixture, record the baseline, run the scoped check with no action token, run the second scoped check for the removed unit, run the `--json` form and the engine directly, capture the dashboards and the report fields, then compare the fixture with the baseline.\n27: - Expected signals: Preflight confirms the current directory is inside the fixture repository and the engine exists. `node .skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/release-update.cjs check --repo . --json` exits 0 when a report is produced and exit 2 is usage failure, and the report carries `schemaVersion`, `command`, `repo`, `head`, `release`, `releaseCommit`, `localLatest`, `upstream.status`, `upstream.latest`, `upstream.error`, `checkout.position`, `checkout.aheadBy`, `checkout.behindBy`, `checkout.dirty`, `status`, `baseRecording`, `units`, `files` and `counts`. The `v4.0.0.2` check reports `skill:sk-code/sk-code-webflow` as `customized`, `skill:sk-code/sk-code-web-dev` as `local` and `skill:sk-git` as `conflict`, and the `v4.0.0.3-fixture` check with `--include-prerelease` reports `skill:sk-code/sk-code-obsidian` as `removed`. Unit statuses stay inside `current`, `local`, `update`, `new`, `customized`, `conflict`, `removed`, `blocked`, `downgrade` and `unknown`, and the report status stays inside `current`, `updates-available`, `blocked` and `unknown`. An offline run reports `upstream.status` unknown with `upstream.error` naming offline mode, so the report status reads `unknown` as well. The dashboard shows `Spec-kit Release Check`, the release position, `Upstream latest`, the checkout line with ahead, behind and dirty values, `Report status`, one quiet line combining the `current` and `local` counts, and a row for every other unit grouped by status. A `--json` run returns the parsed report as one JSON document and omits the prose dashboard and next steps. `current` and `updates-available` map to `STATUS=OK`, `blocked` maps to `STATUS=UNKNOWN` and names the blocked units, and `unknown` maps to `STATUS=UNKNOWN`. A check whose `baseRecording.needed` is true names `/doctor:update record-base --release=<installed-release> [--remote=<framework-remote>]` in its next steps, while the fixture's local base record leaves `baseRecording.needed` false. Unless `--json` was requeste... (line truncated to 2000 chars)\n28: - Desired user-visible outcome: A dashboard that names the fixture release position, upstream latest or UNKNOWN, and the per-unit statuses, recommends a next step, and leaves no trace on the checkout.\n29: - Pass/fail: PASS if the dashboard and the direct engine report carry the release position and the fixture unit statuses `customized`, `local`, `conflict` and `removed`, the offline run keeps upstream UNKNOWN and names offline mode, the JSON run adds no prose, a terminal status is reported, and no checkout file, ref or state-log file changes.\n30: - Classification: Manual scenario. Valid verdicts are `PASS`, `FAIL`, or `SKIP`. Record `SKIP` only when a named environment prerequisite, credential, or command binary is unavailable. A scenario that cannot be run for any other reason is a `FAIL`.\n31: \n32: ---\n33: \n34: ## 3. TEST EXECUTION\n35: \n36: ### Prompt\n37: \n38: ```\n39: Check where this checkout stands against the latest spec-kit release.\n40: ```\n41: \n42: ### Commands\n43: \n44: 1. `cd .worktrees/.doctor-update-test-environment`, then confirm `git status --porcelain` prints nothing and no run directory exists under `.skilled/skills/.state/doctor-update/runs/`. Confirm `git rev-parse --show-toplevel` names the fixture checkout and `.skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/release-update.cjs` exists.\n45: 2. Record the baseline: `git status --porcelain`, `git rev-parse HEAD` and `shasum -a 256 .skilled/skills/.state/doctor-update/base.json`.\n46: 3. Run `/doctor:update --release=v4.0.0.2 --offline --scope=skill:sk-code/sk-code-webflow,skill:sk-code/sk-code-web-dev,skill:sk-git` through the real runtime. The missing action token selects `check`. Capture the complete `v4.0.0.2` dashboard.\n47: 4. Run `/doctor:update check --release=v4.0.0.3-fixture --include-prerelease --offline --scope=skill:sk-code/sk-code-obsidian` and capture the dashboard for the removed unit.\n48: 5. Run `/doctor:update check --release=v4.0.0.2 --offline --scope=skill:sk-code/sk-code-webflow,skill:sk-code/sk-code-web-dev,skill:sk-git --json`. Confirm the reply is one JSON report with no prose dashboard and no next steps.\n49: 6. Run `node .skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/release-update.cjs check --repo . --release v4.0.0.2 --offline --json --scope skill:sk-code/sk-code-webflow,skill:sk-code/sk-code-web-dev,skill:sk-git` directly and record the exit code, each unit's key and status, `upstream.status`, `upstream.error`, `status`, `baseRecording` and every other field listed in the contract.\n50: 7. Run `node .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/upgrade-legacy.mjs --layout-map` and `node .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/repo-era.mjs .` from the fixture root. The fixture is built on v4.0.0.0, which predates both scripts, so both commands are expected to fail there with empty stdout and exit 1. Record each exit code and stderr tail, and confirm that the Spec Folder Compatibility block in the step 3 dashboard reads `Compatibility: UNKNOWN` with that stderr tail.\n51: 8. Confirm no state log appeared under `.skilled/skills/.state/doctor-update/runs/` and that the run root still holds no run directory.\n52: 9. Compare `git status --porcelain` and HEAD with step 2 and confirm the fixture is unchanged.\n53: \n54: ### Expected\n55: \n56: The preflight passes and the engine returns a report. The dashboard renders the release position, upstream latest or UNKNOWN, the ahead and behind counts, the dirty flag, the report status, the combined quiet line and one row per remaining unit. The `v4.0.0.2` run shows `customized`, `local` and `conflict` for the three fixture units. The `v4.0.0.3-fixture` run shows the removed `skill:sk-code/sk-code-obsidian` unit. The offline runs never present unknown upstream data as current, so upstream latest and the report status read UNKNOWN and the offline mode error is visible. The JSON run omits the prose dashboard and the next steps. The dashboard carries the Spec Folder Compatibility block, which reads `Compatibility: UNKNOWN` with the stderr tail on this fixture because both commands are absent from it. The compatibility commands write nothing, so the final comparison still holds.\n57: \n58: Next steps follow the report. A customized or conflict unit offers `/doctor:update align` with the same release and scope. An update or new unit offers `/doctor:update apply`. A removed, blocked or unknown unit gets its status explanation and no automatic-apply recommendation. A downgrade unit explains that apply never writes it. A report with nothing to do says the selected units are current or local, and a report whose base recording is needed names the record-base action with the installed release.\n59: \n60: Check writes only an in-memory result, so no state-log file appears and the checkout files and refs keep their baseline content. The fixture ends with an empty `git status --porcelain` and no run directory under `.skilled/skills/.state/doctor-update/runs/`.\n61: \n62: ### Evidence\n63: \n64: - The preflight observations for the fixture git repository, the engine path and the empty run root.\n65: - The complete `v4.0.0.2` dashboard from the no-action run, with `skill:sk-code/sk-code-webflow` as `customized`, `skill:sk-code/sk-code-web-dev` as `local` and `skill:sk-git` as `conflict`.\n66: - The `v4.0.0.3-fixture` dashboard with `skill:sk-code/sk-code-obsidian` reported as `removed`.\n67: - The offline upstream block with `upstream.status`, `upstream.error` and the terminal status.\n68: - The `--json` reply and the observation that no prose was added around it.\n69: - The direct engine run with its exit code and parsed report fields, including each unit's status.\n70: - The listing of `.skilled/skills/.state/doctor-update/runs/` showing no new state log.\n71: - The exit code and stderr tail of each compatibility command, and the Spec Folder Compatibility block from the step 3 dashboard.\n72: - The comparison of `git status --porcelain` and HEAD from steps 2 and 9.\n73: \n74: ### Pass / Fail\n75: \n76: - **Pass**: The dashboard and the engine report carry the release position and the fixture unit statuses `customized`, `local`, `conflict` and `removed`, the offline runs keep upstream UNKNOWN and name offline mode, the JSON run adds no prose, the compatibility block is present and reads `Compatibility: UNKNOWN` with its stderr tail on this fixture, a terminal status is reported, and no checkout file, ref or state-log file changes.\n77: - **Fail**: Unknown upstream data is presented as current, a state log appears, a checkout file or ref changes, the JSON reply carries prose, a fixture unit reports another status, the compatibility block is missing from the prose dashboard, or a required report field or dashboard section is missing.\n78: \n79: ### Failure Triage\n80: \n81: If the preflight stops, inspect the git repository check and the engine path in `doctor-update-check.yaml`. If a fixture unit reports another status, compare its files across `v4.0.0.0`, the fixture and the release with `git diff --name-status`, because each status comes from the three-way classification in `release-update.cjs`. If the offline run still reaches the network, inspect the offline flag handling and its engine mapping. If a unit status falls outside the listed values, preserve it visibly as unknown and inspect the engine status mapping. If a checkout file or ref changes, the check crossed its mutation boundary, which is a failure of the read-only invariant. If a compatibility command runs on a fixture that carries both scripts and the block still reads UNKNOWN, read its stderr tail. If a Layout line disagrees with the layout map, check that the compatibility phase reads the map state and not the era report. The fixture predates both scripts, so its UNKNOWN block is the expected result until the fixture is rebuilt with them.\n82: \n83: ---\n84: \n85: ## 4. SOURCE FILES\n86: \n87: - Root playbook: [manual-testing-playbook.md](../manual-testing-playbook.md)\n88: - Command entrypoint: [.skilled/commands/doctor/update.md](../../commands/doctor/update.md)\n89: - Matching YAML asset: [.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-update-check.yaml](../../commands/doctor/assets/doctor-update-check.yaml)\n90: - Presentation contract: [.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-update-presentation.txt](../../commands/doctor/assets/doctor-update-presentation.txt)\n91: - Engine: [.skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/release-update.cjs](../../commands/doctor/scripts/release-update.cjs)\n92: - Layout map: [upgrade-legacy.mjs](../../skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/upgrade-legacy.mjs)\n93: - Era report: [repo-era.mjs](../../skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/repo-era.mjs)\n94: - Route manifest: [.skilled/commands/doctor/_routes.yaml](../../commands/doctor/_routes.yaml)\n95: - Environment guide: [doctor-commands README](README.md)\n96: \n97: Provenance: manual only - /doctor:update check\n98: \n99: ---\n100: \n101: ## 5. SOURCE METADATA\n102: \n103: - Group: Doctor commands\n104: - Playbook ID: DOC-357\n105: - Feature name: Doctor update check\n106: - Command mode: `/doctor:update check`\n107: - YAML asset: `doctor-update-check.yaml`\n108: - Mutation boundary: The fixture checkout and its refs stay read-only. The engine may fetch a release commit it lacks into the git object store and `FETCH_HEAD`, which creates no ref, and `--offline` prevents every fetch. The scenario reports the `customized`, `local`, `conflict` and `removed` fixture units and writes none of their files. Check writes no state-log file.\n109: - Feature file path: `doctor-commands/doctor-update-check.md`","title":"read","metadata":{"metadata":{"truncated":false},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Read file .skilled/manual-testing-playbook/doctor-commands/doctor-update-check.md, lines 1-109\n1: ---\n2: title: \"DOC-357 -- Doctor update check\"\n3: description: \"Manual scenario validating that /doctor:update check on the shared update fixture reports the release position, upstream latest and per-unit status, keeps unavailable upstream data visible as UNKNOWN, and writes no checkout file or state log.\"\n4: version: 1.2.0.0\n5: id: doctor-commands-doctor-update-check\n6: expected_workflow_mode: UNKNOWN\n7: expected_leaf_resources: []\n8: ---\n9: # DOC-357 -- Doctor update check\n10: \n11: ## 1. OVERVIEW\n12: \n13: This scenario validates the default action of `/doctor:update` against the shared doctor update fixture at `.worktrees/.doctor-update-test-environment`. A `/doctor:update` invocation with no action token runs `check`, which reports where the fixture stands against a named release: the release position, the ahead and behind counts, the upstream latest release or UNKNOWN, and every unit status. Check is read-only for the checkout. The only network write it may perform is a release-commit fetch into the git object store, which creates no ref, and `--offline` prevents every fetch.\n14: \n15: The scenario also confirms that unavailable upstream data stays visible as UNKNOWN, that a `--json` run returns one JSON report with no prose around it, that check writes no state-log file, and that the fixture keeps its baseline files, refs and empty run root after the runs. It also confirms that the spec folder compatibility block reports the layout map and the era report, or `Compatibility: UNKNOWN` when the fixture cannot run them, and that both compatibility commands write nothing.\n16: \n17: ---\n18: \n19: ## 2. SCENARIO CONTRACT\n20: \n21: - Objective: Prove the check reports the fixture release position and per-unit status, keeps unknown upstream data visible as UNKNOWN, and leaves the checkout, its refs and the state-log paths untouched.\n22: - Playbook ID: DOC-357.\n23: - Real user request: `Check where this checkout stands against the latest spec-kit release.`\n24: - Prompt: `Check where this checkout stands against the latest spec-kit release.`\n25: - Preconditions: The `/doctor:update` fixture at `.worktrees/.doctor-update-test-environment` with its committed fixture units, an empty `git status --porcelain` and no run directory under `.skilled/skills/.state/doctor-update/runs/`, plus a runtime that can execute `/doctor:update` with Bash access. Node and git available. The offline runs need no network reachability.\n26: - Expected execution process: Move into the fixture, record the baseline, run the scoped check with no action token, run the second scoped check for the removed unit, run the `--json` form and the engine directly, capture the dashboards and the report fields, then compare the fixture with the baseline.\n27: - Expected signals: Preflight confirms the current directory is inside the fixture repository and the engine exists. `node .skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/release-update.cjs check --repo . --json` exits 0 when a report is produced and exit 2 is usage failure, and the report carries `schemaVersion`, `command`, `repo`, `head`, `release`, `releaseCommit`, `localLatest`, `upstream.status`, `upstream.latest`, `upstream.error`, `checkout.position`, `checkout.aheadBy`, `checkout.behindBy`, `checkout.dirty`, `status`, `baseRecording`, `units`, `files` and `counts`. The `v4.0.0.2` check reports `skill:sk-code/sk-code-webflow` as `customized`, `skill:sk-code/sk-code-web-dev` as `local` and `skill:sk-git` as `conflict`, and the `v4.0.0.3-fixture` check with `--include-prerelease` reports `skill:sk-code/sk-code-obsidian` as `removed`. Unit statuses stay inside `current`, `local`, `update`, `new`, `customized`, `conflict`, `removed`, `blocked`, `downgrade` and `unknown`, and the report status stays inside `current`, `updates-available`, `blocked` and `unknown`. An offline run reports `upstream.status` unknown with `upstream.error` naming offline mode, so the report status reads `unknown` as well. The dashboard shows `Spec-kit Release Check`, the release position, `Upstream latest`, the checkout line with ahead, behind and dirty values, `Report status`, one quiet line combining the `current` and `local` counts, and a row for every other unit grouped by status. A `--json` run returns the parsed report as one JSON document and omits the prose dashboard and next steps. `current` and `updates-available` map to `STATUS=OK`, `blocked` maps to `STATUS=UNKNOWN` and names the blocked units, and `unknown` maps to `STATUS=UNKNOWN`. A check whose `baseRecording.needed` is true names `/doctor:update record-base --release=<installed-release> [--remote=<framework-remote>]` in its next steps, while the fixture's local base record leaves `baseRecording.needed` false. Unless `--json` was requeste... (line truncated to 2000 chars)\n28: - Desired user-visible outcome: A dashboard that names the fixture release position, upstream latest or UNKNOWN, and the per-unit statuses, recommends a next step, and leaves no trace on the checkout.\n29: - Pass/fail: PASS if the dashboard and the direct engine report carry the release position and the fixture unit statuses `customized`, `local`, `conflict` and `removed`, the offline run keeps upstream UNKNOWN and names offline mode, the JSON run adds no prose, a terminal status is reported, and no checkout file, ref or state-log file changes.\n30: - Classification: Manual scenario. Valid verdicts are `PASS`, `FAIL`, or `SKIP`. Record `SKIP` only when a named environment prerequisite, credential, or command binary is unavailable. A scenario that cannot be run for any other reason is a `FAIL`.\n31: \n32: ---\n33: \n34: ## 3. TEST EXECUTION\n35: \n36: ### Prompt\n37: \n38: ```\n39: Check where this checkout stands against the latest spec-kit release.\n40: ```\n41: \n42: ### Commands\n43: \n44: 1. `cd .worktrees/.doctor-update-test-environment`, then confirm `git status --porcelain` prints nothing and no run directory exists under `.skilled/skills/.state/doctor-update/runs/`. Confirm `git rev-parse --show-toplevel` names the fixture checkout and `.skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/release-update.cjs` exists.\n45: 2. Record the baseline: `git status --porcelain`, `git rev-parse HEAD` and `shasum -a 256 .skilled/skills/.state/doctor-update/base.json`.\n46: 3. Run `/doctor:update --release=v4.0.0.2 --offline --scope=skill:sk-code/sk-code-webflow,skill:sk-code/sk-code-web-dev,skill:sk-git` through the real runtime. The missing action token selects `check`. Capture the complete `v4.0.0.2` dashboard.\n47: 4. Run `/doctor:update check --release=v4.0.0.3-fixture --include-prerelease --offline --scope=skill:sk-code/sk-code-obsidian` and capture the dashboard for the removed unit.\n48: 5. Run `/doctor:update check --release=v4.0.0.2 --offline --scope=skill:sk-code/sk-code-webflow,skill:sk-code/sk-code-web-dev,skill:sk-git --json`. Confirm the reply is one JSON report with no prose dashboard and no next steps.\n49: 6. Run `node .skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/release-update.cjs check --repo . --release v4.0.0.2 --offline --json --scope skill:sk-code/sk-code-webflow,skill:sk-code/sk-code-web-dev,skill:sk-git` directly and record the exit code, each unit's key and status, `upstream.status`, `upstream.error`, `status`, `baseRecording` and every other field listed in the contract.\n50: 7. Run `node .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/upgrade-legacy.mjs --layout-map` and `node .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/repo-era.mjs .` from the fixture root. The fixture is built on v4.0.0.0, which predates both scripts, so both commands are expected to fail there with empty stdout and exit 1. Record each exit code and stderr tail, and confirm that the Spec Folder Compatibility block in the step 3 dashboard reads `Compatibility: UNKNOWN` with that stderr tail.\n51: 8. Confirm no state log appeared under `.skilled/skills/.state/doctor-update/runs/` and that the run root still holds no run directory.\n52: 9. Compare `git status --porcelain` and HEAD with step 2 and confirm the fixture is unchanged.\n53: \n54: ### Expected\n55: \n56: The preflight passes and the engine returns a report. The dashboard renders the release position, upstream latest or UNKNOWN, the ahead and behind counts, the dirty flag, the report status, the combined quiet line and one row per remaining unit. The `v4.0.0.2` run shows `customized`, `local` and `conflict` for the three fixture units. The `v4.0.0.3-fixture` run shows the removed `skill:sk-code/sk-code-obsidian` unit. The offline runs never present unknown upstream data as current, so upstream latest and the report status read UNKNOWN and the offline mode error is visible. The JSON run omits the prose dashboard and the next steps. The dashboard carries the Spec Folder Compatibility block, which reads `Compatibility: UNKNOWN` with the stderr tail on this fixture because both commands are absent from it. The compatibility commands write nothing, so the final comparison still holds.\n57: \n58: Next steps follow the report. A customized or conflict unit offers `/doctor:update align` with the same release and scope. An update or new unit offers `/doctor:update apply`. A removed, blocked or unknown unit gets its status explanation and no automatic-apply recommendation. A downgrade unit explains that apply never writes it. A report with nothing to do says the selected units are current or local, and a report whose base recording is needed names the record-base action with the installed release.\n59: \n60: Check writes only an in-memory result, so no state-log file appears and the checkout files and refs keep their baseline content. The fixture ends with an empty `git status --porcelain` and no run directory under `.skilled/skills/.state/doctor-update/runs/`.\n61: \n62: ### Evidence\n63: \n64: - The preflight observations for the fixture git repository, the engine path and the empty run root.\n65: - The complete `v4.0.0.2` dashboard from the no-action run, with `skill:sk-code/sk-code-webflow` as `customized`, `skill:sk-code/sk-code-web-dev` as `local` and `skill:sk-git` as `conflict`.\n66: - The `v4.0.0.3-fixture` dashboard with `skill:sk-code/sk-code-obsidian` reported as `removed`.\n67: - The offline upstream block with `upstream.status`, `upstream.error` and the terminal status.\n68: - The `--json` reply and the observation that no prose was added around it.\n69: - The direct engine run with its exit code and parsed report fields, including each unit's status.\n70: - The listing of `.skilled/skills/.state/doctor-update/runs/` showing no new state log.\n71: - The exit code and stderr tail of each compatibility command, and the Spec Folder Compatibility block from the step 3 dashboard.\n72: - The comparison of `git status --porcelain` and HEAD from steps 2 and 9.\n73: \n74: ### Pass / Fail\n75: \n76: - **Pass**: The dashboard and the engine report carry the release position and the fixture unit statuses `customized`, `local`, `conflict` and `removed`, the offline runs keep upstream UNKNOWN and name offline mode, the JSON run adds no prose, the compatibility block is present and reads `Compatibility: UNKNOWN` with its stderr tail on this fixture, a terminal status is reported, and no checkout file, ref or state-log file changes.\n77: - **Fail**: Unknown upstream data is presented as current, a state log appears, a checkout file or ref changes, the JSON reply carries prose, a fixture unit reports another status, the compatibility block is missing from the prose dashboard, or a required report field or dashboard section is missing.\n78: \n79: ### Failure Triage\n80: \n81: If the preflight stops, inspect the git repository check and the engine path in `doctor-update-check.yaml`. If a fixture unit reports another status, compare its files across `v4.0.0.0`, the fixture and the release with `git diff --name-status`, because each status comes from the three-way classification in `release-update.cjs`. If the offline run still reaches the network, inspect the offline flag handling and its engine mapping. If a unit status falls outside the listed values, preserve it visibly as unknown and inspect the engine status mapping. If a checkout file or ref changes, the check crossed its mutation boundary, which is a failure of the read-only invariant. If a compatibility command runs on a fixture that carries both scripts and the block still reads UNKNOWN, read its stderr tail. If a Layout line disagrees with the layout map, check that the compatibility phase reads the map state and not the era report. The fixture predates both scripts, so its UNKNOWN block is the expected result until the fixture is rebuilt with them.\n82: \n83: ---\n84: \n85: ## 4. SOURCE FILES\n86: \n87: - Root playbook: [manual-testing-playbook.md](../manual-testing-playbook.md)\n88: - Command entrypoint: [.skilled/commands/doctor/update.md](../../commands/doctor/update.md)\n89: - Matching YAML asset: [.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-update-check.yaml](../../commands/doctor/assets/doctor-update-check.yaml)\n90: - Presentation contract: [.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-update-presentation.txt](../../commands/doctor/assets/doctor-update-presentation.txt)\n91: - Engine: [.skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/release-update.cjs](../../commands/doctor/scripts/release-update.cjs)\n92: - Layout map: [upgrade-legacy.mjs](../../skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/upgrade-legacy.mjs)\n93: - Era report: [repo-era.mjs](../../skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/repo-era.mjs)\n94: - Route manifest: [.skilled/commands/doctor/_routes.yaml](../../commands/doctor/_routes.yaml)\n95: - Environment guide: [doctor-commands README](README.md)\n96: \n97: Provenance: manual only - /doctor:update check\n98: \n99: ---\n100: \n101: ## 5. SOURCE METADATA\n102: \n103: - Group: Doctor commands\n104: - Playbook ID: DOC-357\n105: - Feature name: Doctor update check\n106: - Command mode: `/doctor:update check`\n107: - YAML asset: `doctor-update-check.yaml`\n108: - Mutation boundary: The fixture checkout and its refs stay read-only. The engine may fetch a release commit it lacks into the git object store and `FETCH_HEAD`, which creates no ref, and `--offline` prevents every fetch. The scenario reports the `customized`, `local`, `conflict` and `removed` fixture units and writes none of their files. Check writes no state-log file.\n109: - Feature file path: `doctor-commands/doctor-update-check.md`"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"limit\": 110, \"path\": \".skilled/manual-testing-playbook/doctor-commands/doctor-update-check.md\"}"},"time":{"start":1794670764038,"end":1794670765982}}}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794670765998,"sessionID":"ses_e255ff46effe7EWyuOLOEwVdy1","part":{"partID":"prt_1dab69ff6001ncMrb1EulXEqdu","sessionID":"ses_e255ff46effe7EWyuOLOEwVdy1","messageID":"msg_1dab65c94001re0hvhsUzXh4mK","type":"tool","id":"chatcmpl-tool-b468d9887c8859a7","tool":"read","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"limit":110,"path":".skilled/manual-testing-playbook/doctor-commands/doctor-setup-run.md"},"output":"Read file .skilled/manual-testing-playbook/doctor-commands/doctor-setup-run.md, lines 1-110\n1: ---\n2: title: \"DOC-391 -- Doctor setup umbrella run\"\n3: description: \"Manual scenario validating that /doctor:setup lists every doctor target with what it checks, runs the five read-only legs once, names the repair command for each failing leg and leaves the working tree unchanged.\"\n4: version: 1.0.9.0\n5: id: doctor-commands-doctor-setup-run\n6: expected_workflow_mode: UNKNOWN\n7: expected_leaf_resources: []\n8: ---\n9: \n10: # DOC-391 -- Doctor setup umbrella run\n11: \n12: ## 1. OVERVIEW\n13: \n14: This scenario validates `/doctor:setup`, the umbrella diagnostic that lists every doctor target with what it checks, runs five read-only legs once and names the doctor command that repairs each failing leg.\n15: \n16: The run writes nothing in the repository. The advisor leg's CLI creates its socket directory, `/tmp/system-skill-advisor` by default, when that directory is absent, and the working-tree comparison cannot see that write. The scenario records the working tree before and after, and it checks that an unexpected argument fails with the documented wording.\n17: \n18: ---\n19: \n20: ## 2. SCENARIO CONTRACT\n21: \n22: - Objective: Prove `/doctor:setup` prints the 25-command target table, runs all five read-only legs, names the mapped repair command for each failing leg, ends with a status that agrees with the leg results, leaves the working tree unchanged and rejects an unexpected argument.\n23: - Playbook ID: DOC-391.\n24: - Real user request: `/doctor:setup`\n25: - Prompt: `/doctor:setup`\n26: - Preconditions: The advisor runtime is built (`npm --prefix .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime run build` exits 0) and the bridge projection is fresh (`node .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/command-bridges/derive-command-bridges.cjs --check` prints `\"status\": \"fresh\"`). Every command runs from the repository root.\n27: - Expected execution process: Record `git status --porcelain` into `/tmp/doc-391-before.txt`. Run `/doctor:setup` in an AI session, or run the five legs directly and record each exit code and last line. Record `git status --porcelain` into `/tmp/doc-391-after.txt` and diff the two files. Run `/doctor:setup extra` and read the argument error.\n28: - Expected signals:\n29:   - The command prints the target table first. It has 25 rows and starts with `/doctor:setup`. It includes `/doctor:env list`, `/doctor:git setup`, `/doctor:sk-code quality` and `/doctor:ci report`.\n30:   - The command prints one row per leg with PASS, FAIL, SKIP, DEGRADED or ERROR. Every failing leg names its mapped repair command: sk-code -> `/doctor:sk-code setup`, sk-git -> `/doctor:git setup`, trigger-index -> `/doctor:speckit`, runtime-mirrors -> `/doctor:runtime-mirrors` and advisor -> `npm --prefix .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime run build` for stale builds or `/doctor:skill-advisor rebuild` for other failures.\n31:   - The advisor reports PASS for exit 0 when `data.freshness` is `live`. Any other freshness on exit 0 is DEGRADED and names `/doctor:skill-advisor rebuild`.\n32:   - The advisor reports FAIL for exit 75 when stderr JSON includes `staleDistWarning`. Its repair command is `npm --prefix .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime run build`. Exit 75 without that field is SKIP because the daemon is stopped. Any other advisor exit is FAIL and names `/doctor:skill-advisor rebuild`.\n33:   - A sk-git exit 2 is ERROR because it indicates a usage error or crash. Exit 3 is DEGRADED, never FAIL.\n34:   - The step 3 diff is empty. Step 4 prints `Unknown argument: extra`, then `/doctor:setup takes no target and no flag. Run /doctor:setup on its own.` and ends with `STATUS=FAIL ERROR=\"unknown_argument\"`. The result ends with `STATUS=OK`, `STATUS=FAIL` or `STATUS=ERROR`, according to the leg results.\n35: - Desired user-visible outcome: A first-run overview of every doctor target plus a per-leg verdict and repair line, so the operator knows which doctor command to run next without the diagnostic writing anything.\n36: - Pass/fail: Through `/doctor:setup`, PASS needs the target table, all five leg rows, the correct repair command on every FAIL row, a final status that agrees with all leg results including ERROR, and an empty diff. Through the direct legs, PASS needs all five legs run with their exit code and last line recorded, each leg classified by the rules in Expected including advisor JSON freshness and stderr plus sk-git exit 2 as ERROR, a mapped repair named for every FAIL, an empty diff and step 4 recorded as not run.\n37: - Classification: Manual scenario. Valid verdicts are `PASS`, `FAIL`, or `SKIP`. Record `SKIP` only when a named environment prerequisite, credential, or command binary is unavailable. A scenario that cannot be run for any other reason is a `FAIL`.\n38: \n39: ---\n40: \n41: ## 3. TEST EXECUTION\n42: \n43: ### Prompt\n44: \n45: ```\n46: /doctor:setup\n47: ```\n48: \n49: ### Commands\n50: \n51: Run every command from the repository root.\n52: \n53: 1. Run `git status --porcelain > /tmp/doc-391-before.txt`.\n54: \n55: 2. In an AI session in this repository, run `/doctor:setup`. An agent without slash commands runs the five legs directly instead, each from the repository root, recording exit code and last line. Replace `<name>` with the runtime running the scenario: claude, codex, devin, cursor, opencode or pi. On any other runtime, drop `--tool=<name>`:\n56: \n57: ```bash\n58: node .skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/sk-code-setup-check.cjs\n59: node .skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/git-setup-check.cjs --tool=<name>\n60: node .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/retrieval/generate-trigger-index.mjs --check --json\n61: node .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/runtime-mirrors/sync-runtime-mirrors.cjs --check\n62: node .skilled/bin/skill-advisor.cjs advisor_status --workspace-root \"$PWD\" --format json --timeout-ms 500 --warm-only\n63: ```\n64: \n65: 3. Run `git status --porcelain > /tmp/doc-391-after.txt` and `diff /tmp/doc-391-before.txt /tmp/doc-391-after.txt`.\n66: \n67: 4. Run `/doctor:setup extra` in the AI session. When no AI session is available, record step 4 as not run. It does not change the verdict.\n68: \n69: ### Expected\n70: \n71: When step 2 runs `/doctor:setup` in an AI session, it prints the doctor target table first. When the five legs run directly, there is no table. Check each exit code and the advisor JSON. Exit 0 passes for sk-code, sk-git, trigger-index and runtime-mirrors. Advisor exit 0 with `data.freshness` set to `live` is PASS. Any other freshness is DEGRADED and names `/doctor:skill-advisor rebuild`. Exit 75 with `staleDistWarning` in stderr JSON is FAIL and names `npm --prefix .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime run build`. Exit 75 without that field is SKIP because the daemon is stopped. Any other advisor exit is FAIL and names `/doctor:skill-advisor rebuild`. A sk-git exit 2 is ERROR for a usage error or crash. Exit 3 is DEGRADED. Any other sk-git exit is FAIL. Any other nonzero exit is FAIL. The table has 25 rows. It starts with `/doctor:setup` and includes `/doctor:env list` and `/doctor:git setup`.\n72: \n73: Then the command prints one row per leg with PASS, FAIL, SKIP, DEGRADED or ERROR. The mapped repair commands are sk-code -> `/doctor:sk-code setup`, sk-git -> `/doctor:git setup`, trigger-index -> `/doctor:speckit` and runtime-mirrors -> `/doctor:runtime-mirrors`. The advisor shows the build command for a stale build and `/doctor:skill-advisor rebuild` for other FAIL or DEGRADED results. Exit 75 without `staleDistWarning` is SKIP because the daemon is stopped. A sk-git exit 2 shows ERROR. Exit 3 shows DEGRADED, never FAIL. After the leg rows, a `Last session hop:` line shows the newest hop history entry, or says no hop is recorded yet. While a handoff note is still open, an `open notes:` line follows it with the count and the oldest note. An orphans line follows, either `orphans: none` or the count, the size and the `--reap` command that lists them. All three are information only and never change the status.\n74: \n75: Through `/doctor:setup`, the run ends with a `DOCTOR DIAGNOSTIC RESULT` block whose last line is `STATUS=OK`, `STATUS=FAIL` or `STATUS=ERROR`. The status agrees with the leg results. `STATUS=ERROR` means a leg reports ERROR or its output cannot be read. The direct legs print no combined block.\n76: \n77: The step 3 diff is empty, because the run writes nothing in the repository.\n78: \n79: The step 4 command prints `Unknown argument: extra`, then `/doctor:setup takes no target and no flag. Run /doctor:setup on its own.` and ends with `STATUS=FAIL ERROR=\"unknown_argument\"`.\n80: \n81: ### Evidence\n82: \n83: - The target table from step 2, with its row count.\n84: - The five leg rows and their results.\n85: - The `DOCTOR DIAGNOSTIC RESULT` block and its last line, on the slash-command path.\n86: - The step 3 diff output.\n87: - The step 4 argument error block.\n88: \n89: ### Pass / Fail\n90: \n91: - **Pass**: Through `/doctor:setup`, PASS needs the target table, all five leg rows, a mapped repair command on every FAIL row, a final status that agrees with the leg results including ERROR cases and an empty diff. Through the direct legs, PASS needs all five legs run with their exit code and last line recorded, each leg classified as PASS, FAIL, SKIP, DEGRADED or ERROR by the rules in Expected, a mapped repair named for every FAIL, an empty diff and step 4 recorded as not run.\n92: - **Fail**: Any leg is missing, a repair command is wrong, the status disagrees, or any file changed.\n93: \n94: ### Failure Triage\n95: \n96: If a file changed, find which leg wrote it and compare with the read-only invariant in `.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-setup.yaml`. If the target table is short, compare it with section 2 of `doctor-setup-presentation.txt`.\n97: \n98: ---\n99: \n100: ## 4. SOURCE FILES\n101: \n102: - Root playbook: [manual-testing-playbook.md](../manual-testing-playbook.md)\n103: - Feature catalog: [scorer-fusion/doctor-command-routing.md](../../skills/system-skill-advisor/feature-catalog/scorer-fusion/doctor-command-routing.md)\n104: - Command entrypoint: [.skilled/commands/doctor/setup.md](../../commands/doctor/setup.md)\n105: - Matching YAML asset: [.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-setup.yaml](../../commands/doctor/assets/doctor-setup.yaml)\n106: - Presentation contract: [.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-setup-presentation.txt](../../commands/doctor/assets/doctor-setup-presentation.txt)\n107: - Route manifest: [.skilled/commands/doctor/_routes.yaml](../../commands/doctor/_routes.yaml)\n108: \n109: ---\n110: \n[Output truncated. Continue reading with offset: 111]","title":"read","metadata":{"metadata":{"truncated":true},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Read file .skilled/manual-testing-playbook/doctor-commands/doctor-setup-run.md, lines 1-110\n1: ---\n2: title: \"DOC-391 -- Doctor setup umbrella run\"\n3: description: \"Manual scenario validating that /doctor:setup lists every doctor target with what it checks, runs the five read-only legs once, names the repair command for each failing leg and leaves the working tree unchanged.\"\n4: version: 1.0.9.0\n5: id: doctor-commands-doctor-setup-run\n6: expected_workflow_mode: UNKNOWN\n7: expected_leaf_resources: []\n8: ---\n9: \n10: # DOC-391 -- Doctor setup umbrella run\n11: \n12: ## 1. OVERVIEW\n13: \n14: This scenario validates `/doctor:setup`, t