other freshness is DEGRADED and names `/doctor:skill-advisor rebuild`. Exit 75 with `staleDistWarning` in stderr JSON is FAIL and names `npm --prefix .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime run build`. Exit 75 without that field is SKIP because the daemon is stopped. Any other advisor exit is FAIL and names `/doctor:skill-advisor rebuild`. A sk-git exit 2 is ERROR for a usage error or crash. Exit 3 is DEGRADED. Any other sk-git exit is FAIL. Any other nonzero exit is FAIL. The table has 25 rows. It starts with `/doctor:setup` and includes `/doctor:env list` and `/doctor:git setup`.\n72: \n73: Then the command prints one row per leg with PASS, FAIL, SKIP, DEGRADED or ERROR. The mapped repair commands are sk-code -> `/doctor:sk-code setup`, sk-git -> `/doctor:git setup`, trigger-index -> `/doctor:speckit` and runtime-mirrors -> `/doctor:runtime-mirrors`. The advisor shows the build command for a stale build and `/doctor:skill-advisor rebuild` for other FAIL or DEGRADED results. Exit 75 without `staleDistWarning` is SKIP because the daemon is stopped. A sk-git exit 2 shows ERROR. Exit 3 shows DEGRADED, never FAIL. After the leg rows, a `Last session hop:` line shows the newest hop history entry, or says no hop is recorded yet. While a handoff note is still open, an `open notes:` line follows it with the count and the oldest note. An orphans line follows, either `orphans: none` or the count, the size and the `--reap` command that lists them. All three are information only and never change the status.\n74: \n75: Through `/doctor:setup`, the run ends with a `DOCTOR DIAGNOSTIC RESULT` block whose last line is `STATUS=OK`, `STATUS=FAIL` or `STATUS=ERROR`. The status agrees with the leg results. `STATUS=ERROR` means a leg reports ERROR or its output cannot be read. The direct legs print no combined block.\n76: \n77: The step 3 diff is empty, because the run writes nothing in the repository.\n78: \n79: The step 4 command prints `Unknown argument: extra`, then `/doctor:setup takes no target and no flag. Run /doctor:setup on its own.` and ends with `STATUS=FAIL ERROR=\"unknown_argument\"`.\n80: \n81: ### Evidence\n82: \n83: - The target table from step 2, with its row count.\n84: - The five leg rows and their results.\n85: - The `DOCTOR DIAGNOSTIC RESULT` block and its last line, on the slash-command path.\n86: - The step 3 diff output.\n87: - The step 4 argument error block.\n88: \n89: ### Pass / Fail\n90: \n91: - **Pass**: Through `/doctor:setup`, PASS needs the target table, all five leg rows, a mapped repair command on every FAIL row, a final status that agrees with the leg results including ERROR cases and an empty diff. Through the direct legs, PASS needs all five legs run with their exit code and last line recorded, each leg classified as PASS, FAIL, SKIP, DEGRADED or ERROR by the rules in Expected, a mapped repair named for every FAIL, an empty diff and step 4 recorded as not run.\n92: - **Fail**: Any leg is missing, a repair command is wrong, the status disagrees, or any file changed.\n93: \n94: ### Failure Triage\n95: \n96: If a file changed, find which leg wrote it and compare with the read-only invariant in `.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-setup.yaml`. If the target table is short, compare it with section 2 of `doctor-setup-presentation.txt`.\n97: \n98: ---\n99: \n100: ## 4. SOURCE FILES\n101: \n102: - Root playbook: [manual-testing-playbook.md](../manual-testing-playbook.md)\n103: - Feature catalog: [scorer-fusion/doctor-command-routing.md](../../skills/system-skill-advisor/feature-catalog/scorer-fusion/doctor-command-routing.md)\n104: - Command entrypoint: [.skilled/commands/doctor/setup.md](../../commands/doctor/setup.md)\n105: - Matching YAML asset: [.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-setup.yaml](../../commands/doctor/assets/doctor-setup.yaml)\n106: - Presentation contract: [.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-setup-presentation.txt](../../commands/doctor/assets/doctor-setup-presentation.txt)\n107: - Route manifest: [.skilled/commands/doctor/_routes.yaml](../../commands/doctor/_routes.yaml)\n108: \n109: ---\n110: \n[Output truncated. Continue reading with offset: 111]"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"limit\": 110, \"path\": \".skilled/manual-testing-playbook/doctor-commands/doctor-setup-run.md\"}"},"time":{"start":1794670764022,"end":1794670765998}}}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794670766020,"sessionID":"ses_e255ff46effe7EWyuOLOEwVdy1","part":{"partID":"prt_1dab69ff5002mOKwT0dU5CtuuV","sessionID":"ses_e255ff46effe7EWyuOLOEwVdy1","messageID":"msg_1dab65c94001re0hvhsUzXh4mK","type":"tool","id":"chatcmpl-tool-847026d3941a13ac","tool":"read","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"path":".skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/feature-catalog/scorer-fusion/doctor-command-routing.md"},"output":"Read file .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/feature-catalog/scorer-fusion/doctor-command-routing.md, lines 1-82\n1: ---\n2: title: \"Doctor Command Routing\"\n3: description: \"Doctor routes from the doctor route manifest become advisor command bridges, so setup and health prompts surface a runnable /doctor:x line.\"\n4: trigger_phrases:\n5:   - \"doctor command routing\"\n6:   - \"doctor command bridges\"\n7:   - \"runnable doctor command line\"\n8:   - \"doctor setup hint\"\n9:   - \"/doctor:setup\"\n10: version: 1.0.13.0\n11: ---\n12: \n13: # Doctor Command Routing\n14: \n15: ## 1. OVERVIEW\n16: \n17: Doctor routes from the doctor route manifest become advisor command bridges, so setup and health prompts surface a runnable /doctor:x line.\n18: \n19: A passing skill keeps first place on a contested prompt and the doctor command shows as a second line. A doctor phrase listed in its route's `lead_phrases` is the exception: it ranks the doctor command first, which is how `check my environment variables` keeps `/doctor:env` ahead of system-spec-kit. The Python fallback matches a doctor bridge only on a typed slash command.\n20: \n21: ---\n22: \n23: ## 2. HOW IT WORKS\n24: \n25: ### Bridge Generation\n26: \n27: `derive-command-bridges.cjs` reads `.skilled/commands/doctor/_routes.yaml` as a third inventory source. Each route becomes one bridge `command-doctor-<command>-<target>`, or `command-doctor-<command>` when the command owns one route. Each standalone command becomes one bridge. Each `mcp_subroutes` entry becomes one bridge `command-doctor-mcp-<sub_action>`. The owning skill comes from the router's `skill_agent` tag. Each route needs a hand-written entry in both the `typescript` and `python` lists in `scoring-compatibility.json`. The deriver fills the TypeScript keywords from the manifest's trigger phrases and the Python slash markers from the runnable string, plus the bare command for a route that declares `default_target`. Every derived doctor bridge is active, `command-doctor-helper`, the three `command-doctor-agents-md-*` bridges, the three `command-doctor-symlink-*` bridges and `command-doctor-install` included, so the activation list names a bridge once and the reach probe proves every phrase it carries; a route added without its entry stays derived and unrouted until that entry lands. A route whose manifest class is `read-only` also gets `readOnly: true` in its generated bridge.\n28: \n29: ### Ranking\n30: \n31: A doctor bridge passes on its own wording, an explicit-author match on one of its manifest phrases or its runnable string. With the local embedder running it can also pass on meaning, as [command-meaning-matching.md](./command-meaning-matching.md) describes. When none passes and none was typed, the scorer asks `/doctor:helper`'s ranker whether the prompt describes a doctor problem, and if it does the command the ranker puts first passes by name when its policy is `run`, and `/doctor:helper` passes instead when that command asks first or has no bridge. A prompt that asks for a `repair path` or says `I have a problem`, with no ranked command and no passing skill, gets `/doctor:helper`. `stopped converging` counts as a wrong state beside a passing skill. Beside a passing skill this needs a wrong state or health check in the prompt, so ordinary requests that share doctor words get no doctor line. A `/doctor:` command counts as typed when the prompt starts with `/doctor:` or when it directly follows `run`, `execute`, `start`, `launch`, `use` or `kick off` outside quotes and backticks. A quoted command or a bare mid-sentence mention does not count. A typed command puts its own passing bridge first. For other prompts, a passing skill stays first and passing doctor bridges sit right after the second passing skill or the only passing skill. This keeps a doctor line within the CLI's three shown results. Doctor bridges never change skill scores. The scorer computes skill ambiguity and abstention as if no doctor bridge existed. The Python native wrapper keeps the same order. A read-only question, such as a list or show prompt, holds every candidate under the read-only confidence floor, unless the prompt names the skill, a command bridge marked `readOnly` matches one of its own phrases, or a skill-specific rule lifts it. A prompt with a no-write phrase, such as `no edits` or `just list`, gets none of these lifts. Mutating bridges stay gated.\n32: \n33: ### Brief Text\n34: \n35: The renderer reads a generated lookup of runnable strings, so a doctor bridge shows as `/doctor:git setup` and never as its raw id. An unmapped doctor id renders nothing. When a doctor bridge is the top pick it is the top line. When a skill is first and a doctor bridge also passes, the brief adds `Also: /doctor:<command> <target>` inside the same token cap. For no-match and outage prompts, the fallback adds one sentence naming `/doctor:setup` when the setup check matches. The check matches set up, set-up or setup wording, install or reinstall wording including installation and installer, configure or configuration wording or `check` followed within three words by environment, env, config, hooks, tools, tooling, toolchain or skilled. The command also checks the advisor. The Claude hook sets the flag, Pi passes it on the deadline fallback and the OpenCode plugin uses its copy of the setup check. The renderer never reads prompt text.\n36: \n37: ### Reach Probe\n38: \n39: `doctor-phrase-reach.cjs` keeps the three results shown by the CLI in the reach check. Its rank-first check requires the runnable doctor command, and it rejects any activated phrase with fewer than three words. `/doctor:skill-advisor router-reach` runs it.\n40: \n41: ---\n42: \n43: ## 3. SOURCE FILES\n44: \n45: ### Implementation\n46: \n47: | File | Layer | Role |\n48: |---|---|---|\n49: | `.skilled/commands/doctor/_routes.yaml` | Script | Doctor route manifest and trigger phrases |\n50: | `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/command-bridges/derive-command-bridges.cjs` | Script | Third inventory source, runtime fields and the renderer lookup block |\n51: | `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/command-bridges/scoring-compatibility.json` | Script | Activation of each admitted doctor bridge |\n52: | `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/scorer/fusion.ts` | Shared | Phrase-anchor rule and skill-first ordering |\n53: | `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/render.ts` | Shared | Runnable doctor line, second line and setup hint |\n54: | `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/hooks/claude/user-prompt-submit.ts` | Handler | Setup-wording flag for the no-match hint |\n55: | `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/hooks/pi/prompt-advisor.ts` | Handler | Passes the setup flag on Pi's deadline path |\n56: | `.opencode/plugins/lib/skill-advisor-render.js` | Shared | OpenCode copy of the setup check |\n57: | `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/skill_advisor.py` | Script | Python slash markers and the native wrapper order |\n58: | `.skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/doctor-phrase-reach.cjs` | Script | Doctor reach probe |\n59: \n60: ### Validation And Tests\n61: \n62: | File | Type | Role |\n63: |---|---|---|\n64: | `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/doctor-routing-slice.vitest.ts` | Vitest | Doctor routing slice gate |\n65: | `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/doctor-command-bridges.vitest.ts` | Vitest | Manifest-to-bridge parity |\n66: | `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/scorer/doctor-ordering.vitest.ts` | Vitest | Phrase anchor and skill-first ordering |\n67: | `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/doctor-brief-render.vitest.ts` | Vitest | Runnable line, second line and sanitizer |\n68: | `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/hooks/doctor-setup-hint.vitest.ts` | Vitest | Setup hint on and off |\n69: | `Playbook scenarios [DOC-385](../../../../manual-testing-playbook/doctor-commands/doctor-routing-setup-onboarding.md) to [DOC-391](../../../../manual-testing-playbook/doctor-commands/doctor-setup-run.md).` | Manual playbook | Agent-runnable end-to-end checks |\n70: \n71: ---\n72: \n73: ## 4. SOURCE METADATA\n74: \n75: - Group: Scorer fusion\n76: - Canonical catalog source: `feature-catalog.md`\n77: - Feature file path: `scorer-fusion/doctor-command-routing.md`\n78: \n79: Related references:\n80: \n81: - [projection.md](./projection.md) - Generated deep-loop routing projection, freshness hash guard and workflowMode publication.\n82: - [ambiguity.md](./ambiguity.md) - Top-2 ambiguity window that returns an ambiguous brief when the top two candidates are within 0.05.","title":"read","metadata":{"metadata":{"truncated":false},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Read file .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/feature-catalog/scorer-fusion/doctor-command-routing.md, lines 1-82\n1: ---\n2: title: \"Doctor Command Routing\"\n3: description: \"Doctor routes from the doctor route manifest become advisor command bridges, so setup and health prompts surface a runnable /doctor:x line.\"\n4: trigger_phrases:\n5:   - \"doctor command routing\"\n6:   - \"doctor command bridges\"\n7:   - \"runnable doctor command line\"\n8:   - \"doctor setup hint\"\n9:   - \"/doctor:setup\"\n10: version: 1.0.13.0\n11: ---\n12: \n13: # Doctor Command Routing\n14: \n15: ## 1. OVERVIEW\n16: \n17: Doctor routes from the doctor route manifest become advisor command bridges, so setup and health prompts surface a runnable /doctor:x line.\n18: \n19: A passing skill keeps first place on a contested prompt and the doctor command shows as a second line. A doctor phrase listed in its route's `lead_phrases` is the exception: it ranks the doctor command first, which is how `check my environment variables` keeps `/doctor:env` ahead of system-spec-kit. The Python fallback matches a doctor bridge only on a typed slash command.\n20: \n21: ---\n22: \n23: ## 2. HOW IT WORKS\n24: \n25: ### Bridge Generation\n26: \n27: `derive-command-bridges.cjs` reads `.skilled/commands/doctor/_routes.yaml` as a third inventory source. Each route becomes one bridge `command-doctor-<command>-<target>`, or `command-doctor-<command>` when the command owns one route. Each standalone command becomes one bridge. Each `mcp_subroutes` entry becomes one bridge `command-doctor-mcp-<sub_action>`. The owning skill comes from the router's `skill_agent` tag. Each route needs a hand-written entry in both the `typescript` and `python` lists in `scoring-compatibility.json`. The deriver fills the TypeScript keywords from the manifest's trigger phrases and the Python slash markers from the runnable string, plus the bare command for a route that declares `default_target`. Every derived doctor bridge is active, `command-doctor-helper`, the three `command-doctor-agents-md-*` bridges, the three `command-doctor-symlink-*` bridges and `command-doctor-install` included, so the activation list names a bridge once and the reach probe proves every phrase it carries; a route added without its entry stays derived and unrouted until that entry lands. A route whose manifest class is `read-only` also gets `readOnly: true` in its generated bridge.\n28: \n29: ### Ranking\n30: \n31: A doctor bridge passes on its own wording, an explicit-author match on one of its manifest phrases or its runnable string. With the local embedder running it can also pass on meaning, as [command-meaning-matching.md](./command-meaning-matching.md) describes. When none passes and none was typed, the scorer asks `/doctor:helper`'s ranker whether the prompt describes a doctor problem, and if it does the command the ranker puts first passes by name when its policy is `run`, and `/doctor:helper` passes instead when that command asks first or has no bridge. A prompt that asks for a `repair path` or says `I have a problem`, with no ranked command and no passing skill, gets `/doctor:helper`. `stopped converging` counts as a wrong state beside a passing skill. Beside a passing skill this needs a wrong state or health check in the prompt, so ordinary requests that share doctor words get no doctor line. A `/doctor:` command counts as typed when the prompt starts with `/doctor:` or when it directly follows `run`, `execute`, `start`, `launch`, `use` or `kick off` outside quotes and backticks. A quoted command or a bare mid-sentence mention does not count. A typed command puts its own passing bridge first. For other prompts, a passing skill stays first and passing doctor bridges sit right after the second passing skill or the only passing skill. This keeps a doctor line within the CLI's three shown results. Doctor bridges never change skill scores. The scorer computes skill ambiguity and abstention as if no doctor bridge existed. The Python native wrapper keeps the same order. A read-only question, such as a list or show prompt, holds every candidate under the read-only confidence floor, unless the prompt names the skill, a command bridge marked `readOnly` matches one of its own phrases, or a skill-specific rule lifts it. A prompt with a no-write phrase, such as `no edits` or `just list`, gets none of these lifts. Mutating bridges stay gated.\n32: \n33: ### Brief Text\n34: \n35: The renderer reads a generated lookup of runnable strings, so a doctor bridge shows as `/doctor:git setup` and never as its raw id. An unmapped doctor id renders nothing. When a doctor bridge is the top pick it is the top line. When a skill is first and a doctor bridge also passes, the brief adds `Also: /doctor:<command> <target>` inside the same token cap. For no-match and outage prompts, the fallback adds one sentence naming `/doctor:setup` when the setup check matches. The check matches set up, set-up or setup wording, install or reinstall wording including installation and installer, configure or configuration wording or `check` followed within three words by environment, env, config, hooks, tools, tooling, toolchain or skilled. The command also checks the advisor. The Claude hook sets the flag, Pi passes it on the deadline fallback and the OpenCode plugin uses its copy of the setup check. The renderer never reads prompt text.\n36: \n37: ### Reach Probe\n38: \n39: `doctor-phrase-reach.cjs` keeps the three results shown by the CLI in the reach check. Its rank-first check requires the runnable doctor command, and it rejects any activated phrase with fewer than three words. `/doctor:skill-advisor router-reach` runs it.\n40: \n41: ---\n42: \n43: ## 3. SOURCE FILES\n44: \n45: ### Implementation\n46: \n47: | File | Layer | Role |\n48: |---|---|---|\n49: | `.skilled/commands/doctor/_routes.yaml` | Script | Doctor route manifest and trigger phrases |\n50: | `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/command-bridges/derive-command-bridges.cjs` | Script | Third inventory source, runtime fields and the renderer lookup block |\n51: | `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/command-bridges/scoring-compatibility.json` | Script | Activation of each admitted doctor bridge |\n52: | `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/scorer/fusion.ts` | Shared | Phrase-anchor rule and skill-first ordering |\n53: | `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/render.ts` | Shared | Runnable doctor line, second line and setup hint |\n54: | `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/hooks/claude/user-prompt-submit.ts` | Handler | Setup-wording flag for the no-match hint |\n55: | `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/hooks/pi/prompt-advisor.ts` | Handler | Passes the setup flag on Pi's deadline path |\n56: | `.opencode/plugins/lib/skill-advisor-render.js` | Shared | OpenCode copy of the setup check |\n57: | `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/skill_advisor.py` | Script | Python slash markers and the native wrapper order |\n58: | `.skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/doctor-phrase-reach.cjs` | Script | Doctor reach probe |\n59: \n60: ### Validation And Tests\n61: \n62: | File | Type | Role |\n63: |---|---|---|\n64: | `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/doctor-routing-slice.vitest.ts` | Vitest | Doctor routing slice gate |\n65: | `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/doctor-command-bridges.vitest.ts` | Vitest | Manifest-to-bridge parity |\n66: | `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/scorer/doctor-ordering.vitest.ts` | Vitest | Phrase anchor and skill-first ordering |\n67: | `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/doctor-brief-render.vitest.ts` | Vitest | Runnable line, second line and sanitizer |\n68: | `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/hooks/doctor-setup-hint.vitest.ts` | Vitest | Setup hint on and off |\n69: | `Playbook scenarios [DOC-385](../../../../manual-testing-playbook/doctor-commands/doctor-routing-setup-onboarding.md) to [DOC-391](../../../../manual-testing-playbook/doctor-commands/doctor-setup-run.md).` | Manual playbook | Agent-runnable end-to-end checks |\n70: \n71: ---\n72: \n73: ## 4. SOURCE METADATA\n74: \n75: - Group: Scorer fusion\n76: - Canonical catalog source: `feature-catalog.md`\n77: - Feature file path: `scorer-fusion/doctor-command-routing.md`\n78: \n79: Related references:\n80: \n81: - [projection.md](./projection.md) - Generated deep-loop routing projection, freshness hash guard and workflowMode publication.\n82: - [ambiguity.md](./ambiguity.md) - Top-2 ambiguity window that returns an ambiguous brief when the top two candidates are within 0.05."}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"provide