{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794670845724,"sessionID":"ses_e255ff46effe7EWyuOLOEwVdy1","part":{"partID":"prt_1dab7cb430017I5Ih0WMlG7s9W","sessionID":"ses_e255ff46effe7EWyuOLOEwVdy1","messageID":"msg_1dab77d2f001DJetwoegP8trag","type":"tool","id":"chatcmpl-tool-a7cd19bc375a9240","tool":"shell","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"rg -n 'doctor:setup|doctor:update|intent phrase|plain tune|tune row|no-recommendation|what changed|what to fix' specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/016-claude-create-reach-and-doctor-default/acceptance-criteria.md specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/016-claude-create-reach-and-doctor-default/spec.md | head -60","workdir":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research"},"output":"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/016-claude-create-reach-and-doctor-default/acceptance-criteria.md:60:| AC-005 | REQ-005 | Given the rebuilt cue, When `doctorProblemCue` reads a negated \"show up\" or \"appear\" and the capture runs, Then it returns `strong` for the two problem phrases, `null` for the two view phrases, and `BASE` reads `\"offered\":true` for `cmd-doctor-mcp-plain-tune-01` and `false` for `cmd-doctor-skill-advisor-plain-tune-01` | The T011 cases in `HOT` and `HCT` and the T021 row lines Met 2026-11-13: `reads a tool that does not show up as a strong cue` and `offers the helper beside the skills for a tool that does not show up` pass in the close-out run of seven files, 57 passed. T030 added `it doesn't appear to cover the routing case` and `don't show up-to-date entries only` as `null`. `BASE` reads `true` for the mcp tune row and `false` for the skill-advisor tune row, from `false` and `false`. Receipts: `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/scorer/doctor-helper-handoff.ts:55` `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/doctor-helper-handoff.vitest.ts:40` `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/scorer/doctor-handoff-command.vitest.ts:117` `scratch/after.txt:83` `scratch/after.txt:84` | Met | - |\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/016-claude-create-reach-and-doctor-default/acceptance-criteria.md:62:| AC-007 | REQ-007 | Given all changes, When the floors and the suites run, Then typed recall is at least 24 of 44, both false offer counts are 0 of 35, typed delivery is 44 of 44, plain tune combined is at least 23 of 45, `EVAL` holds `[160,50,21,5]` with the fourth value no higher than 5, and `TC`, `VALL`, `DALL` and `CRS` pass | `$SP/after.txt` beside `$SP/before.txt` from T027 Met 2026-11-13: typed 24 of 44, both false offer counts 0 of 35, typed delivery 44 of 44 and plain tune combined 28 of 45, from 23. The 28 is tune reach the new phrases built in, not a gain. `EVAL` reads `[160,50,21,5]`. `TC` exits 0, `VALL` reads 1758 passed and 0 failed over 183 files, `DALL` reads `pass 1189` and `fail 0` and `CRS` prints both lines. Receipts: `scratch/after.txt:6` `scratch/after.txt:9` `scratch/after.txt:12` `scratch/after.txt:18` `scratch/after.txt:21` `scratch/after-vall.log:13` | Met | - |\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/016-claude-create-reach-and-doctor-default/spec.md:3:description: \"Claude Code lists 32 of the 44 tracked commands, because a command file named skill.md makes it read the create folder as one skill. This phase renames /create:skill to /create:sk-skill on every runtime with no alias, offers /doctor:helper on a doctor prompt that says a tool is not showing up, shows the AGENTS.md Gate 2 call with the request on stdin, adds intent phrases to five no-recommendation commands and keeps the brief-cost run out of the shared health log.\"\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/016-claude-create-reach-and-doctor-default/spec.md:10:  - \"command intent phrases for doctor install setup speckit update\"\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/016-claude-create-reach-and-doctor-default/spec.md:44:**Scope Boundary**: The rename of `/create:skill` to `/create:sk-skill` in every live file outside `specs/`, the mirror check that counts Claude's commands, the doctor problem cue, `AGENTS.md` line 65 with its two derived copies, the intent phrases of five commands and the child environment of the brief-cost script. Generated files change only through their generators. No scorer weight, hub routing logic or renderer changes. `/create:skill-parent`, the `sk-create-skill` mode and its folder, the `.claude/skills` link, every file under `specs/`, every published changelog entry, the dated benchmark reports and the served copy of the sk-doc canary fixture keep the old text.\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/016-claude-create-reach-and-doctor-default/spec.md:56:- Intent phrases for `/doctor:install`, `/doctor:setup`, `/doctor:speckit`, `/doctor:update` and `/speckit:search`, re-embedded and measured on holdout as a count.\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/016-claude-create-reach-and-doctor-default/spec.md:71:**Core need served:** Claude Code listed 32 of the 44 commands before the rename, so a model there could not take the other 12 workflows at all. Now it lists all 44, and the doctor helper and the new intent phrases bring more prompts to the right workflow.\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/016-claude-create-reach-and-doctor-default/spec.md:169:From `research-segment-4.md` section 4 (a), rerun there at `087888ec4a` with `--real-embedding`: typed 24 of 44, plain tune top-1 13 of 45, plain tune with attached commands 28 of 45, plain holdout 3 of 44, false offers 0 of 35 and attached false offers 0 of 35. With the lineage's 23 phrases on copies of the database, holdout reads 5 of 44 and tune top-1 18 of 45, and for each command one phrase equals its tune prompt word for word. Every count in this spec quotes this block or that section.\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/016-claude-create-reach-and-doctor-default/spec.md:211:- D. Add intent phrases to five commands, paraphrasing any phrase that repeats a tune prompt, re-embed and measure holdout as a count.\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/016-claude-create-reach-and-doctor-default/spec.md:256:| REQ-007 | The fixture floors hold after every change: typed recall at least 24 of 44, false offers 0 of 35, attached false offers 0 of 35, typed delivery 44 of 44, plain tune combined at least 23 of 45, and the scorer eval at least `[160,50,21,5]` with the fourth value no higher than 5. Typecheck, the full advisor suite, the doctor script tests and the compiled-route closure check pass. |\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/016-claude-create-reach-and-doctor-default/spec.md:280:- **SC-003**: `FLOOR` prints `{\"correct\":24,\"total\":44}` or better, `{\"count\":0,\"total\":35}`, `{\"own\":24,\"attached\":20,\"combined\":44,\"total\":44}`, a plain tune `combined` of 23 or more and `{\"count\":0,\"total\":35}`, and the mcp tune row reads `\"offered\":true`.\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/016-claude-create-reach-and-doctor-default/spec.md:355:- Q2. Which rule offers `/doctor:helper` on the doctor wrong-top pair? Answered by the operator on 2026-11-13: option 1, a negated \"show up\" or \"appear\" as a strong cue. The mcp tune row gains the helper and the skill-advisor tune row stays silent.\n","title":"shell","metadata":{"metadata":{"status":"completed","truncated":false,"exit":0},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/016-claude-create-reach-and-doctor-default/acceptance-criteria.md:60:| AC-005 | REQ-005 | 