`/doctor:speckit`, `/doctor:update` and `/speckit:search`, re-embedded and measured on holdout as a count.\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/016-claude-create-reach-and-doctor-default/spec.md:71:**Core need served:** Claude Code listed 32 of the 44 commands before the rename, so a model there could not take the other 12 workflows at all. Now it lists all 44, and the doctor helper and the new intent phrases bring more prompts to the right workflow.\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/016-claude-create-reach-and-doctor-default/spec.md:169:From `research-segment-4.md` section 4 (a), rerun there at `087888ec4a` with `--real-embedding`: typed 24 of 44, plain tune top-1 13 of 45, plain tune with attached commands 28 of 45, plain holdout 3 of 44, false offers 0 of 35 and attached false offers 0 of 35. With the lineage's 23 phrases on copies of the database, holdout reads 5 of 44 and tune top-1 18 of 45, and for each command one phrase equals its tune prompt word for word. Every count in this spec quotes this block or that section.\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/016-claude-create-reach-and-doctor-default/spec.md:211:- D. Add intent phrases to five commands, paraphrasing any phrase that repeats a tune prompt, re-embed and measure holdout as a count.\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/016-claude-create-reach-and-doctor-default/spec.md:256:| REQ-007 | The fixture floors hold after every change: typed recall at least 24 of 44, false offers 0 of 35, attached false offers 0 of 35, typed delivery 44 of 44, plain tune combined at least 23 of 45, and the scorer eval at least `[160,50,21,5]` with the fourth value no higher than 5. Typecheck, the full advisor suite, the doctor script tests and the compiled-route closure check pass. |\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/016-claude-create-reach-and-doctor-default/spec.md:280:- **SC-003**: `FLOOR` prints `{\"correct\":24,\"total\":44}` or better, `{\"count\":0,\"total\":35}`, `{\"own\":24,\"attached\":20,\"combined\":44,\"total\":44}`, a plain tune `combined` of 23 or more and `{\"count\":0,\"total\":35}`, and the mcp tune row reads `\"offered\":true`.\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/016-claude-create-reach-and-doctor-default/spec.md:355:- Q2. Which rule offers `/doctor:helper` on the doctor wrong-top pair? Answered by the operator on 2026-11-13: option 1, a negated \"show up\" or \"appear\" as a strong cue. The mcp tune row gains the helper and the skill-advisor tune row stays silent.\n"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"command\": \"rg -n 'doctor:setup|doctor:update|intent phrase|plain tune|tune row|no-recommendation|what changed|what to fix' specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/016-claude-create-reach-and-doctor-default/acceptance-criteria.md specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/016-claude-create-reach-and-doctor-default/spec.md | head -60\", \"workdir\": \"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research\"}"},"time":{"start":1794670840643,"end":1794670845724}}}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794670845793,"sessionID":"ses_e255ff46effe7EWyuOLOEwVdy1","part":{"partID":"prt_1dab7d465001Z6JKRx8O5jEG7m","sessionID":"ses_e255ff46effe7EWyuOLOEwVdy1","messageID":"msg_1dab77d2f001DJetwoegP8trag","type":"tool","id":"chatcmpl-tool-bd2864fd1b5487b3","tool":"shell","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"rg -n 'doctor:setup|doctor:update|what changed|what to fix|phrase' specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/017-review-pass-two-remediation specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/024-fable-review-remediation specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/025-release-notes-and-doc-sync --glob '*.md' | head -60","workdir":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research"},"output":"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/024-fable-review-remediation/spec.md:4:trigger_phrases:\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/024-fable-review-remediation/spec.md:111:PROMPT: no need to run /doctor:setup, the hooks are fine\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/024-fable-review-remediation/spec.md:112:  row 0: command-doctor-setup 0.826/0.16 command=/doctor:setup policy=run owner=system-skilled-doctor ambiguous=false\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/024-fable-review-remediation/plan.md:4:trigger_phrases:\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/024-fable-review-remediation/scratch/implementation-summary.scaffold.md:3:description: \"Open with a hook: what changed and why it matters. One paragraph, impact first.\"\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/024-fable-review-remediation/scratch/implementation-summary.scaffold.md:4:trigger_phrases:\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/024-fable-review-remediation/scratch/implementation-summary.scaffold.md:50:[YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Opening hook: 2-3 sentences on what changed and why it matters. Lead with impact.]\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/024-fable-review-remediation/implementation-summary.md:4:trigger_phrases:\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/024-fable-review-remediation/implementation-summary.md:92:| `no need to run /doctor:setup, the hooks are fine` | command-doctor-setup, `command=/doctor:setup policy=run` | system-skilled-doctor, `command=-` |\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/025-release-notes-and-doc-sync/acceptance-criteria.md:4:trigger_phrases:\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/025-release-notes-and-doc-sync/tasks.md:4:trigger_phrases:\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/025-release-notes-and-doc-sync/tasks.md:57:- [ ] T002 [C] Collect the facts (`FACTS`). For each of the six phases, in order, write a heading `## <number> <folder slug>` and under it copy, word for word and each with its source as `<file>:<line>`, the lines of that phase's `implementation-summary.md` that state what changed for a user, the files it changed, the numbers it printed and the limits it names. Under `## 024` also copy the Codex lines of `$PK/024-fable-review-remediation/scratch/rescore-delta.txt`. Under a last heading `## checks` write the last result line of each suite phase 024 recorded in its `scratch/after.txt`, the five floor lines of its `scratch/floor-after.txt` and the case count `VX tests/command-meaning-anchor.vitest.ts` prints. Write nothing that is not a copy. Verify: `rg -c -e '^## (019|020|021|022|023|024) ' $FACTS` prints 6, `rg -c -e '^## checks$' $FACTS` prints 1, `rg -c -e 'implementation-summary\\.md:[0-9]+' $FACTS` prints at least 18 and `rg -c -e 'Tests +[0-9]+ passed' $FACTS` prints at least 1.\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/025-release-notes-and-doc-sync/tasks.md:90:- [ ] T014 [P] Show the companion line with its policy word (`BR`). In the paragraph that starts `A doctor bridge passes on its own wording (an explicit-author phrase match).`, replace the code span that starts ``Also: /doctor:<command>`` with ``Also: /doctor:<command> <target> (<policy>)``, and add after that sentence: `The policy is run, start or ask, and the line is left out when the head already names that command.` Verify: `rg -c -F 'Also: /doctor:<command> <target> (<policy>)' $BR` prints 1, `rg -c -F 'left out when the head already names that command' $BR` prints 1, `DOC $BR` exits 0 and `VX tests/command-attach-guards.vitest.ts` reports 0 failed, because its case `the command-bridges README names every command row field` reads this file.\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/025-release-notes-and-doc-sync/goal.md:4:trigger_phrases:\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/025-release-notes-and-doc-sync/scratch/implementation-summary.scaffold.md:3:description: \"Open with a hook: what changed and why it matters. One paragraph, impact first.\"\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/025-release-notes-and-doc-sync/scratch/implementation-summary.scaffold.md:4:trigger_phrases:\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/025-release-notes-and-doc-sync/scratch/implementation-summary.scaffold.md:50:[YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Opening hook: 2-3 sentences on what changed and why it matters. Lead with impact.]\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/024-fable-review-remediation/tasks.md:4:trigger_phrases:\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/024-fable-review-remediation/tasks.md:62:- [x] T002 [C] Record the reproductions (`$SP/repro-before.txt`). Run `MENTION`, `OFFERS`, `CODEX $RL/runs-pre.jsonl`, `CODEX $RL/runs-post.jsonl`, `SHELL`, `node TSX $PL/probe-skill-label.mts` and `node $PL/probe-plugin-flake.mjs 20`, and write each command with its output into `repro-before.txt`. Verify: `rg -c -F 'SHIPPED: 40 of 46 agree' $SP/repro-before.txt` prints 1, `rg -c -e 'row 0: .* command=/(doctor:setup|create:changelog|speckit:resume) ' $SP/repro-before.txt` prints 3, `rg -c -e '^shell events with no command text: (58|53)$' $SP/repro-before.txt` prints 2, `rg -c -F 'same head with and without the label: true' $SP/repro-before.txt` prints 1 and `rg -c -e '^termination grace test: 20 passed, 0 failed' $SP/repro-before.txt` prints 1. When the flake line reports a failed run, record the line in the parent goal log and plan no fix without a new task: the item was declined because it could not be shown. Evidence: scratch/repro-before.txt: SHIPPED 40 of 46 once, three row-0 command lines, both Codex lines 58 and 53, same head true. The flake line read 18 passed, 2 failed of 20 runs, recorded in the parent goal log.\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/024-fable-review-remediation/tasks.md:73:- [x] T004 [P] Read `no need to`, `need not` and `needn't` before a use verb as a refusal (`CAT`, then `CA` constant `COMMAND_DECLINE_LEADS`). This task changes the first string of that array and nothing else in `CA`. Test first: in `CAT`, inside `describe('a command the prompt only mentions')`, add `it('reads no need to run as a refusal of the command')` expecting `commandOnlyMentioned('no need to run /doctor:setup, the hooks are fine', '/doctor:setup')` to be `true`, and `it('still reads a request after no need to ask')` expecting `commandOnlyMentioned('no need to ask, run /speckit:save', '/speckit:save')` to be `false`. Run `VX tests/command-attach-guards.vitest.ts` and see the first case return `false` while the second passes. Then in `CA`, in the first string of `COMMAND_DECLINE_LEADS`, replace `no longer|cannot|can't)` with `no longer|cannot|can't|no need to|need not|needn't)`. Verify: the first run fails as described, then `VX tests/command-attach-guards.vitest.ts` reports 0 failed and `rg -c -F \"can't|no need to|need not|needn't)\" $CA` prints 1. Evidence: Opus check PASS: first run 1 failed (no need to run case), then 106 passed of 106. Probes: needn't and need not read as refusals, no need to worry and no need to ask do not\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/024-fable-review-remediation/tasks.md:108:- [x] T020 [C] Rerun the reproductions (`$SP/repro-after.txt`). Run the seven probes of T002 and write each command with its output. Verify: `rg -c -F 'SHIPPED: 46 of 46 agree' $SP/repro-after.txt` prints 1. In the `OFFERS` block the two refusal prompts and the question-mark prompt print no row with `command=/doctor:setup`, `command=/create:changelog` or `command=/speckit:resume`, each of the three request prompts prints `command=/speckit:plan`, `command=/create:readme` or `command=/create:agent` on some row, and the two control prompts print what `$SP/repro-before.txt` printed for them. In both `CODEX` blocks the count after `shell events with no command text:` is below the count after `shell events:`. In the `SHELL` block the first eight lines end in `none`, `none`, `none`, `none`, `none`, `skill`, `skill` and `none`. When a request prompt prints no command, mark the task `[B]` with its row lines: the mention reader no longer withholds it, so another gate does, and that needs its own probe before any edit. Evidence: Coordinator: SHIPPED 46 of 46 agree. OFFERS: the refusals and the question print no command, the three requests print /speckit:plan, /create:readme and /create:agent. CODEX no-command shell events 7 of 58 pre and 4 of 53 post. SHELL first eight lines none x5, skill, skill, none. FLAKE 20 of 20\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/024-fable-review-remediation/tasks.md:225:- [x] CHK-040 [P1] `RA` names `offeredAsPartner`, the Codex body rule and the three shell-read rules (T017). Evidence: `rg -c` prints 1 for each of the three phrases in the routing-accuracy README.\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/024-fable-review-remediation/goal.md:4:trigger_phrases:\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/025-release-notes-and-doc-sync/spec.md:4:trigger_phrases:\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/025-release-notes-and-doc-sync/spec.md:85:132:| `command-attach.ts` | `attachCommand()` names the slash command for a hub recommendation whose compiled route picks one `workflowMode`. It reads the `MODE_COMMANDS` table that `derive-command-bridges.cjs` generates from each hub's `mode-registry.json`. A `system-deep-loop` command needs the same command typed in the prompt or a `DEPTH_WORDING` phrase, and a prompt that matches `NO_EDIT_REQUEST` gets no command. The module has no imports. |\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/025-release-notes-and-doc-sync/spec.md:90:command-bridges/README.md:68: A doctor bridge passes on its own wording (an explicit-author phrase match). ...\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/025-release-notes-and-doc-sync/plan.md:4:trigger_phrases:\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/024-fable-review-remediation/acceptance-criteria.md:4:trigger_phrases:\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/017-review-pass-two-remediation/acceptance-criteria.md:4:trigger_phrases:\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/017-review-pass-two-remediation/tasks.md:4:trigger_phrases:\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/017-review-pass-two-remediation/spec.md:4:trigger_phrases:\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/017-review-pass-two-remediation/spec.md:43:- Phase 016 is built and committed before this phase starts. It renames `/create:skill` to `/create:sk-skill` with no alias, adds a doctor cue in `runtime/lib/scorer/doctor-helper-handoff.ts`, edits `AGENTS.md` line 65 and adds intent phrases to `command-metadata.json` files and `_routes.yaml`. It also edits `command-attach.ts`, `command-attach-guards.vitest.ts`, `fusion.ts`, `measure-brief-cost.mjs`, its test and the routing-accuracy README, which lanes here edit after it. So every task re-reads its files before its first edit, and a task whose quoted anchor is gone marks itself `[B]` with the line it found. No test input or expected output in this phase names `/create:skill`.\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/017-review-pass-two-remediation/plan.md:4:trigger_phrases:\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/017-review-pass-two-remediation/implementation-summary.md:4:trigger_phrases:\n","title":"shell","metadata":{"metadata":{"status":"completed","truncated":false,"exit":0},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/024-fable-review-remediation/spec.md:4:trigger_phrases:\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/024-fable-review-remediation/spec.md:111:PROMPT: no need to run /doctor:setup, the hooks are fine\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/024-fable-review-remediation/spec.md:112:  row 0: command-doctor-setup 0.826/0.16 command=/doctor:setup policy=run owner=system-skilled-doctor ambiguous=false\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/024-fable-review-remediation/plan.md:4:trigger_phrases:\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/024-fable-review-remediation/scratch/implementation-summary.scaffold.md:3:description: \"Open with a hook: what changed and why it matters. One paragraph, impact first.\"\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/024-fable-review-remediation/scratch/implementation-summary.scaffold.md:4:trigger_phrases:\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/024-fable-review-remediation/scratch/implementation-summary.scaffold.md:50:[YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Opening hook: 2-3 sentences on what changed and why it matters. Lead with impact.]\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/024-fable-review-remediation/implementation-summary.md:4:trigger_phrases:\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/024-fable-review-remediation/implementation-summary.md:92:| `no need to run /doctor:setup, the hooks are fine` | command-doctor-setup, `command=/doctor:setup policy=run` | system-skilled-doctor, `command=-` |\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/025-release-notes-and-doc-sync/acceptance-criteria.md:4:trigger_phrases:\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/025-release-notes-and-doc-sync/tasks.md:4:trigger_phrases:\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/025-release-notes-and-doc-sync/tasks.md:57:- [ ] T002 [C] Collect the facts (`FACTS`). For each of the six phases, in order, write a heading `## <number> <folder slug>` and under it copy, word for word and each with its source as `<file>:<line>`, the lines of that phase's `implementation-summary.md` that state what changed for a user, the files it changed, the numbers it printed and the limits it names. Under `## 024` also copy the Codex lines of `$PK/024-fable-review-remediation/scratch/rescore-delta.txt`. Under a last heading `## checks` write the last result line of each suite phase 024 recorded in its `scratch/after.txt`, the five floor lines of its `scratch/floor-after.txt` and the case count `VX tests/command-meaning-anchor.vitest.ts` prints. Write nothing that is not a copy. Verify: `rg -c -e '^## (019|020|021|022|023|024) ' $FACTS` prints 6, `rg -c -e '^## checks$' $FACTS` prints 1, `rg -c -e 'implementation-summary\\.md:[0-9]+' $FACTS` prints at least 18 and `rg -c -e 'Tests +[0-9]+ passed' $FACTS` prints at least 1.\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/025-release-notes-and-doc-sync/tasks.md:90:- [ ] T014 [P] Show the companion line with its policy word (`BR`). In the paragraph that starts `A doctor bridge passes on its own wording (an explicit-author phrase match).`, replace the code span that starts ``Also: /doctor:<command>`` with ``Also: /doctor:<command> <target> (<policy>)``, and add after that sentence: `The policy is run, start or ask, and the line is left out when the head already names that command.` Verify: `rg -c -F 'Also: /doctor:<command> <target> (<policy>)' $BR` prints 1, `rg -c -F 'left out when the head already names that command' $BR` prints 1, `DOC $BR` exits 0 and `VX tests/command-attach-guards.vitest.ts` reports 0 failed, because its case `the command-bridges README names every command row field` reads this file.\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/025-release-notes-and-doc-sync/goal.md:4:trigger_phrases:\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/025-release-notes-and-doc-sync/scratch/implementation-summary.scaffold.md:3:description: \"Open with a hook: what changed and why it matters. One paragraph, impact first.\"\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/025-release-notes-and-doc-sync/scratch/implementation-summary.scaffold.md:4:trigger_phrases:\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/025-release-notes-and-doc-sync/scratch/implementation-summary.scaffold.md:50:[YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Opening hook: 2-3 sentences on what changed and why it matters. Lead with impact.]\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/024-fable-review-remediation/tasks.md:4:trigger_phrases:\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/024-fable-review-remediation/tasks.md:62:- [x] T002 [C] Record the reproductions (`$SP/repro-before.txt`). Run `MENTION`, `OFFERS`, `CODEX $RL/runs-pre.jsonl`, `CODEX $RL/runs-post.jsonl`, `SHELL`, `node TSX $PL/probe-skill-label.mts` and `node $PL/probe-plugin-flake.mjs 20`, and write each command with its output into `repro-before.txt`. Verify: `rg -c -F 'SHIPPED: 40 of 46 agree' $SP/repro-before.txt` prints 1, `rg -c -e 'row 0: .* command=/(doctor:setup|create:changelog|speckit:resume) ' $SP/repro-before.txt` prints 3, `rg -c -e '^shell events with no command text: (58|53)$' $SP/repro-before.txt` prints 2, `rg -c -F 'same head with and without the label: true' $SP/repro-before.txt` prints 1 and `rg -c -e '^termination grace test: 20 passed, 0 failed' $SP/repro-before.txt` prints 1. When the flake line reports a failed run, record the line in the parent goal log and plan no fix without a new task: the item was declined because it could not be shown. Evidence: scratch/repro-before.txt: SHIPPED 40 of 46 once, three row-0 command lines, both Codex lines 58 and 53, same head true. The flake line read 18 passed, 2 failed of 20 runs, recorded in the parent goal log.\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/024-fable-review-remediation/tasks.md:73:- [x] T004 [P] Read `no need to`, `need not` and `needn't` before a use verb as a refusal (`CAT`, then `CA` constant `COMMAND_DECLINE_LEADS`). This task changes the first string of that array and nothing else in `CA`. Test first: in `CAT`, inside `describe('a command the prompt only mentions')`, add `it('reads no need to run as a refusal of the command')` expecting `commandOnlyMentioned('no need to run /doctor:setup, the hooks are fine', '/doctor:setup')` to be `true`, and `it('still reads a request after no need to ask')` expecting `commandOnlyMentioned('no need to ask, run /speckit:save', '/speckit:save')` to be `false`. Run `VX tests/command-attach-guards.vitest.ts` and see the first case return `false` while the second passes. Then in `CA`, in the first string of `COMMAND_DECLINE_LEADS`, replace `no longer|cannot|can't)` with `no longer|cannot|can't|no need to|need not|needn't)`. Verify: the first run fails as described, then `VX tests/command-attach-guards.vitest.ts` reports 0 failed and `rg -c -F \"can't|no need to|need not|needn't)\" $CA` prints 1. Evidence: Opus check PASS: first run 1 failed (no need to run case), then 106 passed of 106. Probes: needn't and need not read as refusals, no need to worry and no need to ask do not\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/024-fable-review-remediation/tasks.md:108:- [x] T020 [C] Rerun the reproductions (`$SP/repro-after.txt`). Run the seven probes of T002 and write each command with its output. Verify: `rg -c -F 'SHIPPED: 46 of 46 agree' $SP/repro-after.txt` prints 1. In the `OFFERS` block the two refusal prompts and the question-mark prompt print no row with `command=/doctor:setup`, `command=/create:changelog` or `command=/speckit:resume`, each of the three request prompts prints `command=/speckit:plan`, `command=/create:readme` or `command=/create:agent` on some row, and the two control prompts print what `$SP/repro-before.txt` printed for them. In both `CODEX` blocks the count after `shell events with no command text:` is below the count after `shell events:`. In the `SHELL` block the first eight lines end in `none`, `none`, `none`, `none`, `none`, `skill`, `skill` and `none`. When a request prompt prints no command, mark the task `[B]` with its row lines: the mention reader no longer withholds it, so another gate does, and that needs its own probe before any edit. Evidence: Coordinator: SHIPPED 46 of 46 agree. OFFERS: the refusals and the question print no command, the three requests print /speckit:plan, /create:readme and /create:agent. CODEX no-command shell events 7 of 58 pre and 4 of 53 post. SHELL first eight lines none x5, skill, skill, none. FLAKE 20 of 20\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/024-fable-review-remediation/tasks.md:225:- [x] CHK-040 [P1] `RA` names `offeredAsPartner`, the Codex body rule and the three shell-read rules (T017). Evidence: `rg -c` prints 1 for each of the three phrases in the routing-accuracy README.\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/024-fable-review-remediation/goal.md:4:trigger_phrases:\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/025-release-notes-and-doc-sync/spec.md:4:trigger_phrases:\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/025-release-notes-and-doc-sync/spec.md:85:132:| `command-attach.ts` | `attachCommand()` names the slash command for a hub recommendation whose compiled route picks one `workflowMode`. It reads the `MODE_COMMANDS` table that `derive-command-bridges.cjs` generates from each hub's `mode-registry.json`. A `system-deep-loop` command needs the same command typed in the prompt or a `DEPTH_WORDING` phrase, and a prompt that matches `NO_EDIT_REQUEST` gets no command. The module has no imports. |\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/025-release-notes-and-doc-sync/spec.md:90:command-bridges/README.md:68: A doctor bridge passes on its own wording (an explicit-author phrase match). ...\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/025-release-notes-and-doc-sync/plan.md:4:trigger_phrases:\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/024-fable-review-remediation/acceptance-criteria.md:4:trigger_phrases:\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/017-review-pass-two-remediation/acceptance-criteria.md:4:trigger_phrases:\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/017-review-pass-two-remediation/tasks.md:4:trigger_phrases:\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/017-review-pass-two-remediation/spec.md:4:trigger_phrases:\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/017-review-pass-two-remediation/spec.md:43:- Phase 016 is built and committed before this phase starts. It renames `/create:skill` to `/create:sk-skill` with no alias, adds a doctor cue in `runtime/lib/scorer/doctor-helper-handoff.ts`, edits `AGENTS.md` line 65 and adds intent phrases to `command-metadata.json` files and `_routes.yaml`. It also edits `command-attach.ts`, `command-attach-guards.vitest.ts`, `fusion.ts`, `measure-brief-cost.mjs`, its test and the routing-accuracy README, which lanes here edit after it. So every task re-reads its files before its first edit, and a task whose quoted anchor is gone marks itself `[B]` with the line it found. No test input or expected output in this phase names `/create:skill`.\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/017-review-pass-two-remediation/plan.md:4:trigger_phrases:\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/017-review-pass-two-remediation/implementation-summary.md:4:trigger_phrases:\n"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"command\": \"rg -n 'doctor:setup|doctor:update|what changed|what to fix|phrase' specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/017-review-pass-two-remediation specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/024-fable-review-remediation specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/025-release-notes-and-doc-sync --glob '*.md' | head -60\", \"workdir\": \"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research\"}"},"time":{"start":1794670842981,"end":1794670845793}}}}
