102: \n103: - A holdout-leak finding is ruled out so far: the changed files do not read either prompt corpus; `_routes.yaml` only declares trigger phrases, and the route derivation output was checked without opening a prompt row. (iteration 1)\n104: - A cross-runtime branching defect in the changed presentation is ruled out so far: `create-skill-presentation.txt` is plain text read by every runtime, and the canonical Gate 3 constant it must match lives in one shared module. (iteration 1)\n105: - A P0/P1 in the A11 count logic is ruled out: the count is derived from the same arrays that build the printed lines, and the test's malformed row keeps its rule path so it is not reported missing. (iteration 1)\n106: - A P1 on the removed doctor phrases is ruled out: the remaining phrases cover each route's core requests, the derived bridge data is in sync, and the hand-off test pins the generic repair and release-note prompts as no-match. (iteration 1)\n107: - A P1 on the create sub-track wording is ruled out: the canonical Gate 3 menu and `suggest-subtracks.mjs` own sub-track creation, and the create workflow consumes an existing `spec_path`. (iteration 1)\n108: - A transcript-scorer phantom-count finding is out of area: the changed files contain no transcript-scoring code. (iteration 1)\n109: \n110: <!-- ANCHOR:next-focus -->\n111: ## 11. NEXT FOCUS\n112: - Dimension: security + traceability (rotation; the 3-iteration cap requires combining the two after correctness). - Focus area: the doctor route mutation classes and phrase reach, the derived bridge policy (`read-only`/`add-only`/`mutates`), the packet's `016`/`025` spec and acceptance docs for these files, the feature-catalog and playbook descriptions, and the cross-runtime command mirrors. - Reason: iteration 1 found one advisory docs gap; the next pass must prove no question, refusal or command mention can attach a mutating route, and that the changed behavior is traceable to the packet's requirements. - Rotation status: correctness completed; security and traceability next; maintainability remains for the final pass. - Blocked/productive carry-forward: carry `DR4-P2-001` for a check that no other doctor doc names a repair for the malformed case. - Required evidence: `_routes.yaml` mutation classes and phrase lists, the policy derivation in `derive-command-bridges.cjs`, `doctor-helper-handoff.ts` thresholds, the packet's spec/tasks/acceptance docs, the feature catalog, and the manual playbook. - Recovery note: none. Review verdict: PASS\n113: \n114: <!-- /ANCHOR:next-focus -->\n115: ## 13. KNOWN CONTEXT\n116: \n117: ### Bounded Context Snapshot\n118: \n119: - **Target pointers**: the four changed files above; the diff `0cdc9fa3ef..400c90e158` is +11/-9; the changed lines are `agents-md-check.cjs:798-809`, `agents-md-check.test.cjs:763-764`, `_routes.yaml:403-406,797-806`, and `create-skill-presentation.txt:89`.\n120: - **Behavior claims to verify**: A11 now names a malformed row in its detail when nothing is missing; the create Q3 option C matches the canonical `GATE_3_CHOICE_RELATED` constant; the removed `/doctor:setup` and `/doctor:update` phrases keep generic code-repair and release-note questions off those routes; the remaining phrases stay three or more words and still reach their derived bridges; the test suite's A11 malformed case pins the new detail.\n121: - **Reuse and conventions**: A11 states are PASS/FINDING/UNKNOWN/INFO; the doctor presentation owns the repair mapping; `_routes.yaml` is the source of truth for route phrases and mutation class, and `derive-command-bridges.cjs` copies them into `command-bridges.generated.json`; `GATE_3_CHOICE_RELATED` is the canonical Gate 3 option C; `review-core.md` owns P0/P1/P2 reach calibration.\n122: - **Prior context (read-only, outside this area)**: pass-three lineage `doctor-docs-3` carried P1 `DR3-P1-001` on `hook-wiring-check.cjs:264-269` (attached node flag spellings). That file is not in this pass's area; the carried fi