{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794671089599,"sessionID":"ses_e255ff46effe7EWyuOLOEwVdy1","part":{"partID":"prt_1dabb88ab002o9b1rDiqyih5Bn","sessionID":"ses_e255ff46effe7EWyuOLOEwVdy1","messageID":"msg_1dabb658b001K3tbUyJHPlHUwq","type":"tool","id":"chatcmpl-tool-a44373ef53507282","tool":"edit","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"newString":"## 8. WHAT WORKED\n\n- Tracing the changed A11 detail to its two consumers (the presentation's repair table and the embed engine's router write) found the one actionable gap in an otherwise clean diff. (iteration 1)\n- Querying the derived `command-bridges.generated.json` as data, rather than reading a prompt corpus, proved all six removed phrases reached the advisor surface's removal. (iteration 1)\n- Comparing the create presentation line against `GATE_3_CHOICE_RELATED` and its parity test proved the canonical wording match without a runtime branch. (iteration 1)\n- Reading the derived `commandPolicies` instead of the route prose settled the attach question: every `mutating: mutates` doctor route is `ask`, and only read-only or add-only spec-folder routes are `run`. (iteration 2)\n- The refusal/question guards and the spec 016/024 evidence closed the security and traceability passes without a new finding. (iteration 2)\n\n## 9. WHAT FAILED\n\n- The A11-specific troubleshooting row was assumed to cover every A11 finding; it covers missing rows only, so the malformed-row case has no named repair. Recorded as `DR4-P2-001`, not a failed approach. (iteration 1)\n- No new finding came from the security or traceability pass; the only active item remains the carried P2. (iteration 2)","oldString":"## 8. WHAT WORKED\n\n- Tracing the changed A11 detail to its two consumers (the presentation's repair table and the embed engine's router write) found the one actionable gap in an otherwise clean diff. (iteration 1)\n- Querying the derived `command-bridges.generated.json` as data, rather than reading a prompt corpus, proved all six removed phrases reached the advisor surface's removal. (iteration 1)\n- Comparing the create presentation line against `GATE_3_CHOICE_RELATED` and its parity test proved the canonical wording match without a runtime branch. (iteration 1)\n\n## 9. WHAT FAILED\n\n- The A11-specific troubleshooting row was assumed to cover every A11 finding; it covers missing rows only, so the malformed-row case has no named repair. Recorded as `DR4-P2-001`, not a failed approach. (iteration 1)","path":"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/doctor-docs-4/deep-review-strategy.md"},"output":"Edited specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/doctor-docs-4/deep-review-strategy.md (1 replacement)","title":"edit","metadata":{"metadata":{"files":[{"file":"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/doctor-docs-4/deep-review-strategy.md","patch":"Index: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/doctor-docs-4/deep-review-strategy.md\n===================================================================\n--- specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/doctor-docs-4/deep-review-strategy.md\n+++ specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/doctor-docs-4/deep-review-strategy.md\n@@ -56,12 +56,15 @@\n \n - Tracing the changed A11 detail to its two consumers (the presentation's repair table and the embed engine's router write) found the one actionable gap in an otherwise clean diff. (iteration 1)\n - Querying the derived `command-bridges.generated.json` as data, rather than reading a prompt corpus, proved all six removed phrases reached the advisor surface's removal. (iteration 1)\n - Comparing the create presentation line against `GATE_3_CHOICE_RELATED` and its parity test proved the canonical wording match without a runtime branch. (iteration 1)\n+- Reading the derived `commandPolicies` instead of the route prose settled the attach question: every `mutating: mutates` doctor route is `ask`, and only read-only or add-only spec-folder routes are `run`. (iteration 2)\n+- The refusal/question guards and the spec 016/024 evidence closed the security and traceability passes without a new finding. (iteration 2)\n \n ## 9. WHAT FAILED\n \n - The A11-specific troubleshooting row was assumed to cover every A11 finding; it covers missing rows only, so the malformed-row case has no named repair. Recorded as `DR4-P2-001`, not a failed approach. (iteration 1)\n+- No new finding came from the security or traceability pass; the only active item remains the carried P2. (iteration 2)\n \n <!-- ANCHOR:exhausted-approaches -->\n ## 9. EXHAUSTED APPROACHES (do not retry)\n ### A cross-runtime defect in the changed create presentation is ruled out: the line is plain text, the canonical constant is shared, and the parity test covers it. -- BLOCKED (iteration 1, 1 attempts)\n","status":"modified","additions":3,"deletions":0}],"truncated":false},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Edited specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/doctor-docs-4/deep-review-strategy.md (1 replacement)"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"newString\": \"## 8. WHAT WORKED\\n\\n- Tracing the changed A11 detail to its two consumers (the presentation's repair table and the embed engine's router write) found the one actionable gap in an otherwise clean diff. (iteration 1)\\n- Querying the derived `command-bridges.generated.json` as data, rather than reading a prompt corpus, proved all six removed phrases reached the advisor surface's removal. (iteration 1)\\n- Comparing the create presentation line against `GATE_3_CHOICE_RELATED` and its parity test proved the canonical wording match without a runtime branch. (iteration 1)\\n- Reading t