{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794671098413,"sessionID":"ses_e255ff46effe7EWyuOLOEwVdy1","part":{"partID":"prt_1dabbb0b20021ZmAEofgZXuMoX","sessionID":"ses_e255ff46effe7EWyuOLOEwVdy1","messageID":"msg_1dabba29d001UOCO7GXBXX59ld","type":"tool","id":"chatcmpl-tool-a6fe05e5d8aac816","tool":"edit","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"newString":"- A transcript-scorer phantom-count finding is out of area: the changed files contain no transcript-scoring code. (iteration 1)\n- A mutating command attached or started by a refusal, question or mention is ruled out: mutating doctor routes derive `ask`, and `command-attach.ts:470-483` suppresses no-edit and command-only-mention prompts, with the guards test covering both. (iteration 2)\n- A cross-runtime rename gap is ruled out: the command is a symlink on Claude and Cursor, a generated file at the new name on Codex, Pi and DSH, and absent by design on Devin; no old-name command file remains. (iteration 2)\n- A spec/code contradiction on the phrase removal is ruled out: the `a494145dd0` body names the two false-offer reproductions, the `024` tests pin the refusal behavior, and the 016 floors are reported unchanged. (iteration 2)\n- Feature-catalog drift on the doctor routing policy is ruled out: the catalog's gating, `readOnly`, and three-word reach claims match the generated data and the deriver. (iteration 2)","oldString":"- A transcript-scorer phantom-count finding is out of area: the changed files contain no transcript-scoring code. (iteration 1)","path":"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/doctor-docs-4/deep-review-strategy.md"},"output":"Edited specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/doctor-docs-4/deep-review-strategy.md (1 replacement)","title":"edit","metadata":{"metadata":{"files":[{"file":"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/doctor-docs-4/deep-review-strategy.md","patch":"Index: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/doctor-docs-4/deep-review-strategy.md\n===================================================================\n--- specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/doctor-docs-4/deep-review-strategy.md\n+++ specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/doctor-docs-4/deep-review-strategy.md\n@@ -108,8 +108,12 @@\n - A P0/P1 in the A11 count logic is ruled out: the count is derived from the same arrays that build the printed lines, and the test's malformed row keeps its rule path so it is not reported missing. (iteration 1)\n - A P1 on the removed doctor phrases is ruled out: the remaining phrases cover each route's core requests, the derived bridge data is in sync, and the hand-off test pins the generic repair and release-note prompts as no-match. (iteration 1)\n - A P1 on the create sub-track wording is ruled out: the canonical Gate 3 menu and `suggest-subtracks.mjs` own sub-track creation, and the create workflow consumes an existing `spec_path`. (iteration 1)\n - A transcript-scorer phantom-count finding is out of area: the changed files contain no transcript-scoring code. (iteration 1)\n+- A mutating command attached or started by a refusal, question or mention is ruled out: mutating doctor routes derive `ask`, and `command-attach.ts:470-483` suppresses no-edit and command-only-mention prompts, with the guards test covering both. (iteration 2)\n+- A cross-runtime rename gap is ruled out: the command is a symlink on Claude and Cursor, a generated file at the new name on Codex, Pi and DSH, and absent by design on Devin; no old-name command file remains. (iteration 2)\n+- A spec/code contradiction on the phrase removal is ruled out: the `a494145dd0` body names the two false-offer reproductions, the `024` tests pin the refusal behavior, and the 016 floors are reported unchanged. (iteration 2)\n+- Feature-catalog drift on the doctor routing policy is ruled out: the catalog's gating, `readOnly`, and three-word reach claims match the generated data and the deriver. (iteration 2)\n \n <!-- ANCHOR:next-focus -->\n ## 11. NEXT FOCUS\n - Dimension: security + traceability (rotation; the 3-iteration cap requires combining the two after correctness). - Focus area: the doctor route mutation classes and phrase reach, the derived bridge policy (`read-only`/`add-only`/`mutates`), the packet's `016`/`025` spec and acceptance docs for these files, the feature-catalog and playbook descriptions, and the cross-runtime command mirrors. - Reason: iteration 1 found one advisory docs gap; the next pass must prove no question, refusal or command mention can attach a mutating route, and that the changed behavior is traceable to the packet's requirements. - Rotation status: correctness completed; security and traceability next; maintainability remains for the final pass. - Blocked/productive carry-forward: carry `DR4-P2-001` for a check that no other doctor doc names a repair for the malformed case. - Required evidence: `_routes.yaml` mutation classes and phrase lists, the policy derivation in `derive-command-bridges.cjs`, `doctor-helper-handoff.ts` thresholds, the packet's spec/tasks/acceptance docs, the feature catalog, and the manual playbook. - Recovery note: none. Review verdict: PASS\n","status":"modified","additions":4,"deletions":0}],"truncated":false},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Edited specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/doctor-docs-4/deep-review-strategy.md (1 replacement)"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"newString\": \"- A transcript-scorer phantom-count finding is out of area: the changed files contain no transcript-scoring code. (iteration 1)\\n- A mutating command attached or started by a refusal, question or mention is ruled out: mutating doctor routes derive `ask`, and `command-attach.ts:470-483` suppresses no-edit and command-only-mention prompts, with the guards test covering both. (iteration 2)\\n- A cross-runtime rename gap is ruled out: the command is a symlink on Claude and Cursor, a generated file at the new name on Codex, Pi and DSH, and absent by design on Devin; no old-name command file remains. (iteration 2)\\n- A spec/code contradiction on the phrase removal is ruled out: the `a494145dd0` body names the two false-offer reproductions, the `024` tests pin the refusal behavior, and the 016 floors are reported unchanged. (iteration 2)\\n- Feature-catalog drift on the doctor routing policy is ruled out: the catalog's gating, `readOnly`, and three-word reach claims match the generated data and the deriver. (iteration 2)\", \"oldString\": \"- A transcript-scorer phantom-count finding is out of area: the changed files contain no transcript-scoring code. (iteration 1)\", \"path\": \"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/doctor-docs-4/deep-review-strategy.md\"}"},"time":{"start":1794671095986,"end":1794671098413}}}}
