{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794671355247,"sessionID":"ses_e255ff46effe7EWyuOLOEwVdy1","part":{"partID":"prt_1dabf5415002xm7pPolm2YpGz7","sessionID":"ses_e255ff46effe7EWyuOLOEwVdy1","messageID":"msg_1dabf44d3001SB4DNzZoxw1Uaj","type":"tool","id":"chatcmpl-tool-b550085c230189d4","tool":"write","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"content":"# Iteration 003: Maintainability and final cross-reference\n\n## Dispatcher\n\n- Lineage `doctor-docs-4`, session `fanout-doctor-docs-4-1794669272137-9v23rz`, generation 1, lineage mode `new`.\n- Mode: review. Focus dimension: `maintainability` (final rotation; correctness, security and traceability are complete). Budget profile: `scan`.\n- Operator review focus: pass-four review of the doctor-docs area under `review-brief-4.txt`. This iteration addresses the brief's docs-that-disagree-with-code check at the style and maintainability level: whitespace, comment hygiene, test shape, documentation consistency and the final cross-reference before synthesis.\n- Steering: `steer.md` is absent in the lineage directory; no ruling was available to apply.\n- Sources read: `review-brief-4.txt:1`, `review-scope-4.txt:6-9`, `agents-md-check.cjs:790-815`, `agents-md-check.test.cjs:742-765`, `create-skill-presentation.txt:86-90`, `_routes.yaml:396-406,797-806`, `doctor-agents-md-presentation.txt:258-283`, `doctor-agents-md-check.md:30,102`, the reducer dashboard and registry, and the `git diff --check` and style probes over the four changed files.\n\n## Files Reviewed\n\n- `.skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/agents-md-check.cjs:790-815` (comment wording and count derivation)\n- `.skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/tests/agents-md-check.test.cjs:742-765` (new assertion and fixture)\n- `.skilled/commands/create/assets/create-skill-presentation.txt:86-90` (Q3 option C wording)\n- `.skilled/commands/doctor/_routes.yaml:396-406,797-806` (removed phrases and the remaining phrase lists)\n- `.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-agents-md-presentation.txt:258-283` (A11 repair and next-step wording)\n- `.skilled/manual-testing-playbook/doctor-commands/doctor-agents-md-check.md:30,102` (the repair-per-finding pass condition)\n- `deep-review-dashboard.md` and `deep-review-findings-registry.json` (final reducer views)\n\n## Findings - New\n\n### P0 Findings\n\nNone.\n\n### P1 Findings\n\nNone.\n\n### P2 Findings\n\nNone new. The carried `DR4-P2-001` remains active at P2. The maintainability review found no additional actionable issue in the changed lines: the new comment explains the durable why without an ephemeral label, the test pins the detail contract, the presentation line carries the canonical wording, and the route phrases keep their three-word floor.\n\n## Traceability Checks\n\n| Protocol | Status | Evidence |\n|----------|--------|----------|\n| `spec_code` | pass | The changed detail and phrase removal match the A-2 alignment item (`goal.md:216`), the T027 contract (`014-review-remediation/tasks.md:115`), the `a494145dd0` body, and the 016 REQ-007 floor. |\n| `checklist_evidence` | pass | AC-017, AC-003, AC-005 and AC-007 remain Met; the carried P2 is outside the checklist rows. |\n| `skill_agent` | notApplicable | No skill/agent pair changed. |\n| `agent_cross_runtime` | pass | The create command is consistent on every command-carrying runtime; the changed presentation is runtime-neutral. |\n| `feature_catalog_code` | pass | `doctor-command-routing.md` matches the generated policy and reach-probe behavior. |\n| `playbook_capability` | partial | The carried A11 repair mapping gap remains; the setup and update playbooks use typed commands and do not quote the removed phrases. |\n\n## Integration Evidence\n\n- `git diff --check 0cdc9fa3ef..HEAD` over the four changed files prints nothing: no trailing whitespace or conflict marker in the changed hunks.\n- `rg -n 'TODO|FIXME|HACK|XXX'` over the four files finds nothing, so no unresolved marker was introduced on a production path.\n- The new A11 comment at `agents-md-check.cjs:798-799` states the durable reason (\"a finding with nothing missing\") and carries no spec path, task id or phase label.\n- The new test assertion at `agents-md-check.test.cjs:763-764` pins the detail prefix and the earlier assertions pin the malformed line, the absent missing line, and the FINDING state, so the test covers the behavior rather than the implementation shape alone.\n- The create presentation line at `:89` is the canonical `GATE_3_CHOICE_RELATED` text; the parity test at `gate-3-menu-parity.test.mjs:46-57` covers the file.\n- The reducer dashboard reports `Provisional Verdict: PASS`, `hasAdvisories: true`, `hasSearchDebt: false`, and one active P2 after iteration 2.\n\n## Edge Cases\n\n- The carried P2 is a documentation mapping, not a code defect: the generic FINDING row at `doctor-agents-md-presentation.txt:262` still tells the operator to fix the requirement, so the advisory does not rise above P2.\n- The malformed count is derived as `lines.length - missing.length`; a future line family added to `lines` would silently join the count. No current input produces a wrong count, the malformed test keeps its rule path, and the expression is covered by the changed test, so this is a note rather than a finding.\n- The final stop is the three-iteration cap, not a converged stop; the synthesis must record `maxIterationsReached` and release readiness `in-progress`, even though the active findings are P2-only.\n- The holdout rule held across all three iterations: no prompt corpus was opened, and the commit's holdout evidence is a count only.\n\n## Confirmed-Clean Surfaces\n\n- The changed hunks pass `git diff --check` and carry no unresolved TODO/FIXME/HACK markers.\n- The new comment is durable and free of ephemeral artifact labels.\n- The new test pins the new detail and the malformed-row state without weakening the existing assertions.\n- The presentation line matches the canonical Gate 3 constant, and the route phrases keep the three-word floor.\n- The reducer views agree with the iteration records: one active P2, zero P0/P1, zero search debt, correctness/security/traceability covered.\n\n## Ruled Out\n\n- A maintainability finding on comment hygiene is ruled out: the new comment carries the why and no spec, task or phase label. (iteration 3)\n- A maintainability finding on whitespace or conflict markers is ruled out: `git diff --check` over the four changed files is clean. (iteration 3)\n- A test-brittleness finding on the new assertion is ruled out: the test pins the detail contract and the malformed state, and the existing lines keep the rule-path assertion. (iteration 3)\n- A hidden-coupling finding on `lines.length - missing.length` is ruled out as a current finding: no input in the check's stated contract produces a wrong count, and the malformed test covers the subtraction. (iteration 3)\n- The `sk-skill.md` \"OpenCode skills\" description stays ruled out as pre-existing and defensible: it is not a changed line and the `.skilled/skills` target is the OpenCode-origin skill tree. (iteration 2)\n\n## Next Focus\n\n- Dimension: none remaining; all four dimensions are covered.\n- Focus area: synthesis only.\n- Reason: the three-iteration cap is reached, the only active finding is the carried P2, and no new maintainability issue exists.\n- Rotation status: complete (correctness, security, traceability, maintainability).\n- Blocked/productive carry-forward: carry `DR4-P2-001` into the report; do not re-enter the ruled-out directions.\n- Required evidence: the final report's Active Finding Registry, Planning Packet and Audit Appendix.\n- Recovery note: none.\n\nReview verdict: PASS\n","path":"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/doctor-docs-4/iterations/iteration-003.md"},"output":"Created file successfully: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/doctor-docs-4/iterations/iteration-003.md","title":"write","metadata":{"metadata":{"truncated":false},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Created file successfully: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/doctor-docs-4/iterations/iteration-003.md"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"content\": \"# Iteration 003: Maintainability and final cross-reference\\n\\n## Dispatcher\\n\\n- Lineage `doctor-docs-4`, session `fanout-doctor-docs-4-1794669272137-9v23rz`, generation 1, lineage mode `new`.\\n- Mode: review. Focus dimension: `maintainability` (final rotation; correctness, security and traceability are complete). Budget profile: `scan`.\\n- Operator review focus: pass-four review of the doctor-docs area under `review-brief-4.txt`. This iteration addresses the brief's docs-that-disagree-with-code check at the style and maintainability level: whitespace, comment hygiene, test shape, documentation consistency and the final cross-reference before synthesis.\\n- Steering: `steer.md` is absent in the lineage directory; no ruling was available to apply.\\n- Sources read: `review-brief-4.txt:1`, `review-scope-4.txt:6-9`, `agents-md-check.cjs:790-815`, `agents-md-check.test.cjs:742-765`, `create-skill-presentation.txt:86-90`, `_routes.yaml:396-406,797-806`, `doctor-agents-md-presentation.txt:258-283`, `doctor-agents-md-check.md:30,102`, the reducer dashboard and registry, and the `git diff --check` and style probes over the four changed files.\\n\\n## Files Reviewed\\n\\n- `.skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/agents-md-check.cjs:790-815` (comment wording and count derivation)\\n- `.skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/tests/agents-md-check.test.cjs:742-765` (new assertion and fixture)\\n- `.skilled/commands/create/assets/create-skill-presentation.txt:86-90` (Q3 option C wording)\\n- `.skilled/commands/doctor/_routes.yaml:396-406,797-806` (removed phrases and the remaining phrase lists)\\n- `.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-agents-md-presentation.txt:258-283` (A11 repair and next-step wording)\\n- `.skilled/manual-testing-playbook/doctor-commands/doctor-agents-md-check.md:30,102` (the repair-per-finding pass condition)\\n- `deep-review-dashboard.md` and `deep-review-findings-registry.json` (final reducer views)\\n\\n## Findings - New\\n\\n### P0 Findings\\n\\nNone.\\n\\n### P1 Findings\\n\\nNone.\\n\\n### P2 Findings\\n\\nNone new. The carried `DR4-P2-001` remains active at P2. The maintainability review found no additional actionable issue in the changed lines: the new comment explains the durable why without an ephemeral label, the test pins the detail contract, the presentation line carries the canonical wording, and the route phrases keep their three-word floor.\\n\\n## Traceability Checks\\n\\n| Protocol | Status | Evidence |\\n|----------|--------|----------|\\n| `spec_code` | pass | The changed detail and phrase removal match the A-2 alignment item (`goal.md:216`), the T027 contract (`014-review-remediation/tasks.md:115`), the `a494145dd0` body, and the 016 REQ-007 floor. |\\n| `checklist_evidence` | pass | AC-017, AC-003, AC-005 and AC-007 remain Met; the carried P2 is outside the checklist rows. |\\n| `skill_agent` | notApplicable | No skill/agent pair changed. |\\n| `agent_cross_runtime` | pass | The create command is consistent on every command-carrying runtime; the changed presentation is runtime-neutral. |\\n| `feature_catalog_code` | pass | `doctor-command-routing.md` matches the generated policy and reach-probe behavior. |\\n| `playbook_capability` | partial | The carried A11 repair mapping gap remains; the setup and update playbooks use typed commands and do not quote the removed phrases. |\\n\\n## Integration Evidence\\n\\n- `git diff --check 0cdc9fa3ef..HEAD` over the four changed files prints nothing: no trailing whitespace or conflict marker in the changed hunks.\\n- `rg -n 'TODO|FIXME|HACK|XXX'` over the four files finds nothing, so no unresolved marker was introduced on a production path.\\n- The new A11 comment at `agents-md-check.cjs:798-799` states the durable reason (\\\"a finding with nothing missing\\\") and carries no spec path, task id or phase label.\\n- The new test assertion at `agents-md-check.test.cjs:763-764` pins the detail prefix and the earlier assertions pin the malformed line, the absent missing line, and the FINDING state, so the test covers the behavior rather than the implementation shape alone.\\n- The create presentation line at `:89` is the canonical `GATE_3_CHOICE_RELATED` text; the parity test at `gate-3-menu-parity.test.mjs:46-57` covers the file.\\n- The reducer dashboard reports `Provisional Verdict: PASS`, `hasAdvisories: true`, `hasSearchDebt: false`, and one active P2 after iteration 2.\\n\\n## Edge Cases\\n\\n- The carried P2 is a documentation mapping, not a code defect: the generic FINDING row at `doctor-agents-md-presentation.txt:262` still tells the operator to fix the requirement, so the advisory does not rise above P2.\\n- The malformed count is derived as `lines.length - missing.length`; a future line family added to `lines` would silently join the count. No current input produces a wrong count, the malformed test keeps its rule path, and the expression is covered by the changed test, so this is a note rather than a finding.\\n- The final stop is the three-iteration cap, not a converged stop; the synthesis must record `maxIterationsReached` and release readiness `in-progress`, even though the active findings are P2-only.\\n- The holdout rule held across all three iterations: no prompt corpus was opened, and the commit's holdout evidence is a count only.\\n\\n## Confirmed-Clean Surfaces\\n\\n- The changed hunks pass `git diff --check` and carry no unresolved TODO/FIXME/HACK markers.\\n- The new comment is durable and free of ephemeral artifact labels.\\n- The new test pins the new detail and the malformed-row state without weakening the existing assertions.\\n- The presentation line matches the canonical Gate 3 constant, and the route phrases keep the three-word floor.\\n- The reducer views agree with the iteration records: one active P2, zero P0/P1, zero search debt, correctness/security/traceability covered.\\n\\n## Ruled Out\\n\\n- A maintainability finding on comment hygiene is ruled out: the new comment carries the why and no spec, task or phase label. (iteration 3)\\n- A maintainability finding on whitespace or conflict markers is ruled out: `git diff --check` over the four changed files is clean. (iteration 3)\\n- A test-brittleness finding on the new assertion is ruled out: the test pins the detail contract and the malformed state, and the existing lines keep the rule-path assertion. (iteration 3)\\n- A hidden-coupling finding on `lines.length - missing.length` is ruled out as a current finding: no input in the check's stated contract produces a wrong count, and the malformed test covers the subtraction. (iteration 3)\\n- The `sk-skill.md` \\\"OpenCode skills\\\" description stays ruled out as pre-existing and defensible: it is not a changed line and the `.skilled/skills` target is the OpenCode-origin skill tree. (iteration 2)\\n\\n## Next Focus\\n\\n- Dimension: none remaining; all four dimensions are covered.\\n- Focus area: synthesis only.\\n- Reason: the three-iteration cap is reached, the only active finding is the carried P2, and no new maintainability issue exists.\\n- Rotation status: complete (correctness, security, traceability, maintainability).\\n- Blocked/productive carry-forward: carry `DR4-P2-001` into the report; do not re-enter the ruled-out directions.\\n- Required evidence: the final report's Active Finding Registry, Planning Packet and Audit Appendix.\\n- Recovery note: none.\\n\\nReview verdict: PASS\\n\", \"path\": \"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/doctor-docs-4/iterations/iteration-003.md\"}"},"time":{"start":1794671334421,"end":1794671355247}}}}
